    <node id="New Legislative Framework">
      <data key="d0">New Legislative Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The New Legislative Framework is a comprehensive set of European regulations designed to ensure that products comply with health, safety, and environmental standards while defining clear obligations for manufacturers. This framework governs various sectors within the European Union, facilitating harmonization and compliance across products. It outlines the EU's approach to product legislation, ensuring consistency in safety and compliance for member states regarding a diverse array of products, including those related to artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Furthermore, the New Legislative Framework provides detailed guidelines and requirements for compliance, emphasizing legal certainty for operators in relation to AI systems and their supply chains. Overall, it plays a crucial role in reinforcing the regulatory structure that governs product safety and compliance across the European market.&lt;SEP&gt;The New Legislative Framework is a legislative initiative in the Union aimed at ensuring product safety and conformity assessment across various sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66e6524323a5bff7a82ba7868399e18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1853942fcfd185abaf07003a8b70ff38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92136a9226f18376c3de5d9f6b6485ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9512f56ddf79fc1a7f65b696c84e2eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63123bed96791237f23a210dcf270306</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/124/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/87/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/64/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation refers to a comprehensive legal framework established by the European Union (EU) governing the deployment and use of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems across its member states. This binding legislative act must be applied uniformly in its entirety, ensuring the protection of individual rights and promoting the safety and reliability of AI technologies in accordance with established legal and ethical standards. 

The framework outlines obligations for product manufacturers and AI system providers, particularly emphasizing small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) to ensure their offerings are both safe and compliant with regulatory requirements. By providing a harmonized approach across all EU member states, the Regulation eliminates the complexity of having separate national legislation, thereby simplifying the compliance processes for various stakeholders, including SMEs and EU institutions.

The Regulation specifically addresses high-risk areas in AI applications, such as biometric identification and sectors related to military and national security. It mandates that AI systems maintain thorough documentation for compliance assessments and operational monitoring, ensuring accountability and safety. Governance procedures articulated in the Regulation include a framework for an independent Board and AI Office that oversee third-party conformity assessments related to cybersecurity and effective risk management protocols. 

Furthermore, the Regulation facilitates research and development in AI while balancing innovation with essential safeguards for public safety and individual rights. It specifies conditions under which certain AI systems may enter the market without undergoing full conformity assessments, particularly in areas impacting public safety and health. It also defines key terms, such as "publicly accessible space," and establishes criteria for the classification and access conditions of various physical environments where AI systems may be deployed.

Additionally, the Regulation addresses obligations for compliance with data privacy and protection laws, ensuring legal certainty for AI model providers. Overall, the Regulation serves as a vital legal foundation governing AI technologies within the EU, promoting ethical practices, safeguarding individual rights, and fostering an innovative environment while ensuring robust regulatory oversight. It emphasizes transparency, user understanding, and the ethical management of high-risk AI systems, and upholds compliance with health, safety, and fundamental rights standards.&lt;SEP&gt;This Regulation pertains to conformity assessment and outlines various duties and responsibilities associated with AI systems across the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation refers to a set of rules or directives made and maintained by an authority, in this case governing the use of law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation refers to legal frameworks governing the use of technology, particularly in the context of data protection and law enforcement.</data>
