    <node id="European Union">
      <data key="d0">European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Union (EU) is a political and economic union comprising primarily European member states aimed at promoting integration and cooperation among its members. This union is essential for maintaining stability and fostering collaborative relationships across the continent. The EU operates under a comprehensive regulatory framework that governs a multitude of sectors, including artificial intelligence (AI), cybersecurity, financial services, and biometric identification systems.

To address key issues such as human rights, accessibility, migration, asylum, defense, and security, the EU formulates and implements harmonized policies that significantly influence its member nations. By establishing common regulations and policies, the EU enhances collaboration and strengthens its role in international political and economic affairs.

In the context of AI, the EU oversees legislation concerning high-risk AI systems, rigorously enforcing regulations to ensure safety and compliance among AI model providers. Significant directives, including Directive (EU) 2016/680, focus on AI, data protection standards, and privacy rights, highlighting the EU's commitment to promoting ethical and trustworthy AI systems. Additionally, the EU drafts and enforces regulations aimed at supporting small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) in adapting to AI, contributing to a unified regulatory environment that addresses systemic risks.

By setting regulatory standards and negotiating agreements with third countries, the EU demonstrates a dedication to enhancing governance effectiveness. The comprehensive approach to governance and regulation that the EU embodies reflects its commitment to fostering cooperation and integration among its member states while implementing collective legislation that spans product safety, compliance in AI systems, and transparency in AI applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union is a political and economic union of member states located primarily in Europe, that works on harmonizing laws and policies among its members.</data>
