lligenceact.eu/recital/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/168/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428543</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member State">
      <data key="d0">Member State</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A Member State is defined as a sovereign country that is part of the European Union (EU). These countries exercise governance and authority within the framework of the EU, complying with its regulations and laws, especially concerning biometric systems and the oversight of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies, particularly in high-risk applications. Member States play a critical role in implementing decisions made by the European Commission regarding the authorization and regulation of high-risk AI systems. 

Each Member State is recognized as a separate entity within the EU and is responsible for ensuring compliance through national notified bodies. These designated entities assess adherence to established standards across various sectors, including AI. Moreover, Member States have the autonomy to establish their own competent authorities to monitor AI systems, as well as the ability to create national notified bodies according to their own legal frameworks.

Furthermore, Member States can develop AI regulatory sandboxes to foster experimentation and innovation while remaining within the existing regulatory environment. They are also responsible for implementing conformity assessment procedures to promote a cohesive regulatory landscape throughout the EU. A crucial aspect of their duties is adhering to directives aimed at protecting individual rights, highlighting their significant role in the EU’s regulatory oversight.

In addition to these responsibilities, Member States coordinate effectively to ensure the implementation of AI regulations, with each state represented by a designated official on the Board. They have the authority to enact national laws under EU regulations and determine the language and accessibility of instructions regarding the use of AI systems. Overall, Member States are pivotal to the political structure of the EU, fulfilling essential duties in the regulation and oversight of AI technologies and data protection measures, thereby ensuring compliance and safety within their jurisdictions in alignment with shared EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A Member State refers to any country that is part of the European Union and is subject to EU regulations, including those regarding AI practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The Member State refers to a nation within the EU that is responsible for ensuring compliance with the AI regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ae5c70e1b98b5f33eb047bb55022e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fbdf24f8b746547b54a3e43daaf33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d8a464e00ff30e1ae415351b48c67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7195e1644a22885c55968d2c801e0064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56424a5db573173fc67a6e62dd2d96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce4de2ee2430b55395c19336af7c01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26fcdeec947c5dfd024232093934843&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b4f722f831bc4c8c4594e971e7b7654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031fbe0de70cf6f462d8e21fea6487e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85726b1098cb96ad81df40234ad5da52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d21ee76ebe03dd794f42225c64861fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbacc8a39fa85eaf6afc731174af8109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcb340351b261f219fcf1a78d4f2f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c53f2e5a51e855855cf3895a52eefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e142ac7019ab93d80ef49579e8d0866e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd90900e1cf6e0c8072e210c7e853791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c78946b57af53cc3de27b286cf36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e43bf41139a924443fd8b200d694f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712fbb27f2ad82df6098ef5c90507342&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adccf24f1ddc4835908b879bcbe8674</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="market surveillance authority">
      <data key="d0">market surveillance authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance authorities oversee the compliance of products and services with regulatory standards to protect consumers and maintain market integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;The market surveillance authority is a regulatory entity tasked with monitoring compliance with market regulations across various sectors, including artificial intelligence (AI). This authority is responsible for overseeing and enforcing standards in alignment with European Union (EU) regulations and ensuring that providers adhere to their obligations. Specifically, the market surveillance authority addresses grievances related to AI usage and verifies compliance with regulations, as outlined in Article 74. Its mandate includes comprehensive oversight of market activities, ensuring that all entities operate within the established regulatory framework to promote fair and safe market practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The market surveillance authority is a regulatory body in each Member State responsible for overseeing testing plans and compliance with Union laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2763d61443dcf3aa274192c53e098997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-442777921e9a3bd01b79336245710651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b23a5bf3ea6e9c99542abdf17cfaa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fadd3405f1febb84753df655c577486</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/170/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428305</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CE marking">
      <data key="d0">CE marking</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The CE marking indicates compliance with health, safety, and environmental protection standards for products sold within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU declaration of conformity">
      <data key="d0">EU declaration of conformity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU declaration of conformity is a document that a manufacturer must draw up to declare that a product meets all necessary EU requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI system">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A high-risk AI system is defined as one that poses significant risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights of individuals and requires rigorous compliance and assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-risk AI system refers to advanced artificial intelligence technologies that are identified as having the potential to pose significant risks, particularly to health and safety. These systems necessitate strict regulation and compliance with specific obligations under various regulatory frameworks, including guidelines set forth by the European Union. High-risk AI systems are classified under particular regulations and are subject to various directives to ensure they operate safely and in accordance with legal requirements. They are designed for use in critical areas where safety is paramount, and their function must be carefully managed and maintained to ensure proper operation. Moreover, these systems can have significant impacts on human decision-making, thereby requiring stringent oversight to mitigate risks associated with their usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235710f8867a0e47878a2233118ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ca70346de523ce75c24d3a1979714d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1630fe82dedd2af2d49f1b480b55eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65688cdd97448f1f3932957595156d18</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Market Surveillance Authority is a regulatory body within a Member State responsible for overseeing compliance with EU laws regarding AI practices and market requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority is a public regulatory entity appointed by Member States to oversee compliance with market regulations, particularly concerning financial services and artificial intelligence (AI). Its primary function is to ensure adherence to legislation relevant to products and services, focusing on the safety and deployment of products, including high-risk AI systems.

The Authority plays a pivotal role in maintaining order within the marketplace by monitoring that products placed on the market meet necessary regulatory requirements across various sectors, especially within the European Union. This involves overseeing compliance with safety and performance standards, enforcing laws to protect public interests, and promoting consumer protection and overall market integrity.

One of the key responsibilities of the Market Surveillance Authority is to require deployers of AI systems to notify it after conducting impact assessments, enabling the evaluation of compliance concerning risk classifications and serious incidents, particularly for high-risk AI systems. It also has the authority to issue authorizations for these systems, ensuring compliance with legal requirements related to public security, health, and environmental protections.

Market Surveillance Authorities are tasked with approving and monitoring testing plans for high-risk AI systems and overseeing the compliance of providers in the testing of these systems under real-world conditions. This includes organizing tests to ensure that high-risk AI systems adhere to safety regulations and market standards. Additionally, the Authority has the power to withdraw unjustified authorizations for AI systems, further reinforcing its regulatory oversight.

In summary, the Market Surveillance Authority is essential in evaluating and monitoring products, especially high-risk AI systems, to ensure they conform to safety standards and regulations, thereby fostering a secure and compliant marketplace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2207c69786b5e6add33d2fe8c768a341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d8a464e00ff30e1ae415351b48c67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25e9684f684f1a6f65a611ff0868319c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7195e1644a22885c55968d2c801e0064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb2b1ecdb0a779493d4236bdef52a5f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26fcdeec947c5dfd024232093934843&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-893f47aa930b4d23e13586827fdcfea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd25b8a323071b471e7df42fd1a91ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c78946b57af53cc3de27b286cf36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ccfe5fb33f83ead7b5c0eb2f0576d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/153/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/85/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 48">
      <data key="d0">Article 48</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 48 refers to a specific regulation concerning the affixing of CE markings, which is critical for market compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 48 specifies the requirement to affix the CE marking to indicate conformity of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426023</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 47">
      <data key="d0">Article 47</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 47 discusses the requirement for an EU declaration of conformity for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 47 outlines the requirements for the EU declaration of conformity, which is essential for product compliance with EU standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 47 refers to a specific regulation that outlines the requirements for conformity assessments concerning AI systems, particularly those deemed high risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 47 specifies the production of the EU Declaration of Conformity accompanying a high-risk AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 47 includes provisions related to the adoption of delegated acts and the conditions surrounding them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 71">
      <data key="d0">Article 71</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 71 discusses the functioning of the EU database referenced in the regulation for managing information related to AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 is a part of EU regulations detailing the requirements for registering high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 is a specific provision within a regulation that may involve compliance or reporting requirements in the context of the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 mandates the registration processes for certain regulatory requirements within the EU framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 refers to a specific provision within EU regulations that highlights the framework for the management and reporting of data within the EU Database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f59bf399061bc73d559d6d3328c3ac41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-compliance">
      <data key="d0">Non-compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-compliance refers to failure or inability of AI systems and operators to meet the regulatory requirements as set by relevant authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-compliance refers to instances where providers fail to meet the necessary requirements set forth in EU legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-risk AI System">
      <data key="d0">High-risk AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A high-risk AI system is an artificial intelligence solution identified by regulators as having the potential to impact safety and compliance standards significantly.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-risk AI system refers to artificial intelligence technologies that are subject to strict regulatory requirements to ensure safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4321aa547f7fa9333c105c2b833ed9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities">
      <data key="d0">United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities is an international treaty aimed at protecting the rights and dignity of persons with disabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b15dea67a3df634ebeaeb58168eda214</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/80/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425971</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union">
      <data key="d0">Union</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union refers to a collective organization of states or entities that establishes regulations and laws affecting member countries.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union refers to the collective of countries, primarily associated with the European Union (EU), that forms a political and economic entity aimed at fostering democracy, rule of law, and innovation, particularly in the realm of artificial intelligence (AI). This organization comprises multiple member states that collaborate on a variety of policies and regulations, playing a critical role in shaping legislative frameworks focused on significant issues, especially those related to high-risk AI systems and services. 

The Union is responsible for creating and implementing comprehensive guidelines that govern these high-risk AI systems, ensuring adherence to fundamental rights and international agreements, particularly in protecting vulnerable populations. It strives for coherent practices across various sectors, including data protection, market surveillance, financial services, and law enforcement, thus crafting a unified legal structure that guides the development and enforcement of national laws.

To address challenges arising from rapid technological advancements, the Union has established regulatory sandboxes, which serve as experimental environments aimed at balancing the need for innovation with the necessity of protecting civil liberties and the interests of member states and their citizens. Furthermore, the Union is committed to advancing shared policies that promote economic growth and innovation through collaborative regulatory frameworks that encompass not only AI systems but also worker rights.

Central to its operations is a dedication to fundamental values such as human dignity, freedom, equality, democracy, and the rule of law, as enshrined in its Charter. Operating under a framework of treaties and regulations, the Union functions as a pivotal body in overseeing and regulating general-purpose AI models while ensuring a cohesive and responsible approach to technological development across its member nations. Through its efforts, the Union ensures the harmonization of laws related to various areas, including property rights, trade, and the secure movement of goods within internal markets, thereby reaffirming its position as a vital entity in fostering collaboration and legal standards among its member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union refers to the European Union, a political and economic union of member states that are located primarily in Europe, which is involved in the regulation of AI and support for SMEs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union refers to the collective of countries or states governed by the specified regulations around AI systems and conformity assessment.</data>
