    </node>
    <node id="online social network services">
      <data key="d0">online social network services</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Online social network services allow users to share content and may employ filters to modify images based on biometric features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e08e9858fc93c9af5672c3ebfa00189d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425975</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric data">
      <data key="d0">biometric data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric data consists of unique physical or behavioral characteristics of individuals, used in identification systems to match against reference databases.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data refers to personal data derived from biological characteristics of individuals, used for identification and categorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data refers to unique physical or behavioral characteristics of individuals used for identification purposes, such as fingerprints, facial recognition, and iris patterns, which are governed by strict legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data refers to unique physical characteristics used for identification purposes, such as fingerprints, facial recognition, and iris scans.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data refers to the unique physical or behavioral characteristics used to identify individuals, such as facial expressions, gestures, and voice attributes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35f73469c0e0803dabff693c3a8808fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08e9858fc93c9af5672c3ebfa00189d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="natural persons">
      <data key="d0">natural persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural persons are defined as individual human beings, distinguishing them from organizations or legal entities. They play a crucial role in various contexts, including legal investigations and proceedings, where their rights and interests must be protected, especially in relation to the use of AI technologies. Additionally, natural persons are often subject to biometric categorization, as their biometric data can be processed by identification systems for verification purposes. The deployment of AI technologies can have a direct impact on their rights and safety, emphasizing the importance of safeguarding these aspects in the context of artificial intelligence. Overall, natural persons are vital in legal contexts and should be recognized for their unique status and the importance of protecting their rights and interests.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons refer to individuals who are responsible for registering the system and have legal authority to represent the provider or deployer.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons in this context are individuals assigned to monitor and oversee the operation of high-risk AI systems, ensuring proper understanding and management of their limitations.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons refer to individual human beings whose rights and safety are considered during the regulation and application of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8637916ea42060e68c1064d171c7c635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08e9858fc93c9af5672c3ebfa00189d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235710f8867a0e47878a2233118ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c050cd15355d97e10ed144cad8796e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5345c3cccd7883e192f55328579d86d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d447a0dff9a51bc6e0b8b9c92046aaae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/130/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="filters">
      <data key="d0">filters</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Filters that categorize facial or body features are tools used in digital platforms to modify images based on biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e08e9858fc93c9af5672c3ebfa00189d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425975</data>
    </node>
    <node id="commercial service">
      <data key="d0">commercial service</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Commercial services involve the provision of goods or services to consumers, potentially utilizing biometric categorisation features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e08e9858fc93c9af5672c3ebfa00189d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425975</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content Sharing">
      <data key="d0">Content Sharing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Content Sharing refers to the act of distributing information and media through digital platforms, facilitating interaction and engagement among users online.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e5a0cdbed468e89c8732f44194704d8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425975</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Online Interaction">
      <data key="d0">Online Interaction</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e5a0cdbed468e89c8732f44194704d8</data>
      <data key="d2">Content Sharing encompasses various forms of Online Interaction, allowing users to engage and exchange information."|&gt;"digital interaction, online activity</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425975</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union law">
      <data key="d0">Union law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law comprises the legal statutes and regulations that govern the actions of Member States and organizations within the Union, including the use of AI and biometric systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law consists of the laws and regulations enacted by the European Union that govern member states and ensure compliance with common standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to the comprehensive body of laws and regulations established by the European Union that governs its member states. It encompasses various legal frameworks intended to protect individuals' rights and data, while also overseeing the research, development, and regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems within its jurisdiction. Union law is characterized by its focus on fundamental rights protection, consumer rights, and the legal principles articulated in European Union treaties and regulations. In summary, Union law serves as the foundational legal structure that regulates the interactions among member states, ensuring the safeguarding of rights and the orderly regulation of emerging technologies like AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to the body of laws established by the European Union, governing member states and their interactions with EU policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab6fc5c923f500a88ff985caeb05f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7127c7bb3049241e70ac955f8f0024b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5345c3cccd7883e192f55328579d86d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f7f5e50e0159a18231b3da95f30cab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427845</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charter">
      <data key="d0">Charter</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charter refers to the Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union, a significant document that enshrines a variety of essential rights and freedoms. It guarantees rights to freedom of expression, as well as the arts and sciences, which are particularly relevant in the context of AI-generated content. The Charter outlines fundamental rights that must be upheld when processing personal data, encompassing key protections such as data protection, privacy, and the rights of the child. 

Additionally, it establishes the right to nondiscrimination and emphasizes the importance of upholding democratic values and principles within the Union. The Charter serves as a foundational framework that must be consistent with regulations concerning high-risk AI systems, ensuring that the fundamental rights it enshrines are respected and protected in the rapidly evolving technological landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de89422ce8e678b380eeca18a71bfb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a11bcb90e7333ffe457649980a31a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93e6a954a9283acf571ff61858a432ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f7f5e50e0159a18231b3da95f30cab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428238</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Law encompasses legal protections for public interests and fundamental rights against harm caused by technological developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Law refers to the comprehensive legal framework established by the European Union (EU), which regulates a wide array of areas, including the relationship and obligations of its Member States. This framework addresses numerous legal matters that are vital for the functioning of the EU, particularly focusing on technology usage, employment conditions, fundamental rights, financial practices, and the governance of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and biometric technologies.

Union Law encompasses various regulations and legal frameworks that Member States must adhere to, particularly regarding liability, testing protocols, administrative fines, and infringements related to high-risk AI systems. It emphasizes the importance of risk management processes, compliance with data protection regulations, and the confidentiality and effective functionality of these technologies. 

The primary objectives of Union Law are to ensure consistency across Member States while protecting individual rights, particularly concerning privacy, fairness, non-discrimination, and data rights, which are critical in dealing with sensitive information, such as biometric data. Furthermore, it outlines the responsibilities of AI system providers and provides necessary guidelines for Member States and institutions regarding their obligations in data protection and confidentiality.

Additionally, Union Law encompasses regulations related to copyright, consumer protection, and competition law, thereby governing a diverse range of activities within the EU. Overall, Union Law plays a crucial role in fostering a safe, ethical, and equitable framework for the development and use of technologies, ensuring that the rights and interests of individuals are respected and upheld amidst the rapid advancements in technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law represents a framework of regulations and directives governing the rights of data subjects, particularly in relation to data protection and privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Law refers to the legal framework governing the standards and regulations that apply to AI systems and their quality management.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Law refers to the body of laws enacted by the European Union aimed at protecting fundamental rights and regulating AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0d79706d66f4b2474faeded28100a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c69786b5e6add33d2fe8c768a341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb1781c5c0edcb30e49953ca1852eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078bfdf1b899d975b7606b4acd63166d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57118cd489d78b33ed75c63f33151aee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc4d8b4e0e145ee1cf76386d881919f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b1b6d000ef2c2e744936b8e5264e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7195e1644a22885c55968d2c801e0064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b12370838dd1a62b5ded5dc20979b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ef04b3893d2080962790dc78128cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da6e9cf5fd822e42b8f37d6d2798af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d21ee76ebe03dd794f42225c64861fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f000e09b1fe2828e775be2862b588e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5ea4945288b78b6ce93568aea26b18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df1f3eba6d36bfd15e8ab3333ac4fd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afaea4dcd95d49cc4d21cf9078216b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b4365b37f348c4492d16b0258db2b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f7f5e50e0159a18231b3da95f30cab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5878750a2a2a6290f1a946976f92b6e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951511d7a62f58da07aebc05f3e4f1c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b917b23f883123c9ae4bf6c69ae5e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fbb87b8107271f1fe959942ad2e3666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4425b51346d70d56a2933633cfeb0018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9c861dfef84b47d382d7c3a57b94afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c89fbb177b0adfb819460dd999b9788d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9e7815086e5c37a3beb2705ee18d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3200d57c186d7db38b0cfb2e5cddca1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ef56265dcb6096b96bc5ee3bfe08c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad430846dc3448ba37c9f18d213e761</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/172/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/171/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/155/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/119/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/86/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428497</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Law">
      <data key="d0">National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National Law encompasses the legal statutes and regulations established by individual Member States to govern activities within their territories in compliance with overarching Union law. It refers to the legal systems operating within specific countries, which may impose distinct requirements for artificial intelligence (AI) systems and biometric identification. This body of law includes various legal rules that govern multiple aspects of technology, particularly concerning the handling and retention of logs for AI systems, ensuring that such practices align with domestic regulations.

Additionally, National Law articulates the rights and obligations of workers and employers, reflecting the unique legal principles formulated by each country's governing body. While National Law must adhere to the standards set by Union law, it may also delineate specific provisions that either complement or contrast with those regulations, resulting in a complex legal landscape. Ultimately, National Law serves to guide the behaviors of individuals and organizations, detailing their responsibilities related to the use of AI technology and the management of associated data handling practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19fe8af9bab5bc955f3f1bb6e0c9c017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a33f9372e32e8879cc6f97cd662934d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9c861dfef84b47d382d7c3a57b94afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e43bf41139a924443fd8b200d694f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f7f5e50e0159a18231b3da95f30cab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce4de2ee2430b55395c19336af7c01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/167/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Polygraphs">
      <data key="d0">Polygraphs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Polygraphs are tools used to detect emotional states and are mentioned in the context of regulations on personal data and AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-09f7f5e50e0159a18231b3da95f30cab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/63/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Personal Data refers to any information related to an identified or identifiable natural person, which can be processed in various ways for different purposes under data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data encompasses any information that relates to an identified or identifiable individual, subject to protection under various laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data represents information about natural persons that requires protection under both Union law and the Charter when processed by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data encompasses any information that relates to an identified or identifiable individual, which is protected under various regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data consists of information relating to identified or identifiable individuals, which requires special handling under data protection laws to prevent misuse or discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c8c5c853ef5b667f9cd6deb981812e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f7f5e50e0159a18231b3da95f30cab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-on-demand platform">
      <data key="d0">AI-on-demand platform</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI-on-demand platform aims to promote and protect innovation within the context of European Union funding and initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI-on-demand platform is an initiative aimed at supporting the implementation of AI regulations and facilitating compliance among providers and notified bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816d4247559a68f4b8ceca952f4e1069</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/144/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Digital Innovation Hubs">
      <data key="d0">European Digital Innovation Hubs</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">European Digital Innovation Hubs are centers that support innovation and digital transformation within the EU, assisting businesses in navigating AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs are entities that assist organizations in adopting digital technologies and innovations at both Union and national levels.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs are entities that support the digital transformation of businesses and public services across Europe with access to technology and expertise.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs serve as organizations that facilitate access to high-quality data sets for high-risk AI systems and promote innovation in digital transformation across Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2f4cab7db3f8f9288f3fd79ff9595e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission">
      <data key="d0">Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission refers to a body responsible for overseeing and designating Union AI testing support structures in the regulation of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission refers to the European Commission, which is responsible for proposing legislation, implementing decisions, upholding treaties, and managing the day-to-day business of the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission, formally known as the European Commission, is the executive branch and governing body of the European Union (EU), playing a pivotal role in the oversight and regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) and related technologies. It is responsible for implementing regulations, assessing compliance, and overseeing the recommendations of the Advisory Forum. One of its primary functions is the evaluation and classification of AI models based on their operational capabilities and potential impacts, including the identification of systemic risks associated with such models, especially general-purpose ones.

To fulfill its regulatory mandate, the Commission adopts implementing acts, establishes common specifications for standardization requirements, and collaborates with specialized entities like the AI Office and the Scientific Panel, which provide expert advice and impartial oversight. Additionally, it develops guidelines and regulations for both microenterprises and high-risk AI systems, actively involving itself in consultations about conformity assessments and assessing the competence of notified bodies.

The Commission is also responsible for approving codes of practice, ensuring compliance with content detection and labeling obligations, and promoting AI literacy among Member States. It works alongside the European Artificial Intelligence Board to develop voluntary codes of conduct and sets legal criteria for evaluating AI models. The Commission appoints independent experts for assessments and manages access to testing and experimentation facilities in line with EU harmonization legislation.

Moreover, the Commission oversees a comprehensive EU database for monitoring compliance with established regulations, reporting on administrative fines imposed by Member States, and issuing guidelines related to enforcement measures and penalties. Through these activities, the Commission champions transparency and compliance with AI legislation, facilitates communication around emerging technologies, and promotes innovation within the EU’s regulatory framework. Its sum of responsibilities highlights the Commission's essential role in the evolving landscape of AI regulation across Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7127c7bb3049241e70ac955f8f0024b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214363bac320d3b288355fb10d6c0537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d8a464e00ff30e1ae415351b48c67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3917f629d239e59c1197ea2404615c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6884d6c4641c256f66289e2e2b56965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79b7078e45aa680595b27c1baab1b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816d4247559a68f4b8ceca952f4e1069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb8d7d117faa045c40802649821c422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b84ed9e420c0ae0245bb808d08db0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c53f2e5a51e855855cf3895a52eefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe20aa0cce0b31f6a43c755317350d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b6d55e2d7c256240e44f70df0e5d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bff2cb7a8bc7b162d1d512fa7d0a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcf2e7f28d217ab321153caf980fbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17415cb7c434857a3d1c816705105aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638834e00b09677a065c6dc80878fa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0ab303aa0764433ae306cd3e410cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eef924ac2e26af24531952fcd79e9d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c0980cd75cdf016ff776144a4a70db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56424a5db573173fc67a6e62dd2d96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fb722dbde5159480cfd0e4534fc632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4903f69522ce55807b4320731843ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb2b1ecdb0a779493d4236bdef52a5f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4825b8c430847477f9ab6dc8f1b19797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e116bc92c8c7cf688c26ea188fd0b2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85726b1098cb96ad81df40234ad5da52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ac4d6cae0afd3292516531be7716e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafe6ac227379dad776c22a5abc16ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88552f4423ec18db9bfb3db0f708349&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede6b0da3acfca47d4e90d51eb5fc4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553e3df123166674b26c5dc07f2a83af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d447a0dff9a51bc6e0b8b9c92046aaae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb1781c5c0edcb30e49953ca1852eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ae5c70e1b98b5f33eb047bb55022e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-408ee65c3eab1e86c1c4207deaf4f216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094ac0cdb13f3aae73279288ea0dd3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c361588e67b3e6b1c6d9ddf94840a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a24148385124cc6a8cba737414c55a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee723ad2204a364a1d2dbe158b59a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9e7815086e5c37a3beb2705ee18d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab65b498e8d012c9f396c7e602afc69f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8c2328a0858ecaf11e83a00191d499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294b469b584f56e6e7fcf1b55e7e0df7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-893f47aa930b4d23e13586827fdcfea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f93de63e4907e805d3e56afc25c0472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e43bf41139a924443fd8b200d694f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6b3a7a24bfd18cc84baf6173985e105</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/127/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/117/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/162/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/146/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/174/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/175/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/135/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/64/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/98/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/144/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing and Experimentation Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Testing and Experimentation Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing and Experimentation Facilities are facilities established to provide technical and scientific support for compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing and Experimentation Facilities are organizations that provide support for the practical testing of AI systems in controlled environments, often linked with regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing and experimentation facilities provide the necessary infrastructure for testing products and systems, including AI technologies, to ensure they meet regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="implementation risks">
      <data key="d0">implementation risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Implementation risks refer to potential obstacles and challenges that may arise when applying regulations, particularly due to lack of knowledge and expertise in the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers">
      <data key="d0">providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are entities that offer products or services, who need to comply with regulations to operate legally and efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="small and medium enterprises (SMEs)">
      <data key="d0">small and medium enterprises (SMEs)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">SMEs refer to businesses with a limited scale of operations, often highlighted for their potential in fostering innovation, particularly in the development of AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) are businesses whose personnel numbers fall below certain limits, facing unique challenges in compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bfe284b31053ed0488ca88518b58ac1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/8/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427716</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notified bodies">
      <data key="d0">notified bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Notified bodies are organizations designated by national authorities to assess the conformity of products before they are placed on the market, ensuring compliance with specific regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified bodies are organizations designated by national authorities to assess the conformity of products before they are placed on the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426975</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation compliance">
      <data key="d0">Regulation compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation compliance involves adhering to the laws and rules established to govern practices within specific industries, ensuring safety and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="testing facilities">
      <data key="d0">testing facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing facilities are specialized sites that carry out evaluations and experiments to ensure products meet regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ccb1e24a4a8b04a03f252f2403ed11a4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/145/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Advisory Forum">
      <data key="d0">Advisory Forum</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Advisory Forum consists of stakeholders consulted by the Commission to ensure diverse representation and input in standardisation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Advisory Forum is proposed to ensure stakeholder involvement in implementing regulations and provide technical expertise to governing bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Advisory Forum refers to a group of experts or stakeholders that may provide input or feedback during the Board's decision-making processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Advisory Forum is a group established to provide technical expertise and advise the Board and the Commission regarding regulations, with a focus on AI.&lt;SEP&gt;The Advisory Forum is responsible for holding meetings, inviting experts, and preparing reports based on the objectives of specific regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbc432dadad605b2e47a18258f70a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ac4d6cae0afd3292516531be7716e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Board">
      <data key="d0">Board</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Board is a governing body established to oversee activities related to market surveillance, regulations, and the regulatory landscape of artificial intelligence (AI). It is composed of representatives from Member States and plays a crucial role in implementing regulations that govern AI. The Board is responsible for communicating decisions on fines imposed by the European Commission to relevant stakeholders, providing guidance and advice to national competent authorities and the Commission. 

In its efforts to ensure adherence to codes of practice within the AI sector, the Board has the authority to establish both standing and temporary sub-groups that address specific issues, fostering cooperation with various Union bodies and groups. The Board receives informed updates from the AI Office regarding measures and alerts related to systemic risks associated with AI models, which is vital for monitoring the effectiveness of codes of practice and ensuring that objectives are met by all participants.

Moreover, the Board is tasked with receiving annual reports and overseeing the implementation of the AI regulatory sandbox. It also consults with the Commission while preparing standardisation requests and discussions concerning AI standards, playing an integral role in the standardisation process. Through these activities, the Board facilitates dialogue and compliance, enhancing regulatory oversight and effectiveness within the rapidly evolving AI landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Board is an entity that oversees the activities of the Advisory Forum and the overall regulatory framework.&lt;SEP&gt;The Board is mentioned as a body that can request opinions and reports from the Advisory Forum.&lt;SEP&gt;The Board is a regulatory body that the Commission consults to ensure proper guidelines for AI systems, particularly those related to high-risk classifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294b469b584f56e6e7fcf1b55e7e0df7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a24148385124cc6a8cba737414c55a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da283c72662f2af740c6edac711fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbc432dadad605b2e47a18258f70a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ac4d6cae0afd3292516531be7716e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f3473e38ccd9ad84662b373166a5c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1552bf93eb98e5313a0207e768b7d357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428525</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights Agency">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fundamental Rights Agency is a permanent member of the Advisory Forum, contributing expertise in fundamental rights issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fundamental Rights Agency is an EU agency that influences policy-making to promote fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENISA">
      <data key="d0">ENISA</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ENISA is the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity and serves as a permanent member of the Advisory Forum.&lt;SEP&gt;ENISA is the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity, responsible for providing expertise and support on various cybersecurity issues, particularly in relation to AI systems under EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;ENISA, the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity, is responsible for enhancing the cybersecurity capabilities across Europe and collaborating on related regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;ENISA, the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity, provides expertise and advice on cybersecurity issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b330c1d8e73efeff5ccfef0a4f9ecd54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Committee for Standardization (CEN)">
      <data key="d0">European Committee for Standardization (CEN)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">CEN is a body that develops and maintains European standards and is a permanent member of the Advisory Forum.&lt;SEP&gt;CEN is an organization that focuses on developing and promoting European standards across various industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization (CENELEC)">
      <data key="d0">European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization (CENELEC)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">CENELEC is an organization responsible for standards in the electrotechnical field in Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;CENELEC is responsible for European standardization in electrotechnical matters and is a permanent member of the Advisory Forum.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI)">
      <data key="d0">European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ETSI is an organization that develops globally applicable standards for information and communications technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;ETSI is involved in standardization in telecommunications and is a permanent member of the Advisory Forum.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stakeholders">
      <data key="d0">Stakeholders</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholders are diverse actors within the artificial intelligence (AI) ecosystem, encompassing a wide range of individuals and organizations that contribute to the development, implementation, and regulation of AI technologies. This group includes researchers, innovators, industry leaders, advocacy groups, and standardization organizations, all of whom play a critical role in shaping AI practices and policies.

Recognized as various parties who may be impacted by AI regulations, stakeholders represent both commercial and non-commercial interests. They consist of multiple interest groups such as civil society, industry players, and academics, emphasizing the importance of inclusive participation in discussions surrounding AI. Stakeholders provide valuable input at both Union and national levels regarding the development and implications of AI systems, ensuring a collaborative approach to the regulatory framework of the AI landscape.

In addition to shaping policies, stakeholders also play a crucial role in the standardization process by offering input and feedback on standards and regulations related to AI. They include all individuals, groups, and organizations with an interest in or affected by the use of AI technologies, comprising providers, users, and advocacy groups. Furthermore, stakeholders are relevant parties involved in advisory forums and may participate in meetings to express their interests and concerns. Overall, stakeholders are essential to fostering an inclusive and effective dialogue about the deployment and governance of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30361d2283908d9b7babf63ae110a691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ac4d6cae0afd3292516531be7716e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f3473e38ccd9ad84662b373166a5c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafe6ac227379dad776c22a5abc16ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Expertise">
      <data key="d0">Technical Expertise</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical expertise represents the knowledge and skills provided to support regulatory implementation and decision-making processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425983</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs)">
      <data key="d0">Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">SMEs are a category of business entities that play a significant role in the economy and are included in the stakeholder representation efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425983</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Industry">
      <data key="d0">Industry</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Industry encompasses various business sectors involved in commercial activities, participating in the advisory forum.&lt;SEP&gt;The industry refers to businesses and corporations involved in the development and application of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Industry includes businesses and companies that are stakeholders in the AI domain, contributing to the codes of practice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426359</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Start-ups">
      <data key="d0">Start-ups</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Start-ups are early-stage companies that develop innovative products or services, particularly in the area of AI, and share similar regulatory needs as SMEs.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups are new businesses seeking to establish themselves in the commercial landscape and are part of stakeholder representation.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups are newly established businesses, often aimed at innovation and technology, that may take part in AI regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6741d9dacc504660a09282cfdfdfe32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427022</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Academia">
      <data key="d0">Academia</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Academia refers to a collective of educational institutions and researchers dedicated to the exploration and dissemination of knowledge. This sector plays a critical role in providing insights and support for the development of AI codes of practice, contributing to both regulatory practices and the ethical understanding of AI systems. Through their research and educational initiatives, academia contributes to the advancement of trustworthy AI, emphasizing the importance of AI ethics and the implications of AI technologies. Scholars within academia engage in extensive discussions and research focused on the ethical dimensions and societal impacts of artificial intelligence, making them a vital part of the conversation surrounding AI and its regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civil Society">
      <data key="d0">Civil Society</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil Society encompasses various non-governmental organizations and groups that advocate for ethical standards in AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil society includes a wide range of organizations and groups that advocate for ethical practices in AI development and deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil society represents non-governmental organizations and community groups advocating for public interest and rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0cbfdb0213c7d2eb8c1b2d49876e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/150/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI value chain">
      <data key="d0">AI value chain</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI value chain encapsulates the stages of AI system development, deployment, and oversight, including responsibility sharing among stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain refers to the sequence of processes involving the development and deployment of AI systems, tools, and services that work together to create high-risk AI applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457bf0e90f1920e6839b11cd66b1060b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/85/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tools and Services">
      <data key="d0">Tools and Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Tools and services encompass various software and applications designed for public use, including those related to AI, that aim to aid developers and organizations in their integration efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Tools and services encompass various software applications and support systems that facilitate the development, implementation, and operation of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Training">
      <data key="d0">Model Training</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model training is the process of teaching an AI system to recognize patterns using a dataset, allowing it to make predictions or decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425986</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Testing">
      <data key="d0">Model Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model testing involves evaluating an AI model's performance and accuracy, ensuring it meets the required standards before deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425986</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Model Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model evaluation is the assessment of an AI model's effectiveness based on defined metrics and performance criteria after it has been trained.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425986</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Integration into Software">
      <data key="d0">Integration into Software</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Integration into software refers to the process of embedding AI systems within existing software frameworks to automate tasks and enhance functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425986</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider">
      <data key="d0">Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Provider is an entity that can be either a natural or legal person involved in the development, supply, and distribution of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. These Providers are essential to the AI ecosystem, particularly concerning high-risk AI technologies, as they are responsible for placing these systems on the market and putting them into service. To ensure compliance with regulatory requirements, Providers must establish a representative within the European Union.

Providers are entrusted with significant obligations related to the safety and regulatory compliance of the AI technologies they distribute. This includes conducting initial reporting and investigations of serious incidents involving their AI systems, as well as registering these systems in the EU Database prior to market placement or deployment. They must maintain comprehensive documentation and collaborate with regulatory authorities to ensure adherence to applicable laws and standards.

In addition to supplying high-risk AI systems, Providers are responsible for evaluating any predetermined changes during the conformity assessment process, ensuring that their operations align with established regulations. They play a critical role in overseeing the development and implementation of safety measures for these high-risk AI systems before their market release, consequently facilitating the safe and responsible development and distribution of AI technologies. Furthermore, Providers must ensure that the AI systems they offer are used in compliance with safety and regulatory standards, embodying a crucial aspect of the governance and regulation of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;A provider is an entity that develops or supplies the AI system, responsible for its testing and adherence to regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Provider refers to any organization or entity that conducts or intends to conduct testing of products, including high-risk AI systems in real-world conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider refers to individuals or companies that develop and deploy AI systems and are involved in testing and compliance processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8c2328a0858ecaf11e83a00191d499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89272eea67d32d6ca0a58d004c2f75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a9cac9d5c84dcacd663b50bbd6c7786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b453ab3d6dba9c33ee17222e5c44491b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb293bcc156cb87ef4a7db6744a38f0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-893f47aa930b4d23e13586827fdcfea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d21ee76ebe03dd794f42225c64861fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bca7fe15bcbe076f97f98b2f3479775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-858c2a77ba4972f9c4e3f47479bfef07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/128/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/86/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/65/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428310</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intellectual Property Rights">
      <data key="d0">Intellectual Property Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intellectual Property Rights are legal rights that grant creators exclusive control over the use of their inventions, designs, and artistic works.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights protect the creations of individuals and organizations, ensuring ownership and preventing unauthorized use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a33f9372e32e8879cc6f97cd662934d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/167/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trade Secrets">
      <data key="d0">Trade Secrets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade Secrets are confidential business information that provides a company with a competitive edge and needs protection from disclosure.&lt;SEP&gt;Trade secrets are confidential business practices or information that provide competitive advantages and are protected from disclosure.&lt;SEP&gt;Trade secrets are confidential business information that provides a competitive edge, the protection of which is mandated under confidentiality obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Trade secrets are practices, designs, formulas, processes, or any other information that is kept confidential to maintain a competitive advantage in business.&lt;SEP&gt;Trade Secrets refer to practices, designs, formulas, processes, or any confidential business information that provide a competitive edge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a33f9372e32e8879cc6f97cd662934d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7ec602a72f4c2f19a5693b37872b32</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/167/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI HLEG">
      <data key="d0">AI HLEG</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI HLEG (High-Level Expert Group on Artificial Intelligence) is an independent group that developed the Ethics guidelines for trustworthy AI, appointed by the European Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI are a set of non-binding guidelines established to ensure that AI is trustworthy and ethically sound.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="seven non-binding ethical principles">
      <data key="d0">seven non-binding ethical principles</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The seven non-binding ethical principles for AI include human agency and oversight, technical robustness and safety, privacy and data governance, transparency, diversity, non-discrimination and fairness, societal and environmental well-being, and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="human agency and oversight">
      <data key="d0">human agency and oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human agency and oversight is one of the seven ethical principles that emphasize the role of humans in controlling AI systems to respect human dignity and personal autonomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="technical robustness and safety">
      <data key="d0">technical robustness and safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical robustness and safety is an ethical principle focusing on the reliable and safe functioning of AI systems to minimize risks and unintended consequences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="privacy and data governance">
      <data key="d0">privacy and data governance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Privacy and data governance is an ethical principle that ensures AI systems comply with data protection rules and maintain high standards of data quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="transparency">
      <data key="d0">transparency</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency is an ethical principle that promotes clarity and understanding about AI systems' capabilities and limitations while ensuring user awareness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="diversity, non-discrimination and fairness">
      <data key="d0">diversity, non-discrimination and fairness</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This ethical principle advocates for diverse representation in AI development and prohibits discriminatory impacts and biases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="societal and environmental well-being">
      <data key="d0">societal and environmental well-being</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Societal and environmental well-being is an ethical principle focused on developing AI systems that are sustainable and beneficial for society as a whole.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="accountability">
      <data key="d0">accountability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Accountability is one of the ethical principles that requires AI systems to be used responsibly, with clear lines of responsibility for their impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standardisation Organisations">
      <data key="d0">Standardisation Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Standardisation Organisations are entities involved in the development of standards that AI providers must follow to ensure compliance and interoperability.&lt;SEP&gt;Standardisation organisations are bodies that develop norms and standards, assisting in the ethical oversight of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Standardisation organisations develop and promote standards to ensure quality and consistency in products and services, including those related to AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Privacy">
      <data key="d0">Privacy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Privacy refers to the right of individuals to control their personal information, ensuring it is protected and managed in compliance with relevant laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Privacy refers to the right of individuals to keep their personal information from being disclosed or accessed by unauthorized parties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Governance">
      <data key="d0">Data Governance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Governance provides a framework for managing personal data in accordance with legal and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Data governance encompasses the management of data availability, usability, integrity, and security in organizations, especially concerning AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Data governance involves the management of data integrity, security, and availability, ensuring that data handling is compliant with legal and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Data governance involves practices and processes that ensure data integrity and compliance with legal and regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Data governance involves the overall management of data availability, usability, integrity, and security in AI systems, ensuring compliance with legal standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e010ebb9b0353d97d9e67673267bc415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b1b6d000ef2c2e744936b8e5264e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ef56265dcb6096b96bc5ee3bfe08c2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/69/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428214</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency">
      <data key="d0">Transparency</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency involves the clear communication of how AI systems function, ensuring users are aware of their interactions with such technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diversity">
      <data key="d0">Diversity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Diversity refers to the inclusion of various demographics in the development and utilization of AI systems to prevent biases and enhance fairness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Discrimination">
      <data key="d0">Non-Discrimination</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-discrimination emphasizes that AI systems should be developed to ensure equal treatment and opportunities for all individuals, free from biases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fairness">
      <data key="d0">Fairness</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fairness is the principle that AI systems should operate impartially and equitably, ensuring just outcomes for all users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social and Environmental Well-Being">
      <data key="d0">Social and Environmental Well-Being</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Social and environmental well-being focuses on ensuring that AI development supports societal good and sustainability, reflecting on its impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="academia">
      <data key="d0">academia</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Academia encompasses educational institutions and organizations focused on research and teaching across various disciplines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="civil society">
      <data key="d0">civil society</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil society refers to organizations and institutions that represent the interests and will of citizens, often including non-governmental organizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="standardisation organisations">
      <data key="d0">standardisation organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Standardisation organizations are entities that develop and publish standards across different sectors to ensure quality and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethical Principles">
      <data key="d0">Ethical Principles</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethical principles refer to the guidelines and standards developed to govern conduct and decision-making in various fields, including academia and civil society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voluntary Best Practices">
      <data key="d0">Voluntary Best Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Voluntary best practices are informal guidelines that organizations can choose to adopt to improve performance and ensure ethical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standards">
      <data key="d0">Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Standards are established norms or requirements that entities follow to ensure quality, safety, and efficiency in various processes and products.&lt;SEP&gt;Standards refer to established guidelines and specifications that organizations must follow to ensure compliance and ensure quality, particularly in the context of AI models and their development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Development">
      <data key="d0">Development</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Development refers to the process of creating and refining ethical principles and best practices in standardization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standardisation">
      <data key="d0">Standardisation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Standardisation is the process of establishing common standards to ensure consistency and quality across different fields and industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425994</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI Systems are advanced artificial intelligence technologies that are regulated under European Union law due to their potential to significantly impact fundamental rights, health, and safety. These systems are classified as high-risk because they can adversely affect legal outcomes for individuals, necessitating robust compliance and oversight mechanisms prior to their deployment. 

These AI applications are particularly relevant in critical sectors such as law enforcement, immigration, border control, financial services, and education, where they pose considerable risks to individuals and society at large. To ensure safety and compliance, High-Risk AI Systems must undergo extensive evaluations and conformity assessments, adhering to strict regulatory frameworks that mandate safety and ethical standards, especially in sensitive applications such as biometric identification.

High-Risk AI Systems are required to be trained and tested within specific geographical, behavioral, contextual, or functional parameters. Rigorous conformity assessment procedures verify compliance with established guidelines, while enhanced market surveillance mechanisms are implemented across EU Member States to ensure public safety. With a focus on careful data management and governance practices, these systems must display a CE marking to indicate market conformity.

Overall, High-Risk AI Systems constitute a critical category of artificial intelligence that requires diligent management and oversight to mitigate substantial risks associated with their deployment. Ensuring robust standards for accuracy, effectiveness, and cybersecurity throughout their lifecycle is essential to safeguarding individual rights and freedoms, and human oversight is vital to further mitigate potential risks.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Risk AI Systems refer to AI technologies that pose significant risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights, necessitating stringent assessments for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de89422ce8e678b380eeca18a71bfb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7e9eb6e4da61705e152386e4c7c8412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3917f629d239e59c1197ea2404615c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9acb869e8831be994323dab5f07993e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86466adf4635fac6d6e5e3aa66afb723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bca7fe15bcbe076f97f98b2f3479775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2252cbe714fc3b6aee570acd5f270ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f557a252b7f04ee224d608a6628bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c78946b57af53cc3de27b286cf36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcf2e7f28d217ab321153caf980fbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1853942fcfd185abaf07003a8b70ff38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ccfe5fb33f83ead7b5c0eb2f0576d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3477a6053ebda4f7122ba6adc497a9ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3167c49292549db4146e77b8eba160c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078bfdf1b899d975b7606b4acd63166d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fb722dbde5159480cfd0e4534fc632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b8c1b5bed6b60b1da1d9246d31aca8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d9