lligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/64/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/124/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/61/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are entities governed by public law or private organizations that play a crucial role in the implementation and management of high-risk AI systems. They are responsible for ensuring that these systems operate in accordance with established regulatory guidelines and standards. This includes conducting impact assessments and adhering to specific obligations set forth under relevant regulations. Deployers can be individuals or organizations that utilize high-risk AI systems and are tasked with monitoring their functioning, ensuring compliance, reporting any issues, and collaborating in investigations when necessary. Their responsibilities underscore the importance of accountability and oversight in the deployment of advanced AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are entities that implement AI systems in practical applications, responsible for ensuring the proper operation and disclosure of those systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers refer to organizations or entities responsible for managing and implementing AI systems, ensuring compliance with relevant laws and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are the entities or individuals responsible for implementing and utilizing high-risk AI systems, and they must understand their functionality and limitations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1630fe82dedd2af2d49f1b480b55eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712fbb27f2ad82df6098ef5c90507342&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428081</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A fundamental rights impact assessment is a process that evaluates the potential effects of a law enforcement action on individual rights and freedoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment is a process conducted to identify and mitigate risks to individual rights posed by high-risk AI systems before their deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment is an evaluation process to identify and mitigate potential impacts on human rights resulting from the use of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment is a process that evaluates the potential impact of high-risk AI systems on individual rights and freedoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e142ac7019ab93d80ef49579e8d0866e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Impact Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Impact Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection Impact Assessment is a process mandated for organizations to evaluate the impact of high-risk AI systems on personal data protection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Data Protection Impact Assessment is a legal requirement under Article 35 to evaluate the implications of data processing on individual rights, which may overlap with the fundamental rights impact assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6(2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 6(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 6(2) refers to a specific legal provision governing the deployment of high-risk AI systems and their assessment procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex III">
      <data key="d0">Annex III</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex III is a critical component of the regulatory framework governing artificial intelligence (AI) systems within the European Union (EU). It contains a comprehensive list of AI systems categorized according to their risk levels, specifically focusing on those identified as high-risk. This distinction is made due to their potential to negatively impact health, safety, or fundamental rights.

As part of its regulatory oversight, Annex III delineates the necessary compliance requirements pertinent to high-risk AI systems. These systems must undergo additional regulatory scrutiny and conformity assessments, and they are subject to strict reporting obligations to ensure that their deployment is closely monitored. The annex emphasizes the necessity for these systems to be registered in the EU Database prior to deployment, highlighting the importance of accountability in their operation.

Furthermore, Annex III provides explicit criteria for identifying high-risk AI systems and lays out a detailed framework for the evaluation processes that their deployers must follow. This framework includes specific guidelines for their operation and monitoring, ensuring that all high-risk AI technologies are governed effectively, compliant with regulations, and aligned with safety standards. Overall, Annex III serves as a foundational guideline for managing high-risk AI technologies, detailing the conditions, definitions, and procedures essential for their compliance and safety within the AI regulatory landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex III outlines various categories of high-risk AI systems and the testing requirements necessary for their deployment, including measures for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex III refers to a section of regulatory documents that lists the high-risk AI systems subject to specific testing regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex III specifies criteria for AI systems under its jurisdiction, with a maximum certificate validity of four years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7195e1644a22885c55968d2c801e0064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bca7fe15bcbe076f97f98b2f3479775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe20aa0cce0b31f6a43c755317350d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65d9e388dd47f8c8604a909fc7bfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad430846dc3448ba37c9f18d213e761</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/86/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/44/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428597</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Persons">
      <data key="d0">Natural Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural Persons are individual human beings recognized as legal entities with specific rights and obligations under the law. They hold a crucial position in the context of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly as these technologies increasingly integrate into public spaces where fundamental rights and freedoms are at stake. The European Union has established regulations aimed at safeguarding the rights of Natural Persons, ensuring that their interests are prioritized and protected.

This category includes a diverse range of individuals, particularly vulnerable groups who may be adversely impacted by AI technologies. Natural Persons can be subjects of profiling or investigations conducted by law enforcement utilizing AI systems, which involve the assessment and classification of their characteristics and social behaviors. Such practices raise significant concerns regarding privacy, discrimination, and the potential misuse of sensitive information for identification purposes. Therefore, interactions between Natural Persons and AI systems necessitate essential transparency obligations to ensure individuals understand how their data is utilized. This underscores the importance of obtaining informed consent, especially when individuals participate in the testing of high-risk AI systems.

Advanced technologies, such as Emotion Recognition Systems, can identify or infer emotions of Natural Persons based on biometric data, raising additional ethical considerations. It is imperative to uphold the fundamental rights of Natural Persons and ensure that data protection regulations are strictly observed to safeguard their privacy and prevent discrimination.

Moreover, Natural Persons include individuals who oversee the functioning of high-risk AI systems, ensuring these systems perform as intended and addressing issues that may arise. These individuals must possess the competence, training, and authority necessary for verifying identifications made by AI systems. The regulations mandate that Natural Persons be assessed based on their actual behavior rather than profiling based on traits or characteristics.

The health, safety, and fundamental rights of Natural Persons are taken into consideration during risk assessments of AI systems. They may require assistance from public authorities, and their access to services can be influenced by AI systems. Natural Persons can also be affected by decisions made by AI systems regarding creditworthiness, health, and emergency services, highlighting the need for diligent protection of their rights and interests in light of advancing AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58ec10f8fea631de27f7f3ef17b5594a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0d79706d66f4b2474faeded28100a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a11bcb90e7333ffe457649980a31a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62fe981c6c449c0068294efc1c020de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35f73469c0e0803dabff693c3a8808fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06455acfb04ed0ea0e1fcd7b8fa89595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac3e101757a5789343d428cd14e4874e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b27dc39e557245814845f393e9bb76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc4d8b4e0e145ee1cf76386d881919f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c64c31df8d81ee8c4452fc69542d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8871d96b04df0305284cbd20bfc2bf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bca7fe15bcbe076f97f98b2f3479775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afaea4dcd95d49cc4d21cf9078216b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c3bb945919e1b0c6e146fabaaeff87b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b580305cd4ba71a7cf07559aa87a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4425b51346d70d56a2933633cfeb0018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3200d57c186d7db38b0cfb2e5cddca1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/42/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Private Entities">
      <data key="d0">Private Entities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Private entities are non-governmental organizations that provide public services and also have responsibilities related to the deployment of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Private entities are organizations that, while providing public services, are not governed by public law. They may operate in sectors such as banking and insurance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Law Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Public Law Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Public law bodies are government entities that must comply with assessments and regulations surrounding the use of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Oversight Measures">
      <data key="d0">Human Oversight Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Oversight Measures include protocols and procedures established to ensure that AI systems operate in a manner that aligns with ethical standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight measures refer to actions and strategies in place to ensure humans can intervene in the functioning of high-risk AI systems to prevent harm.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight measures are protocols put in place to ensure that the outputs of high-risk AI systems are interpreted correctly by users.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight measures are protocols put in place to allow individuals to monitor and control high-risk AI systems during their operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk of Harm">
      <data key="d0">Risk of Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk of harm describes potential adverse impacts identified during an assessment of the deployment of high-risk AI systems on individuals or groups.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Governance Measures">
      <data key="d0">Internal Governance Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal governance measures are policies and structures put in place by deployers to manage and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaint Mechanisms">
      <data key="d0">Complaint Mechanisms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Complaint Mechanisms are established processes through which stakeholders can raise concerns or report issues related to the AI system's operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Complaint mechanisms are processes established to address grievances related to the deployment and impact of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Office">
      <data key="d0">AI Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Office is a pivotal regulatory body within the European Union, established to enhance expertise and oversight regarding artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly those deemed to pose systemic risks. Operating under the European Commission, the AI Office holds market surveillance authority, actively monitoring AI systems to ensure compliance with established governance standards and regulations.

This authoritative entity is responsible for implementing actions related to AI regulations, including providing resources and support for small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and start-ups. It oversees practices concerning AI systems, emphasizing transparency obligations, especially for AI-generated content. The AI Office engages in structured dialogues with AI model providers to assess compliance, identify potential risks, and coordinate investigations into high-risk AI systems.

In addition to its regulatory functions, the AI Office plays a crucial role in fostering collaboration among various stakeholders and promoting codes of practice for general-purpose AI models. This encompasses tasks such as assessing and approving codes of practice and harmonized standards, as well as promoting the voluntary application of relevant codes of conduct. The organization supports national competent authorities by managing AI regulatory sandboxes and developing essential compliance templates and tools that align with data protection regulations.

The AI Office is also tasked with overseeing conformity assessment fees and regulations, maintaining information platforms, and conducting communication campaigns to ensure public awareness and stakeholder participation. Furthermore, it prioritizes the detection and labeling of artificially generated or manipulated content, guaranteeing transparency regarding the data used for training AI models.

Formalized by a Commission Decision aimed at strengthening the regulatory framework for AI, the AI Office is dedicated to upholding compliance, promoting best practices, and enhancing the governance of AI within the European Union while simultaneously investing in scientific research and advancing expertise in AI regulation at the Union level.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is a regulatory body responsible for overseeing the use of general-purpose AI models and ensuring compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-408ee65c3eab1e86c1c4207deaf4f216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094ac0cdb13f3aae73279288ea0dd3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fe126564dfd9a342c90d435dae0173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831c946b1acae90a683cbc5ac489ffaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a409c89b3b9a2d182dbd568b48e2e16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0ab303aa0764433ae306cd3e410cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da283c72662f2af740c6edac711fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff5e73e3b7c1de9ffa48661e94e87a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02c1809d1e7a16e9c8b3d0effff3a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e116bc92c8c7cf688c26ea188fd0b2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8363b7ff75e2a59a44c744564b484596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b4f722f831bc4c8c4594e971e7b7654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1b5a22fa12a7caf6d6a82166e9ac79b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbc432dadad605b2e47a18258f70a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7982e6435aa73ec0e21cfbbfe3f5ea87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0873f73c77d97fdb97b3523748b32638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933ead385d4e52b665df0118cb006cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede6b0da3acfca47d4e90d51eb5fc4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4425b51346d70d56a2933633cfeb0018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30361d2283908d9b7babf63ae110a691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee723ad2204a364a1d2dbe158b59a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a644c604bba8cdc33a7125c5db02395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994612dc34fa7cbfaae3dc6fdd1036d3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/117/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/162/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/75/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/116/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/151/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/64/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/88/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Risk Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk Assessment is the process of evaluating potential risks that may be involved in a projected activity or undertaking, identifying the nature and level of risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk Assessment refers to the systematic evaluation mandated for investigating serious incidents concerning high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk assessment involves evaluating the potential risks associated with the deployment of high-risk AI systems, including fundamental rights impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk Assessment is the systematic process of evaluating potential risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6dce971d3a69afaac4e79066740b9aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3477a6053ebda4f7122ba6adc497a9ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/125/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployer">
      <data key="d0">Deployer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Deployer" refers to an entity or individual, including natural persons, legal persons, public authorities, and agencies, that is responsible for the implementation and utilization of high-risk AI systems in operational environments. Deployers have specific regulatory obligations under the AI Value Chain Regulation, which necessitate adherence to applicable standards and guidelines provided by the AI system provider. 

This role is crucial as deployers are accountable for ensuring compliance and must report serious incidents that arise during the operation of high-risk AI systems. They play a vital role in making decisions that can impact individuals, ensuring that actions are based on verified identifications and that there is appropriate human oversight throughout the implementation and management of the AI technology. Essentially, the deployer is tasked with overseeing the operational safety and responsible deployment of AI systems in real-world applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ec10f8fea631de27f7f3ef17b5594a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69800a0e24a3f7afd28e97d0e1079c4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235710f8867a0e47878a2233118ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-858c2a77ba4972f9c4e3f47479bfef07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad430846dc3448ba37c9f18d213e761</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/86/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428066</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Governance">
      <data key="d0">Internal Governance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal Governance refers to the organizational policies and structures established to manage oversight and compliance for AI deployments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58f0e847b8539a8464411c02db611351</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2016/679, commonly referred to as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), is a comprehensive legal framework that governs the processing of personal data within the European Union. Its primary objective is to ensure the protection of data and privacy rights for individuals, establishing fundamental principles and guidelines for the handling of personal information.

The GDPR sets high standards for data protection and privacy, emphasizing the importance of accountability and data security. It provides detailed rules regarding the collection and processing of personal data, including sensitive categories such as biometric data. This regulation delineates key definitions and rights related to personal data, ensuring that individuals' privacy rights are safeguarded.

As a crucial piece of data protection legislation in the EU, Regulation (EU) 2016/679 plays a significant role in shaping the legal landscape surrounding data privacy. It fosters a unified approach among member states to protect individuals' privacy, reinforcing their rights concerning their personal data. The GDPR also addresses specific risks associated with modern technologies, such as AI systems, that may pose threats to individual rights.

In summary, Regulation (EU) 2016/679 is instrumental in guiding contemporary data protection practices, ensuring that the privacy rights of individuals are respected and upheld throughout the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57118cd489d78b33ed75c63f33151aee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e35e35e2f589e83baa732e4cdf12f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a409c89b3b9a2d182dbd568b48e2e16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0d2c55c34335ae38db203f32e428ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcb340351b261f219fcf1a78d4f2f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5ea4945288b78b6ce93568aea26b18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e142ac7019ab93d80ef49579e8d0866e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22dbef3b29da3394b10b69bcc6aa4f59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5414adf1ebf7087a1a00f2e4fb3570b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ccfe5fb33f83ead7b5c0eb2f0576d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b88de119a362d1ff7d1500b9782d0c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65688cdd97448f1f3932957595156d18</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/140/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/680 is a comprehensive legislative framework within the European Union aimed at enhancing the protection of personal data processed for law enforcement purposes. It specifically addresses the processing of personal data by competent authorities involved in the prevention, investigation, detection, or prosecution of criminal offenses, as well as the execution of criminal penalties. The directive establishes essential principles and guidelines designed to ensure that personal data is handled with care, respecting individual rights and complying with fundamental rights.

One of the directive’s key components is its focus on protecting individuals regarding the processing of their personal data by law enforcement authorities. It includes specific regulations on the use of artificial intelligence systems for processing biometric data in law enforcement contexts, establishing necessary compliance measures and safeguards. Additionally, Directive (EU) 2016/680 facilitates the free movement of personal data within the EU while upholding rigorous data protection standards.

Overall, this directive serves to reinforce privacy rights and promotes responsible data handling practices by law enforcement agencies, effectively safeguarding personal data linked to criminal justice activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2016/680 is focused on the protection of personal data processed for law enforcement purposes, providing safeguards for individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2016/680 provides regulations concerning the protection of personal data processed in the course of law enforcement activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2016/680 sets rules for the processing of personal data by competent authorities for law enforcement purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b27dc39e557245814845f393e9bb76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57118cd489d78b33ed75c63f33151aee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e35e35e2f589e83baa732e4cdf12f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b477112713d917a03ba6f595ed62f6c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a409c89b3b9a2d182dbd568b48e2e16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da6e9cf5fd822e42b8f37d6d2798af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9acb869e8831be994323dab5f07993e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0d2c55c34335ae38db203f32e428ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5ea4945288b78b6ce93568aea26b18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc185ecb84a12901d24ae59e4dd5dfe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22dbef3b29da3394b10b69bcc6aa4f59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5414adf1ebf7087a1a00f2e4fb3570b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ebb4e641a55d31b962b56d6017d2734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ccfe5fb33f83ead7b5c0eb2f0576d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65688cdd97448f1f3932957595156d18</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/140/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/38/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428600</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 27 refers to a provision within Directive (EU) 2016/680 that outlines requirements for a fundamental rights impact assessment related to data processing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a409c89b3b9a2d182dbd568b48e2e16</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data protection impact assessment">
      <data key="d0">data protection impact assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A data protection impact assessment is a process designed to evaluate the potential effects of data processing activities on the privacy of individuals, mandated under various data protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a409c89b3b9a2d182dbd568b48e2e16</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights impact assessment">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights impact assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A fundamental rights impact assessment evaluates the implications of using biometric systems on individuals' rights and freedoms, ensuring compliance with legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental rights impact assessment focuses on evaluating how certain activities may impact fundamental rights, including privacy and data protection rights.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental rights impact assessment is a process undertaken to evaluate the implications of using biometric systems on individuals' rights and freedoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4e750c132cad9fbfb3f5174e1949ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a409c89b3b9a2d182dbd568b48e2e16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fbdf24f8b746547b54a3e43daaf33</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/34/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="template for a questionnaire">
      <data key="d0">template for a questionnaire</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A template for a questionnaire is a standardized form designed to gather information and viewpoints from deployers regarding compliance with data protection obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a409c89b3b9a2d182dbd568b48e2e16</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748425998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CE Marking">
      <data key="d0">CE Marking</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">CE Marking is a certification mark indicating that a product meets EU safety, health, and environmental protection standards.&lt;SEP&gt;CE Marking is a certification mark that signifies a product's compliance with safety, health, and environmental protection standards set by the European Union (EU). This certification is applicable to products sold within the European Economic Area and indicates that these products meet the necessary EU safety and environmental requirements. In particular, the CE marking is relevant for artificial intelligence (AI) systems, ensuring that they conform to the pertinent regulations established by the EU. Overall, CE Marking serves as an assurance that products, including AI systems, adhere to the rigorous standards aimed at protecting health, safety, and the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;CE marking is a certification mark that indicates conformity with health, safety, and environmental protection standards for products within the European Economic Area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e442b04ad431e8e1a74bf9fa0f8bc5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4321aa547f7fa9333c105c2b833ed9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-584f5e95ee85fabd563b7893e4be4e42</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/129/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427788</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 765/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 765/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 establishes the requirements for accreditation and market surveillance relating to the marketing of products in the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 provides the framework for the assessment and monitoring of conformity assessment bodies within Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 is a legislative framework established by the European Parliament and Council related to product regulation and market placement procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 sets out the requirements for accreditation in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation outlines requirements for product accreditation within the EU, affecting market oversight and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1219d54497e2a4a6af07e6b10274bc72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-584f5e95ee85fabd563b7893e4be4e42</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notified body">
      <data key="d0">notified body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A notified body is an organization designated by a national authority to assess the conformity of certain products before being placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified body signifies organizations designated to assess conformity for high-risk AI systems, involved in compliance verification.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified bodies are organizations designated to assess the conformity of products before they are placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body is an organization designated to assess conformity to regulatory standards, particularly in high-risk areas like AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-442777921e9a3bd01b79336245710651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-584f5e95ee85fabd563b7893e4be4e42</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems are automated technologies recognized for their potential to pose significant risks to individuals' rights, safety, and freedoms, necessitating rigorous regulatory measures to ensure their ethical and safe deployment. These systems are characterized by their ability to significantly impact various sectors, particularly in law enforcement, border control, migration, and education, where the implications of their misuse can be profound. Given their potential consequences, high-risk AI systems are subjected to thorough impact assessments and stringent compliance mandates aimed at mitigating associated risks. 

Regulatory requirements for these systems include adherence to specific safety standards, which are critical for maintaining transparency and safeguarding the interests of those affected by their use. The classification of high-risk AI systems includes particular applications listed in Annex III of regulatory frameworks, emphasizing their relevance in sensitive areas where rights and safety could be compromised. Therefore, the deployment of high-risk AI systems demands careful scrutiny and oversight to protect individuals and ensure that their use aligns with ethical and legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are those that have significant implications and therefore must demonstrate consistent performance in accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity throughout their lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79b7078e45aa680595b27c1baab1b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-584f5e95ee85fabd563b7893e4be4e42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc185ecb84a12901d24ae59e4dd5dfe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457bf0e90f1920e6839b11cd66b1060b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f557a252b7f04ee224d608a6628bd4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/85/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428538</data>
    </node>
    <node id="conformity assessment procedures">
      <data key="d0">conformity assessment procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity assessment procedures are systematic processes to ensure that products meet specified standards and legal requirements before they can be marketed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-584f5e95ee85fabd563b7893e4be4e42</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="machine-readable code">
      <data key="d0">machine-readable code</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Machine-readable code is a type of code that can be easily interpreted by computers, often used for providing information about products such as CE Marking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-584f5e95ee85fabd563b7893e4be4e42</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law">
      <data key="d0">Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Law is a critical field of knowledge necessary for competent personnel engaged in the operational tasks of notifying authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;The law in question refers to regulations that govern the safety and compliance of high-risk AI systems within the jurisdiction.&lt;SEP&gt;Law represents the system of rules that are created and enforced through social or governmental institutions to regulate behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e4321aa547f7fa9333c105c2b833ed9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Requirements refer to the specific criteria and guidelines that high-risk AI systems must adhere to concerning various aspects like risk management, data quality, and transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;Requirements refer to the specific criteria and guidelines that high-risk AI systems must meet to ensure safety and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Requirements represent the specific criteria that high-risk AI systems must meet to attain compliance and certification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2116d706005368a535fd7d7c2950cc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-492be2be76ac28fb634286d651691400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4321aa547f7fa9333c105c2b833ed9e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427248</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 80">
      <data key="d0">Article 80</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 80 discusses the procedures and regulations for dealing with AI systems classified as non-high-risk in the context of market surveillance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-893f47aa930b4d23e13586827fdcfea9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 6(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 6(3) refers to a specific provision in EU regulations that categorizes AI systems as high-risk based on defined conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-893f47aa930b4d23e13586827fdcfea9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation 2019/1020">
      <data key="d0">Regulation 2019/1020</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation 2019/1020 outlines the regulatory framework for market surveillance of products, including AI systems, within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-893f47aa930b4d23e13586827fdcfea9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fines">
      <data key="d0">Fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fines are penalties that may be imposed on providers of AI systems that fail to comply with regulations or corrective actions mandated by market surveillance authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines refer to financial penalties imposed by the European Commission following legal provisions such as Article 98, intended to ensure compliance with EU laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines refer to monetary penalties imposed for violations of data protection and AI practices, as indicated in the regulatory text.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines refer to monetary penalties imposed for violations of regulations, including those related to data protection and privacy violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17415cb7c434857a3d1c816705105aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1552bf93eb98e5313a0207e768b7d357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8744b41e4885f10e1fd533f0c9de4aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-893f47aa930b4d23e13586827fdcfea9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2019/1020">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2019/1020</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 establishes procedures and rights for the providers of economic operators, specifically in the context of AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 is a comprehensive legislative framework established by the European Parliament and Council to address market surveillance and compliance of products within the European Union (EU). This regulation specifically focuses on high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems and products, setting forth guidelines aimed at ensuring that these systems adhere to EU safety and security standards. By doing so, it protects public health, safety, and fundamental rights.

The regulation delineates specific obligations for both operators and authorities, detailing their roles in compliance monitoring and enforcement of EU product legislation. It emphasizes the need for stringent oversight and accountability in the rapidly evolving landscape of AI technologies. Furthermore, Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 provides a structured framework for market surveillance authorities, outlining their responsibilities and reporting obligations related to compliance.

An important aspect of this regulation is its provision for individuals and entities to lodge complaints concerning market surveillance, which enhances the procedural rights for providers of general-purpose AI models. Additionally, it underscores the necessity of promptly notifying authorities about serious incidents that may arise from the use of high-risk AI systems, thus fostering a robust approach to incident management and compliance evaluation.

In summary, Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 serves as a critical piece of Union harmonization legislation, facilitating a regulatory environment for effective market surveillance and compliance evaluation of products, particularly focusing on high-risk AI systems to ensure they meet the established EU standards for safety and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 provides the framework for market surveillance and compliance regarding AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab65b498e8d012c9f396c7e602afc69f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094ac0cdb13f3aae73279288ea0dd3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25e9684f684f1a6f65a611ff0868319c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4825b8c430847477f9ab6dc8f1b19797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b4f722f831bc4c8c4594e971e7b7654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f123082dcc9e4aa9993ce2a5fd0377de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceb3dc76830ec642fabf4620edacf57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1219d54497e2a4a6af07e6b10274bc72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf62816a29ef191c053775d76e7693ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0873f73c77d97fdb97b3523748b32638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933ead385d4e52b665df0118cb006cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/85/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/75/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/158/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/156/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 99">
      <data key="d0">Article 99</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 99 outlines penalties, particularly administrative fines, for infringements of the AI Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 99 refers to a section of the regulation that outlines the penalties for non-compliance related to AI systems among providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 79">
      <data key="d0">Article 79</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 79 establishes the definition and implications of risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79 pertains to regulations regarding the evaluation of high-risk AI systems and the responsibilities of authorities in this process.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79 sets forth provisions connected to corrective actions for AI systems that are misclassified as non-high-risk by their providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79 is a legal provision within EU regulations focusing on procedures and responsibilities regarding objections raised by market surveillance authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d8a464e00ff30e1ae415351b48c67e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 11">
      <data key="d0">Article 11</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 11 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 delineates the powers of market surveillance authorities in monitoring compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 11 sets forth further procedures and rules that govern the delegation of power to the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 11 of Regulation (EU) 2019/2144 specifically adds provisions related to AI systems as safety components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b3beca6b2129e6e4eb44988d1de112</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU database">
      <data key="d0">EU database</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU database is a regulatory database containing information registered in accordance with EU regulations, aimed at market surveillance.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU database is a regulatory framework for the management and registration of biometric identification systems within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU database is intended to register high-risk AI systems and facilitate transparency and accessibility for the public concerning AI system information.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU database referenced in the regulation is a repository of information used by market surveillance authorities to perform checks on AI systems and their compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d447a0dff9a51bc6e0b8b9c92046aaae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fbdf24f8b746547b54a3e43daaf33</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427966</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Market">
      <data key="d0">Union Market</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Market is the economic area in which AI systems are facilitated for access, particularly emphasizing compliance for SMEs and start-ups.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union Market refers to the collective market across Member States where AI systems are made available and regulated under common regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union Market refers to the collective market of the European Union where AI systems must comply with regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union market refers to the economic area within the European Union where specific regulations apply to the sale and distribution of products, including AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union Market refers to the collective market within the European Union where regulations apply to AI systems and other economic operators.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b0c7969cb66b898e1cf29a29c2c3923&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60a602cb4413f08687b677f68eb970c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d8a464e00ff30e1ae415351b48c67e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/82/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427552</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU">
      <data key="d0">EU</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Union (EU) is a political and economic union of member states primarily located in Europe. It is governed by treaties and regulations that establish various regulatory frameworks to facilitate cooperation and integration among its members. The EU is responsible for enacting directives and regulations that impact a range of areas, including high-risk AI systems. Its main objective is to foster collaboration among its member countries, ensuring that they work towards shared goals while adhering to established laws and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-709fc77dabe05ab003b8d7217d546cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f59bf399061bc73d559d6d3328c3ac41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc185ecb84a12901d24ae59e4dd5dfe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf62816a29ef191c053775d76e7693ca</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428640</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Database">
      <data key="d0">Database</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU database is a repository of information and records related to compliance with EU regulations and laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59bf399061bc73d559d6d3328c3ac41</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/80/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 79">
      <data key="d0">Recital 79</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 79 refers to a specific legal provision that discusses responsibility regarding high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b453ab3d6dba9c33ee17222e5c44491b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426007</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural or Legal Person">
      <data key="d0">Natural or Legal Person</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural or legal person is defined in a legal context, here referring to individuals or organizations responsible for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural or legal persons refer to individuals or entities that have the legal capacity to submit complaints when they believe regulations have been infringed upon.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25e9684f684f1a6f65a611ff0868319c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b453ab3d6dba9c33ee17222e5c44491b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/85/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market">
      <data key="d0">Market</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market refers to the broader economic environment in which high-risk AI systems are introduced and assessed for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Market refers to the system or environment in which AI systems are made available and traded.&lt;SEP&gt;The market refers to the economic space where high-risk AI systems are offered and exchanged, highlighting the commercial aspect of such technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market refers to the economic arena where goods and services, including high-risk AI systems, are offered for sale or utilization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b8c1b5bed6b60b1da1d9246d31aca8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bff2cb7a8bc7b162d1d512fa7d0a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b453ab3d6dba9c33ee17222e5c44491b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/123/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 182/2011">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 182/2011</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 is a legal measure enacted by the European Parliament that outlines the rules and principles for the control by Member States over the Commission's exercise of implementing powers.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 provides the legal framework for the operation and procedures of EU Committees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c638834e00b09677a065c6dc80878fa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f93de63e4907e805d3e56afc25c0472</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/175/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/98/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission Work Programme 2021">
      <data key="d0">Commission Work Programme 2021</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission Work Programme 2021 outlines various initiatives and considerations for implementing AI systems in the employment sector. It highlights the need to ensure fair treatment in employment practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems in Employment">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems in Employment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Systems in Employment refers to artificial intelligence technologies used in various aspects of job recruitment, management, and worker evaluations, which may impact employment dynamics significantly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Workers Management">
      <data key="d0">Workers Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Workers Management encompasses the processes and systems used to oversee employee performance, allocation of tasks, and evaluation of personnel in work settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Employment Access">
      <data key="d0">Self-Employment Access</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-Employment Access pertains to the opportunities and barriers faced by individuals attempting to engage in self-employment through various platforms and technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Work-Related Relationships">
      <data key="d0">Work-Related Relationships</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Work-Related Relationships refer to the contractual and professional associations between employees and employers, including those who provide services through digital platforms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Employment Discrimination">
      <data key="d0">Employment Discrimination</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Employment Discrimination highlights the unequal treatment individuals may face in the job market based on traits such as gender, age, or ethnicity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Privacy Rights">
      <data key="d0">Data Privacy Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Privacy Rights are the entitlements of individuals regarding the handling of their personal data, especially in relation to monitoring and evaluation through AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Historical Patterns of Discrimination">
      <data key="d0">Historical Patterns of Discrimination</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Historical Patterns of Discrimination signify the ingrained biases in employment practices that can affect hiring and retention processes across various demographics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94cf79937618f93bac06bd8f8fb623bf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulatory Sandboxes">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulatory Sandboxes</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Regulatory Sandboxes are controlled environments created to test AI technologies under regulatory oversight, facilitating innovation while ensuring compliance with laws.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulatory Sandboxes are controlled environments designed to facilitate the testing, development, and validation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems while ensuring compliance with relevant laws and regulations. These frameworks are particularly focused on supporting small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and start-ups, allowing them to innovate within a legally regulated context. By providing a space for experimentation and oversight, AI Regulatory Sandboxes aim to foster innovation in AI technologies while maintaining regulatory supervision by national authorities. This established structure helps to mitigate legal risks and encourages responsible AI development, thereby promoting technological advancement within a compliant framework.&lt;SEP&gt;AI regulatory sandboxes are experimental environments that allow for the testing of AI models under regulatory oversight to ensure compliance and safety before full deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;AI regulatory sandboxes are frameworks established by authorities to facilitate the development and testing of AI technologies in a controlled environment.&lt;SEP&gt;AI regulatory sandboxes are controlled environments set up to allow SMEs and start-ups to test innovative AI solutions with regulatory oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bba75fb7db46076875feb4aca1bd671&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8363b7ff75e2a59a44c744564b484596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SMEs">
      <data key="d0">SMEs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) are a crucial segment of businesses within the European Union, playing a significant role in innovation and the development of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Defined by their limited number of employees and revenue that falls below certain predefined thresholds, SMEs encompass a diverse range of businesses, including start-ups, which receive particular attention in regulatory frameworks.

The European Commission recognizes the importance of SMEs in the economic landscape and actively incorporates their needs into its guidelines. To promote innovation and enhance market access, SMEs are encouraged to participate in the development of AI systems. This participation often necessitates specific regulatory support tailored to the unique challenges faced by smaller enterprises. Accordingly, SMEs are targeted for involvement in AI regulatory sandboxes—controlled testing environments that allow them to develop and evaluate their AI solutions while ensuring compliance with relevant regulations. These sandboxes provide SMEs with streamlined compliance procedures, enabling them to successfully navigate the complicated regulatory framework.

Moreover, SMEs are considered in discussions regarding high-risk AI systems, notably in terms of simplifying technical documentation requirements to facilitate compliance. The policies being formulated by the EU also acknowledge the potential impact of penalties and enforcement measures on the economic viability of these enterprises. Consequently, SMEs are fundamental in the establishment and implementation of codes of conduct for AI systems, with an emphasis on addressing their specific needs and challenges.

In summary, SMEs, as a vital component of the EU economy, are poised to thrive in an ever-evolving marketplace, significantly contributing to innovation in artificial intelligence while receiving essential support from regulatory frameworks designed to assist their development and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6741d9dacc504660a09282cfdfdfe32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bff2cb7a8bc7b162d1d512fa7d0a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30361d2283908d9b7babf63ae110a691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8363b7ff75e2a59a44c744564b484596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c21c2e02a12c7ec585b20f1ef155db81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f3abbad4dddf2a8a56efeaa03cc7f28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c0980cd75cdf016ff776144a4a70db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428569</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Digital Innovation Hubs">
      <data key="d0">EU Digital Innovation Hubs</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Digital Innovation Hubs are entities that may be involved in providing support and resources for AI innovation and experimentation in conjunction with regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Innovation">
      <data key="d0">AI Innovation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Innovation refers to the advancements and development of artificial intelligence technologies aimed at improving efficiency and fostering new solutions across various sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Competent Authorities (NCAs) are designated governmental bodies within each Member State of the European Union, tasked with the crucial oversight and regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly those classified as high-risk. Appointed by Member States, these authorities operate independently and impartially to ensure compliance with laws and regulations pertaining to AI technologies.

The primary responsibilities of NCAs encompass handling notifications and actions related to serious incidents involving high-risk AI systems, as required by EU regulations. They monitor adherence to regulatory standards, provide guidance on the implementation of AI systems, and enforce compliance with relevant legislation, particularly in areas such as data protection and security. This oversight includes managing notifications concerning Notified Bodies to ensure objectivity in their activities and the effective implementation of regulations.

Each NCA functions as a specialized agency responsible for managing the compliance and operational aspects of AI systems within its jurisdiction. They oversee the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes designed to promote innovation while ensuring safety and adherence to legal requirements. Additionally, NCAs are responsible for enforcing compliance with regulations and addressing infringements, often imposing administrative fines as necessary.

Furthermore, NCAs are tasked with submitting annual reports on the operation of AI sandboxes and ensuring that all activities align with the regulatory framework. Through these various responsibilities, National Competent Authorities safeguard the public interest and promote responsible AI development that aligns with EU laws and standards, effectively managing and overseeing the implementation of AI regulations and risk assessments within their respective regions.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are bodies within Member States responsible for establishing and overseeing AI regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;National Competent Authorities are the governmental bodies tasked with overseeing and ensuring compliance with regulations related to AI systems in their jurisdictions.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing compliance with EU regulations concerning AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are the regulatory entities tasked with enforcing compliance with AI regulations and guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea411b75c6825aab3a6b8a4983e34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb1781c5c0edcb30e49953ca1852eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1bd36f2082e6f670210d08c02e3d502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc730bebf215fc150b211b590e39bd0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd25b8a323071b471e7df42fd1a91ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe20aa0cce0b31f6a43c755317350d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6741d9dacc504660a09282cfdfdfe32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22dbef3b29da3394b10b69bcc6aa4f59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a6eb47abd8e339b7c043651460a0bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9e7815086e5c37a3beb2705ee18d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b88de119a362d1ff7d1500b9782d0c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/153/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/154/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/138/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/126/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental Rights are basic human rights essential for upholding individual freedoms and dignity in all aspects of life, particularly in the context of artificial intelligence (AI) development and deployment. These rights, recognized by law, protect individuals against infringement by governments, social organizations, and private entities. They encompass vital liberties such as equality, the right to privacy, data protection, freedom of assembly, and protection against discrimination.

In the realm of AI, it is crucial that these Fundamental Rights are incorporated into regulatory frameworks to ensure ethical compliance and safeguard against potential harm that may arise from the use of technology, particularly with high-risk AI systems. Ensuring that AI systems and their providers respect and uphold these rights is imperative for maintaining justice and freedom for all individuals.

The significance of enshrining Fundamental Rights in legislation and their protection under Union Law further underscores the need for vigilance in preventing discrimination and preserving individual well-being. Upholding these rights throughout the deployment and governance of AI technologies is essential to protect individuals from adverse impacts and to promote social protection and dignity in an increasingly technology-driven environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental Rights are basic legal protections granted to individuals that safeguard their dignity and freedom, which may be threatened by AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62fe981c6c449c0068294efc1c020de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043dd859ed68e9fbb76ff618fe32c054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc4d8b4e0e145ee1cf76386d881919f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2db5390248e67c8de7693a5d073f62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df1f3eba6d36bfd15e8ab3333ac4fd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e87c64b9193b8ef1ad64f22e59474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db48dde4f93da16c9531d8351b22c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6741d9dacc504660a09282cfdfdfe32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ef56265dcb6096b96bc5ee3bfe08c2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/176/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/140/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/65/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428477</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Research and Experimentation Labs">
      <data key="d0">Research and Experimentation Labs</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Research and Experimentation Labs facilitate scientific inquiry and testing in AI, contributing to the development of innovative AI solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Research and Experimentation Labs focus on investigating and developing AI technologies, often collaborating with regulatory authorities to ensure compliance and innovation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stakeholder and Civil Society Organisations">
      <data key="d0">Stakeholder and Civil Society Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholder and civil society organisations engage with regulatory processes to represent public interests and ensure accountability in the development of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Assessment Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Assessment Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Compliance Assessment Procedure is a systematic process used to evaluate whether AI systems adhere to established guidelines and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risks">
      <data key="d0">Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risks refer to potential adverse effects or hazards that can impact individuals, organizations, or systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Risks refer to potential hazards or issues identified during the development and testing of AI systems that could impact safety and efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f152e01179f38fbc8a7c14fe196e7aca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426175</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Process">
      <data key="d0">Testing Process</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Testing Process involves evaluating AI systems under specific conditions to ensure they meet regulatory and performance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Testing Process within the AI Regulatory Sandbox involves evaluating AI systems to ensure they meet necessary safety and compliance standards before broader deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment is a critical procedure designed to determine whether a product, particularly high-risk AI systems, complies with the legal and technical standards required by legislation. This comprehensive process is essential for ensuring that such products meet specified requirements before they are allowed to enter the market. Conformity Assessment includes systematic examinations and evaluations that verify compliance with applicable standards and regulatory frameworks, thereby promoting safety and efficacy across various industries.

For high-risk AI systems, adherence to a specific set of regulatory standards is imperative. The assessments involved in this process not only fulfill compliance obligations but also play a vital role in confirming that these systems operate legally and safely. By ensuring that products meet established benchmarks, Conformity Assessment significantly contributes to consumer protection and regulatory integrity, especially in highly regulated sectors such as medical devices under EU regulations. Overall, Conformity Assessment serves as a vital mechanism for guaranteeing that high-risk AI systems comply with necessary legal and technical standards, thus ensuring their reliability and safety in the marketplace.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment refers to the processes and procedures undertaken to evaluate the compliance of a product with specified requirements and standards set forth in regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment is a systematic process to evaluate whether a product meets specified requirements, crucial for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbacc8a39fa85eaf6afc731174af8109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b8c1b5bed6b60b1da1d9246d31aca8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb293bcc156cb87ef4a7db6744a38f0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba752b306c578e6ee0a31563b30db893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a9cac9d5c84dcacd663b50bbd6c7786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-647c11490314deffe2ceff0b84c7700c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3477a6053ebda4f7122ba6adc497a9ee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/128/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/86/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/123/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/125/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mutual Agreement">
      <data key="d0">Mutual Agreement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Mutual Agreement in this context refers to the understanding reached between authorities and participants in an AI regulatory sandbox for testing procedures and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulatory Sandbox">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulatory Sandbox</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI regulatory sandbox is a controlled environment where innovative AI systems can be developed and tested under regulatory oversight before market entry.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Regulatory Sandbox refers to a structured and controlled environment established by Member States to facilitate the testing, development, and validation of innovative artificial intelligence (AI) systems under regulatory supervision. This framework enables providers to assess their AI technologies in real-world conditions, ensuring compliance with relevant regulations, including data protection laws and public interest requirements. Within the sandbox, AI systems are closely monitored to evaluate their real-world implications, promoting safety and adherence to guidelines set forth by regulatory bodies. The environment balances the need for innovation with compliance and oversight, allowing for responsible development and experimentation of AI technologies before they are deployed to the market. Overall, the AI Regulatory Sandbox serves as a crucial mechanism for fostering innovation while ensuring that AI systems operate within the bounds of regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Regulatory Sandbox is a controlled environment that allows providers to test and develop AI systems under regulatory oversight to ensure compliance with data protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e35e35e2f589e83baa732e4cdf12f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6741d9dacc504660a09282cfdfdfe32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79bb1d49d28abcc35adddfe5e79f3fe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bba75fb7db46076875feb4aca1bd671&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06455acfb04ed0ea0e1fcd7b8fa89595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1bd36f2082e6f670210d08c02e3d502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/140/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/138/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Real World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real World Conditions denote the specific context in which testing of high-risk AI systems is supposedly conducted, ensuring regulations are upheld.&lt;SEP&gt;Real World Conditions refer to the practical environments where AI technologies are deployed and evaluated for performance and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Real world conditions refer to the actual environment in which the AI system is evaluated during its testing process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d21ee76ebe03dd794f42225c64861fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79bb1d49d28abcc35adddfe5e79f3fe7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428310</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Official Journal of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Official Journal of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Official Journal of the European Union is a key publication that serves as the official medium for disseminating legal acts, official documents, and regulatory information pertinent to the European Union (EU). It encompasses a range of materials, including EU regulations, directives, and legal texts such as delegated acts and decisions issued by EU institutions. Additionally, the journal includes references to harmonised standards, certified artificial intelligence systems, and other regulatory materials, making it an essential resource for understanding and accessing the legislative framework of the EU. As the formal publication for announcing new EU legislation and acts, the Official Journal plays a crucial role in the governance and regulatory processes within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union is the publication where EU laws, regulations, and other official documents are published for transparency and reference.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union is the publication where references to harmonised standards are officially published, signaling compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union publishes references to harmonised standards and other important EU legal documents.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union is a publication that contains legal acts and official documents of the EU, including regulations and directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd90900e1cf6e0c8072e210c7e853791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-709fc77dabe05ab003b8d7217d546cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214363bac320d3b288355fb10d6c0537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ae5c70e1b98b5f33eb047bb55022e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-898f28f6e8efad67180019da048d2612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92cfda36b862b878836fea8d791f2b81</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428640</data>
    </node>
