    <node id="2 February 2025">
      <data key="d0">2 February 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The date when Chapters I and II of the Regulation shall begin to apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898f28f6e8efad67180019da048d2612</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2025">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">2 August 2025 is the cut-off date for finalizing the codes of practice if they cannot be completed by the initial deadline.&lt;SEP&gt;2 August 2025 is the potential date by which a code of practice should be finalized or assessed for adequacy by the AI Office.&lt;SEP&gt;The date when specific sections of the Regulation shall start to be enforceable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-898f28f6e8efad67180019da048d2612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2027">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2027</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The date when Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations of the Regulation shall apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898f28f6e8efad67180019da048d2612</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="20th Day After Publication">
      <data key="d0">20th Day After Publication</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to the date that marks the entry into force of the Regulation, which occurs 20 days after its publication in the Official Journal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898f28f6e8efad67180019da048d2612</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 101">
      <data key="d0">Article 101</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 101 outlines fines for failure to provide access to the general-purpose AI model as requested during evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;This article is referenced as an exception and will not come into effect on 2 August 2025 like other sections.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 101 specifies penalties for providing incorrect, incomplete, or misleading information to regulatory bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898f28f6e8efad67180019da048d2612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 6(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">This article and corresponding obligations in the Regulation will apply starting from 2 August 2027.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898f28f6e8efad67180019da048d2612</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of High-Risk AI Systems are companies or organizations responsible for developing and deploying AI technologies that present potential risks to users and society.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of High-Risk AI Systems are organizations that develop, manufacture, and supply AI technologies classified as high-risk, operating under stringent regulatory frameworks to ensure safety and compliance. These entities are responsible for maintaining detailed logs of their AI systems to demonstrate adherence to legal standards and must follow rigorous quality management protocols as outlined by relevant Union regulations. Furthermore, they must navigate complex regulatory requirements, particularly when significant changes are made to their AI designs.

By August 2030, these providers are expected to ensure that their high-risk AI technologies, especially those intended for use by public authorities, meet specific compliance standards. Additionally, they are tasked with demonstrating conformity with AI regulatory requirements as requested by competent authorities. Furthermore, the provision of advanced AI technologies may necessitate specific contractual terms to ensure safety and compliance. Overall, Providers of High-Risk AI Systems play a crucial role in ensuring the responsible deployment of their technologies while upholding regulatory commitments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3167c49292549db4146e77b8eba160c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d709837f2bf640b25f168a3359606f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9c861dfef84b47d382d7c3a57b94afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951511d7a62f58da07aebc05f3e4f1c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92136a9226f18376c3de5d9f6b6485ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078bfdf1b899d975b7606b4acd63166d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f0b636a44a9e0af30b88362b202119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/21/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/155/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/64/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428497</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 17">
      <data key="d0">Article 17</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 17 outlines the requirements for a quality management system that high-risk AI providers must implement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426023</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 18">
      <data key="d0">Article 18</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 18 is a specific section within Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 detailing the procedural rights of operators in response to compliance actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 18 refers to the documentation high-risk AI providers are required to keep for compliance purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 18 refers to a specific provision within Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 which outlines procedural rights for economic operators providing general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf62816a29ef191c053775d76e7693ca</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 19">
      <data key="d0">Article 19</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 19 mandates that providers maintain automatically generated logs from their high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 outlines the obligations for market surveillance authorities concerning the notification of serious incidents related to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 43">
      <data key="d0">Article 43</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 43 details the conformity assessment procedures required for high-risk AI systems prior to market placement.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 refers to a specific article in the regulation outlining required conformity assessment procedures for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 specifies the conformity assessment procedures that Notified Bodies must follow for assessing high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 discusses the delegation of act adoption related to the powers and responsibilities of the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 is a provision that outlines the framework for setting fees related to conformity assessments in the context of AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 49(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 49(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 49(1) addresses the registration obligations for providers of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426023</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 2 is a crucial segment of regulatory documentation that delineates specific requirements and guidelines aimed at ensuring compliance for high-risk AI systems, as mandated by regulation. It details the obligations that providers must adhere to in order to demonstrate conformity and outlines the necessary criteria for the evaluation and assessment of these systems. Section 2 serves as a framework to help high-risk AI systems meet applicable norms and standards, thereby facilitating a thorough conformity assessment and compliance process. 

In addition, this section articulates the requirements that high-risk AI systems must fulfill for the EU Declaration of Conformity, emphasizing the responsibilities of both providers and distributors in achieving compliance. Furthermore, it refers to requirements applicable to harmonised standards and obligations, making it an essential component of the legal text related to AI system regulation. Overall, Section 2 is integral in defining the pathways for validating AI systems as compliant within the regulatory framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fbacc8a39fa85eaf6afc731174af8109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a6eb47abd8e339b7c043651460a0bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214363bac320d3b288355fb10d6c0537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ca70346de523ce75c24d3a1979714d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b577700d28d7be8a3a9320e2d5ff1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f0b636a44a9e0af30b88362b202119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/21/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428428</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations of Providers">
      <data key="d0">Obligations of Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations of Providers involve the requirements set forth by regulations that demand transparency and accountability from AI system developers.&lt;SEP&gt;The obligations of providers summarize the responsibilities that companies must uphold when delivering high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Corrective Actions">
      <data key="d0">Corrective Actions</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Corrective Actions are measures that Operators must take to address non-compliance of AI systems as directed by the Market Surveillance Authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Corrective actions refer to steps that providers must take to address any issues or ensure compliance with legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Corrective actions refer to the measures taken by a distributor or relevant authority to address non-compliance of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Corrective Actions refer to the measures that providers of high-risk AI systems must take to address non-compliance with regulations, including withdrawal or recall of the product.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 49">
      <data key="d0">Article 49</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 49 is a key legislative provision within the European Union regulations that governs the registration process for biometric systems and high-risk AI systems in the EU database. It establishes specific obligations for both public authorities and deployers of these systems to ensure oversight and regulation. Article 49 details the required actions for compliance, including the processes and information needed for proper registration of AI systems. This regulation aims to facilitate enhanced governance of high-risk technologies, ensuring that they meet necessary standards before deployment within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ca70346de523ce75c24d3a1979714d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fbdf24f8b746547b54a3e43daaf33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d447a0dff9a51bc6e0b8b9c92046aaae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427966</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 20">
      <data key="d0">Article 20</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 20 mandates corrective actions and the provision of information by relevant parties.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 20 refers to a specific provision within Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 that pertains to the notification of serious incidents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab65b498e8d012c9f396c7e602afc69f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ca70346de523ce75c24d3a1979714d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national competent authority">
      <data key="d0">national competent authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A national competent authority is a regulatory body that has the power to request demonstrations of conformity for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities refer to bodies or authorities responsible for overseeing the use and implementation of AI systems within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The national competent authority is a designated body within a Member State responsible for enforcing regulations related to AI systems and compliance with laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ca70346de523ce75c24d3a1979714d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Council">
      <data key="d0">European Council</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Council consists of the heads of state or government of EU member states and is responsible for setting the EU's overall political direction and priorities.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Council consists of the heads of state or government of EU member states and sets the EU's overall political direction and priorities.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Council is a vital institution of the European Union (EU) that consists of the heads of state or government from EU member states. It is responsible for providing political direction and setting the overall priorities of the EU. As a key decision-making body, the European Council plays a significant role in defining the general political agenda for the union and is actively involved in establishing regulations on various matters, including artificial intelligence (AI). Additionally, the European Council collaborates closely with the European Parliament on legislative matters, ensuring that its defined priorities are effectively translated into actionable policies within the EU framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5878750a2a2a6290f1a946976f92b6e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ebb4e641a55d31b962b56d6017d2734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bfe284b31053ed0488ca88518b58ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32100de89356334a47cd2317dde09df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fb722dbde5159480cfd0e4534fc632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4324ec2284f40e56458ffbe5d2da80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9d6472f6799d71df39a63934dcde4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/8/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/166/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/174/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/172/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428375</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 establishes harmonised rules on artificial intelligence and modifies several earlier regulations and directives.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 is a legal document established by the European Parliament and Council that focuses on harmonized rules regarding artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This regulation outlines safety requirements and addresses components of AI classified as safety-critical. It forms part of a broader legislative framework aimed at regulating AI technologies and includes amendments to several previous regulations and directives concerning AI. Overall, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 seeks to create a cohesive and safe environment for the deployment of artificial intelligence systems across the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 outlines harmonized rules on artificial intelligence, focusing on safety components and technical specifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 lays down harmonized rules on artificial intelligence and amends multiple previous regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 lays down harmonized rules concerning artificial intelligence and includes amendments to various regulations regarding safety and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e684e7a7455e5a2acc2023aa30291f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0325a6544b6b69856a2fcf978648cb23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204417a83231993542d757c6207e53bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bed819423b33e0b2ff5ff94cc09d52e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99768c8a9d9e625e95c97ba673449e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79114aa8214caf01a991b9fd731ca2f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b3beca6b2129e6e4eb44988d1de112</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2020/1828">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2020/1828</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2020/1828 concerns collective actions for the protection of consumers' interests in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2020/1828 relates to consumer protection against unfair commercial practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2020/1828 relates to the European Union's framework for ensuring compliance and accessibility of data use.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2020/1828 deals with mechanisms for consumer protection, which is relevant to product safety under the European legislative framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32100de89356334a47cd2317dde09df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb86d6b70eaa122acc5132e883f67477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/166/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427650</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence Act">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence Act</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Artificial Intelligence Act is a significant piece of EU legislation designed to regulate artificial intelligence technologies and their applications across member states. This legislative framework categorizes various regulations and requirements to ensure that AI systems are safe, compliant, and adhere to ethical standards. Introduced in Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the Act outlines the rules and governance structures associated with the implementation of artificial intelligence within the European Union. It aims to manage and ensure the safety of AI technologies while establishing a comprehensive approach to their use and approval. Overall, the Artificial Intelligence Act represents a crucial effort to create a safe and responsible environment for the advancement and application of artificial intelligence in Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;The Artificial Intelligence Act is an overarching framework set to regulate artificial intelligence technologies, ensuring their safe use while promoting innovation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Artificial Intelligence Act refers to overarching legislative efforts in the EU to regulate artificial intelligence technologies and their safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e684e7a7455e5a2acc2023aa30291f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204417a83231993542d757c6207e53bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bed819423b33e0b2ff5ff94cc09d52e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79114aa8214caf01a991b9fd731ca2f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428583</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EC) No 300/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EC) No 300/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations (EC) No 300/2008 pertain to the security of the European Union's external borders and are a part of the amendments in Regulation (EU) 2024/1689.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations (EC) No 300/2008 relate to the rules for aviation security in Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 167/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 167/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 governs the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles, influencing high-risk AI systems in that sector.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 regulates the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 relates to the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles, possibly influencing AI in agricultural technology.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation pertains to the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 167/2013 is a European Union regulation concerning safety components and artificial intelligence systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79114aa8214caf01a991b9fd731ca2f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428583</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 168/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 168/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 covers the type approval of two- and three-wheeled vehicles and quadricycles.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 governs the approval and market surveillance of two or three-wheel vehicles, impacting the design and safety protocols including AI technologies in this domain.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 pertains to the approval and market surveillance of two- or three-wheel vehicles and quadricycles, addressing high-risk AI applications in these vehicles.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation sets standards for the approval and market surveillance of two- or three-wheel vehicles and quadricycles in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 is an official legislative document in the EU related to Artificial Intelligence systems, outlining rules and requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bed819423b33e0b2ff5ff94cc09d52e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427692</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2018/858">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2018/858</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2018/858 concerns the approval and in-service control of motor vehicles and their trailers, with an emphasis on safety, compliance, and market surveillance. It includes provisions related to Artificial Intelligence functionalities in transportation, reflecting the evolving nature of vehicle technology. This legislative act is crucial for ensuring that motor vehicles and their components adhere to EU standards and regulatory policies. Furthermore, Regulation (EU) 2018/858 focuses on type approval processes, which are essential for maintaining automotive safety and regulation within the European Union. Notably, this regulation is complemented by Regulation (EU) 2019/2144, which amends certain aspects of the approval and market surveillance frameworks. Overall, Regulation (EU) 2018/858 plays a vital role in overseeing the compliance of motor vehicles and trailers, ensuring they meet stringent safety and performance criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204417a83231993542d757c6207e53bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427665</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2018/1139">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2018/1139</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 is a comprehensive legislative framework dedicated to aviation safety within the European Union. The regulation establishes common rules for civil aviation, encompassing the certification of aircraft and aircraft engines, and emphasizes the implementation of safety standards and procedures. A significant aspect of this regulation is its acknowledgment of the role of Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems in aviation, highlighting its amendments regarding AI applications to ensure safety standards are upheld. Additionally, Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 creates a framework for the oversight of aviation safety within the EU by establishing an aviation safety agency, thus reinforcing the commitment to maintaining high safety standards across aircraft and airports.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0325a6544b6b69856a2fcf978648cb23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427667</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2019/2144">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2019/2144</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2019/2144 establishes a comprehensive framework for safety requirements related to motor vehicles within the European Union's road safety strategy. It specifically focuses on the approval process for motor vehicles and their trailers, incorporating provisions that address the integration of smart technologies and artificial intelligence (AI). This regulation not only outlines the type-approval requirements for vehicles but also emphasizes the significance of enhancing safety for both occupants and other road users.

In addition to setting standards for vehicle safety, Regulation (EU) 2019/2144 includes directives that affect the implementation of AI applications aimed at improving automotive safety. The regulation is designed to regulate the adoption of implementing acts concerning AI systems that are characterized as safety components, ensuring that these technologies meet stringent safety criteria. Overall, Regulation (EU) 2019/2144 plays a crucial role in promoting the safe operation of vehicles in the EU, facilitating the innovation of automotive technologies while prioritizing the protection of all road users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b3beca6b2129e6e4eb44988d1de112</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2014/90/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2014/90/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2014/90/EU is a legislative document established by the European Union that outlines comprehensive regulations regarding marine equipment placed on the market. This directive not only pertains to the safety technologies inherent in marine equipment but has also been amended to incorporate considerations for Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems developed for maritime applications. It governs marine equipment standards, which include safety measures and quality assurance, reflecting the directive's role in influencing the development and implementation of technology in maritime contexts. Furthermore, Directive 2014/90/EU repeals a previous directive, reinforcing its importance in ensuring the ongoing evolution of safety and quality standards within the marine equipment sector.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e684e7a7455e5a2acc2023aa30291f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/797">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/797</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/797 is a legislative document of the European Union that focuses on rail interoperability and the associated regulations aimed at managing risks related to artificial intelligence (AI) in the rail sector. The directive establishes comprehensive rules to ensure the interoperability of rail systems within the European Union, which is crucial for facilitating cross-border rail operations and ensuring seamless transport across member states. By addressing both railway safety and interoperability, Directive (EU) 2016/797 plays a pivotal role in enhancing the efficiency and safety of the European rail network.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99768c8a9d9e625e95c97ba673449e27</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427661</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2009/22/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2009/22/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2009/22/EC focuses on consumer protection in the context of collective actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2009/22/EC is a legislative document aimed at protecting the collective interests of consumers, which is set to be repealed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6dfb0ca97a1019ccd3fb3c11e00149f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b19e3b24207a0c4ca2dafab289e7bb</data>
