    <node id="Consumer Protection">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer Protection refers to laws and regulations aimed at safeguarding the interests of consumers against unfair trade practices and ensuring their rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Consumer protection encompasses laws and regulations aimed at safeguarding the rights of consumers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dfb0ca97a1019ccd3fb3c11e00149f4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 5">
      <data key="d0">Article 5</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/797 serves as a critical component of the regulatory framework concerning artificial intelligence (AI) systems within the European Union. It has been amended to incorporate specific provisions related to AI practices, highlighting the importance of compliance and ethical standards. The article delineates prohibitions on certain AI practices that institutions within the Union must strictly adhere to, ensuring that entities engaging with AI technologies do so in a responsible manner. 

Failing to comply with the stipulations set forth in Article 5 could lead to significant repercussions, including the imposition of fines. This section of the regulation thus emphasizes the necessity for regulated entities to understand and follow the outlined prohibitions to avoid violations. Overall, Article 5 stands as a fundamental regulation aimed at safeguarding ethical practices in the deployment of AI systems throughout the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5 outlines prohibitions related to certain AI practices and is referenced concerning penalties for non-compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5 outlines prohibitions related to specific AI practices that are considered non-compliant with EU law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8744b41e4885f10e1fd533f0c9de4aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dfd9a8d23f85f04843c95f20a9172df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99768c8a9d9e625e95c97ba673449e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c0980cd75cdf016ff776144a4a70db</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence Systems">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificial Intelligence Systems encompass technologies and algorithms that generate outputs or content based on data inputs, raising concerns about authenticity.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence systems are technological frameworks that can autonomously process information and perform tasks, categorized under safety components according to EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence Systems refer to computer systems that perform tasks typically requiring human intelligence, categorized based on their risk level as per regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99768c8a9d9e625e95c97ba673449e27</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Council of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Council of the European Union is an institution that represents the executive governments of the member states and works alongside the European Parliament.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union, also known as the Council of Ministers, is a vital institution within the European Union (EU) that serves as the main decision-making body. It represents the governments of the EU member states and plays a significant role in the legislative process, working closely with the European Parliament and the European Commission.

The Council is a forum where national ministers from each EU member state convene to adopt laws and coordinate various policies. This institution is central to shaping legislation, particularly in critical areas such as artificial intelligence and cybersecurity, as exemplified by regulations like Regulation (EU) 2022/2065. The Council's functions include discussing, amending, and adopting directives and other legislative measures essential for the EU's operation.

By engaging in close collaboration with the European Parliament, the Council ensures the enactment of legislation and the implementation of policies across member states, contributing to a cohesive approach to governance within the EU. Overall, the Council of the European Union plays a crucial role in facilitating policy discussions, coordinating legislation, and promoting unity among member states in addressing pressing issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union works alongside the European Parliament to adopt legislation, including regulations on artificial intelligence systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e684e7a7455e5a2acc2023aa30291f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ebb4e641a55d31b962b56d6017d2734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b330c1d8e73efeff5ccfef0a4f9ecd54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204417a83231993542d757c6207e53bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f49bab3ffe15bdb9d4d12f5b8ce62182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afaea4dcd95d49cc4d21cf9078216b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2bf8c519aff48aa30866bbefc0dc688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-557acf7764c3014cc0e27cf73b9a0fb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99768c8a9d9e625e95c97ba673449e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79114aa8214caf01a991b9fd731ca2f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b3beca6b2129e6e4eb44988d1de112</data>
