    <node id="12.7.2024">
      <data key="d0">12.7.2024</data>
      <data key="d1">date</data>
      <data key="d2">12.7.2024 refers to a specific date related to a European regulatory publication. It marks the issuance of legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;12.7.2024 signifies the date associated with the adoption or publication of EU Law Regulation 1689.&lt;SEP&gt;12.7.2024 refers to the date of publication of the regulation in the OJ L.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71fde45d5020bf70e473581364a21516&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b42c0274197e8080b65deb108448800&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32afd2b9878a3241576e8f1d00ae478c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELI">
      <data key="d0">ELI</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ELI (European Legislation Identifier) is an organization responsible for providing unique identifiers for European legislative documents, facilitating their identification and citation.&lt;SEP&gt;ELI, which stands for the European Legislation Identifier, is an organization and initiative within the European Union dedicated to providing unique identifiers for European legislative documents. This system facilitates the identification and citation of legal texts and regulations across the EU. ELI plays a crucial role in offering a unified structure for European legislation and regulatory information. It operates as a digital legal information system that grants access to a wide range of legal documents and regulations. Through the European Legal Information website, ELI ensures comprehensive access to pertinent legal texts and documentation, aiding in the effective organization and retrieval of EU laws and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-709fc77dabe05ab003b8d7217d546cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-989b8f3b82689be8b7b178fea223a1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32afd2b9878a3241576e8f1d00ae478c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71fde45d5020bf70e473581364a21516&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3feec38e6ec4549038a615544ae6733b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b42c0274197e8080b65deb108448800</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj">
      <data key="d0">http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj</data>
      <data key="d1">link</data>
      <data key="d2">The URL leads to the official document for EU Law Regulation 1689, allowing for easy access and retrieval of the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;This link provides access to the specific document detailing regulation 2024/1689 in the EU legal framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71fde45d5020bf70e473581364a21516&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b42c0274197e8080b65deb108448800</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Commission">
      <data key="d0">European Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Commission is responsible for proposing legislation and implementing decisions in the European Union and oversees high-risk AI systems testing.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is responsible for proposing legislation, enforcing EU laws, and managing the EU's policies and budget.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is the executive body of the European Union (EU), playing a crucial role in the governance and administration of the Union. It is responsible for proposing legislation, enforcing EU laws, managing policy implementation, and ensuring compliance with a comprehensive range of EU regulations. The Commission is integral to the day-to-day operations of the EU, overseeing functions that are essential for maintaining the integrity and functionality of its regulatory framework.

Among its diverse responsibilities, the European Commission regulates high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems and implements related acts concerning AI regulatory sandboxes across member states. This initiative is aimed at preventing fragmentation among the member states and ensuring coherence in compliance with EU laws and standards. Additionally, the Commission provides access to expertise for Member States to support the effective implementation of these regulations and other significant matters.

The European Commission is also tasked with updating the EU Declaration of Conformity and promoting specific policies that benefit small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs). Furthermore, it is involved in the establishment of European common data spaces, reinforcing its dedication to fostering a unified regulatory landscape across various sectors in the Union.

In summary, the European Commission plays a pivotal role in upholding EU treaties, proposing and enforcing legislation, and facilitating policy implementation, particularly in areas such as AI regulation and support for SMEs, thereby enhancing the overall governance structure of the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is the executive body of the European Union, responsible for proposing legislation and ensuring compliance with Union law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c69786b5e6add33d2fe8c768a341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7350246beee832b58d5c53fa874095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7195e1644a22885c55968d2c801e0064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9d6472f6799d71df39a63934dcde4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2f4cab7db3f8f9288f3fd79ff9595e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc730bebf215fc150b211b590e39bd0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e87c64b9193b8ef1ad64f22e59474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4324ec2284f40e56458ffbe5d2da80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b4365b37f348c4492d16b0258db2b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f3473e38ccd9ad84662b373166a5c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b23a5bf3ea6e9c99542abdf17cfaa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d56158a4a9411ebe99783effcebca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd90900e1cf6e0c8072e210c7e853791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fbb87b8107271f1fe959942ad2e3666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a6eb47abd8e339b7c043651460a0bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1552bf93eb98e5313a0207e768b7d357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/69/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/8/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/126/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428483</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Interinstitutional Agreement of 13 April 2016">
      <data key="d0">Interinstitutional Agreement of 13 April 2016</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Interinstitutional Agreement of 13 April 2016 established principles for Better Law-Making among EU institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;This agreement aims to improve law-making processes within the European Union, ensuring better participation and transparency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427953</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Framework">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Regulatory Framework refers to the set of rules and guidelines that govern the development and implementation of AI systems within the EU, ensuring safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 290 TFEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 290 TFEU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 290 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union relates to the delegation of powers to the European Commission, allowing it to make regulations regarding the adaptation of existing laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Procedures are systematic processes designed to ensure that high-risk AI systems adhere to established regulatory standards and safety requirements prior to their deployment. These procedures involve protocols that evaluate whether AI systems meet specific regulatory requirements before receiving approval for use. Established methods and processes outlined in regulations are utilized to verify compliance of high-risk AI systems. Additionally, Conformity Assessment Procedures are essential for ensuring that products, including AI models, align with specified safety standards and requirements, thereby facilitating their safe introduction to the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427522</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council">
      <data key="d0">Council</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Council, formally known as the Council of the European Union, serves as a pivotal decision-making body within the European Union. It comprises government ministers from each EU country, representing the executive governments of the member states. The Council is closely involved in the legislative process, working alongside the European Parliament to adopt EU laws and directives. Its responsibilities extend to various regulations, including those concerning artificial intelligence (AI) systems and their assessment. Through collaboration with the European Parliament, the Council plays a significant role in shaping and overseeing the regulatory framework of the EU, including its adoption of directives related to liability and other legislative matters. Overall, the Council functions as a crucial institution that coordinates policies and decision-making among the EU member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council, or the Council of the European Union, represents the governments of EU member states and works alongside the European Parliament in the legislative process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eef924ac2e26af24531952fcd79e9d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd90900e1cf6e0c8072e210c7e853791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f66c7cfe484df668dde369788c6d3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79b7078e45aa680595b27c1baab1b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02c1809d1e7a16e9c8b3d0effff3a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428538</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Delegated Acts">
      <data key="d0">Delegated Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Delegated Acts are provisions that allow the European Commission to amend existing regulations, specifically regarding AI systems and their classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated acts are regulatory acts adopted by the Commission to amend or supplement non-essential elements of legislation, enabling detailed regulations on implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated Acts refer to legislative acts adopted by the Commission based on the powers conferred by the legislator for a defined period.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated acts are legal instruments used by the European Commission to supplement or amend non-essential elements of EU legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d56158a4a9411ebe99783effcebca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b4365b37f348c4492d16b0258db2b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experts">
      <data key="d0">Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Experts are individuals who may be invited to meetings of the advisory forum to provide their knowledge and insights on various issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Experts selected by the Commission for the Scientific Panel possess scientific or technical expertise in AI and are tasked with advising and supporting related activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Experts within the context refer to professionals or specialists who are involved in the preparation and evaluation of delegated acts, providing technical knowledge and input.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ac4d6cae0afd3292516531be7716e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Meetings of Commission Expert Groups">
      <data key="d0">Meetings of Commission Expert Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Meetings of Commission expert groups are gatherings where experts collaborate and provide advice on preparing legislative acts and policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426041</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Members States">
      <data key="d0">Members States</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States are involved in the legislative process that includes the creation and review of delegated acts, ensuring national interests are represented.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426041</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance Authorities are governmental entities tasked with ensuring compliance with regulations and monitoring market practices related to various products, with a particular focus on high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems, within their respective Member States. Acting as national bodies, they play a critical role in enforcing laws and standards that ensure AI systems adhere to applicable regulatory frameworks.

Their responsibilities encompass overseeing compliance with market regulations, especially during the real-world testing of AI systems, and conducting investigations into potential infringements. These authorities possess enforcement powers, which enable them to effectively monitor compliance, initiate investigations, and solicit assistance from higher bodies such as the Commission when necessary. Additionally, they may collaborate with specialized entities, such as the Scientific Panel, to enhance their capabilities in overseeing and enforcing compliance.

Market Surveillance Authorities are essential for regulating and safeguarding market activities associated with AI technologies and other products within the Union market. They ensure that a high standard of compliance is maintained, protecting consumers and stakeholders alike. Their role reflects their importance in monitoring the application of Union law and ensuring adherence among economic operators, while also overseeing the confidentiality and compliance of information related to high-risk AI systems. Overall, Market Surveillance Authorities serve as regulatory bodies that ensure compliance, safety, and integrity in market operations, significantly contributing to the effective management of information concerning AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are governmental bodies responsible for monitoring and enforcing compliance with product regulations and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are tasked with overseeing compliance during testing and ensuring the safe development of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094ac0cdb13f3aae73279288ea0dd3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294b469b584f56e6e7fcf1b55e7e0df7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff5e73e3b7c1de9ffa48661e94e87a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b4f722f831bc4c8c4594e971e7b7654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f123082dcc9e4aa9993ce2a5fd0377de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbc432dadad605b2e47a18258f70a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0873f73c77d97fdb97b3523748b32638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933ead385d4e52b665df0118cb006cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba752b306c578e6ee0a31563b30db893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9e7815086e5c37a3beb2705ee18d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0ab303aa0764433ae306cd3e410cb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/162/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/75/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/156/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/88/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428325</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Level">
      <data key="d0">Union Level</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Level refers to the collective governance level where systemic risks are evaluated and managed across member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Level refers to the overarching level of governance within the European Union regarding the supervision of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Level represents the collective governance structure of EU Member States overseeing the regulation and implementation of AI legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Level">
      <data key="d0">National Level</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">National Level refers to individual countries' governance focusing on the supervision of AI systems within their jurisdictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426044</data>
