    <node id="Regulation for General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Regulation for General-Purpose AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">This Regulation outlines the rules and obligations related to the deployment and market introduction of general-purpose AI models, especially those posing systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2f1f6979dcac05f71b03e16c6362efe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations for Providers">
      <data key="d0">Obligations for Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations for Providers relate to the legal requirements that entities engaging with AI Systems must fulfill to mitigate risks and ensure compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of general-purpose AI models are mandated to comply with specific duties upon market placement, ensuring safety and legal compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations for providers refer to the set of regulations and requirements that organizations must follow in developing general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f1f6979dcac05f71b03e16c6362efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Placement">
      <data key="d0">Market Placement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market placement refers to the process by which general-purpose AI models are introduced to the market through various distribution methods, including libraries and APIs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2f1f6979dcac05f71b03e16c6362efe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Processes">
      <data key="d0">Internal Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal processes refer to the use of AI models within an organization for non-commercial activities that do not affect third parties or product/service delivery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2f1f6979dcac05f71b03e16c6362efe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Risks">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic Risks are defined as risks that have the potential to cause significant and widespread disruption within a system, impacting multiple entities across various sectors. They are particularly relevant in the context of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies, where the misuse or failure of general-purpose AI models can lead to considerable negative consequences. These risks encompass the potential for widespread harm that could arise from AI systems, affecting not only individual components but entire systems and processes, including those in political arenas. As such, the existence of systemic risks necessitates strict adherence to safety regulations during the development and deployment of AI technologies, to mitigate the potential hazards that they may pose to society and the economy as a whole.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Risks are potential hazards associated with general-purpose AI models that codes of practice aim to assess and mitigate at the Union level.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Risks relate to potential adverse effects that can affect a wide range of systems due to the high-impact capabilities of AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risks refer to potential widespread negative effects associated with various factors, particularly in the context of advanced technologies such as AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831c946b1acae90a683cbc5ac489ffaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c51b7bfc502a0e1b7fc0c076f574e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6a477f9413013f3c0b13fcd9449cbb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f1f6979dcac05f71b03e16c6362efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e116bc92c8c7cf688c26ea188fd0b2fe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/116/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI models are standard AI tools, services, or components that do not fall under the high-risk category and can be shared under free and open-source licenses.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are versatile artificial intelligence systems designed to perform a wide range of tasks across various domains. These models are intended for broad applications, making them capable of being integrated into numerous contexts. However, the deployment and usage of general-purpose AI models can pose systemic risks, necessitating comprehensive oversight and regulatory compliance to mitigate such risks effectively. At the Union level, these AI systems require monitoring and enforcement to ensure their development and application align with established safety and ethical standards. Consequently, while general-purpose AI models offer significant potential for innovation and utility, their regulation is crucial to address the challenges they present.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models refer to AI systems designed for a wide range of tasks and applications, as opposed to specialized AI, and are subject to regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c249a013e89cafa4541f334c555079&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7bb3413d9de075f3d726ec4825bbdf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI systems">
      <data key="d0">AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems are sophisticated technological frameworks that encompass a wide range of artificial intelligence applications across various domains, including data analysis, automation, machine learning, and biometric verification. Recognized as high-risk ventures, these systems are subject to rigorous monitoring and certification processes to ensure compliance with regulatory frameworks, particularly concerning applications that impact health, safety, and environmental protection.

These systems utilize methodologies that enable machines to perform tasks typically requiring human intelligence, such as facial recognition and data processing. For example, AI systems used in biometric verification authenticate individuals using their unique biometric data, highlighting their critical role in security and personal identification.

Given their deployment in sensitive areas such as law enforcement, the performance, accuracy, and fairness of AI systems pose significant ethical and operational concerns. The need for transparency and effective risk mitigation strategies is paramount, especially in high-stakes environments where their functionality can have profound implications. Thus, oversight and regulation are essential to ensure that the benefits of AI systems are maximized while minimizing potential risks.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems refer to computer systems that are designed to mimic human cognitive functions such as learning, problem-solving, and decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab6fc5c923f500a88ff985caeb05f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8637916ea42060e68c1064d171c7c635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e666c69f3a12c76222f3212a19f9ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc185ecb84a12901d24ae59e4dd5dfe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2763d61443dcf3aa274192c53e098997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb82b7a542b998e2bf38a47deb40006e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea591e8c170e7b5ae61060a7a9c9e5fb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/174/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/170/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/130/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/15/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI system">
      <data key="d0">AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI system is an advanced technological product that encompasses algorithms and machine learning technologies designed to perform tasks traditionally requiring human intelligence, such as identification through biometric data. These systems are implementations that utilize AI models to execute various functions or provide services to users. AI systems operate with different levels of autonomy, enabling them to infer outputs based on varying inputs, thereby impacting both physical and virtual environments. Given their potential implications, AI systems are subject to specific regulations concerning safety and the identification of non-compliance, and they may be overseen by market surveillance authorities to ensure adherence to legal obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fadd3405f1febb84753df655c577486</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427308</data>
    </node>
    <node id="internal processes">
      <data key="d0">internal processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal processes refer to operations conducted within an organization that do not affect third-party services and thus may not require regulatory compliance under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="rights of natural persons">
      <data key="d0">rights of natural persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Rights of natural persons encompass personal rights and freedoms that must be protected in the context of AI deployment and usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="model">
      <data key="d0">model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A model in the context of AI refers to the mathematical or algorithmic representations used in machine learning to perform tasks or make predictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="research and development">
      <data key="d0">research and development</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Research and development activities focus on the innovation and improvement of AI models, aiming to enhance their capabilities before being placed on the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A General-Purpose AI Model is a type of artificial intelligence designed to perform a wide range of tasks and possesses high capabilities that can pose systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;General-Purpose AI Models are systems designed to perform a wide range of tasks, which may present systemic risks that need regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are versatile artificial intelligence systems that may pose systemic risks and require compliance measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The General-Purpose AI Model is a versatile artificial intelligence framework engineered to manage a broad range of tasks and applications across various fields. Characterized by its adaptability, this AI system can perform a wide array of functions, leveraging techniques such as machine learning and neural networks. These models are not confined to specific tasks, allowing them to be integrated into diverse AI systems and utilized in multiple contexts.

Due to their extensive capabilities and potential for significant impact, General-Purpose AI Models require rigorous evaluations for compliance and must undergo systemic risk assessments. This process is crucial for addressing the inherent risks associated with their deployment. Furthermore, these models are subject to access regulations and must comply with specific regulatory oversight mandated by relevant authorities, such as the Commission. This regulatory framework is essential to ensure the ethical and safe use of General-Purpose AI Models, highlighting the importance of careful classification and risk assessment in their development and application.&lt;SEP&gt;A General-Purpose AI Model refers to an AI system designed for a wide range of tasks, which may have capabilities classified as posing systemic risk based on certain criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933ead385d4e52b665df0118cb006cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c99635d8be9520a61f07475e6f38b608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf62816a29ef191c053775d76e7693ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e116bc92c8c7cf688c26ea188fd0b2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/75/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428352</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Integration">
      <data key="d0">Integration</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Integration refers to the process by which different AI models, such as a general-purpose AI model, are combined into a single system to enhance its capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c99635d8be9520a61f07475e6f38b608</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426062</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 97">
      <data key="d0">Article 97</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 97 is a significant legislative provision within the European Union's regulatory framework that empowers the European Commission to adopt delegated acts concerning artificial intelligence (AI) regulations. This article allows the Commission to make necessary amendments to specific paragraphs and criteria linked to AI assessments, ensuring that the regulations remain responsive to the evolving technological landscape.

Specifically, Article 97 grants the Commission the authority to update regulations and standards related to both general-purpose and high-risk AI systems. It enables the amendment of critical components of the regulatory framework, including Annex IV. By allowing adjustments to thresholds and criteria for evaluating AI models, Article 97 plays a crucial role in maintaining the relevance and effectiveness of AI legislation.

Overall, Article 97 is fundamental in enhancing the European Commission's capacity to implement timely updates to legislation and assessments concerning AI practices, thereby facilitating a framework that addresses the complexities of contemporary AI technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c361588e67b3e6b1c6d9ddf94840a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d56158a4a9411ebe99783effcebca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe20aa0cce0b31f6a43c755317350d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b4365b37f348c4492d16b0258db2b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428355</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent Authorities are designated regulatory bodies within Member States that play a vital role in overseeing the application of regulations, particularly in the context of artificial intelligence (AI), law enforcement, and safety standards. They are responsible for supervising compliance with regulations in the AI regulatory sandbox environment, especially focusing on high-risk AI systems.

Their key functions include the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes where organizations must adhere to relevant AI regulations and standards. Competent Authorities enhance safety and ethical standards in the Union’s AI landscape by maintaining governance and overseeing compliance with market regulations. They are integral in the monitoring and enforcement of compliance measures, ensuring adherence to frameworks that pertain to law enforcement and judicial cooperation.

Competent Authorities are also empowered to authorize and supervise the use of biometric identification systems for law enforcement purposes. They request information from providers of high-risk AI systems to ensure that these entities comply with legal requirements, and they are responsible for receiving reports of serious incidents involving high-risk AI systems. In such cases, they may take follow-up actions, including requesting additional information from distributors to ensure compliance with regulations.

Furthermore, Competent Authorities support access to data necessary for the training, validation, and testing of AI systems, while also overseeing compliance with data protection laws. They provide guidance to data controllers and processors to ensure that legal and ethical standards are upheld. By collaborating with the AI Office, Competent Authorities enforce laws and regulations effectively, maintaining oversight within their respective jurisdictions and thereby fostering a safer and more compliant AI ecosystem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06455acfb04ed0ea0e1fcd7b8fa89595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457bf0e90f1920e6839b11cd66b1060b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e35e35e2f589e83baa732e4cdf12f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b477112713d917a03ba6f595ed62f6c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6884d6c4641c256f66289e2e2b56965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2f4cab7db3f8f9288f3fd79ff9595e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bba75fb7db46076875feb4aca1bd671&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f0b636a44a9e0af30b88362b202119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/140/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/21/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/85/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/38/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428606</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and Safety encompasses the protection of individuals from potential risks associated with the deployment of AI systems in regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and Safety includes the standards set to protect individuals from risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and Safety is a comprehensive category that encompasses various practices, regulations, and considerations aimed at ensuring the protection and well-being of individuals. This includes specific measures and standards designed to safeguard against risks associated with technologies, particularly artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Health and Safety emphasizes the importance of protecting individuals from potential harm and ensuring their physical well-being, as well as safeguarding their fundamental rights in the context of technology usage.

Within the realm of Health and Safety, there are particular focuses on the regulations and practices that address the risks posed by high-risk AI systems. This category also extends to the management of infrastructure, further highlighting the broad scope of individual protection. Overall, Health and Safety involves a commitment to ensuring that emerging technologies do not compromise individual rights or health, establishing a crucial framework for responsible technology usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety refer to the principles and regulations ensuring the well-being and protection of individuals impacted by AI technologies within the framework established by the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety refer to the fundamental rights and protections aimed at preventing harm to individuals while using AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e87c64b9193b8ef1ad64f22e59474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-414a5bbdb827f9d405cd31cc218f4ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec304def59e7573aa1fecc006d51bea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db48dde4f93da16c9531d8351b22c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043dd859ed68e9fbb76ff618fe32c054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/176/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428024</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Processing">
      <data key="d0">Data Processing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Processing involves the collection, storage, and analysis of data, which must comply with legal frameworks when performed by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Data processing involves handling and analyzing data, particularly personal data, which is crucial in assessing risks related to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Data processing refers to the operations performed on data, such as collection, preparation, and analysis, which are critical for AI system functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ef56265dcb6096b96bc5ee3bfe08c2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427776</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Position">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Position</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulnerable Position describes a state where individuals or groups are at risk of being disproportionately affected by AI outcomes due to various factors such as status or economic circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable position refers to scenarios where individuals are more exposed to potential harm or adverse impact due to their social or economic circumstances in relation to AI systems and their deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426070</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Commission">
      <data key="d0">The Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission is an authoritative body that can amend regulatory annexes to adapt to technological advancements in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission refers to a governing body that may create guidelines for contractual terms regarding high-risk AI systems and their third-party providers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission, referring specifically to the European Commission, serves as a governing body with a comprehensive role in the regulation of artificial intelligence systems, particularly focusing on general-purpose and high-risk AI models. This entity possesses the authority to impose fines on providers for regulatory non-compliance, thereby ensuring adherence to established standards. As an executive body, The Commission is empowered to adopt acts that regulate AI systems, which are designed to safeguard rights and safety and to amend regulations pertaining to conformity assessments for high-risk AI systems.

In addition to its regulatory functions, The Commission is engaged in market surveillance to ensure compliance with the regulations and protect confidentiality. This includes evaluating national measures implemented by Member States and communicating decisions regarding their justifications. Moreover, The Commission plays a critical role in authorizing operations related to high-risk AI systems and establishing market regulations, thereby reinforcing its status as an authoritative entity in the oversight of AI practices.

The Commission is also tasked with developing initiatives aimed at lowering technical barriers for AI development and facilitating data exchange among stakeholders. Furthermore, it is responsible for adopting implementing acts related to post-market monitoring plans for AI systems and associated legislation. As an institutional body with exclusive powers, The Commission supervises and enforces obligations related to AI models and has the authority to adopt delegated acts for amending technical documentation linked to compliance assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3167c49292549db4146e77b8eba160c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c78946b57af53cc3de27b286cf36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff5e73e3b7c1de9ffa48661e94e87a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b577700d28d7be8a3a9320e2d5ff1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e56d671277fe8565010a9fee689d53d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/88/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Risk">
      <data key="d0">AI Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Risk encompasses the potential negative impacts, including harm to health, safety, and rights that can arise from the usage of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426070</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System Deployment">
      <data key="d0">AI System Deployment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">AI System Deployment refers to the implementation and use of artificial intelligence systems, which raises considerations about risks to safety and rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b4365b37f348c4492d16b0258db2b4a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426070</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Public Authorities are bodies at the country level responsible for cooperating with the Market Surveillance Authority and ensuring regulation compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;National Public Authorities are government entities responsible for supervising the application of Union law and ensuring compliance with fundamental rights and data protection.&lt;SEP&gt;National public authorities are entities that supervise and enforce compliance with Union law protecting fundamental rights, including non-discrimination in relation to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency Requirements are standards established to ensure that AI systems operate in a clear and accountable manner, preventing violations of rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency requirements refer to the obligations imposed on AI models to disclose information regarding their architecture, data sets, and usage policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7bb7f2671f4090f24b5396183a3f1e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safeguard Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Safeguard Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safeguard Procedure refers to the regulatory steps that ensure effective enforcement against AI systems that pose risks to health and fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426074</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Panel">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Panel</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Scientific Panel consists of independent experts selected for their expertise in AI, tasked with supporting the implementation and enforcement of regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel is a body that provides assessments and recommendations regarding AI models, particularly in identifying those that may pose systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel is composed of independent experts who are responsible for evaluating and providing advice on general-purpose AI models while ensuring compliance with relevant laws and regulations. This panel plays a crucial role in supporting enforcement activities needed for the implementation of these regulations. Additionally, the Scientific Panel is tasked with identifying and alerting the AI Office to systemic risks associated with AI models, delivering qualified warnings regarding potential threats posed by these technologies. Furthermore, when necessary, the Scientific Panel has the authority to request information from AI model providers to fulfill its responsibilities as defined under specific regulatory frameworks. Overall, the Scientific Panel serves as an essential entity focused on both the oversight and regulation of AI advancements, ensuring that they adhere to established legal and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel is a group of experts the AI Office may consult to ensure that codes of practice reflect the state of the art in AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel provides insights and alerts to the Commission regarding the capabilities and risks associated with AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-831c946b1acae90a683cbc5ac489ffaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a644c604bba8cdc33a7125c5db02395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7350246beee832b58d5c53fa874095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1b5a22fa12a7caf6d6a82166e9ac79b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/116/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/151/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/69/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428352</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union AI Testing Support">
      <data key="d0">Union AI Testing Support</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union AI Testing Support assists Member States in testing and implementing AI technologies as outlined in relevant articles of the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d7350246beee832b58d5c53fa874095</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/69/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426079</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enforcement Activities">
      <data key="d0">Enforcement Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Enforcement Activities refer to actions taken to ensure compliance with regulations regarding general-purpose AI models and systems as guided by the Scientific Panel.&lt;SEP&gt;Enforcement activities involve the measures and actions taken by Member States to comply with regulations and ensure effective implementation of policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d7350246beee832b58d5c53fa874095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/69/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426680</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 51">
      <data key="d0">Article 51</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 51 outlines the specific conditions under which a general-purpose AI model may be deemed to meet certain criteria for alerting the AI Office about potential systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 51 specifies the conditions under which a general-purpose AI model is required to notify the Commission regarding systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 51 refers to specific procedural rules that guide the delegation of powers to the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 90">
      <data key="d0">Article 90</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 90 outlines the need for alerting the AI Office of potential systemic risks associated with general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 90 outlines the procedures and criteria under which the Commission may designate a general-purpose AI model as presenting systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 90 provides the basis for alerts issued by the Scientific Panel regarding systemic risks in AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 90 pertains to regulations concerning the alerting of the AI Office regarding systemic risks posed by AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex XIII">
      <data key="d0">Annex XIII</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex XIII outlines criteria for evaluating AI models, serving as a reference for classifications relating to their impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XIII outlines the criteria for determining systemic risks associated with general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XIII provides criteria for evaluating whether a general-purpose AI model presents systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c361588e67b3e6b1c6d9ddf94840a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428352</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 51(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 51(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 51(1) specifies the exact criteria for general-purpose AI models regarding notification requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426083</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 90(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 90(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 90(1) outlines the procedural aspects and authority related to the designation of general-purpose AI models presenting systemic risks within the regulatory framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 90(1) provides authority for the Commission to act on designated models presenting systemic risks, following reports from a scientific panel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c361588e67b3e6b1c6d9ddf94840a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426083</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notification Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Notification Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Notification requirements stipulate the actions that providers must take when their AI models meet specified conditions for systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426083</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI model">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI model is an artificial intelligence system characterized by its ability to perform a wide range of tasks and applications with significant generality. These models are supported by large datasets and typically utilize self-supervised training methods to enhance their adaptability. As they are designed for diverse functionalities, they are subject to evaluation for systemic risks associated with their deployment, necessitating oversight to ensure safety and compliance, particularly at a regulatory level. Overall, general-purpose AI models are intended to be versatile and effective across various domains while being mindful of the potential risks involved in their use.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI model refers to a type of artificial intelligence that is designed to perform a wide range of tasks, and it is being evaluated for systemic risks by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c361588e67b3e6b1c6d9ddf94840a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8c2328a0858ecaf11e83a00191d499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="systemic risk">
      <data key="d0">systemic risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic risk is a potential threat that arises from the capabilities of general-purpose AI models, which can affect public safety and rights across the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to the potential for a crisis in one part of a system to cause failures in other parts, particularly in financial systems or industries.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to the potential for a general-purpose AI model to have widespread negative effects on systems or society due to its operation or misuse.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk relates to the potential widespread negative impact of high-impact AI capabilities on public health, safety, rights, and societal stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to the potential for a general-purpose AI model to cause widespread harm or negative consequences and is the key focus of the Commission's evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c361588e67b3e6b1c6d9ddf94840a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8c2328a0858ecaf11e83a00191d499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c249a013e89cafa4541f334c555079&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428194</data>
    </node>
    <node id="scientific panel">
      <data key="d0">scientific panel</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The scientific panel is a designated group that assesses AI models and can alert the Commission about potential systemic risks associated with general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The scientific panel supports the governance systems for AI and may provide alerts or investigations concerning AI models that may pose risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c361588e67b3e6b1c6d9ddf94840a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426098</data>
    </node>
    <node id="confidential business information">
      <data key="d0">confidential business information</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidential business information encompasses sensitive data that companies wish to keep private, including trade secrets, proprietary formulas, and client lists.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential business information refers to sensitive data and trade secrets that businesses must protect to maintain competitive advantage and comply with legal and regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential business information includes private data and insights that companies might need to keep secure to maintain competitive advantages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c249a013e89cafa4541f334c555079&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="trade secrets">
      <data key="d0">trade secrets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade secrets are practices, designs, formulas, processes, or any information that provides a business advantage over competitors who do not know or use it.&lt;SEP&gt;Trade secrets refer to practices, designs, formulas, processes, or information that provide a business advantage over competitors who do not know or use it, protected under law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c249a013e89cafa4541f334c555079&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national law">
      <data key="d0">national law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National law refers to the comprehensive legal framework established by individual countries that governs various aspects of life within their territories, including the rights and freedoms affected by artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It includes regulations pertaining to intellectual property, business practices, the handling of personal data, and the operations of AI systems, often in alignment with or in response to Union regulations. National law encompasses the legal statutes and regulations that specifically address areas such as confidential business information, trade secrets, and other vital matters that influence the relationship between citizens and their governing bodies. Additionally, national law represents the unique legal systems enacted by each country, which may occasionally overlap with Union law, reflecting a complex interplay between local and international legal standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5345c3cccd7883e192f55328579d86d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2763d61443dcf3aa274192c53e098997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c249a013e89cafa4541f334c555079&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7ec602a72f4c2f19a5693b37872b32</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/170/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427848</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement encompasses a comprehensive system of agencies and personnel dedicated to upholding laws, maintaining public order, and preventing, detecting, and investigating criminal activities. This includes a range of government agencies and authorities that are tasked with enforcing laws and ensuring safety within society. Law Enforcement plays a crucial role in crime prevention and investigation, employing various technologies to enhance their capabilities.

Among the technological advancements in Law Enforcement, artificial intelligence (AI) is increasingly being integrated into operations for criminal investigations and public security. While AI offers significant benefits in terms of efficiency and effectiveness, its use is subject to specific regulations designed to ensure ethical practices and protect citizens' rights. This vigilance is essential as Law Enforcement agencies adapt to rapid technological changes while balancing their responsibilities to uphold public safety and order.

Additionally, biometric identification systems and high-risk AI technologies are also being employed in various capacities within Law Enforcement. Overall, the collective aim of Law Enforcement is to create a safer society by ensuring compliance with laws and effectively addressing criminal activity through innovative approaches and practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b477112713d917a03ba6f595ed62f6c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcb340351b261f219fcf1a78d4f2f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62fe981c6c449c0068294efc1c020de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6884d6c4641c256f66289e2e2b56965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89272eea67d32d6ca0a58d004c2f75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5ea4945288b78b6ce93568aea26b18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c161e929fac0056f1c945505892ad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e142ac7019ab93d80ef49579e8d0866e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c3bb945919e1b0c6e146fabaaeff87b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/38/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428611</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Publicly Accessible Spaces">
      <data key="d0">Publicly Accessible Spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly Accessible Spaces refer to areas where individuals can gather and where surveillance and identification systems may be applied for law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly Accessible Spaces refer to locations where individuals have the freedom to enter, serving as the sites where biometric identification systems may be deployed for law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are areas that can be accessed by the general public, excluding certain restricted locations like prisons.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are areas where individuals are free to enter and move about, such as streets and parks, which are subject to surveillance technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26fcdeec947c5dfd024232093934843&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b477112713d917a03ba6f595ed62f6c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62fe981c6c449c0068294efc1c020de6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/38/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428606</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Surveillance refers to the monitoring of individuals, often through technology, which can lead to feelings of being watched and impact personal freedoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62fe981c6c449c0068294efc1c020de6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/32/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426096</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discriminatory Effects">
      <data key="d0">Discriminatory Effects</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discriminatory effects arise from biases in AI processing, particularly regarding sensitive characteristics like age, ethnicity, or disabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Discriminatory effects refer to biased outcomes that can arise from technologies, particularly impacting groups based on age, ethnicity, race, sex, or disabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62fe981c6c449c0068294efc1c020de6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="risk">
      <data key="d0">risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk refers to the potential adverse consequences that a general-purpose AI model may pose if not properly monitored and governed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="documentation">
      <data key="d0">documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation pertains to the formal records or data that are required for oversight and compliance evaluations involving AI providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Notified Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Notified Bodies are designated organizations recognized and authorized by national authorities of the European Union member states. Their primary role involves conducting thorough assessments of conformity for specific products, with a particular emphasis on high-risk AI systems, before these products can be introduced to the market. These organizations are critical in verifying compliance with stringent regulatory standards established by EU legislation, ensuring the safeguarding of public safety and interests.

Each Notified Body operates under formal listings that detail their identification numbers and the specific activities they undertake, which promotes transparency and accountability within the conformity assessment process. They are mandated to embody principles of independence, objectivity, and impartiality, which are essential for maintaining professional integrity and competence throughout their evaluations.

Notified Bodies are specifically tasked with ensuring that high-risk AI systems and other related products comply with applicable regulatory requirements, facilitating market access while simultaneously upholding safety standards. Their responsibilities encompass assessing compliance with legal requirements, evaluating Union technical documentation for product certifications, and approving quality management systems. They also assess conformity according to standards established within the regulatory frameworks for AI systems. Overall, Notified Bodies play a vital role in the robust regulatory framework that governs the deployment of advanced technologies in the EU market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0b135294c63adb38cabe2c028de2021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-647c11490314deffe2ceff0b84c7700c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99a919766b7813dbc97c458f95cc9ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4903f69522ce55807b4320731843ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2f4cab7db3f8f9288f3fd79ff9595e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc730bebf215fc150b211b590e39bd0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbacc8a39fa85eaf6afc731174af8109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcfeac23bcf45d7f7b0140796cad07f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc759fa1feac4c57c23af89232f9785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65d9e388dd47f8c8604a909fc7bfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bff2cb7a8bc7b162d1d512fa7d0a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba752b306c578e6ee0a31563b30db893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3477a6053ebda4f7122ba6adc497a9ee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/125/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/126/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428595</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notifying Authority">
      <data key="d0">Notifying Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Notifying Authority refers to a regulatory body designated by a national competent authority, which plays a crucial role in the oversight and compliance regarding high-risk AI systems and conformity assessments. This authority is responsible for designating organizations as Notified Bodies, which are tasked with assessing compliance with relevant regulations. Additionally, the Notifying Authority ensures the objectivity and impartiality of these assessments by overseeing the monitoring and performance of conformity assessment bodies.

Moreover, the Notifying Authority has the responsibility of notifying decisions and facilitating consultations regarding objections to authorizations. It establishes the necessary procedures for the assessment and ongoing monitoring of conformity assessment bodies, thereby ensuring they comply with regulatory requirements. Overall, the Notifying Authority serves as a key entity in promoting adherence to safety and regulatory standards in the realm of high-risk AI systems and their associated assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;The notifying authority is responsible for investigating and making decisions regarding the designation of notified bodies, ensuring they meet certain legal requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The notifying authority is a governmental body responsible for overseeing the operations of notified bodies and ensuring compliance with relevant regulations and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The notifying authority is the entity within a Member State that receives applications for notification from conformity assessment bodies and is responsible for their oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcf2e7f28d217ab321153caf980fbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba752b306c578e6ee0a31563b30db893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-647c11490314deffe2ceff0b84c7700c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88552f4423ec18db9bfb3db0f708349&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031fbe0de70cf6f462d8e21fea6487e6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sectoral Group of Notified Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Sectoral Group of Notified Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Sectoral Group of Notified Bodies is a collaborative forum for the exchange of knowledge and best practices among organizations involved in AI system assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426107</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificially Generated Content">
      <data key="d0">Artificially Generated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificially generated content includes text, audio, video, or image materials that have been created or manipulated using AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificially generated content refers to media or information that is created using artificial intelligence technologies, which may need to be labeled for authenticity and provenance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b6d55e2d7c256240e44f70df0e5d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/135/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427864</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency Obligations are requirements that necessitate the disclosure of information regarding AI interactions to Natural Persons.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency Obligations are the requirements set forth in regulations for entities to disclose certain information about their AI systems to ensure compliance with legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency obligations refer to requirements put in place that mandate clarity and openness regarding practices, particularly concerning the labeling and detection of AI-generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fcb2e4f81b296d92eea24f66dd7abee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c3bb945919e1b0c6e146fabaaeff87b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b6d55e2d7c256240e44f70df0e5d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/135/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/137/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Detection Mechanisms">
      <data key="d0">Detection Mechanisms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Detection mechanisms are systems or processes developed to identify whether content is artificially generated or manipulated, aimed at maintaining authenticity in media.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-032b6d55e2d7c256240e44f70df0e5d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/135/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Value Chain Actors">
      <data key="d0">Value Chain Actors</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Value chain actors include various entities involved in the production, dissemination, and verification of content, playing a role in ensuring the authenticity of information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-032b6d55e2d7c256240e44f70df0e5d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/135/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public">
      <data key="d0">Public</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The public refers to the general population that needs to be informed and educated about distinguishing AI-generated content from authentic media.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-032b6d55e2d7c256240e44f70df0e5d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/135/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems Providers">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Systems Providers are entities engaged in developing, training, validating, and testing AI systems, often under regulatory frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI systems are entities that design, develop, or operate artificial intelligence technologies, which are governed by regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0938655f22b840224fc49f2018dbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/21/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems Deployers">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers of AI systems are organizations or individuals that implement or utilize AI technologies within their operations or services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0938655f22b840224fc49f2018dbf1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/21/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426119</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of AI Systems are entities that develop, implement, and maintain AI technologies, playing a key role in ensuring ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems are organizations that create or distribute AI technologies and must adhere to European regulations for equitable treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems include entities responsible for developing and deploying artificial intelligence technologies that generate content.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems are individuals or entities that develop, train, and provide AI technologies for market deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems include companies and organizations that develop, deploy, and manage AI technologies, and are responsible for their ethical use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0938655f22b840224fc49f2018dbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/21/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Deployers of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers of AI Systems are entities that establish or operate within the Union, using AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers of AI Systems use AI technologies in their operations, and they must also follow the established regulations within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers of AI systems refer to entities or individuals responsible for implementing AI technologies that generate or manipulate text for informing the public on matters of public interest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4425b51346d70d56a2933633cfeb0018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c89fbb177b0adfb819460dd999b9788d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0938655f22b840224fc49f2018dbf1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/21/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427864</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rights and Freedoms of Individuals">
      <data key="d0">Rights and Freedoms of Individuals</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Rights and Freedoms of Individuals refer to the legal protections and liberties that must be upheld for people within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0938655f22b840224fc49f2018dbf1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/21/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426119</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 31">
      <data key="d0">Article 31</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 31 addresses the requirements and obligations of notified bodies for maintaining regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 is a specific legal provision included in regulatory texts, primarily focused on the requirements for compliance and conformity of AI systems as detailed in the related document. This article lays out the requirements that conformity assessment bodies must satisfy to gain recognition from notifying authorities, ensuring that these bodies meet specific standards set forth by European Union regulations. Additionally, Article 31 delineates the legal obligations that subcontractors or subsidiaries must fulfill when they are involved in conformity assessments conducted by notified bodies. Furthermore, the article specifies the responsibilities and requirements that notified bodies themselves must meet in order to maintain their notification status. Additionally, Article 31 addresses the criteria for conformity assessment bodies operating under agreements with third countries, thus broadening its scope within the framework of international cooperation in regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 is a specific provision within the regulation that outlines the requirements for conformity assessment bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 refers to a specific legislative provision outlining requirements for notified bodies to ensure compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0569fee390e7e2b777d0bdf161494796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c53f2e5a51e855855cf3895a52eefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92cfda36b862b878836fea8d791f2b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-647c11490314deffe2ceff0b84c7700c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcfeac23bcf45d7f7b0140796cad07f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc759fa1feac4c57c23af89232f9785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031fbe0de70cf6f462d8e21fea6487e6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/39/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Body">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Conformity Assessment Body is an entity authorized to evaluate and certify that products, processes, or systems meet specified standards required for conformity assessments. This organization plays a vital role in the authorization process by ensuring that products and services comply with relevant regulations and standards. In particular, the Conformity Assessment Body is involved in third-party evaluations, which include activities such as testing, certification, and inspection, especially in the context of AI systems. To operate effectively, a conformity assessment body must undergo a notification process with the Member State authority, which further highlights its role in maintaining compliance and ensuring safety and reliability in various industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92cfda36b862b878836fea8d791f2b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88552f4423ec18db9bfb3db0f708349&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031fbe0de70cf6f462d8e21fea6487e6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Standards">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonised Standards are European standards specifically developed to support the application of EU legislation, ensuring that products meet essential safety, health, and environmental protection requirements. These standards consist of technical specifications that promote interoperability, safety, and reliability of various systems, including artificial intelligence (AI) systems, throughout the European Union. Harmonised Standards also facilitate the uniform application of laws across EU member states and ensure compliance with relevant regulations. By establishing these guidelines, Harmonised Standards contribute to the uniformity in product safety and performance, helping to create a consistent framework for both products and services within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are technical specifications established to ensure that products meet EU legislation requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bafee65696de6d27593351f1c77561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214363bac320d3b288355fb10d6c0537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92cfda36b862b878836fea8d791f2b81</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/122/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/32/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428428</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Requirements Relating to Notified Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Requirements Relating to Notified Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Requirements relating to notified bodies refer to the criteria that assessment bodies must meet to be recognized for compliance with EU standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-92cfda36b862b878836fea8d791f2b81</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/32/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter III, Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Chapter III, Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter III, Section 2 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 details the requirements and standards for artificial intelligence systems regarded as safety components.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter III, Section 2 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 outlines comprehensive requirements related to Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems that are classified as safety components. This section delineates specific safety standards and compliance criteria that high-risk AI systems must adhere to in order to ensure their safety and effectiveness in the market. It emphasizes the necessity for post-market monitoring to continually assess compliance with these established requirements.

Additionally, Chapter III, Section 2 specifies the technical specifications and existing standards applicable to these AI systems, ensuring that they meet stringent safety components criteria. It also includes requirements for the assessment of conformity for high-risk AI systems as mandated by Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, reinforcing the framework of accountability and reliability for AI technologies categorized under this classification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0325a6544b6b69856a2fcf978648cb23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204417a83231993542d757c6207e53bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b3beca6b2129e6e4eb44988d1de112</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation 2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">Regulation 2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation 2024/1689 is a specific legal regulation published by the European Union addressing certain legal matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3feec38e6ec4549038a615544ae6733b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426126</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OJ">
      <data key="d0">OJ</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">OJ refers to the Official Journal of the European Union, which publishes legal documents and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;OJ stands for Official Journal, which is the publication in which the legal texts and regulations of the European Union are formally published.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3feec38e6ec4549038a615544ae6733b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-989b8f3b82689be8b7b178fea223a1b3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428587</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-709fc77dabe05ab003b8d7217d546cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3feec38e6ec4549038a615544ae6733b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71fde45d5020bf70e473581364a21516</data>
      <data key="d2">2024/1689 refers to a specific legislative act identifier associated with European regulations published in the Official Journal of the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;2024/1689 refers to a specific legislative act identifier associated with European regulations published in the Official Journal of the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;ELI provides digitized legal information regarding the regulation with reference number 2024/1689.&lt;SEP&gt;The event of 2024/1689 pertains to a specific regulation made in the year 2024, as published in the OJ L.</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2022/2065">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 establishes rules concerning the use of AI systems as intermediary services within the Union law framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 is a comprehensive European legislative framework designed to establish obligations for AI system providers, ensuring transparency about generated or manipulated content with a particular emphasis on democratic processes. This regulation facilitates accountability and oversight for AI systems, focusing specifically on the detection of artificially generated content. Additionally, it outlines provisions regarding the liability of intermediary service providers within the Single Market for Digital Services, thereby governing their responsibilities and risk management practices in relation to AI systems. As a part of European Union law, Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 underscores the importance of compliance and accountability among those providing intermediary services within the EU context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b917b23f883123c9ae4bf6c69ae5e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f49bab3ffe15bdb9d4d12f5b8ce62182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/11/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/119/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Very Large Online Platforms">
      <data key="d0">Very Large Online Platforms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Very Large Online Platforms are major digital platforms required by the regulation to manage risks associated with AI-generated content.&lt;SEP&gt;Very Large Online Platforms refer to significant digital services that must comply with specific obligations related to AI regulations outlined in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Very Large Online Search Engines">
      <data key="d0">Very Large Online Search Engines</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Very Large Online Search Engines refer to significant search portals that are also obliged to comply with the regulation's mandates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Democratic Processes">
      <data key="d0">Democratic Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Democratic Processes involve systems and practices that enable governance by the electorate, impacted by the accurate dissemination of information.&lt;SEP&gt;Democratic processes involve the functioning of democratic governance, which can be endangered by negative impacts of AI like misinformation and bias.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c51b7bfc502a0e1b7fc0c076f574e26</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civic Discourse">
      <data key="d0">Civic Discourse</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civic Discourse encompasses the conversations and debates within a society that are crucial for democratic engagement and decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electoral Processes">
      <data key="d0">Electoral Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electoral Processes refer to the methods and practices of conducting elections, which can be influenced by the authenticity of the information circulated among the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulation">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Regulation refers to the framework established by European Union legislation that governs various aspects of technology use, including AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Detection and Disclosure">
      <data key="d0">Detection and Disclosure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Detection and Disclosure refer to processes mandated by the regulation that require entities to reveal the nature of AI-generated outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426129</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disinformation">
      <data key="d0">Disinformation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Disinformation involves the spread of false information, which AI technologies can facilitate, thereby threatening democratic values and human rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Disinformation is the intentional spreading of false information to deceive and mislead individuals or communities, often undermining democratic values and human rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Disinformation pertains to information that is intentionally misleading or false, particularly in the context of its impact on societal processes like elections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6012d8db7105015b96b93aa82ad47129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff9241c3a9f5f8fc78557cf5705c8c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c51b7bfc502a0e1b7fc0c076f574e26</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/120/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Court of Justice of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Court of Justice of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Court of Justice is the judicial body of the European Union, ensuring that EU law is interpreted and applied uniformly across Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union has the authority to review and modify fines imposed by the Commission under this regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union is an EU institution that has the authority to review and make rulings on the legality of decisions made by the Commission, including fines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union is the judicial authority responsible for reviewing decisions made by the Commission under the applicable regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union operates in its judicial capacity, independent from market surveillance activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1552bf93eb98e5313a0207e768b7d357</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TFEU">
      <data key="d0">TFEU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">TFEU, or the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union, is one of the primary treaties that forms the constitutional basis for the European Union, outlining the functions, policies, and governance structures of the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The TFEU, or Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union, outlines the operational functions and policies applicable within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union (TFEU) provides legal frameworks and principles governing EU law, including jurisdiction and penalties.&lt;SEP&gt;The Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union (TFEU) outlines the operational framework of the EU, including regulations affecting member states' cooperation in criminal matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4075031022597f5cdfdd7494b828c25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55631cb4906af7cdbc5803cac20d432d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4890e9eeb54e25c3b0d85a99559ee80</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/40/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fines">
      <data key="d0">fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fines are monetary penalties imposed as enforcement measures under the Regulation for failing to meet compliance obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426131</data>
    </node>
    <node id="obligations on providers of general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">obligations on providers of general-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations refer to the requirements and standards that must be met by AI model providers to ensure compliance with the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426131</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Court of Justice">
      <data key="d0">Court of Justice</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Court of Justice is the highest court in the European Union responsible for interpreting EU law and ensuring uniform application across member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426131</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union or National Law">
      <data key="d0">Union or National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union or National Law consists of the legal obligations that govern the deployment and operation of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union or national law provides a framework of obligations and responsibilities that deployers must adhere to when operating high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union or national law pertains to legal frameworks governing data acquisition and use, affecting how AI systems operate.&lt;SEP&gt;Union or National Law encompasses legal frameworks that govern the use and oversight of high-risk AI systems, including the regulations pertaining to verification and oversight requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22fe2322637df933b39b478cbc8c7a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235710f8867a0e47878a2233118ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428068</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competence">
      <data key="d0">Competence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Competence describes the skills and expertise required by natural persons to verify AI system identifications correctly.&lt;SEP&gt;Competence refers to the necessary skills, training, and authority that individuals must possess to effectively implement and monitor AI systems in accordance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ec10f8fea631de27f7f3ef17b5594a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428074</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Categorisation Systems">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Categorisation Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric categorisation systems utilize biometric data, such as facial features or fingerprints, to classify individuals' characteristics or beliefs.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric categorization systems classify individuals based on their biometric data to infer personal attributes such as race, political beliefs, and more.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dcb340351b261f219fcf1a78d4f2f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Data">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric Data encompasses a range of physical and behavioral characteristics utilized for the identification and categorization of individuals. This includes unique identifiers such as fingerprints, facial features, body shape, eye movement, and voice nuances, along with emotional states. It plays a significant role in AI systems that can process this data to identify emotions and intentions effectively. The data derived from both physiological and behavioral traits is critical for establishing individual identity, making biometric data a vital component in various applications, particularly in security and personal identification. As a special category of personal data, biometric data not only aids in confirming individual identity but also assists in evaluating and interpreting unique human characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric Data is unique physical or behavioral characteristics of individuals, such as fingerprints or facial recognition features, used for identification or categorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data includes unique physical characteristics of individuals, such as facial features, fingerprints, and more, used in identification and categorization processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric data refers to unique physical or behavioral characteristics used for identification or authentication of individuals, including aspects such as fingerprints, facial recognition, and emotional recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric Data refers to personal data related to biological characteristics used for identification purposes, such as fingerprints or facial recognition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0d2c55c34335ae38db203f32e428ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b477112713d917a03ba6f595ed62f6c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcb340351b261f219fcf1a78d4f2f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35f73469c0e0803dabff693c3a8808fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e666c69f3a12c76222f3212a19f9ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c64c31df8d81ee8c4452fc69542d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da6e9cf5fd822e42b8f37d6d2798af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c3bb945919e1b0c6e146fabaaeff87b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8871d96b04df0305284cbd20bfc2bf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/15/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/38/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428600</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Political Opinions">
      <data key="d0">Political Opinions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Political opinions are beliefs or views held by individuals regarding governance, political parties, or political ideologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trade Union Membership">
      <data key="d0">Trade Union Membership</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade union membership represents an individual's affiliation with a labor union for collective bargaining and worker representation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Religious Beliefs">
      <data key="d0">Religious Beliefs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Religious beliefs encompass an individual's spiritual beliefs and practices, often linked to organized religions or personal spirituality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Philosophical Beliefs">
      <data key="d0">Philosophical Beliefs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Philosophical beliefs refer to an individual's fundamental understanding and interpretation of life, existence, and knowledge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Race">
      <data key="d0">Race</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Race categorization is the classification of individuals based on physical traits and ancestry, often bearing societal and cultural implications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sex Life">
      <data key="d0">Sex Life</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sex life refers to the aspects of an individual's sexual activities, preferences, and relationships.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sexual Orientation">
      <data key="d0">Sexual Orientation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sexual orientation is an individual's emotional, romantic, or sexual attraction to others, influencing personal relationships.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-764e9e55c5d7310dcd50b2c3e167eca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2019/881">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2019/881</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2019/881 establishes measures for high-risk AI systems, including data governance and cybersecurity compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/881 is a legislative act that establishes responsibilities for cybersecurity and tasks for ENISA.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/881 is a legislative act that pertains to ENISA's assignments and guidelines concerning cybersecurity policies and tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2019/881 outlines the cybersecurity requirements and certification processes for AI systems within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bafee65696de6d27593351f1c77561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b330c1d8e73efeff5ccfef0a4f9ecd54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/122/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427886</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 10(4)">
      <data key="d0">Article 10(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 10(4) is a provision in the regulatory framework that establishes presumption of compliance for high-risk AI systems based on their training and testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426152</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 15">
      <data key="d0">Article 15</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 15 delineates specific cybersecurity requirements that high-risk AI systems must comply with under Regulation (EU) 2019/881.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 15 outlines the accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity metrics for testing high-risk AI systems and their expected performance levels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Europol">
      <data key="d0">Europol</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Europol is the law enforcement agency of the European Union, facilitating cooperation among member states on criminal matters.&lt;SEP&gt;Europol is the law enforcement agency of the European Union, facilitating cooperation between law enforcement agencies across member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Countries">
      <data key="d0">Third Countries</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Third Countries are defined as nations that are not part of the European Union (EU). They are significant in the context of international agreements and cooperation, particularly in areas such as law enforcement and data protection. These countries may engage in collaborations with the EU and its agencies on various matters, including compliance with EU regulations. 

Given their status outside the EU, Third Countries often have different data protection regulations, necessitating the implementation of safeguards for the transfer of data. Additionally, providers of AI systems from these countries are required to ensure compliance with EU regulations and standards when interacting with the EU framework. Overall, Third Countries play a pivotal role in the EU's regulatory landscape, engaging in agreements aimed at ensuring adherence to compliance protocols and facilitating cooperation in diverse sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0569fee390e7e2b777d0bdf161494796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd4e3bfdc01d686ffb1a660c85e1d7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3af424118c8f8024a835a3de370430b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/39/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427533</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Organisations">
      <data key="d0">International Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">International Organisations refer to entities formed by multiple countries to work together on international issues, such as law enforcement and judicial cooperation.&lt;SEP&gt;International organisations are entities working globally to establish guidelines and facilitate convergence regarding AI systems and their regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;International organisations are entities that operate globally to foster cooperation and regulatory standards among countries regarding AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427533</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Cooperation Agreements">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Cooperation Agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement Cooperation Agreements are pacts created between member states and third countries to facilitate collaboration in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk Activity">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk Activity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk Activity refers to operations performed by AI systems that could pose significant risks to individuals, thus requiring stringent regulatory oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legislation">
      <data key="d0">Legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legislation encompasses the laws and regulations that govern the deployment and use of AI systems, particularly in relation to data protection and user safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cooperation Frameworks">
      <data key="d0">Cooperation Frameworks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooperation Frameworks are agreements established between the European Union and other countries or organizations for the purpose of facilitating collaborative efforts in law enforcement and judicial matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Entities">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Entities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement Entities involve organizations and bodies responsible for enforcing laws and maintaining public order, particularly in the context of international cooperation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Agreements">
      <data key="d0">International Agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">International Agreements refer to treaties or contracts made between countries or organizations to govern cooperation on law enforcement and judicial matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Cooperation">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Cooperation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial Cooperation involves collaborative efforts and agreements between countries to lawfully manage criminal matters and uphold justice.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial Cooperation refers to the collaborative processes between member states in the EU regarding legal matters and enforcement of laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55631cb4906af7cdbc5803cac20d432d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/40/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safeguards">
      <data key="d0">Safeguards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safeguards are measures or protocols integrated into AI systems to ensure safety, ethical standards, and risk mitigation during development.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguards are measures or protocols put in place to protect fundamental rights and freedoms during law enforcement and judicial cooperation activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguards represent measures and protocols established to protect the rights and freedoms of individuals when AI systems are utilized in sensitive contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1bd36f2082e6f670210d08c02e3d502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/138/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Frameworks for Cooperation">
      <data key="d0">Frameworks for Cooperation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Frameworks for Cooperation refer to structured arrangements between jurisdictions that outline the terms and procedures for collaboration on law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations are the rules and standards that govern the deployment and operational context of AI systems, ensuring compliance and appropriate usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations encompass laws or rules established to govern how specific processes, like law enforcement and cooperation, should be conducted.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations refer to the set of rules and standards governing the use and deployment of general-purpose AI models, ensuring safety and compliance for all stakeholders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428627</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member States and Third Countries Agreements">
      <data key="d0">Member States and Third Countries Agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Agreements between Member States and Third Countries define the terms and conditions for collaborative law enforcement efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Financial Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Institutions are entities that provide financial services and are regulated under Union financial services law. They must comply with governance and quality management requirements, which include maintaining specific documentation and adhering to internal governance obligations. These regulations particularly emphasize the oversight of high-risk AI systems, mandating that Financial Institutions have robust internal governance structures in place to ensure compliance and manage associated risks. Additionally, these organizations face additional requirements related to the management and oversight of these AI systems, ensuring that their operations align with established standards and regulatory expectations. Overall, Financial Institutions play a crucial role in the financial services sector while navigating stringent regulations aimed at ensuring safe and responsible service delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial Institutions include banks and other entities that provide financial services and are regulated under Union financial services law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Technical Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Documentation encompasses a comprehensive suite of documents provided by the AI system's provider, essential for ensuring compliance with regulatory standards, particularly for high-risk AI systems. This documentation includes detailed records that outline compliance and operational guidelines, ensuring such systems meet the required regulatory requirements set forth by the European Union. It incorporates vital information related to the design, production, and operational procedures, along with formal records necessary for evaluating AI systems concerning both regulatory compliance and performance. 

Moreover, Technical Documentation serves as a critical resource that supports the compliance and functionality of both high-risk and general-purpose AI models. It encapsulates the necessary information required under legal acts, detailing the training, testing processes, evaluation results, and specifications of AI models. Providers must maintain all relevant records for a period of 10 years, demonstrating adherence to specified regulations and providing comprehensive information to users and regulatory authorities about the AI systems' compliance and operational details.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c9bff2cb7a8bc7b162d1d512fa7d0a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2252cbe714fc3b6aee570acd5f270ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428627</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management System Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management System Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation related to the quality management system ensures that high-risk AI systems meet the required standards and processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426171</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Declaration of Conformity">
      <data key="d0">EU Declaration of Conformity</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Declaration of Conformity is a document required for high-risk AI systems demonstrating compliance with relevant EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Declaration of Conformity is a formal legal document that certifies that a product, specifically a high-risk AI system, complies with applicable European Union (EU) regulations and standards. This declaration is a crucial requirement for providers, as it serves as an assertion that their product meets all relevant regulatory requirements prior to being placed on the market. It encompasses the need for the product to align with necessary EU directives and establishes that the manufacturer acknowledges adherence to the required European standards. Overall, the EU Declaration of Conformity is essential for ensuring that high-risk AI systems are compliant with EU regulations before they can be legally distributed within the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Declaration of Conformity is a formal statement by a provider asserting compliance with specified requirements of legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Declaration of Conformity is a document that certifies that a product, including high-risk AI systems, meets all relevant EU regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a6eb47abd8e339b7c043651460a0bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c66d3fba6e6dadb3426f70cb98376c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b577700d28d7be8a3a9320e2d5ff1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d0">General-purpose AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI Models are tools that may present systemic risks and are subject to alerts as indicated by the Scientific Panel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426173</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Risk">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic Risk pertains to the potential for a general-purpose AI model to cause widespread impact or issues, necessitating careful evaluation and regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Risk refers to the potential for a failure of a system or component to cause significant negative consequences across interconnected entities or systems, particularly in the context of AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to potential threats that a general-purpose AI model might pose at a Union level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428352</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 91 to 94">
      <data key="d0">Articles 91 to 94</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 91 to 94 specify the measures and powers that the Commission may exercise upon receiving an alert from the Scientific Panel or the AI Office regarding AI risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426173</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Qualified Alert">
      <data key="d0">Qualified Alert</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Qualified Alert is a formal notification from the Scientific Panel to the AI Office indicating potential risks associated with AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426173</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importers">
      <data key="d0">Importers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Importers are entities responsible for bringing high-risk AI systems to the market and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Importers are entities responsible for ensuring that high-risk AI systems comply with regulations before being placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Importers are entities that bring high-risk AI systems into the market and must be informed of any compliance issues associated with the products they handle.&lt;SEP&gt;Importers are operators involved in bringing AI systems into a market, carrying specific legal obligations under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-66e6524323a5bff7a82ba7868399e18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Conformity Assessment Procedure is a method utilized by organizations to evaluate whether their high-risk AI systems meet specified regulatory requirements and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Conformity Assessment Procedure is a systematic and regulatory framework designed to verify that high-risk AI systems meet essential safety and performance requirements prior to their market entry. This comprehensive process involves evaluating whether these systems comply with established regulations and specified standards related to cybersecurity and safety. The procedure entails thorough assessments conducted by third-party bodies that assess the products against the required regulations to ensure compliance. By adhering to these standards, the Conformity Assessment Procedure aims to protect consumers and ensure the reliability of high-risk AI systems before they are placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The conformity assessment procedure involves steps taken to evaluate and ensure that high-risk AI systems meet necessary regulations and safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fbb87b8107271f1fe959942ad2e3666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13251cb96e29c95cab559ac75d5b1f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3477a6053ebda4f7122ba6adc497a9ee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/125/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorised Representative">
      <data key="d0">Authorised Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An Authorised Representative is an entity appointed by a provider of an AI system to act on their behalf in regulatory matters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Authorised Representative acts on behalf of the Provider for the purposes of registration and compliance with AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;An authorised representative is a natural or legal person located in the Union who acts on behalf of a provider of an AI system, executing obligations established by regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 11 and Annex IV">
      <data key="d0">Article 11 and Annex IV</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 11 and Annex IV outline the requirements for the technical documentation that providers must prepare.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426175</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 79(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 79(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 79(1) addresses risks associated with high-risk AI systems and the obligations of importers to inform relevant parties.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) outlines the obligations of AI deployers when there is a risk associated with their use of AI systems, requiring them to notify relevant authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) outlines legal definitions and obligations related to the assessment of risks posed by high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) outlines regulations regarding risks presented by high-risk AI systems, which necessitate logging capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) is a regulatory provision concerning the identification and management of risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Body">
      <data key="d0">Notified Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Notified Body is an organization designated by EU member states to assess conformity and certify compliance of products before they can be marketed, particularly focusing on high-risk AI systems. These bodies are recognized according to EU regulations and are responsible for evaluating whether products meet essential safety and effectiveness standards. They ensure that products comply with applicable laws and regulations, thereby maintaining safety standards. Notified Bodies play a crucial role in the regulatory framework by assessing and validating compliance, especially for products that pose higher risks, ensuring their safe operation in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified Bodies are designated organizations that assess the compliance of high-risk AI systems and issue relevant certifications according to regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56424a5db573173fc67a6e62dd2d96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c53f2e5a51e855855cf3895a52eefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcf2e7f28d217ab321153caf980fbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Instructions for Use">
      <data key="d0">Instructions for Use</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Instructions for Use are essential documents that accompany high-risk AI systems, detailing the operational guidelines necessary for their effective and responsible utilization. These instructions provide comprehensive guidance to deployers, outlining how to correctly use the AI system and clarifying its intended purpose. They include critical information on proper operation, safety considerations, performance limitations, and the effective use of the AI systems. By ensuring that users understand these aspects, the Instructions for Use play a vital role in the deployment and operation of high-risk AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712fbb27f2ad82df6098ef5c90507342&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adccf24f1ddc4835908b879bcbe8674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428097</data>
    </node>
    <node id="it">
      <data key="d0">it</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Refers to the subject or phenomenon considered for risk mitigation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f152e01179f38fbc8a7c14fe196e7aca</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426175</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mitigation Strategies">
      <data key="d0">Mitigation Strategies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Mitigation Strategies refer to approaches and actions designed to reduce the severity or impact of identified risks, including various planning and response techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation strategies encompass various approaches and actions undertaken to reduce or eliminate risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6dce971d3a69afaac4e79066740b9aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f152e01179f38fbc8a7c14fe196e7aca</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427151</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers">
      <data key="d0">Providers</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43fe7b5e70d3f0ef6fef527c8f0773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9512f56ddf79fc1a7f65b696c84e2eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adccf24f1ddc4835908b879bcbe8674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-492be2be76ac28fb634286d651691400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043dd859ed68e9fbb76ff618fe32c054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2f4cab7db3f8f9288f3fd79ff9595e</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are entities or individuals that play a crucial role in the development, establishment, and supply of AI systems, particularly those classified as high-risk. They are responsible for ensuring compliance with relevant legal obligations, implementing risk-management measures, and providing necessary documentation and user support. Providers specifically focus on developing post-market monitoring systems tailored for high-risk AI technologies, thus helping to mitigate systemic risks associated with these innovations.

In their capacity, Providers must adhere to specific standards and practices that govern the deployment of AI systems. This includes the appointment of an Authorised Representative to aid in fulfilling regulatory obligations and undergoing compliance assessments conducted by Notified Bodies to verify adherence to these established standards.

Overall, Providers are essential entities that not only develop and place high-risk AI systems on the market but also ensure that these systems comply with all relevant regulations, thereby contributing to the safe and responsible use of AI across various domains.</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/64/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric identification">
      <data key="d0">biometric identification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric identification refers to the automated recognition of unique human features for identity verification purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e666c69f3a12c76222f3212a19f9ffe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426178</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Features">
      <data key="d0">Human Features</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human features encompass the physical, physiological, and behavioral traits that can be recognized through biometric identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e666c69f3a12c76222f3212a19f9ffe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426178</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reference Database">
      <data key="d0">Reference Database</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference database is a collection of stored biometric data used for comparing against an individual's biometric data for identification purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e666c69f3a12c76222f3212a19f9ffe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426178</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Identification">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Identification</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e666c69f3a12c76222f3212a19f9ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric identification involves the automated recognition of individuals based on their physiological or behavioral traits, usually facilitated by AI technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric identification is the automated recognition of human features to establish an individual's identity through stored data comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation defines and governs the practices involved in biometric identification and its applications.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Board">
      <data key="d0">The Board</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Board advises and assists the Commission and Member States on the application of regulations regarding AI models and market surveillance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Board is established to facilitate the harmonized implementation of AI Regulation, composed of representatives from Member States, responsible for advisory tasks related to AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulation">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Regulation refers to the comprehensive legal framework and standards established to ensure the ethical and safe use of artificial intelligence systems. This framework governs the implementation and oversight of AI technologies, focusing on critical aspects such as risk evaluation, transparency, and ethical practices. It encompasses rules and procedures for classifying and monitoring AI models, which are crucial for mitigating risks associated with their deployment. AI Regulation also includes guidelines that define how general-purpose AI models should be developed and used by relevant providers, ensuring compliance with established legal and ethical standards. Overall, AI Regulation aims to promote the responsible development and deployment of artificial intelligence systems while safeguarding public interest and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulation refers to the framework established to govern the development and implementation of artificial intelligence technologies in compliance with ethical standards and Union values.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Regulation refers to the legal and institutional frameworks that govern the ethical and technical aspects of artificial intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fe96efa4389bb1d352d2b400876fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2763d61443dcf3aa274192c53e098997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/170/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulation 2019/1020">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulation 2019/1020</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Regulation 2019/1020 is a legal framework that sets out reporting obligations regarding serious incidents related to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;EU Regulation 2019/1020 provides a legal basis for regulatory actions regarding market surveillance and product compliance within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Entities">
      <data key="d0">Public Entities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Entities refer to governmental bodies from which representatives for the Board may be drawn, possessing the necessary competencies for effective coordination.&lt;SEP&gt;Public entities are organizations governed by public law that provide essential services in the public interest, such as education, healthcare, and justice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Eco-System">
      <data key="d0">AI Eco-System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Eco-System includes various stakeholders involved in the development, regulation, and implementation of artificial intelligence technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Advisory Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Advisory Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Advisory Tasks refer to the responsibilities of the Board in issuing opinions, recommendations, and guidance related to AI regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a753b958cb652b7d0935c682d40c6af2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance encompasses activities aimed at ensuring compliance with market regulations and evaluating market practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance involves the process of monitoring compliance of products, including AI systems, according to set regulations by authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-294b469b584f56e6e7fcf1b55e7e0df7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standing Subgroup for Market Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Standing Subgroup for Market Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Standing Subgroup for Market Surveillance is a specialized group under the Commission that focuses on evaluating the market and coordinating actions among authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-294b469b584f56e6e7fcf1b55e7e0df7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426184</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Evaluations or Studies">
      <data key="d0">Market Evaluations or Studies</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Evaluations or Studies are activities undertaken by the Commission to assess and analyze market conditions and compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-294b469b584f56e6e7fcf1b55e7e0df7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/149/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426184</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Technologies">
      <data key="d0">AI Technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Technologies encompasses various technologies related to artificial intelligence, which national competent authorities must understand for effective regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;AI technologies encompass various systems and applications that utilize artificial intelligence for processing data, contributing to advancements in multiple fields.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Technologies refer to the various advanced applications and systems utilizing artificial intelligence to improve efficiency, manage resources, and provide solutions across different sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-652e6414b5fe8ab54e8a9034ece6d222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/4/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426699</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity involves the practices and measures taken to protect systems and data from cyber threats, highlighted as a necessary requirement for AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity is a field focused on protecting computer systems, networks, and data from cyber threats, ensuring resilience against malicious activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity is a field that focuses on protecting systems, networks, and programs from digital attacks, and is a critical area of expertise for competent authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2116d706005368a535fd7d7c2950cc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427248</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection encompasses legal and regulatory frameworks that govern the collection, storage, and sharing of personal data to protect individual privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Protection pertains to the safeguarding of personal data and compliance with legal requirements, which is essential for the tasks of national competent authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="August 2, 2025">
      <data key="d0">August 2, 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">August 2, 2025 is the deadline by which Member States must publicly communicate the identity of their national competent authorities and single points of contact.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Personnel refers to the staff or individuals that are employed by national competent authorities and must possess the necessary competencies and expertise to carry out their duties effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality Obligations are legal requirements that dictate the necessity for national competent authorities to maintain secrecy in certain activities as outlined in the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electronic Communication Means">
      <data key="d0">Electronic Communication Means</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electronic Communication Means refer to the methods utilized for communication, such as email or online platforms, which Member States must use to provide information about their competent authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Data Protection Supervisor">
      <data key="d0">European Data Protection Supervisor</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Supervisor (EDPS) is an independent supervisory authority that plays a vital role in ensuring compliance with data protection laws and regulations within the European Union (EU). It is tasked with overseeing the respect of individuals' data protection rights within EU institutions and bodies, thereby safeguarding personal data and privacy. As a competent market surveillance authority, the EDPS supervises various Union institutions, agencies, and bodies to ensure they adhere to relevant data protection regulations.

The EDPS is also involved in enforcing data protection matters and has the authority to impose administrative fines for non-compliance with established laws. Furthermore, the supervisor is committed to facilitating the establishment of AI regulatory sandboxes across the EU, highlighting its proactive approach to adapting regulatory frameworks in the face of emerging technologies and safeguarding personal data privacy.

Overall, the European Data Protection Supervisor is dedicated to protecting personal data and privacy rights throughout the Union, serving as a key figure in overseeing that all EU institutions and bodies comply with stringent data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor ensures compliance with data protection laws within Union institutions and agencies.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor is responsible for overseeing compliance with data protection regulations within Union institutions and bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor participates as an observer in the Board's meetings, providing oversight on data protection issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6741d9dacc504660a09282cfdfdfe32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f123082dcc9e4aa9993ce2a5fd0377de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bba75fb7db46076875feb4aca1bd671&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8744b41e4885f10e1fd533f0c9de4aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a360e38774a35c72c4384c10d081a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dfd9a8d23f85f04843c95f20a9172df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17415cb7c434857a3d1c816705105aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b14075f9663187b4b9cee91c38f3025d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b4f722f831bc4c8c4594e971e7b7654</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/180/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/168/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/156/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427806</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contact Details">
      <data key="d0">Contact Details</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Contact details refer to information that allows individuals or organizations to establish communication, essential for transparency and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Resources">
      <data key="d0">Technical Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Resources refer to the tools and technologies that national competent authorities need to perform their regulatory responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical resources include the tools, technologies, and knowledge required to implement and regulate AI systems effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Resources">
      <data key="d0">Financial Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Resources refer to the budget and funding available to national competent authorities to execute their tasks effectively under the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial resources refer to the funding necessary for national competent authorities to operate and fulfill their regulatory obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial resources include monetary assets that individuals require to obtain essential services like housing and utilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial resources include money and assets that individuals may need access to for housing, utilities, or services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc4d8b4e0e145ee1cf76386d881919f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3200d57c186d7db38b0cfb2e5cddca1e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Resources">
      <data key="d0">Human Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Resources consist of the personnel and expertise required by national competent authorities to enforce the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Human resources encompass the personnel and expertise needed by national competent authorities to implement regulations and perform monitoring tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">Infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Infrastructure refers to the foundational systems and services that support the operations of national competent authorities, facilitating effective regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure refers to the physical and organizational structures needed for the operation of a society, which includes critical digital systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 4(2) TEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 4(2) TEU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 4(2) TEU addresses the responsibilities of Member States and the Union's common defence policy concerning national security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 2 of Title V TEU">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 2 of Title V TEU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 2 of Title V TEU details aspects of the Union defence policy which is subjected to public international law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems Exclusion">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems Exclusion</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Systems Exclusion refers to the specific regulatory exemption for AI systems used in military, defence, or national security contexts, highlighting their complex legal treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Military Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Military Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Military Purposes encompass the use of technologies and systems, including AI, in the context of armed forces and defence operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Military purposes involve the use of AI systems in defense and national security, which may not be regulated under these specific provisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89272eea67d32d6ca0a58d004c2f75e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Defence Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Defence Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Defence Purposes involve the utilization of systems and technologies to protect a nation's sovereignty and security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Security Purposes">
      <data key="d0">National Security Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National Security Purposes denote activities and systems that ensure the safety and stability of a nation against threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public International Law">
      <data key="d0">Public International Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public International Law refers to legal norms that govern the interactions between sovereign states, impacting the regulation of military and security activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Necessity">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Necessity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Necessity emphasizes the obligation of entities to conform to regulations applicable to AI systems outside exempt purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civilian Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Civilian Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civilian purposes refer to the non-military use of AI systems, which necessitate compliance with certain regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f89272eea67d32d6ca0a58d004c2f75e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Defense">
      <data key="d0">Defense</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Defense encompasses activities and operations designed to protect a nation from external threats, potentially involving AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f89272eea67d32d6ca0a58d004c2f75e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Security">
      <data key="d0">National Security</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National security includes measures taken by a government to ensure the safety of its citizens and the integrity of its state, often utilizing advanced technologies including AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f89272eea67d32d6ca0a58d004c2f75e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Bodies are organizations responsible for assessing compliance with standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment bodies are entities evaluated and monitored by notifying authorities to ensure compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Bodies are organizations that evaluate and confirm the compliance of products or systems with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Bodies are organizations that assess the compliance of products and systems with regulatory standards, particularly in relation to third countries in agreements with the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0569fee390e7e2b777d0bdf161494796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb8d7d117faa045c40802649821c422</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/127/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Competent Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent personnel are qualified individuals responsible for overseeing the implementation and management of AI systems during testing to ensure compliance with standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent personnel refers to individuals with the necessary expertise employed by notifying authorities for performing tasks related to conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd4e3bfdc01d686ffb1a660c85e1d7e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426696</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notifying Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Notifying Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Notifying Authorities are responsible for informing the Board and other stakeholders about regulatory matters and market surveillance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Notifying Authorities are responsible for notifying conformity assessment bodies that meet specific regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Notifying authorities are designated entities responsible for managing the assessment, designation, and notification of conformity assessment bodies within Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbc432dadad605b2e47a18258f70a0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Accreditation Body">
      <data key="d0">National Accreditation Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A national accreditation body assesses and certifies the competence of conformity assessment bodies to ensure they meet required standards.&lt;SEP&gt;National accreditation bodies may conduct the assessment and monitoring assigned to notifying authorities, ensuring compliance with established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031fbe0de70cf6f462d8e21fea6487e6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conflict of Interest">
      <data key="d0">Conflict of Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conflict of interest refers to situations where impartiality may be compromised; notifying authorities are structured to avoid such conflicts with conformity assessment bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality involves safeguarding sensitive information acquired by notifying authorities, in accordance with legal requirements outlined in Article 78.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality refers to the obligation of notified bodies to keep information private, especially during conformity assessment activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality pertains to the obligation of notified bodies to protect sensitive information acquired during conformity assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality involves the obligation of parties to protect sensitive information and ensure it is not disclosed without proper authorization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a33f9372e32e8879cc6f97cd662934d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99a919766b7813dbc97c458f95cc9ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/167/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Persons">
      <data key="d0">Competent Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent persons are individuals with the necessary skills and expertise engaged by notifying authorities to perform conformity assessment tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Information Technologies">
      <data key="d0">Information Technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Information technologies are areas of expertise relevant for competent personnel ensuring effective operations within notifying authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence (AI)">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence (AI)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificial Intelligence (AI) encompasses systems and technologies designed to simulate human intelligence, which this regulation seeks to govern.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence is a field of expertise that competent personnel may possess, contributing to the efficient assessment and evaluation processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c21c2e02a12c7ec585b20f1ef155db81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982e13bc34bc28efe312a849593f7f07</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="authorities">
      <data key="d0">authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorities refer to competent organizational bodies responsible for oversight and implementation of regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="personnel">
      <data key="d0">personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Personnel are individuals with the necessary expertise tasked with performing specific functions in various fields, including information technologies, AI, and law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="information technologies">
      <data key="d0">information technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Information technologies encompass various technologies used for storing, retrieving, and sending information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI">
      <data key="d0">AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI or Artificial Intelligence encompasses systems and technologies designed to perform tasks that traditionally require human intelligence, emphasizing innovation and ethical considerations in their deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;AI, or Artificial Intelligence, encompasses a broad range of technologies and systems aimed at performing tasks that typically require human intelligence. This fast-evolving family of technologies is utilized across multiple industries, enhancing capabilities by improving predictions, optimizing operations, and personalizing solutions. AI involves the simulation of human cognitive functions in machines, enabling diverse applications, including those that may have both beneficial and potentially harmful outcomes. Furthermore, AI technologies are subject to evaluation and regulation by established panels to assess potential risks and ensure compliance. Overall, AI represents advanced computational capabilities increasingly integrated into various sectors, driving innovation and efficiency in numerous domains.&lt;SEP&gt;AI, or artificial intelligence, is a technology expected to have a major impact on society, necessitating a regulatory framework aligned with Union values.&lt;SEP&gt;AI refers to a rapidly developing family of technologies that requires regulatory oversight and safe experimental spaces for innovation and integration of safeguards.&lt;SEP&gt;AI refers to Artificial Intelligence, which may have various applications and technologies, potentially generating risks to public interests and fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5bfe284b31053ed0488ca88518b58ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652e6414b5fe8ab54e8a9034ece6d222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df1f3eba6d36bfd15e8ab3333ac4fd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1bd36f2082e6f670210d08c02e3d502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafe6ac227379dad776c22a5abc16ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/8/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/138/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/4/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428477</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law">
      <data key="d0">law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Law encompasses systems of rules created and enforced through social or governmental institutions to regulate behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="competent personnel">
      <data key="d0">competent personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent personnel are individuals with the necessary expertise required to perform various regulatory and oversight tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="expertise">
      <data key="d0">expertise</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Expertise denotes specialized knowledge or skills in specific fields necessary for effective task performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental rights are basic human rights that are entitled to all individuals, forming a core aspect of legal systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights are basic human rights that must be protected and upheld within the Union and its member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights are the basic human rights and freedoms guaranteed by law, which can be affected by AI technologies and law enforcement practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0b972a179b165ba7115316ba8d0d987&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427008</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management System">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A quality management system is a formal framework that defines the processes, procedures, and responsibilities for achieving quality policies and objectives within an organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Quality Management System encompasses the processes and guidelines that organizations must follow to maintain product and service quality, as outlined in the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quality Management System pertains to the structured framework and practices required for ensuring compliance and quality assurance in high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quality Management System is a framework established by providers to ensure conformity assessment procedures, documentation, and post-market monitoring for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fbb87b8107271f1fe959942ad2e3666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6b3a7a24bfd18cc84baf6173985e105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3917f629d239e59c1197ea2404615c32</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/146/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/63/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428480</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of high-risk AI systems are entities responsible for implementing quality management systems to ensure regulatory compliance and quality in their AI products.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems are entities that develop or offer advanced artificial intelligence systems that carry significant risks, and they are being encouraged to comply with relevant regulations during the transitional period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5a4e48721924d3a1798f61c8810d78</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/178/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428358</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory Compliance refers to the adherence to laws, regulations, guidelines, and specifications relevant to AI systems, ensuring they meet safety and legal standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Testing Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing Procedures are the methods and processes used to evaluate high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing Procedures encompass the systematic actions and evaluations conducted before, during, and after the development of high-risk AI systems to ensure quality and compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management System">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Risk Management System is an essential framework for identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks associated with the deployment of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Risk Management System is a framework set in place to identify, assess, and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems as outlined in the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;A risk management system refers to processes and protocols that organizations must implement to manage risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Risk Management System refers to a structured process established for identifying, evaluating, and mitigating risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-492be2be76ac28fb634286d651691400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427473</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Market Monitoring System">
      <data key="d0">Post-Market Monitoring System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Post-Market Monitoring System is a regulatory mechanism that assists providers in managing the risks associated with AI systems after they have been deployed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Post-Market Monitoring System involves ongoing assessment of AI systems after they have been placed on the market to ensure they continue to meet safety and performance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Post-Market Monitoring System is a comprehensive framework designed to track the performance and safety of high-risk AI systems once they are available on the market. This system encompasses various processes that facilitate the ongoing compliance and assessment of these AI systems throughout their lifecycle. It involves activities undertaken by providers to collect data and review user experiences, ensuring that these AI systems continue to meet established safety standards. Post-market monitoring encompasses the systematic review of experiences and data associated with AI systems after their deployment, emphasizing the need for continuous observation and analysis to uphold compliance and safety in real-world applications. Overall, the Post-Market Monitoring System plays a crucial role in overseeing the performance and safety of AI technologies post-release.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fbb87b8107271f1fe959942ad2e3666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078bfdf1b899d975b7606b4acd63166d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/155/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Management">
      <data key="d0">Data Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Management involves protocols for handling data, including acquisition, storage, analysis, and retention, which are critical to the integrity of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Incident Reporting">
      <data key="d0">Serious Incident Reporting</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious Incident Reporting refers to protocols for notifying relevant authorities about incidents that significantly affect the functioning or safety of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Serious incident reporting encompasses the actions taken by providers when a serious incident involving a high-risk AI system occurs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426372</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Management Responsibilities">
      <data key="d0">Management Responsibilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Management Responsibilities outline the accountability and roles of organizational leaders in ensuring compliance and oversight of quality management systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 9">
      <data key="d0">Article 9</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 outlines the criteria for identifying high-risk AI systems that present significant risks across multiple Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 9 of the Regulation pertains to the risk management system of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 9 pertains to the regulation and requirements for risk management related to high-risk AI systems, emphasizing compliance and systematic approaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 9 outlines specific risks related to health and safety in the context of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-492be2be76ac28fb634286d651691400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 72">
      <data key="d0">Article 72</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 72 of the Regulation discusses the implementation and maintenance of a post-market monitoring system for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 72 pertains to post-market monitoring activities for high-risk AI systems, ensuring their continued safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 73">
      <data key="d0">Article 73</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 73 of the Regulation relates to the reporting of serious incidents involving high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 73 pertains to serious incident reports within the regulation, emphasizing oversight and accountability mechanisms in place for AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 73 specifies that serious incidents during testing must be reported to national market surveillance authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 73 specifies the reporting requirements concerning serious incidents identified during the testing of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428325</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Acquisition">
      <data key="d0">Data Acquisition</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Acquisition refers to the process of collecting data for further use in analysis and storage, essential in managing high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Collection">
      <data key="d0">Data Collection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Collection is the gathering of information from various sources to prepare for subsequent data processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Data Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Analysis involves examining and interpreting collected data to extract useful insights, particularly for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Labelling">
      <data key="d0">Data Labelling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Labelling is the process of tagging data with relevant identifiers or annotations to facilitate supervised learning in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Storage">
      <data key="d0">Data Storage</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Storage encompasses various methods and technologies used to retain and manage data over time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Filtration">
      <data key="d0">Data Filtration</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Filtration involves the process of cleaning and refining data to enhance its quality for analysis in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Mining">
      <data key="d0">Data Mining</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Mining refers to the analytical process that extracts patterns or knowledge from large sets of data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Aggregation">
      <data key="d0">Data Aggregation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Aggregation is the compilation of data from different sources for analysis and reporting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Retention">
      <data key="d0">Data Retention</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Retention is the practice of keeping data for a specific period to comply with legal and organizational policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reporting Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Reporting Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Reporting Procedures refer to the established protocols for communicating serious incidents concerning high-risk AI systems, as mandated in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems Regulation">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Systems Regulation establishes rules regarding the compliance and transparency obligations required for the deployment of AI systems across Union and Member State laws.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Systems Regulation provides a framework for obligations and quality management systems for high-risk AI systems in various sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fcb2e4f81b296d92eea24f66dd7abee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/137/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426228</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Financial Services Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Financial Services Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal framework governing financial institutions within the European Union, outlining requirements for documentation and governance practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Financial Services Law encompasses regulations governing the operation and oversight of financial institutions within the Union, including requirements related to data management.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Financial Services Law refers to the legal framework governing financial institutions within the Union, including rules on internal governance and quality management systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Financial Services Law refers to the regulations governing the operations of financial institutions under EU law, including AI deployments.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Financial Services Law encompasses the regulations and requirements governing financial services, emphasizing risk management and internal governance for financial institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ceb3dc76830ec642fabf4620edacf57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9c861dfef84b47d382d7c3a57b94afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/158/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427112</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management Systems">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Quality Management Systems are organizational frameworks that ensure products and services meet certain quality standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations regarding Internal Governance">
      <data key="d0">Obligations regarding Internal Governance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations regarding Internal Governance are requirements that financial institutions must fulfill to adhere to relevant governance laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member State Law">
      <data key="d0">Member State Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Member State Law includes the specific laws that individual member states within the Union adopt to regulate various matters, including AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Member State Law refers to the legal statutes enacted by individual EU member states that must comply with EU directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fcb2e4f81b296d92eea24f66dd7abee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da6e9cf5fd822e42b8f37d6d2798af0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/94/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/137/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427441</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System Deployers">
      <data key="d0">AI System Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">AI System Deployers are organizations or entities responsible for the implementation and management of AI systems, subject to various regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fcb2e4f81b296d92eea24f66dd7abee7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/137/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426233</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance with Transparency Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Compliance with Transparency Obligations</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fcb2e4f81b296d92eea24f66dd7abee7</data>
      <data key="d2">This Regulation outlines that compliance with transparency obligations is necessary for AI systems, impacting their lawful use under existing laws.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/137/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426233</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independent Experts">
      <data key="d0">Independent Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Independent Experts are individuals selected for their scientific or technical expertise in AI to form the Scientific Panel for oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Independent Experts are individuals who may be engaged by the AI Office to conduct evaluations and provide expertise in enforcement processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Independent experts are appointed by the Commission to carry out evaluations of general-purpose AI models on its behalf.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a644c604bba8cdc33a7125c5db02395c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/151/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427628</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 18 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020">
      <data key="d0">Article 18 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 18 outlines specific procedural rights that are applicable to providers in the context of compliance and market regulations for AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Copyright Holders">
      <data key="d0">Copyright Holders</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Copyright Holders are individuals or entities that own the rights to specific data or content, protected under copyright law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Collections">
      <data key="d0">Data Collections</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Collections are groups of data sets aggregated for use in training AI models, can be private or public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Privacy">
      <data key="d0">Data Privacy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Privacy refers to the practices and regulations concerned with protecting personal and sensitive data from unauthorized access and use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Providers of AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of AI Models are companies or entities that develop and offer AI systems, requiring compliance with data transparency protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of general-purpose AI models must comply with regulations and provide information to the AI Office during evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training Data">
      <data key="d0">Training Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training Data consists of datasets used to train AI models, which may include copyrighted materials that require careful handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data comprises the datasets utilized to train an AI system, allowing it to optimize its performance and learn from input examples.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data refers to data used to teach an AI system by fitting its learnable parameters to recognize patterns and make decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Training Data pertains to the content used to train AI models, which must be disclosed by providers under copyright compliance policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994612dc34fa7cbfaae3dc6fdd1036d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427689</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Services Act">
      <data key="d0">Digital Services Act</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Digital Services Act is a legislative framework aimed at creating a safer digital space and is associated with Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f49bab3ffe15bdb9d4d12f5b8ce62182</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/11/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2000/31/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2000/31/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2000/31/EC, also known as the E-Commerce Directive, lays the groundwork for digital services legislation and is amended by Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 to address liability concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f49bab3ffe15bdb9d4d12f5b8ce62182</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/11/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single Market for Digital Services">
      <data key="d0">Single Market for Digital Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Single Market for Digital Services is a primary EU initiative aimed at ensuring free movement of digital services across member states, governed by regulations including Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f49bab3ffe15bdb9d4d12f5b8ce62182</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/11/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">High-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems are classified systems that are subject to specific regulations to ensure compliance with safety and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are designed to operate transparently, providing relevant information to deployers regarding their operation and intended use.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refer to artificial intelligence technologies that could pose significant risks to health, safety, and fundamental rights of individuals in the Union, necessitating strict compliance measures.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems refers to systems that require proper design, development, and oversight to ensure their appropriate and safe functioning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="provider">
      <data key="d0">provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A provider is defined as an entity or individual, whether natural or legal, responsible for placing artificial intelligence (AI) systems on the market. They are obligated to ensure compliance with relevant AI regulations and must meet specific requirements related to transparency and performance standards, particularly for high-risk AI systems. This includes maintaining appropriate documentation and providing contact details. Providers can be seen as those who offer goods or services, specifically in the context of AI models, and they are responsible for developing or supplying these systems under their own name. In summary, providers play a crucial role in the development and supply of AI technologies, while also being bound by compliance obligations dictated by regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-442777921e9a3bd01b79336245710651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="deployers">
      <data key="d0">deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are individuals or organizations responsible for implementing and managing high-risk AI systems, ensuring compliance with relevant regulations and guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are individuals or organizations that implement and use AI technologies and must adhere to compliance measures as recommended by the European Artificial Intelligence Office.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are the individuals or organizations that implement high-risk AI systems and must interpret their outputs based on the provided instructions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7aa55ff3193c0e45818701bd0bcd7e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section 3">
      <data key="d0">Section 3</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 3 outlines the obligations that the provider and deployers must adhere to in relation to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 9(2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 9(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 9(2) describes the risks to health, safety, and fundamental rights that can arise from the use of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider Contact Details">
      <data key="d0">Provider Contact Details</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Provider Contact Details refer to the information regarding identity and means of communication of the provider, as required for transparency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92c46bb2da7f7daf8b839c28016c384</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 14">
      <data key="d0">Article 14</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 14 is a part of a legal framework that outlines specific provisions and conditions relevant to the broader legislative context.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 14 refers to human oversight measures designed to facilitate the interpretation of outputs from high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1707a8e9fa1107c63102bdcbf42885d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Training Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training data sets are collections of data specifically designed for training AI models, ensuring they can make accurate predictions and decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data sets are collections of data used to train AI systems, which can be targeted in cyberattacks, leading to potential data poisoning.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data sets refer to the specific data used for training high-risk AI systems, crucial for understanding their functionalities and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data sets are collections of data used to train AI systems, which should be representative and free of errors to enhance AI performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ef56265dcb6096b96bc5ee3bfe08c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65688cdd97448f1f3932957595156d18</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427776</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation and Testing Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Validation and Testing Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Validation and testing data sets are essential for assessing the performance and reliability of high-risk AI systems in real-world applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployment">
      <data key="d0">Deployment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployment refers to the process of implementing high-risk AI systems in practical settings, ensuring they operate correctly and safely.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployment refers to the process of putting the high-risk AI system into operation, requiring careful consideration of its intended use and risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428066</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Logs">
      <data key="d0">Logs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Logs are records generated by the high-risk AI system, crucial for monitoring, debugging, and ensuring compliance with Article 12.&lt;SEP&gt;Logs are records that capture the operational data and interactions of the AI system, which are crucial for monitoring performance and ensuring compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Logs refer to automatically generated data from high-risk AI systems that demonstrate compliance and monitor performance throughout their operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1630fe82dedd2af2d49f1b480b55eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed64bdb2c36cf3a65859258e7888a51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 12">
      <data key="d0">Article 12</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 12 pertains to regulations governing the management and compliance measures for high-risk AI systems, particularly focusing on data logs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1630fe82dedd2af2d49f1b480b55eec</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Software Updates">
      <data key="d0">Software Updates</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Software Updates are essential processes meant to improve the functionality, security, and performance of AI systems by regularly incorporating new features and fixes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1630fe82dedd2af2d49f1b480b55eec</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426251</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Maintenance Measures">
      <data key="d0">Maintenance Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Maintenance Measures are the activities undertaken to preserve the functionality of the AI system, including updates and checks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1630fe82dedd2af2d49f1b480b55eec</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426251</data>
    </node>
    <node id="World Trade Organization">
      <data key="d0">World Trade Organization</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The World Trade Organization is an international body that regulates international trade and facilitates trade agreements among member countries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7fb8d7d117faa045c40802649821c422</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/127/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Country">
      <data key="d0">Third Country</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A third country refers to a nation that is not part of the Union or WTO but may engage in trade and agreements with these entities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7fb8d7d117faa045c40802649821c422</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/127/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Committee">
      <data key="d0">Committee</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Committee is established to assist the Commission, functioning within the framework of EU Regulation (EU) No 182/2011.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f93de63e4907e805d3e56afc25c0472</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/98/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 98">
      <data key="d0">Article 98</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 98 details the examination procedures for regulatory compliance and the approval of implementing acts by relevant bodies, ensuring adherence to rules.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98 refers to a specific legal provision in the EU's regulatory framework governing the examination procedure related to the adoption of decisions by the European Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98 refers to a specific provision within the EU regulatory framework addressing the structure and procedures of committees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1552bf93eb98e5313a0207e768b7d357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f93de63e4907e805d3e56afc25c0472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee723ad2204a364a1d2dbe158b59a8f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/98/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427864</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 108">
      <data key="d0">Article 108</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 108 refers to a specific legislative document or section that pertains to amendments in the Regulation (EU) 2018/1139.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0325a6544b6b69856a2fcf978648cb23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence systems">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificial Intelligence systems refer to technologies and software designed to perform tasks typically requiring human intelligence, governed under the regulations outlined in the Artificial Intelligence Act.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI safety components">
      <data key="d0">AI safety components</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI safety components are critical elements within artificial intelligence systems that ensure their operation adheres to safety standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 300/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 300/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 300/2008 establishes a framework for security measures in civil aviation, which may intersect with discussions on the regulation of AI in safety-critical areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 300/2008 is a European regulation related to security equipment and was subject to amendments regarding artificial intelligence systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 300/2008 establishes common rules in civil aviation security, impacting the deployment of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation outlines common rules related to civil aviation security and is a key legislative framework in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae59e0a0d71d982ef900a9cf17ed916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427657</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2016/797">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2016/797</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2016/797 focuses on railway interoperability, which may involve AI technologies for improving safety and efficiency in rail transport.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2020/1828">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2020/1828</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2020/1828 deals with the regulation of consumer protection, relevant to the use of AI in technologies impacting consumers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2f2633a0fb5f0222ac492dc16170f8b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="(EU) No 167/2013">
      <data key="d0">(EU) No 167/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">(EU) No 167/2013 pertains to the approval and market surveillance of agricultural and forestry vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="(EU) No 168/2013">
      <data key="d0">(EU) No 168/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">(EU) No 168/2013 covers the approval and market surveillance of two or three-wheel vehicles and quadricycles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="(EU) 2018/858">
      <data key="d0">(EU) 2018/858</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">(EU) 2018/858 is related to the approval and market surveillance of motor vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="(EU) 2018/1139">
      <data key="d0">(EU) 2018/1139</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">(EU) 2018/1139 regulates the aviation safety framework within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="(EU) 2019/2144">
      <data key="d0">(EU) 2019/2144</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">(EU) 2019/2144 focuses on the approval and market surveillance of vehicle systems, components, and separate technical units.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e26bac5f6de804a85dcdb8e70cd2a910</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/108/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Deployers of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers of High-Risk AI Systems are entities responsible for using high-risk AI technologies and ensuring their operation complies with established regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers of high-risk AI systems include public law bodies and private entities that utilize AI technology in critical sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers of high-risk AI systems are responsible for overseeing the practical application of AI technologies, ensuring that rights are protected during usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426940</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Measures">
      <data key="d0">Technical Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Measures encompass the procedures and tools that deployers implement to ensure the safe and compliant use of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426279</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Oversight">
      <data key="d0">Human Oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Oversight involves assigning qualified individuals to monitor and manage high-risk AI systems to ensure they operate safely and effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight encompasses arrangements made to ensure that human judgment is integrated into AI system operations to mitigate risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight refers to the involvement of natural persons in monitoring and managing high-risk AI systems to minimize potential risks to health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428066</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Input Data">
      <data key="d0">Input Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Input Data refers to the data used by high-risk AI systems, which must be relevant and representative for the AI to function correctly.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data refers to the data received by an AI system to produce an output based on learned patterns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competence and Training">
      <data key="d0">Competence and Training</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Competence and Training relate to the necessary skills and knowledge that individuals overseeing high-risk AI systems must possess.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c213966187c2de81f63a872522fd168</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426279</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Service Law">
      <data key="d0">Financial Service Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Service Law encompasses regulations governing financial institutions, including their governance processes and internal arrangements related to the use of AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 35">
      <data key="d0">Article 35</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 35 mandates a data protection impact assessment for using certain technologies, including AI systems, to ensure compliance with personal data protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 outlines the requirement for assessing high risks to the rights and freedoms of data subjects during data processing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributor">
      <data key="d0">Distributor</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A distributor is a critical intermediary in the supply chain responsible for the distribution of high-risk AI systems. This entity plays a vital role in making these systems available in the Union market and must adhere to all relevant regulations and obligations, particularly if they modify or label the systems. Distributors are accountable for ensuring compliance with safety requirements and legal standards, reflecting their responsibility to facilitate the proper introduction of high-risk AI systems to the market. When certain conditions are met, distributors are also held accountable under the AI Value Chain Regulation, emphasizing their pivotal role in the regulation of AI systems from providers to deployers. Overall, a distributor acts as a key facilitator in the distribution of AI technologies, ensuring that legal and safety protocols are followed throughout the process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427594</data>
    </node>
    <node id="First Responders">
      <data key="d0">First Responders</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">First responders are individuals who must be informed immediately in the case of serious incidents involving AI systems, ensuring prompt management of risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Workers Representatives">
      <data key="d0">Workers Representatives</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Workers' representatives are individuals who advocate for the interests of employees, especially in matters relating to the deployment of AI systems in the workplace.&lt;SEP&gt;Workers’ Representatives are individuals or groups that represent employees' interests and rights, particularly during the introduction of high-risk systems in workplaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operational Data">
      <data key="d0">Operational Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Operational Data refers to sensitive data generated during the operation of AI systems, which is protected under specific regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b7a97b6144d96bce021cd4b80f21b84</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Database">
      <data key="d0">EU Database</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Database is a centralized and official repository established by the European Union, designed specifically for tracking the registration and management of high-risk AI systems across member states. It serves as a regulatory framework that mandates providers to register their AI systems before they can be placed on the market or utilized. The database contains secure and non-public information, encompassing various regulations and registrations related to these high-risk AI systems. Additionally, the EU Database acts as a digital registry where testing activities and associated data of AI systems are recorded for compliance and regulatory purposes. It is also referenced in the regulation for managing information related to AI compliance and incident reporting, ensuring a comprehensive approach to the oversight of high-risk AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Database is a secure, non-public repository where information related to high-risk AI systems is registered for compliance and oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Database is established under the regulation to enhance traceability and transparency regarding the registration of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU database is a system established for the registration of AI systems, ensuring traceability and transparency in their deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22dbef3b29da3394b10b69bcc6aa4f59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06455acfb04ed0ea0e1fcd7b8fa89595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b88de119a362d1ff7d1500b9782d0c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Authority">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Judicial Authority is an independent administrative body responsible for granting authorizations related to law enforcement activities, ensuring that rights are protected.&lt;SEP&gt;A judicial authority is a legal body responsible for making binding decisions regarding the authorization of the use of AI systems in law enforcement, as described in the context.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial Authority refers to the legal entity that grants authorization for the use of high-risk AI systems in criminal investigations.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authority refers to institutions vested with the power to administer justice and ensure the rule of law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26fcdeec947c5dfd024232093934843&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7e9eb6e4da61705e152386e4c7c8412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce4de2ee2430b55395c19336af7c01</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/61/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Authority">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative Authority is a governing body that can grant or refuse authorization for the deployment of high-risk AI systems when required.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Remote Biometric Identification System">
      <data key="d0">Post-Remote Biometric Identification System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-Remote Biometric Identification System refers to technology used for identifying individuals based on biometric data after the initial contact, particularly for investigative purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9715a176fe159c930bda821593bb9bee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/679 is a regulation in EU law on data protection and privacy in the European Union and the European Economic Area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification refers to AI technologies used for identifying individuals based on biometric data, subject to strict legal requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="judicial authority">
      <data key="d0">judicial authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A judicial authority is a legally empowered institution in a Member State that grants authorization for the use of biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authority refers to the entity that has the power to make legal decisions and grant authorizations related to the use of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fbdf24f8b746547b54a3e43daaf33</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="administrative authority">
      <data key="d0">administrative authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative authority refers to government bodies that make decisions and provide oversight for compliance with laws regarding AI systems and biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law enforcement authorities">
      <data key="d0">law enforcement authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Law enforcement authorities are government agencies tasked with maintaining public order and safety. Their responsibilities encompass the prevention, detection, investigation, and prosecution of criminal offenses, utilizing a variety of tools, including high-risk artificial intelligence systems. These agencies implement AI systems under specific conditions, which may not require prior authorization, as long as they comply with established regulations and legal frameworks. Furthermore, law enforcement authorities are essential in governing AI-related activities that pertain to public security, ensuring that any use of high-risk AI systems adheres to relevant conformity assessment procedures. Through these roles, they play a crucial part in upholding the law and safeguarding the community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8637916ea42060e68c1064d171c7c635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/130/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="personal data">
      <data key="d0">personal data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Personal data consists of any information that is related to an identified or identifiable individual, highlighting the importance of regulatory compliance in its processing, particularly when it comes to the development and testing of AI systems. This data must be protected under various regulations, including those specific to AI practices and data protection laws. According to EU regulation, personal data specifically refers to any information that can be used to identify a natural person. The significance of safeguarding this data is underscored by the stringent legal frameworks that apply to it, ensuring that individuals' privacy is respected and maintained.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e92604946d4eabeb5967b67f4f208c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4075031022597f5cdfdd7494b828c25</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427090</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement Authorities are governmental agencies tasked with enforcing laws and maintaining public order. This includes a variety of entities such as police departments and related organizations. Their primary responsibilities encompass preventing, detecting, and investigating crimes, as well as ensuring public safety and security in various areas such as crime, border control, and immigration. In some cases, these authorities may utilize biometric identification systems while operating under specific regulations. Additionally, Law Enforcement Authorities ensure that their operational data is protected from post-market monitoring, emphasizing the importance of confidentiality and security in their operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afaea4dcd95d49cc4d21cf9078216b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ccfe5fb33f83ead7b5c0eb2f0576d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2bf8c519aff48aa30866bbefc0dc688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078bfdf1b899d975b7606b4acd63166d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/155/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428497</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Remote Biometric Identification Systems">
      <data key="d0">Post-Remote Biometric Identification Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-remote biometric identification systems are advanced technologies used by law enforcement for identifying individuals based on biometric data, often requiring strict regulatory oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-remote biometric identification systems refer to technologies used to identify individuals based on their biometric data collected from video footage without real-time surveillance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-32ccfe5fb33f83ead7b5c0eb2f0576d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5ea4945288b78b6ce93568aea26b18d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/95/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Data Protection Authority">
      <data key="d0">National Data Protection Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The National Data Protection Authority ensures that data protection laws are upheld and that personal data is managed according to national and regional regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Data Protection Authority is an institution in each EU Member State that oversees compliance with data protection laws and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Data Protection Authority oversees the enforcement of data protection regulations within a country, especially pertaining to personal information handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb2b1ecdb0a779493d4236bdef52a5f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26fcdeec947c5dfd024232093934843&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ccfe5fb33f83ead7b5c0eb2f0576d9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Authority">
      <data key="d0">Public Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A public authority is an official governmental entity that has the power to enforce laws and regulations, including those related to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Authority is a governing entity responsible for overseeing the development of AI systems aimed at safeguarding public interest, including health and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Authority refers to any government body or agency that has the legal authority in relation to the registration and management of AI systems in the EU database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69800a0e24a3f7afd28e97d0e1079c4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/13/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Data Protection Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Data Protection Law</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Data Protection Law encompasses legislation aimed at protecting personal data rights and ensuring the lawful processing of such data by organizations in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Union data protection law establishes frameworks for how personal data should be protected and processed in the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Union data protection law refers to the legislative framework established by the European Union to safeguard personal data and protect the rights of individuals within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Data Protection Law establishes the legal framework for data protection and privacy in the context of personal data processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e010ebb9b0353d97d9e67673267bc415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06455acfb04ed0ea0e1fcd7b8fa89595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd4e3bfdc01d686ffb1a660c85e1d7e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/69/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 35 outlines the requirements for conducting Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) to assess risks associated with data processing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 39 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">Article 39 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 39 addresses the responsibilities for ensuring data protection compliance within EU institutions, including risk assessments and safeguarding data subjects' rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Safety">
      <data key="d0">Public Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Safety is a concept referring to the welfare and protection of the general public, often prioritized in the development of AI systems within the sandbox environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Health">
      <data key="d0">Public Health</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Health involves the science of protecting and improving community health through education, promotion of healthy lifestyles, and research for disease and injury prevention, relevant in the context of AI system development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Subjects">
      <data key="d0">Data Subjects</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Subjects are individuals whose personal data is being processed, and their rights and freedoms must be safeguarded during data handling in the AI sandbox.&lt;SEP&gt;Data subjects are individuals whose personal data is collected, processed, or stored under regulations like GDPR, holding rights regarding their data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b5414adf1ebf7087a1a00f2e4fb3570b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428375</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Energy Sustainability">
      <data key="d0">Energy Sustainability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Energy Sustainability refers to practices that meet current energy needs without compromising future generations' ability to meet their needs, which may be a focus area for AI system development in the sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Climate Change Mitigation">
      <data key="d0">Climate Change Mitigation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Climate Change Mitigation includes efforts and policies aimed at reducing greenhouse gas emissions to combat climate change, which can benefit from AI technologies developed in the sandbox.&lt;SEP&gt;Climate Change Mitigation includes strategies supported by AI technologies that aim to reduce the effects of climate change.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-652e6414b5fe8ab54e8a9034ece6d222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0011a0d9e3a2637e314c176ed0dc26c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/4/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426699</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 establishes rules for the processing of personal data by EU institutions and bodies, ensuring protection of personal data within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 is a comprehensive legal framework focused on the protection of personal data within the European Union, specifically governing the handling of such data by EU institutions, bodies, offices, and agencies. This regulation establishes clear rules and responsibilities for ensuring that personal information is managed securely and in compliance with data privacy standards across various EU entities.

Key aspects of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 include its emphasis on the treatment of biometric data, among other types of personal information, thereby enhancing the rights of data subjects. By outlining specific protections for personal data, the regulation plays a crucial role in safeguarding individuals' privacy rights within the context of EU governance. Overall, Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 is integral to establishing a robust framework for data protection in the European Union's administrative landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 regulates the protection of personal data processed by the European institutions and bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e35e35e2f589e83baa732e4cdf12f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0d2c55c34335ae38db203f32e428ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22dbef3b29da3394b10b69bcc6aa4f59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5414adf1ebf7087a1a00f2e4fb3570b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a360e38774a35c72c4384c10d081a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57118cd489d78b33ed75c63f33151aee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65688cdd97448f1f3932957595156d18</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/140/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/180/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI regulatory sandboxes">
      <data key="d0">AI regulatory sandboxes</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">AI regulatory sandboxes are controlled environments where AI systems can be developed, tested, and monitored under specific regulations to ensure compliance with legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;AI regulatory sandboxes are controlled environments where AI systems can be tested and validated while ensuring compliance with data protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="competent authorities">
      <data key="d0">competent authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent authorities are the official organizations responsible for overseeing the regulation and documentation of AI projects developed within the sandbox.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent authorities refer to the bodies or agencies in charge of overseeing the implementation and compliance of data protection regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 39">
      <data key="d0">Article 39</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 39 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 provides specific provisions related to the rights of data subjects and their protection under the data processing framework provided by the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="sandbox experimentation">
      <data key="d0">sandbox experimentation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Sandbox experimentation refers to the controlled and supervised process of testing and validating new technologies, such as AI systems, in a compliant environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data subjects">
      <data key="d0">data subjects</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data subjects are individuals whose personal data is processed, and they have certain rights regarding the protection of their data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union data protection law">
      <data key="d0">Union data protection law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union data protection law encompasses the legal framework set by the EU for safeguarding personal data rights and ensuring compliance during data processing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7a419de4926f1a525df3f4ac669396</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="technical documentation">
      <data key="d0">technical documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical documentation includes detailed reports and summaries regarding the processes, training, testing, and validation of AI systems developed in the sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="criminal offences">
      <data key="d0">criminal offences</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal offences encompass actions or incidents that violate criminal law, leading to law enforcement intervention for prevention or prosecution.&lt;SEP&gt;Criminal offences refer to actions that violate laws and regulations, which may necessitate the involvement of law enforcement authorities during the processing and application of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98864e35252474211ac7cc215880629d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Robustness">
      <data key="d0">Technical Robustness</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical robustness describes the capability of AI systems to remain functional and safe under various conditions, especially in the face of errors or unforeseen situations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426297</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Organizational Measures">
      <data key="d0">Organizational Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Organizational measures involve strategies and policies implemented to enhance the performance and safety of AI systems within their operational environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426297</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fail-Safe Plans">
      <data key="d0">Fail-Safe Plans</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fail-safe plans are protocols designed to ensure that AI systems can safely pause or terminate operations to prevent harm during anomalies or outside defined operational parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426297</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Impacts">
      <data key="d0">Safety Impacts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety impacts refer to the potential harm or adverse effects that may arise from the malfunctioning or biased operation of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426297</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmful Behaviour">
      <data key="d0">Harmful Behaviour</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmful behaviour refers to the unintended actions or outcomes produced by AI systems when they malfunction or operate under unforeseen circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426297</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Solutions">
      <data key="d0">Technical Solutions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Solutions refer to methods and technologies available for the effective design, training, and use of AI systems focusing on efficiency and sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions are methods and technologies designed to address challenges related to AI-generated content, ensuring proper identification and authenticity.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions are methods or tools developed to enhance the reliability and safety of AI systems, especially in high-stakes environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical solutions refer to the methodologies and practices that can address challenges in AI development, including data access and interoperability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30361d2283908d9b7babf63ae110a691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d09524914eef0125fee170a5c8b400e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/133/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Errors and Faults">
      <data key="d0">Errors and Faults</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Errors and faults refer to issues that may arise during the operation of AI systems, leading to incorrect or undesired outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426297</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Anomalies">
      <data key="d0">Anomalies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Anomalies are irregular occurrences identified by AI systems when assessing decision-making patterns for potential inconsistencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Anomalies are unexpected behaviors or outputs that can occur during the operation of high-risk AI systems, requiring monitoring and intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Anomalies are unexpected events or conditions that can disrupt the normal operation of AI systems, requiring strategies to manage their impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Anomalies refer to unexpected behavior or dysfunctions that may arise during the operation of high-risk AI systems, requiring monitoring and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d3235710f8867a0e47878a2233118ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808684c852275ce6793d894fcdacfe17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-992499cbdbb7fa23e4ae622c35e9d42f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/75/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428513</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notification Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Notification Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Notification Procedure outlines the process by which notifying authorities communicate the status of conformity assessment bodies to the Commission and Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 29">
      <data key="d0">Article 29</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 29 details the accreditation process and provisions regarding compliance assessment bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Activities">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Activities refer to the procedures that bodies undertake to evaluate compliance with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment activities are processes conducted by notified bodies to ensure that AI systems meet specific safety and performance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment activities are the procedures carried out by notified bodies to determine whether products meet established standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment activities refer to the procedures carried out to ensure that products meet the required safety and efficacy standards set by regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba752b306c578e6ee0a31563b30db893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428112</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accreditation Certificate">
      <data key="d0">Accreditation Certificate</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">An Accreditation Certificate is an official document that verifies a conformity assessment body's compliance with established standards.&lt;SEP&gt;An accreditation certificate is a formal document issued by a national accreditation body confirming that a conformity assessment body meets regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031fbe0de70cf6f462d8e21fea6487e6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentary Evidence">
      <data key="d0">Documentary Evidence</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentary Evidence refers to the materials or documentation that support claims made under Article 29(3), which are considered in the decision-making process.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentary Evidence refers to the written validation required when a notification is not based on an accreditation certificate.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentary evidence refers to the collection of documents necessary for verifying and monitoring compliance by conformity assessment bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88552f4423ec18db9bfb3db0f708349&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031fbe0de70cf6f462d8e21fea6487e6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 29(2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 29(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 29(2) outlines the requirements for obtaining an accreditation certificate necessary for the recognition of conformity assessment bodies under EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 29(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 29(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 29(3) specifies the requirements and processes for documentation and objections relevant to authorizations, guiding the decision-making framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 29(3) specifies the requirements for submitting documentary evidence related to conformity assessment bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b7923bde8b2532e6e5a248aa4cfb8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c88552f4423ec18db9bfb3db0f708349</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objections">
      <data key="d0">Objections</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Objections refer to challenges raised during the authorization process, which necessitate consultations before a decision can be made.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c88552f4423ec18db9bfb3db0f708349</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/30/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="remote biometric identification system">
      <data key="d0">remote biometric identification system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A remote biometric identification system is an AI system designed to identify individuals from a distance by comparing biometric data against a reference database without their active involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;A remote biometric identification system is an AI technology designed to identify individuals from biometric data without their involvement, typically processing multiple individuals simultaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;This system identifies individuals using biometric data without their direct involvement, typically from a distance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real-time systems">
      <data key="d0">real-time systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-time systems are systems that capture, compare, and identify biometric data instantaneously or with minimal delay, often using live footage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="post systems">
      <data key="d0">post systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post systems refer to biometric identification systems that process previously captured biometric data, comparing it after a delay.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="comparison process">
      <data key="d0">comparison process</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The comparison process is the method by which biometric data from a person is matched against stored biometric data to establish identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reference database">
      <data key="d0">reference database</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference database is a centralized storage of biometric data used to compare and identify individuals in biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A reference database stores biometric data for individuals that can be used to compare against incoming data for identification purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation on Real-Time Use">
      <data key="d0">Regulation on Real-Time Use</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Regulation on ‘Real-Time’ Use outlines guidelines for the implementation and functioning of AI systems that operate in real-time without significant delays.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-59c64c31df8d81ee8c4452fc69542d83</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Closed Circuit Television Cameras">
      <data key="d0">Closed Circuit Television Cameras</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Closed circuit television cameras are devices used to capture video footage for surveillance and monitoring purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-59c64c31df8d81ee8c4452fc69542d83</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-Time Identification">
      <data key="d0">Real-Time Identification</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-Time Identification refers to the process of identifying or recognizing individuals or data points without significant delays, using advanced AI systems to process information instantaneously.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-59c64c31df8d81ee8c4452fc69542d83</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Live Material">
      <data key="d0">Live Material</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Live Material encompasses content such as video footage that is generated in real-time, utilized for immediate identification and assessment in various AI applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-59c64c31df8d81ee8c4452fc69542d83</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post Systems">
      <data key="d0">Post Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post Systems are systems that involve the capture of biometric data prior to identification, leading to potential delays in processing and recognition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-59c64c31df8d81ee8c4452fc69542d83</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance and Enforcement">
      <data key="d0">Governance and Enforcement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Governance and Enforcement refer to the structure and processes in place to ensure compliance with the AI Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Penalties">
      <data key="d0">Penalties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consequences or fines imposed for non-compliance with the regulations, aimed at ensuring adherence to the rules.&lt;SEP&gt;Penalties refer to administrative fines and other consequences that Member States must establish for violations of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f519e0fb15239a9e7db009ac6e0ed402</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment System">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Conformity Assessment System ensures that AI technologies meet specified standards and regulations before being deployed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technological Advancements">
      <data key="d0">Technological Advancements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technological Advancements refer to the rapid development and deployment of AI technologies that pose risks requiring regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Application Date">
      <data key="d0">Application Date</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The specific date of 2 August 2025 marks the point at which the provisions on penalties of the Regulation apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f519e0fb15239a9e7db009ac6e0ed402</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-enabled manipulative techniques">
      <data key="d0">AI-enabled manipulative techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-enabled manipulative techniques refer to methods employed by AI systems that can persuade individuals to engage in unwanted behaviors or make decisions that impair their autonomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426330</data>
    </node>
    <node id="persons">
      <data key="d0">persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Persons are individuals who may be subjected to manipulative tactics by AI technologies, affecting their decision-making and autonomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons refer to individual human beings, both natural and legal, that have rights and freedoms as established in regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2763d61443dcf3aa274192c53e098997</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/170/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="machine-brain interfaces">
      <data key="d0">machine-brain interfaces</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Machine-brain interfaces are systems that can control what stimuli are presented to individuals, which could materially distort their behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="virtual reality">
      <data key="d0">virtual reality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Virtual reality is a technology that can also be used to manipulate perceptions and experiences, potentially leading to harmful behaviors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Person's Autonomy">
      <data key="d0">Person's Autonomy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Person's autonomy refers to the capacity of individuals to make their own choices and control their own actions without external manipulation or coercion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Harms">
      <data key="d0">Significant Harms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Significant harms refer to adverse impacts caused by AI systems that can affect physical, psychological health, or financial interests of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Groups">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulnerable Groups encompass individuals and communities who are at increased risk due to various factors such as age, disability, social status, economic conditions, or health issues, necessitating special considerations in the realm of artificial intelligence (AI) interactions. This includes populations that may be particularly susceptible to exploitation by AI systems, especially those under the age of 18, who may face adverse effects from the deployment and testing of high-risk AI technologies. As a result, these groups require additional safeguards and special attention in both regulatory evaluations and risk management processes associated with AI. Their specific needs and vulnerabilities highlight the importance of implementing protective measures to mitigate potential negative impacts stemming from AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups include individuals belonging to racial or ethnic groups that are particularly affected by discrimination and biases inherent in data sets.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups refer to individuals or communities that may be adversely affected by biases in AI systems, particularly racial or ethnic minorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups include individuals affected by age or disability who require special consideration during testing in real-world conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups refer to individuals who may need additional protection due to factors such as age or disability in the context of AI testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951511d7a62f58da07aebc05f3e4f1c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06455acfb04ed0ea0e1fcd7b8fa89595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c3bb945919e1b0c6e146fabaaeff87b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b1b6d000ef2c2e744936b8e5264e46</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428310</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Manipulative Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Manipulative Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Manipulative techniques are strategies used to influence people's behavior or decisions in ways that are deceptive or coercive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2005/29/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2005/29/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2005/29/EC addresses unfair business-to-consumer commercial practices within the internal market of the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2005/29/EC is a legislative act of the European Parliament and Council that prohibits unfair commercial practices affecting consumers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b8417f540a870b55b1e60c66cd42e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="person">
      <data key="d0">person</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Persons refers to individuals who can be affected by AI systems, particularly those in vulnerable situations such as age or disability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-65b8417f540a870b55b1e60c66cd42e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethnic or Religious Minorities">
      <data key="d0">Ethnic or Religious Minorities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethnic or religious minorities are groups that may face specific vulnerabilities and are often disproportionately affected by exploitative practices of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-65b8417f540a870b55b1e60c66cd42e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Extreme Poverty">
      <data key="d0">Extreme Poverty</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Extreme poverty describes a severe state of economic deprivation which can make individuals more vulnerable to exploitation by AI technologies and systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-65b8417f540a870b55b1e60c66cd42e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Treatment Practices">
      <data key="d0">Medical Treatment Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical Treatment Practices encompass legal protocols for psychological and physical rehabilitation performed in alignment with law and medical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Parliament and Council">
      <data key="d0">European Parliament and Council</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Parliament and Council are bodies of the European Union responsible for legislating and regulating various directives and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament and Council are key institutions within the European Union (EU) that collectively serve as co-legislators responsible for the creation and implementation of laws and directives. They are involved in a variety of legislative processes, particularly those concerning migration and asylum, as exemplified by their work on Directive 2013/32/EU, which pertains to international protection procedures. Additionally, the European Parliament and Council establish regulations governing other critical areas, including cybersecurity requirements for products with digital elements and various directives like Directive 2005/29/EC, Directive (EU) 2019/882, and Directive (EU) 2019/1937. Furthermore, their collaborative efforts extend to enacting regulations such as Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, demonstrating their integral role in shaping EU legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament and Council are legislative bodies of the EU that propose and adopt regulations, including those related to Artificial Intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5878750a2a2a6290f1a946976f92b6e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bed819423b33e0b2ff5ff94cc09d52e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46239d1477a3073a0d3894e967d3cb7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/172/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/104/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427692</data>
    </node>
    <node id="psychological treatment">
      <data key="d0">psychological treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Psychological treatment refers to methods of therapy for mental disorders, which must be performed according to legal standards including obtaining explicit consent from patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="physical rehabilitation">
      <data key="d0">physical rehabilitation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical rehabilitation encompasses treatment processes aimed at helping individuals recover physical function, which should only occur under appropriate legal and medical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="manipulative AI-enabled practices">
      <data key="d0">manipulative AI-enabled practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Manipulative AI-enabled practices refer to unfair or deceptive uses of artificial intelligence systems that can harm consumers and are prohibited under various directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council Directive 84/450/EEC">
      <data key="d0">Council Directive 84/450/EEC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Council Directive 84/450/EEC is a legislative document aimed at protecting consumers against misleading advertising.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directives 97/7/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directives 97/7/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directives 97/7/EC relates to the protection of consumers in distance contracts within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="98/27/EC">
      <data key="d0">98/27/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 98/27/EC is concerned with the protection of consumers and the enforcement of consumer rights across the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2002/65/EC">
      <data key="d0">2002/65/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2002/65/EC deals with the regulation of distance selling of financial services to consumers in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 2006/2004">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 2006/2004</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 2006/2004 establishes cooperation between national authorities enforcing consumer protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unfair Commercial Practices Directive">
      <data key="d0">Unfair Commercial Practices Directive</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Unfair Commercial Practices Directive aims to enhance the protection of consumers from unfair business practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 98/27/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 98/27/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 98/27/EC focuses on enforcing consumer protection laws across EU member states by enabling actions against unfair commercial practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2002/65/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2002/65/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2002/65/EC specifies rules regarding the provision of financial services over distance to ensure consumer protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7aa509a07a54a5a98cca1cc15e7f5e4b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Persons">
      <data key="d0">Persons</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-414a5bbdb827f9d405cd31cc218f4ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafe6ac227379dad776c22a5abc16ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a89ce17cf59281aee293dc5db92f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems can potentially manipulate persons by using techniques that impair their autonomy and decision-making capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons refer to individuals who are legally authorized to act on behalf of an entity or themselves, often in legal contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons refer to individuals who may be affected by the health and safety implications associated with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons refers to individuals who are involved in the development, operation, and usage of AI technologies and are targeted for literacy advancement through the codes of conduct.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civil Society Organisations">
      <data key="d0">Civil Society Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil Society Organisations are groups that may be consulted by the AI Office to provide diverse perspectives in the drawing up of codes of practice for AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Society Organisations are various groups that represent the interests of stakeholders and contribute to the formulation of codes of practice related to AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Society Organisations consist of various groups that may assist in the development of codes of practice and represent public interests.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil society organizations are non-governmental groups that play a crucial role in promoting ethical standards and stakeholder involvement in AI development.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil society organisations play a role in representing the interests of citizens and groups, particularly in discussions surrounding the ethical implications of AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-831c946b1acae90a683cbc5ac489ffaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/116/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Key Performance Indicators">
      <data key="d0">Key Performance Indicators</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) are metrics used to evaluate how well participants are achieving the objectives outlined in the codes of practice.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Performance Indicators are measurable values that demonstrate how effectively objectives related to codes of practice are being achieved.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426359</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Models Providers">
      <data key="d0">AI Models Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Models Providers include various entities that develop and offer general-purpose AI models that are relevant to the establishment of codes of practice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426359</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Downstream Providers">
      <data key="d0">Downstream Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Downstream Providers are entities that use general-purpose AI models and have the right to lodge complaints regarding regulatory infringements.&lt;SEP&gt;Downstream Providers are entities that utilize AI models and may engage in the commitments and processes defined by the codes of practice.&lt;SEP&gt;Downstream providers are entities that utilize general-purpose AI models in their products, relying on the documentation and transparency of these models to ensure proper integration and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428624</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Models">
      <data key="d0">AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Models are sophisticated algorithms or systems that harness artificial intelligence technology for a wide array of applications. These models are specifically designed to perform tasks based on data input and algorithms, enabling machines to process information and learn. AI Models can be utilized in general-purpose applications, particularly within the Union, and are integral to the development of codes of practice concerning their use.

In addition to their functionality, AI Models are subject to regulatory oversight aimed at managing systemic risks associated with their deployment. They represent specific implementations of AI systems that are embedded within various services, establishing a need for compliance with established regulatory requirements for effective risk management. Overall, AI Models encapsulate the intersection of advanced technology with regulatory frameworks, addressing both operational capabilities and the imperative of responsible usage.&lt;SEP&gt;AI models refer to algorithms and computational frameworks that are designed to perform specific tasks within AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Models refer to various artificial intelligence systems designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, such as learning, reasoning, and problem-solving.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Models encompass various types of general-purpose artificial intelligence systems and applications that are subject to regulatory scrutiny.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6a477f9413013f3c0b13fcd9449cbb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a644c604bba8cdc33a7125c5db02395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02c1809d1e7a16e9c8b3d0effff3a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/151/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427628</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commitments or Measures">
      <data key="d0">Commitments or Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Commitments or Measures refer to the obligations outlined in the codes of practice that participants must adhere to in order to achieve specific objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 May 2025">
      <data key="d0">2 May 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">2 May 2025 is the deadline set for having the codes of practice ready for implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;2 May 2025 is the deadline set for the readiness of the codes of practice for AI models in the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="codes of practice">
      <data key="d0">codes of practice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Codes of practice are guidelines intended to help AI model providers demonstrate compliance with obligations and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Codes of practice are guidelines that general-purpose AI model providers must adhere to, ensuring adequate standards and safety measures in AI technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426393</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 98(2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 98(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 98(2) describes the examination procedure that the Commission must follow in the context of implementing acts.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98(2) refers to a procedural regulation in EU law that outlines the examination process for adopting implementing acts.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98(2) refers to the examination procedure used by the Commission for adopting implementing acts regarding the establishment of the scientific panel.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98(2) refers to a section of legal or regulatory texts that outlines specific requirements or procedures related to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 98(2) is a procedural guideline that outlines the examination process for implementing acts concerning AI regulation in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4425b51346d70d56a2933633cfeb0018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c53f2e5a51e855855cf3895a52eefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427864</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 53">
      <data key="d0">Article 53</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 53 establishes the criteria and process for evaluating delegated acts.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 53 refers to a specific regulation that governs the information documentation requirements for AI model providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 53 specifies obligations that must be followed by providers of general-purpose AI models, particularly those not presenting systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="obligations in Article 53">
      <data key="d0">obligations in Article 53</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations outlined in Article 53 specify responsibilities for AI model providers that are not seen as systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="implementation acts">
      <data key="d0">implementation acts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Implementation acts are legal measures adopted by the Commission to enforce common rules and obligations within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations in Articles 53 and 55">
      <data key="d0">Obligations in Articles 53 and 55</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations in Articles 53 and 55 refer to specific legal requirements set forth in legislative documents, guiding implementation processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-081bc40b24333163a9239c2c45190bcc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Implementing Acts">
      <data key="d0">Implementing Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Implementing Acts are regulatory measures adopted to carry out the obligations stated in legislative articles.&lt;SEP&gt;Implementing acts are regulatory measures adopted by the European Commission to guide the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Implementing acts are regulatory measures adopted under Article 11 to enforce provisions related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-081bc40b24333163a9239c2c45190bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b3beca6b2129e6e4eb44988d1de112</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428637</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Examination Procedure in Article 98(2)">
      <data key="d0">Examination Procedure in Article 98(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Examination Procedure in Article 98(2) outlines the process for adopting implementing acts, ensuring adherence to legal frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-081bc40b24333163a9239c2c45190bcc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 53 and 55">
      <data key="d0">Articles 53 and 55</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 53 and 55 refer to specific provisions in a legal or regulatory document setting mandatory obligations for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-081bc40b24333163a9239c2c45190bcc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Participants">
      <data key="d0">Participants</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59</data>
      <data key="d2">Key Performance Indicators are used to evaluate the performance of all participants involved in the codes of practice.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union institutions">
      <data key="d0">Union institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union institutions include various agencies and bodies within the European Union that have specific functions in governance and policy implementation related to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions include various bodies, offices, and agencies within the European Union that may utilize high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Bodies are collective entities within the Union that operate under specific mandates and frameworks to fulfill particular functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426367</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Agencies">
      <data key="d0">Agencies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Agencies are specialized organizations within the Union that carry out regulatory tasks or serve specific roles, often related to implementation of policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426367</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Offices">
      <data key="d0">Offices</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Offices refer to administrative entities within the Union that handle day-to-day operations and governance functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426367</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Fakes">
      <data key="d0">Deep Fakes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep fakes are digital content created by AI that can convincingly represent real people or events but are actually artificially generated or manipulated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Obligation">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Obligation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The transparency obligation requires that AI-generated or manipulated content, such as deep fakes, is clearly labeled to inform the audience about its artificial origin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of AI System">
      <data key="d0">Providers of AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of AI systems are entities that create and deploy artificial intelligence technologies for generating or manipulating content such as images, audio, or video.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployed AI System">
      <data key="d0">Deployed AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployed AI systems refer to the implementation of AI technologies that generate or manipulate media content, particularly within various industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Manipulated Content">
      <data key="d0">Manipulated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Manipulated content refers to digital media that has been altered by AI to resemble real persons, objects, or events, potentially misleading viewers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Interest">
      <data key="d0">Public Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Interest refers to the welfare or well-being of the general public and is a critical consideration in law enforcement actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interest pertains to the general welfare of the public that information or content aims to inform or serve, especially regarding AI-generated or manipulated text.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interest represents the welfare or well-being of the general public, which may be emphasized when considering regulations for AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interest pertains to the welfare or well-being of the general public, serving as a guideline for the deployment and regulation of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interest refers to the consideration for society's general welfare, particularly in terms of data sharing and access in the context of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4425b51346d70d56a2933633cfeb0018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2f4cab7db3f8f9288f3fd79ff9595e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Origin">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Origin</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificial origin denotes content created or altered by artificial intelligence, requiring clear labeling to maintain transparency with viewers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Review Process">
      <data key="d0">Human Review Process</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human review process refers to the critical assessment undertaken by individuals on AI-generated content to verify accuracy, ethics, and authenticity before publication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-generated text">
      <data key="d0">AI-generated text</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-generated text refers to any content created using artificial intelligence technology, especially concerning public interest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="human review">
      <data key="d0">human review</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human review is the process of evaluating AI-generated content to ensure accuracy, reliability, and adherence to editorial standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="editorial control">
      <data key="d0">editorial control</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Editorial control pertains to the guidelines and standards applied by individuals or organizations overseeing published content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="natural or legal person">
      <data key="d0">natural or legal person</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural or legal person refers to an individual or organization that can have legal rights and obligations, particularly in the context of content publication responsibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-generated content">
      <data key="d0">AI-generated content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-generated content refers to text or media produced by artificial intelligence systems, especially in the context of public information and communication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="public interest">
      <data key="d0">public interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public interest relates to matters that concern the welfare or overall good of the general public, often influencing the dissemination and regulation of information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="content publication">
      <data key="d0">content publication</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Content publication involves the release and distribution of information, which can include AI-generated content, to the audience.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="editorial responsibility">
      <data key="d0">editorial responsibility</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Editorial responsibility pertains to the duty of individuals or organizations to ensure the accuracy and integrity of published content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="human oversight">
      <data key="d0">human oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human oversight refers to the involvement of individuals in reviewing and approving content, particularly AI-generated materials, to ensure quality control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Incidents">
      <data key="d0">Serious Incidents</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious Incidents are critical events or malfunctions caused by AI systems that can lead to harm, including death, health issues, and damage to property.&lt;SEP&gt;Serious incidents pertain to significant events involving high-risk AI systems that require immediate reporting to authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-078bfdf1b899d975b7606b4acd63166d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/155/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428497</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Causal Link">
      <data key="d0">Causal Link</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Causal link refers to the connection established between a serious incident and a high-risk AI system, which is required for reporting procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426372</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authorities of Member States">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authorities of Member States</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance authorities in each Member State are responsible for overseeing and enforcing regulations concerning high-risk AI systems and incident reporting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426372</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Initial Report">
      <data key="d0">Initial Report</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An initial report is a preliminary notification about a serious incident, which may be followed by a more detailed report.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Market Surveillance Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Relevant Market Surveillance Authority is the designated entity that receives complaints from natural or legal persons and conducts necessary market surveillance activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The relevant market surveillance authority is the specific authority in a Member State responsible for executing actions based on serious incident notifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25e9684f684f1a6f65a611ff0868319c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/85/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 3">
      <data key="d0">Article 3</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 3 is a reference to a specific section of legislation that defines serious incidents and their reporting requirements for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 3 relates to the definitions and conditions under which an AI system is classified as high-risk or not.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="August 2025">
      <data key="d0">August 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">August 2025 is the deadline by which guidance for compliance with obligations set out in the regulation will be developed and issued.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Incident">
      <data key="d0">Serious Incident</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Serious Incident refers to an occurrence that poses significant risk or harm associated with the functionality of high-risk AI systems that must be reported.&lt;SEP&gt;A serious incident refers to events that require immediate notification to regulatory bodies as per established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab65b498e8d012c9f396c7e602afc69f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2017/745">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2017/745</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2017/745 governs the marketing of medical devices within the EU, establishing safety and performance requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/745 is a legal framework that outlines specific conditions and obligations for medical devices and ensures compliance with applicable requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/745 outlines the requirements for high-risk devices and may overlap with regulations concerning AI systems as safety components.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/745 pertains to medical devices and sets standards for their safety and performance in the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/745 relates to medical devices and includes criteria on safety assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e36887a71116638e4cc965ab67bef7ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/51/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2017/746">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2017/746</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2017/746 focuses on in vitro diagnostic medical devices, establishing compliance requirements in the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/746 pertains to in-vitro diagnostic medical devices and may also govern aspects involving high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/746 sets the framework for in vitro diagnostic medical devices in the EU, repealing older directives and ensuring compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/746 pertains to in vitro diagnostic medical devices and includes conformity assessment processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba1dc3004941b91546fa83dccd4be34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e36887a71116638e4cc965ab67bef7ba</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/51/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">These regulations pertain to safety standards for medical devices and highlight obligations related to high-risk AI systems that are components of such devices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 3, point (49)(c)">
      <data key="d0">Article 3, point (49)(c)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 3, point (49)(c) defines specific incidents regarding high-risk AI systems that must be reported under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-32123438327e3ea3ecbf471a4c04236d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426389</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers of general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">providers of general-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of general-purpose AI models are entities responsible for developing, marketing, and maintaining AI systems with potential systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426393</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European harmonised standards">
      <data key="d0">European harmonised standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">European harmonised standards are regulatory frameworks that provide guidelines for compliance and safety of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426393</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 53 and 54">
      <data key="d0">Articles 53 and 54</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 53 and 54 are part of regulatory measures that outline obligations for compliance that providers must adhere to.&lt;SEP&gt;Articles 53 and 54 refer to specific regulations within a legal framework that outline obligations for AI model providers regarding systemic risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 56">
      <data key="d0">Article 56</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 56 describes the codes of practice relevant to demonstrating compliance for AI model providers until harmonized standards are established.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 56 pertains to the relevant codes of practice guiding the obligations and expectations from AI providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 56 is a provision within legal texts that outlines specific procedures related to the implementation of regulations and obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 56 in Directive (EU) 2019/790 refers to codes of practice that AI model providers can follow to demonstrate compliance with legal obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee723ad2204a364a1d2dbe158b59a8f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 78">
      <data key="d0">Article 78</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 78 is a provision that establishes comprehensive confidentiality obligations related to the handling of sensitive information by market surveillance authorities regarding artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It emphasizes the necessity of protecting information obtained during compliance assessments to safeguard sensitive trade secrets and various forms of confidential data. This article specifically mandates confidentiality for information gathered by public authorities under relevant regulations, reinforcing the protection of sensitive data throughout compliance processes.

Furthermore, Article 78 addresses the confidentiality requirements for sharing exit reports in the context of compliance assessments conducted within AI regulatory sandboxes, ensuring that any information or documentation obtained during these assessments maintains professional secrecy. This provision also pertains to the confidentiality obligations associated with information obtained under Directive (EU) 2019/790. Overall, Article 78 plays a crucial role in upholding the integrity and confidentiality of information related to AI compliance and regulatory oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 78 outlines the confidentiality obligations related to information gathered by competent authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 78 relates to regulations regarding confidentiality of information obtained during conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d56158a4a9411ebe99783effcebca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff66aa445497afef236bf08b342fee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5669bfd412b21e9a27b2f3c99aebc7e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99a919766b7813dbc97c458f95cc9ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c53f2e5a51e855855cf3895a52eefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f0b636a44a9e0af30b88362b202119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0873f73c77d97fdb97b3523748b32638</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/75/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/21/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428112</data>
    </node>
    <node id="model evaluation">
      <data key="d0">model evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model evaluation involves testing and assessing AI models according to standardized protocols to ensure they meet safety and performance standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426393</data>
    </node>
    <node id="cybersecurity protection">
      <data key="d0">cybersecurity protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity protection refers to measures taken to secure AI models against unauthorized access or attacks, ensuring their safe operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426393</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Code of Practice">
      <data key="d0">Code of Practice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Code of Practice outlines the ethical and operational guidelines that must be followed by AI providers to ensure responsible use and minimize risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Code of Practice refers to a set of guidelines and standards that organizations must adhere to for compliance, especially in regulated sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91d56158a4a9411ebe99783effcebca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Assessment involves the evaluation of high-risk AI systems to ensure they meet safety and regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance Assessment refers to the process through which AI model providers demonstrate adherence to established standards and codes, evaluated by regulatory bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance assessment is the process by which high-risk AI systems are evaluated to ensure they meet the regulatory requirements of the Union's legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1853942fcfd185abaf07003a8b70ff38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fe126564dfd9a342c90d435dae0173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/124/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">General-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI models are created and maintained by providers who must adhere to guidelines and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are large generative AI systems capable of creating text, images, and other content, providing innovation opportunities along with challenges for creators.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are versatile AI systems that can be adapted for a variety of tasks, subject to common specifications in their development and deployment.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 53 and 54">
      <data key="d0">Article 53 and 54</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers must adhere to the obligations set forth in Articles 53 and 54 to mitigate systemic risks during the development and usage of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to Explanation of Individual Decision-Making">
      <data key="d0">Right to Explanation of Individual Decision-Making</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Right to Explanation of Individual Decision-Making addresses the rights of individuals affected by decisions made through high-risk AI systems, focusing on transparency in decision-making processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cad430846dc3448ba37c9f18d213e761</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/86/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Affected Person">
      <data key="d0">Affected Person</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An affected person is an individual who is subject to decisions made by AI systems, experiencing potential adverse effects on their health, safety, or fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cad430846dc3448ba37c9f18d213e761</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/86/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Law Exceptions">
      <data key="d0">Union Law Exceptions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law exceptions refer to specific legal allowances or restrictions that apply to the use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cad430846dc3448ba37c9f18d213e761</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/86/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426403</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Elements">
      <data key="d0">Digital Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital elements refer to products that include software components or interfaces subject to specific cybersecurity requirements under EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity requirements are standards that notified bodies must adhere to in order to protect sensitive information during conformity assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity requirements establish the essential standards that products with digital elements must meet to ensure safety and security.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity requirements are the essential standards and protocols set forth to ensure the safety and resilience of digital products, including AI systems, against cyber threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System under this Regulation">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System under this Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI Systems classified under this regulation are subject to stringent cybersecurity assessment procedures due to their potential risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation on horizontal cybersecurity requirements">
      <data key="d0">Regulation on horizontal cybersecurity requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">This regulation outlines the horizontal cybersecurity requirements for various products, including those with digital elements and AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-684d5ab49c1881859fc01c26e46049cb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Act">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Act</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Cybersecurity Act, which includes the provisions of Regulation (EU) 2019/881, outlines the framework for cybersecurity measures across the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b330c1d8e73efeff5ccfef0a4f9ecd54</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Copyright Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Copyright Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union copyright law encompasses the legal framework governing copyright rights and obligations within the European Union, affecting the use and distribution of works.&lt;SEP&gt;Union copyright law governs intellectual property rights within the Union and may impact compliance obligations related to AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f3abbad4dddf2a8a56efeaa03cc7f28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7bb7f2671f4090f24b5396183a3f1e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Providers of General-Purpose AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of General-Purpose AI Models are companies or organizations engaged in the creation, development, and distribution of AI technologies designed for diverse applications across various sectors. These entities are tasked with providing AI systems intended for widespread use within the Union market, necessitating a keen understanding of their capabilities and the implications of their technologies. To ensure regulatory compliance and facilitate operations, providers are required to appoint an authorized representative within the Union. They must also meet compliance obligations set forth by specific regulations within established time frames. Furthermore, these providers are responsible for maintaining adherence to regulatory standards concerning the development and deployment of their AI models, while being mindful of the systemic risks associated with their technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-408ee65c3eab1e86c1c4207deaf4f216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0c7969cb66b898e1cf29a29c2c3923&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f3abbad4dddf2a8a56efeaa03cc7f28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994612dc34fa7cbfaae3dc6fdd1036d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/117/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/109/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428624</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nonprofessional or Scientific Researchers">
      <data key="d0">Nonprofessional or Scientific Researchers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals or groups involved in developing or utilizing AI models for noncommercial, personal, or academic purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f3abbad4dddf2a8a56efeaa03cc7f28</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/109/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Modifications or Fine-Tuning of Models">
      <data key="d0">Modifications or Fine-Tuning of Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of altering existing AI models to improve performance or adapt to new data sources while remaining compliant with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f3abbad4dddf2a8a56efeaa03cc7f28</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/109/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2019/790">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2019/790</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2019/790 is a comprehensive legal framework established by the European Union that regulates copyright and related rights within the Digital Single Market. Passed by the European Parliament, this directive aims to amend previous directives to better address the challenges and opportunities presented by the digital environment. 

The directive introduces important provisions regarding the use of protected content, particularly establishing exceptions for text and data mining under specific conditions. It emphasizes the need for transparency in the use of AI models, reflecting the evolving relationship between digital content and artificial intelligence. Overall, Directive (EU) 2019/790 is a pivotal regulation that shapes the landscape of copyright in the context of digital content and the use of advanced technologies in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9d6472f6799d71df39a63934dcde4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0c7969cb66b898e1cf29a29c2c3923&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7bb7f2671f4090f24b5396183a3f1e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Copyright">
      <data key="d0">Copyright</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Copyright refers to legal rights that grant creators exclusive control over the use and distribution of their original works, impacting AI model training.&lt;SEP&gt;Copyright refers to the legal structure protecting the use of creators' intellectual property, ensuring that authors and artists have rights over their works and the ability to control their distribution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b0c7969cb66b898e1cf29a29c2c3923&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9d6472f6799d71df39a63934dcde4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/106/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426813</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Jurisdiction">
      <data key="d0">Jurisdiction</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Jurisdiction refers to the authority of law in a given area, particularly regarding the enactment and enforcement of copyright provisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b0c7969cb66b898e1cf29a29c2c3923</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/106/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426428</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Identification Numbers">
      <data key="d0">Identification Numbers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Identification Numbers refer to unique identifiers assigned to each notified body for clarity and regulation purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b4903f69522ce55807b4320731843ac</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/35/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426431</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Act">
      <data key="d0">Union Act</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Act refers to the legislative measures under which organizations may be notified as bodies for conformity assessment within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b4903f69522ce55807b4320731843ac</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/35/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426431</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaint">
      <data key="d0">Complaint</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Complaint is a formal expression of dissatisfaction regarding an infringement of regulatory provisions that can be submitted to a market surveillance authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25e9684f684f1a6f65a611ff0868319c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/85/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provisions of the Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Provisions of the Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Provisions of the Regulation refer to specific rules and guidelines set forth in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 that individuals and organizations must adhere to.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25e9684f684f1a6f65a611ff0868319c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/85/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APIs">
      <data key="d0">APIs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) are tools that allow the AI Office to access general-purpose AI models for evaluation purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 68">
      <data key="d0">Article 68</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 68 refers to a specific regulation concerning the appointment of independent experts and their criteria for evaluating AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="legal persons">
      <data key="d0">legal persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal persons refer to entities such as companies or firms that have legal rights and obligations, capable of entering into contracts and being held accountable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="companies">
      <data key="d0">companies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Companies are types of legal persons that operate for profit and can enter contracts, be sued or sue others.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="firms">
      <data key="d0">firms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Firms are often synonymous with companies and represent businesses that provide goods or services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="implementing acts">
      <data key="d0">implementing acts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Implementing acts are regulatory frameworks or regulations adopted by the Commission to detail the procedures and requirements for evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="independent experts">
      <data key="d0">independent experts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Independent experts are professionals with specialized knowledge who can offer unbiased assessments and recommendations regarding high-risk AI systems and their implications.&lt;SEP&gt;Independent experts are qualified individuals tasked with evaluating AI models and providing unbiased assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider of General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d0">Provider of General-Purpose AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Provider of General-Purpose AI Model is the entity responsible for developing and supplying AI models that are subject to regulatory scrutiny by authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Persons">
      <data key="d0">Legal Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Persons refer to organizations or entities, including companies or firms, that can fulfill legal responsibilities, including providing requested information under regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lawyers">
      <data key="d0">Lawyers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lawyers are professionals authorized to act on behalf of clients and supply necessary information in legal contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Lawyers are professionals authorized to act on behalf of clients in legal matters, including providing necessary information as dictated by regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clients">
      <data key="d0">Clients</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Clients are individuals or entities that engage lawyers for representation or assistance and retain ultimate responsibility for information accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Clients are individuals or organizations that seek legal representation and are responsible for the accuracy of the information provided.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 55">
      <data key="d0">Article 55</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 55 refers to another regulation related to documentation and information requests from AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 68(2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 68(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 68(2) is a regulation that outlines the conditions under which the scientific panel can request information from AI providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Statutes">
      <data key="d0">Statutes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Statutes are written laws enacted by legislative bodies at the local, state, or national level, governing conduct within the jurisdiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Information">
      <data key="d0">Information</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Information refers to data or knowledge communicated to fulfill legal requirements or obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider of the General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d0">Provider of the General-Purpose AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An organization responsible for developing and supplying a general-purpose AI model, which can be utilized by various clients in different contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af91b8d0f12ada4bafa5122d248a66ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Specifications">
      <data key="d0">Technical Specifications</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Specifications refer to the detailed norms and standards set forth in regulations to ensure the quality and safety of security equipment and AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Security Equipment">
      <data key="d0">Security Equipment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Security Equipment pertains to tools and devices employed to maintain safety and security, which are regulated under European laws, including those addressing AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="June 13, 2024">
      <data key="d0">June 13, 2024</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">June 13, 2024 marks the date when Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 was established, highlighting the European Union's commitment to regulating artificial intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3accdffb1c2e32b663cc603e80d7c590</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data.europa.eu">
      <data key="d0">data.europa.eu</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">data.europa.eu is the official website providing access to EU data and information, including legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-32afd2b9878a3241576e8f1d00ae478c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1689">
      <data key="d0">1689</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">1689 refers to a specific legislative act or regulation of the European Union issued on the date mentioned.&lt;SEP&gt;The number 1689 identifies a specific regulation or legislation under the ELI framework for the year 2024.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-989b8f3b82689be8b7b178fea223a1b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32afd2b9878a3241576e8f1d00ae478c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428587</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2019/1937">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2019/1937</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2019/1937 is legislation from the European Parliament and Council aimed at protecting whistleblowers who report breaches of Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;The Directive (EU) 2019/1937 is a legal framework established by the European Union to regulate the reporting of infringements and ensure the protection of whistleblowers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5878750a2a2a6290f1a946976f92b6e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2ea81369b9366d970452a60702cb2d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/172/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/87/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringements">
      <data key="d0">Infringements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Infringements refer to violations of a regulation or directive, particularly those outlined in legal frameworks like Directive (EU) 2019/1937.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f2ea81369b9366d970452a60702cb2d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/87/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reporting Persons">
      <data key="d0">Reporting Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Reporting Persons are individuals who alert authorities about infringements or violations, often protected under laws such as Directive (EU) 2019/1937.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f2ea81369b9366d970452a60702cb2d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/87/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426475</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Authorities are governmental bodies that implement and enforce regulations on a national level.&lt;SEP&gt;National Authorities are governmental bodies within EU member states that have access to certain restricted information within the EU Database, as stated in Article 74.&lt;SEP&gt;National Authorities refer to the bodies in EU member states responsible for overseeing compliance with AI system registration.&lt;SEP&gt;National Authorities are local regulatory bodies within Union countries that monitor compliance and enforce regulations regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National authorities are governmental bodies within Member States that may be invited to contribute to discussions in the European Artificial Intelligence Board.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a33f9372e32e8879cc6f97cd662934d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b4f722f831bc4c8c4594e971e7b7654</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/167/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Authorities are governmental entities tasked with the implementation and oversight of regulations related to high-risk AI systems and management systems at national or regional levels. They are required to register their use of high-risk AI systems in the EU Database and ensure compliance with established regulations to promote safety and effectiveness. Additionally, Public Authorities utilize these high-risk AI systems while expecting AI providers to adhere to compliance standards. Furthermore, they are responsible for administering public services and benefits, which includes handling applications from natural persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3d709837f2bf640b25f168a3359606f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fbb87b8107271f1fe959942ad2e3666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc4d8b4e0e145ee1cf76386d881919f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/81/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428483</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex VIII">
      <data key="d0">Annex VIII</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex VIII outlines specific information that must be included in the registration of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VIII refers to a specific section relevant to the registration process in the EU Database, detailing requirements and exceptions for data submission.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VIII specifies the data requirements and sections relevant to the registration and management of information in the EU database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex IX">
      <data key="d0">Annex IX</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex IX contains specific information that must be included in the registration of testing plans for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IX details additional points related to the registration process and information requirements for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IX outlines additional points regarding registration and is referenced for high-risk AI systems in relation to the EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IX refers to a specific section of legal regulations detailing the requirements and information for providers of high-risk AI systems, ensuring their accountability and compliance with EU law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6024a6811c3d1fa27f1ad4e415829f3d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428310</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Registration Process">
      <data key="d0">Registration Process</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The registration process involves various documentation and verification steps required to officially register entities and systems in the EU Database, ensuring adherence to EU standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426477</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 74">
      <data key="d0">Article 74</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 74 is a provision detailing access rights and restrictions regarding the EU Database, particularly who may access restricted sections.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 74 refers to a specific legislative document that outlines the framework for market surveillance and regulation of AI systems within the Union Market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad3003ebe0581d9e97bcd66e0a884b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427560</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 91">
      <data key="d0">Article 91</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 91 outlines the processes and obligations for providers of general-purpose AI models, including compliance requests by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 93">
      <data key="d0">Article 93</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 93 describes measures that may be taken by the Commission towards providers for compliance failures regarding AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 92">
      <data key="d0">Article 92</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 92 involves the evaluation process that helps in identifying serious systemic risks at the Union level for AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 92 provides guidelines for the evaluation of AI models posing systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5923815c3c9119488dbfaacede6dec0c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Means">
      <data key="d0">Technical Means</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical means refer to the resources and methods employed by regulatory bodies to test high-risk AI systems for compliance with obligations under Union law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national public authorities">
      <data key="d0">national public authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National public authorities are government bodies involved in public administration and responsible for organizing testing and handling information confidentiality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5669bfd412b21e9a27b2f3c99aebc7e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authority">
      <data key="d0">Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Authority refers to the governing body responsible for organizing the testing as per the request of the public authorities or bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Authority signifies the official power granted to natural persons to verify and confirm the results generated by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Authority refers to the regulatory body responsible for monitoring and ensuring compliance with legal requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fcfeac23bcf45d7f7b0140796cad07f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5669bfd412b21e9a27b2f3c99aebc7e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ec10f8fea631de27f7f3ef17b5594a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/29/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Requesting Public Authority or Body">
      <data key="d0">Requesting Public Authority or Body</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The requesting public authority or body is an entity that requests testing to be organized by the authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5669bfd412b21e9a27b2f3c99aebc7e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing">
      <data key="d0">Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing is an event organized involving both the authority and the requesting public authority to assess compliance or performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5669bfd412b21e9a27b2f3c99aebc7e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 1">
      <data key="d0">Article 1</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 1 refers to provisions that outline how national public authorities are involved in the testing processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5669bfd412b21e9a27b2f3c99aebc7e8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="internal control">
      <data key="d0">internal control</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal control is a compliance procedure that AI providers may opt for according to Annex VI to ensure standards are met.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex VI">
      <data key="d0">Annex VI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex VI contains details about the conformity assessment procedure concerning internal controls to mitigate risks posed by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VI outlines internal control measures to evaluate the effectiveness of the conformity assessment procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VI specifies the internal control procedures that providers of high-risk AI systems must follow as part of the conformity assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex VII">
      <data key="d0">Annex VII</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex VII is a regulatory framework that outlines the specific requirements and procedures related to the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems. It details additional parts of the conformity assessment procedure applicable to these systems, which includes both the evaluation of quality management systems and the assessment of technical documentation. Additionally, Annex VII specifies the necessary steps and guidelines for obtaining certificates from notified bodies, ensuring compliance with the legal regulatory framework within the Union. Overall, Annex VII serves as a comprehensive guide to the conformity assessment procedures required for market entry of high-risk AI systems, emphasizing the critical aspects of quality management and documentation standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65d9e388dd47f8c8604a909fc7bfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba752b306c578e6ee0a31563b30db893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/45/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428597</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 40">
      <data key="d0">Article 40</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 40 refers to the harmonised standards that high-risk AI systems can rely on to demonstrate compliance under EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 41">
      <data key="d0">Article 41</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 41 is another legal provision in the documents that discusses standards and specifications relevant to the compliance of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 41 outlines common specifications that may be utilized when harmonised standards are not applicable for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="immigration authorities">
      <data key="d0">immigration authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Immigration authorities are potential users of high-risk AI systems that are subject to compliance regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Immigration authorities oversee the regulation and management of individuals entering, residing in, or leaving a country, often working with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="asylum authorities">
      <data key="d0">asylum authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Asylum authorities manage the processing of individuals requesting international protection, which may involve the use of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Asylum authorities may also use high-risk AI systems and must adhere to the relevant compliance standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonisation Legislation">
      <data key="d0">Harmonisation Legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonisation legislation aims to create common standards across member states for products and services, including high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonisation legislation refers to legal frameworks aimed at ensuring consistency across various EU standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f3473e38ccd9ad84662b373166a5c2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Acts">
      <data key="d0">Legal Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Acts denote the specific legislative measures enacted within the European Union to govern various subjects, including AI surveillance.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal acts refer to the formal laws and regulations established by governing bodies to regulate various sectors, including technology and AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal acts denote the legislative frameworks under which technical documentation must be assessed to ensure compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427940</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex I">
      <data key="d0">Annex I</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex I is a crucial component of the regulatory framework concerning high-risk AI systems within the European Union. It contains a list of Union harmonisation legislation that is pertinent to these high-risk AI systems, providing the necessary legal framework for compliance. This section includes specific provisions and guidelines that govern the legislation related to high-risk AI systems, ensuring that manufacturers understand the requirements they must meet.

Additionally, Annex I serves as an appendix that enumerates legal acts permitting product manufacturers to opt-out from certain third-party conformity assessments, but only under defined conditions. It outlines safety requirements for AI systems regarded as components of products, thereby assessing their risk level and ensuring that the safety components of such products meet established standards. Overall, Annex I is integral in detailing which products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation, providing clarity and guidance to stakeholders involved in the development and regulation of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I outlines the criteria and standards that AI systems must meet to qualify for a certificate valid for five years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65d9e388dd47f8c8604a909fc7bfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bff2cb7a8bc7b162d1d512fa7d0a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7195e1644a22885c55968d2c801e0064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bca7fe15bcbe076f97f98b2f3479775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428597</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex IV">
      <data key="d0">Annex IV</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex IV contains technical documentation requirements for post-market monitoring plans for high-risk AI systems, guiding providers on documentation standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV is a section of a regulatory document detailing requirements for technical documentation in conformity assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV is an appendix that provides technical documentation requirements related to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV outlines the elements that must be included in the technical documentation for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV refers to a section that can be amended by the Commission to ensure compliance with the necessary requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c9bff2cb7a8bc7b162d1d512fa7d0a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1e54ed74d0a58b519fd1bbf3dc8f50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annexes VI and VII">
      <data key="d0">Annexes VI and VII</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annexes VI and VII are additional sections of the regulatory document that outline conformity assessment processes for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Provider">
      <data key="d0">The Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Provider is an entity responsible for conducting initial conformity assessments as per defined regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="quality management system">
      <data key="d0">quality management system</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex VII includes procedures that require the assessment of the quality management system in high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="harmonised standards">
      <data key="d0">harmonised standards</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 40 provides the legal basis for using harmonised standards in the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are technical specifications established by European standards organizations that support compliance with EU legislation.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427622</data>
    </node>
    <node id="common specifications">
      <data key="d0">common specifications</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7480046fc569a1b54a7d243d7d5a87b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 41 establishes common specifications that may be relied upon if harmonised standards are unavailable.&lt;SEP&gt;Common specifications are fallback regulations established by the Commission when harmonized standards do not adequately address certain requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Common specifications refer to technical requirements that harmonize standards for the development and operation of products or systems within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428439</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Union Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Institutions refer to the various administrative bodies of the European Union that may participate in AI regulatory sandboxes established by the European Data Protection Supervisor.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Institutions refer to various bodies, offices, and agencies within the European Union that are subject to oversight by the European Data Protection Supervisor regarding compliance with data protection regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions are political and administrative bodies that operate within the framework of the European Union, including agencies supporting law enforcement activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Union Institutions refers to bodies and organizations within the European Union that oversee and regulate various sectors including AI development and implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5dfd9a8d23f85f04843c95f20a9172df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bba75fb7db46076875feb4aca1bd671</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427529</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Fines">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Fines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fines are penalties imposed on organizations or individuals for violations of regulations, and they consider various factors, including the nature of the infringement and the size of the entity involved. These fines can be specifically levied against public authorities and bodies that do not comply with regulations established by Member States. In the context of AI practices, administrative fines may be applied, but there are circumstances under which these fines could potentially be waived, particularly within the framework of an AI sandbox environment. Additionally, these penalties are relevant to the actions of Union institutions and agencies under data protection laws, emphasizing the legal implications for non-compliance. Overall, administrative fines serve as a mechanism to ensure adherence to regulatory requirements, with their amounts varying based on the specifics of each infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb1781c5c0edcb30e49953ca1852eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8744b41e4885f10e1fd533f0c9de4aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dfd9a8d23f85f04843c95f20a9172df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9e7815086e5c37a3beb2705ee18d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc759fa1feac4c57c23af89232f9785</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Practices">
      <data key="d0">AI Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Practices encompass the various applications and methodologies involving artificial intelligence that must comply with regulations established within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Practices encompass various methodologies and technologies used in artificial intelligence that are subject to legal and regulatory scrutiny under EU law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5dfd9a8d23f85f04843c95f20a9172df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Institution">
      <data key="d0">Union Institution</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union institution refers to the various bodies, offices, and agencies within the European Union that are subject to data protection regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8744b41e4885f10e1fd533f0c9de4aa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annual Budget">
      <data key="d0">Annual Budget</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The annual budget of the Union institution refers to financial resources allocated for operations, including those that may incur fines for non-compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8744b41e4885f10e1fd533f0c9de4aa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rights of Defence">
      <data key="d0">Rights of Defence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Rights of defence are legal rights that ensure parties can respond to and contest proceedings related to infringements imposed by the European Data Protection Supervisor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8744b41e4885f10e1fd533f0c9de4aa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General Budget of the Union">
      <data key="d0">General Budget of the Union</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The general budget of the Union refers to the financial plan for the European Union, detailing income and expenditure allocations for various EU activities and operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17415cb7c434857a3d1c816705105aaa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Individuals and Undertakings">
      <data key="d0">Individuals and Undertakings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals and undertakings refer to natural persons and legal entities that can have interests in the protection of their personal data or business secrets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17415cb7c434857a3d1c816705105aaa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Proceedings">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Proceedings</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial Proceedings refer to the legal processes and court actions initiated to resolve disputes under the applicable laws and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17415cb7c434857a3d1c816705105aaa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Litigation">
      <data key="d0">Litigation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Litigation refers to the act of taking legal action in a court, particularly in the context of enforcing rights or defending against claims.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17415cb7c434857a3d1c816705105aaa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426509</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importer">
      <data key="d0">Importer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An importer is a party involved in bringing high-risk AI systems into a market and has obligations to ensure compliance under the Regulation if they alter the system or put their name on it.&lt;SEP&gt;An importer is a person or entity who brings AI systems into the Union market under the brand of a foreign entity.&lt;SEP&gt;An importer is an entity that brings high-risk AI systems into the market and is responsible for their compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Importers are entities that bring high-risk AI systems into the EU market and have obligations to ensure compliance with safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;An importer is responsible for bringing high-risk AI systems into the market, subject to obligations defined in the AI Value Chain Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427594</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third-Party">
      <data key="d0">Third-Party</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A third-party encompasses any external entity that interacts with high-risk AI systems and may incur obligations if they alter or label the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Modification">
      <data key="d0">Modification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Modification refers to changes made to high-risk AI systems that affect their classification and obligations under the relevant Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI System">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI system is a type of AI that has not been classified initially as high-risk but could become high-risk following modifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9ecbbe19a0b82c0cc27910d673dea46</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2017/745">
      <data key="d0">2017/745</data>
      <data key="d1">regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">2017/745 is a regulation establishing guidelines for modifications of high-risk AI systems classified as medical devices, ensuring compliance with applicable requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86466adf4635fac6d6e5e3aa66afb723</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Devices">
      <data key="d0">Medical Devices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical devices are tools or instruments used in the medical field for diagnosis, prevention, monitoring, treatment, or alleviation of diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical devices encompass a wide range of instruments, implants, and software intended for medical purposes, which may include AI technologies and require compliance with regulations like 2017/745.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical devices encompass products used for healthcare purposes, which require strict regulatory compliance to ensure safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86466adf4635fac6d6e5e3aa66afb723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13251cb96e29c95cab559ac75d5b1f1f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/84/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Metrology Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Metrology Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Metrology Authorities are organizations responsible for ensuring the measurement standards and benchmarks are established for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Benchmarking Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Benchmarking Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Benchmarking Authorities help develop methodologies to measure and verify the performance metrics of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical and Organizational Measures">
      <data key="d0">Technical and Organizational Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical and Organizational Measures are strategies and protocols that enhance the resilience of high-risk AI systems against errors, faults, or unauthorized alterations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Feedback Loops">
      <data key="d0">Feedback Loops</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Feedback Loops refer to the cyclical process where outputs of AI systems influence their future inputs, which can pose risks if biased.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops refer to the cycles in which the output of an AI system influences its future operations, which if biased, could lead to further biases being introduced.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops refer to the cycles in which outputs from AI systems influence future inputs, potentially perpetuating biases and discrimination.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops refer to the processes where outputs from AI systems influence the inputs for future operations, which can lead to data biases over time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b1b6d000ef2c2e744936b8e5264e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Poisoning">
      <data key="d0">Data Poisoning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Poisoning is a form of attack where malicious data is introduced to compromise the training data of AI systems, impacting their performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Data poisoning is a type of attack where malicious data is introduced into the training dataset of an AI system to corrupt its learning process.&lt;SEP&gt;Data poisoning is a form of attack where the training data for an AI system is deliberately compromised, affecting the system's performance and integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Poisoning">
      <data key="d0">Model Poisoning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model Poisoning involves manipulating the pre-trained components of AI systems to lead them to make incorrect decisions or outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Model poisoning describes an attack targeting the model components of AI systems, affecting their performance and predictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Examples">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Examples</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Adversarial Examples are specifically crafted inputs designed to deceive AI models into making errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial examples are inputs crafted to deceive AI models, causing them to make incorrect predictions or decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Solutions">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Solutions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity Solutions are technical measures that protect high-risk AI systems from unauthorized access and manipulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f59c6f62bd0ab2d5521810dcbca8373d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unauthorized Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Unauthorized Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Unauthorized third parties are entities or individuals who may attempt to exploit vulnerabilities in AI systems to alter their use, outputs, or performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Measures">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity measures are protocols and technologies implemented to protect systems and data from cyber threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity measures for high-risk AI systems include various technical solutions designed to protect against unauthorized access and manipulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity measures involve systems designed to protect personal data and prevent unauthorized access through biometric authentication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b5f42708d566a2269e407d6a5b3e2847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System Vulnerabilities">
      <data key="d0">AI System Vulnerabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI system vulnerabilities encompass weaknesses that can be exploited by attackers, potentially compromising the system's integrity and functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality Attacks">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality Attacks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality attacks aim to violate the privacy of data processed by AI systems, potentially exposing sensitive information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3615b104e6e36e2c3fca2765ce18eace</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Components">
      <data key="d0">AI Components</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI components are the building blocks of artificial intelligence systems that include algorithms, data structures, and modules essential for AI functionality, which can be made available under open-source licenses.&lt;SEP&gt;AI components refer to software and data, including models and tools that form an AI system and can be freely available or monetized.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f0180b5212a055a4e3ca493be8f830</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open Repositories">
      <data key="d0">Open Repositories</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Open repositories are platforms where free and open-source AI components are developed and shared without charge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2f0180b5212a055a4e3ca493be8f830</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/103/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426529</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Monetization">
      <data key="d0">Monetization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Monetization refers to the process of providing AI components against a price or through additional services, which is regulated under specific guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2f0180b5212a055a4e3ca493be8f830</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/103/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426529</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Support">
      <data key="d0">Technical Support</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical support involves providing assistance and services related to AI components, which can lead to monetization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2f0180b5212a055a4e3ca493be8f830</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/103/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426529</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Microenterprises">
      <data key="d0">Microenterprises</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Microenterprises are small businesses that may engage in transactions exempt from the monetization constraints imposed by the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Microenterprises refer to small businesses defined by the Recommendation 2003/361/EC, which may comply with a simplified quality management system.&lt;SEP&gt;Microenterprises are small-scale operators that may face significant costs associated with establishing a quality management system but are granted simplified requirements to ease their burden.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6b3a7a24bfd18cc84baf6173985e105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3917f629d239e59c1197ea2404615c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f0180b5212a055a4e3ca493be8f830</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/103/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/146/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/63/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Impact Capabilities">
      <data key="d0">High-Impact Capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Impact Capabilities are exceptional functions of AI models that match or exceed performance metrics of the most advanced systems, indicating potential risks.&lt;SEP&gt;High-impact capabilities refer to the abilities of AI models that significantly affect various sectors and can lead to systemic risks if mismanaged.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e116bc92c8c7cf688c26ea188fd0b2fe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open-Source Model">
      <data key="d0">Open-Source Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Open-Source Model describes a collaborative approach to software development where the source code is made publicly available for use and modification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d35688b92a2e68fb5231305abc8e04b7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426552</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI systems and models">
      <data key="d0">AI systems and models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems and models are technologies developed for various purposes, including scientific research and development, but are subject to specific regulations when placed on the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ab6fc5c923f500a88ff985caeb05f2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Research">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Research</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Scientific research encompasses systematic investigation and experimentation aimed at acquiring knowledge and understanding about various phenomena, particularly in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Scientific research is a systematic enterprise that builds and organizes knowledge in the form of testable explanations and predictions about the universe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ab6fc5c923f500a88ff985caeb05f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f000e09b1fe2828e775be2862b588e09</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Research and Development Activity">
      <data key="d0">Research and Development Activity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Research and development activity involves the innovative processes of creating, testing, and implementing new technologies or solutions associated with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ab6fc5c923f500a88ff985caeb05f2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Sandboxes">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Sandboxes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory Sandboxes refer to frameworks that allow entities to test innovations in a controlled environment, ensuring compliance with legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulatory sandboxes are frameworks that allow for the testing of innovations under a regulator's supervision to promote innovation while ensuring safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab6fc5c923f500a88ff985caeb05f2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427354</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethical Standards">
      <data key="d0">Ethical Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethical standards refer to the moral principles guiding the conduct of research and development activities, particularly in relation to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethical standards refer to the principles that guide the conduct of scientific research to ensure integrity and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ab6fc5c923f500a88ff985caeb05f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f000e09b1fe2828e775be2862b588e09</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Development Activity">
      <data key="d0">Development Activity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Development activity involves efforts and processes aimed at improving scientific research in accordance with ethical and professional standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f000e09b1fe2828e775be2862b588e09</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Professional Standards">
      <data key="d0">Professional Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Professional standards encompass the qualifications and benchmarks that ensure quality and reliability in scientific research practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f000e09b1fe2828e775be2862b588e09</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civil Society Organizations">
      <data key="d0">Civil Society Organizations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil Society Organizations represent the interests of individuals or groups and may participate in assessments related to the impact of AI systems on rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil society organizations are non-governmental organizations that advocate for various societal issues, contributing to policy development and stakeholder engagement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Banking Entities">
      <data key="d0">Banking Entities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Banking entities are institutions that provide financial services and are subject to impact assessments when deploying high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Insurance Entities">
      <data key="d0">Insurance Entities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Insurance entities are companies that provide coverage or protection against financial loss and are also governed by regulations related to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Interest Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Public Interest Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public interest tasks refer to the responsibilities of entities that involve serving the community in areas like education, healthcare, and social services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-961024ac487985297e9f077751d6d85d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Artificial Intelligence Office">
      <data key="d0">European Artificial Intelligence Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Artificial Intelligence Office (AI Office) is an organization focused on developing standards and guidelines for artificial intelligence compliance and risk assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Office (AI Office) is responsible for overseeing compliance and impact assessments related to high-risk AI systems in Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Office is established to oversee and promote the responsible use of artificial intelligence across Europe, ensuring compliance with regulations and fostering innovation in the sector.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8673fa897637be6cc00c6fd7cfbcafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7aa55ff3193c0e45818701bd0bcd7e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="governance arrangements">
      <data key="d0">governance arrangements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Governance arrangements refer to the policies and procedures established to oversee the use and management of high-risk AI systems, including human oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="civil society organisations">
      <data key="d0">civil society organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil society organizations play a critical role in representing the interests and rights of groups likely to be affected by high-risk AI systems, advocating for accountability and transparency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="questionnaire">
      <data key="d0">questionnaire</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A questionnaire is a tool developed to facilitate compliance assessments and reduce administrative burdens associated with the deployment of artificial intelligence technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd7aa55ff3193c0e45818701bd0bcd7e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="impact assessment">
      <data key="d0">impact assessment</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-10e179a89fe393b383555ee1c281106f</data>
      <data key="d2">The European AI Office develops guidelines and templates for impact assessments related to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="impact assessments">
      <data key="d0">impact assessments</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd7aa55ff3193c0e45818701bd0bcd7e</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Artificial Intelligence Office is involved in conducting impact assessments related to artificial intelligence and designing compliance measures.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subsidiaries">
      <data key="d0">Subsidiaries</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Subsidiaries are entities controlled by a parent organization, which can perform tasks related to conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-647c11490314deffe2ceff0b84c7700c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/33/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426562</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subcontractors">
      <data key="d0">Subcontractors</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Subcontractors are third-party entities engaged by notified bodies to perform specific tasks related to conformity assessments under the regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-647c11490314deffe2ceff0b84c7700c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/33/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426562</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Full Responsibility">
      <data key="d0">Full Responsibility</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Full Responsibility is the obligation of notified bodies to ensure and take accountability for tasks performed by subcontractors or subsidiaries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-647c11490314deffe2ceff0b84c7700c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/33/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426562</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SMEs (Small and Medium Enterprises)">
      <data key="d0">SMEs (Small and Medium Enterprises)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">SMEs are small and medium-sized enterprises that may apply for participation in AI regulatory sandboxes free of charge to foster innovation and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Obligations are requirements that AI providers must meet to ensure that their products comply with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment obligations refer to the requirements that AI providers must meet to ensure their products comply with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Partners and Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Partners and Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Partners and third parties may include various entities such as deployers and other stakeholders that can collaborate with AI system providers in the sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criteria for Participation">
      <data key="d0">Criteria for Participation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Criteria for participation in AI regulatory sandboxes include eligibility requirements that ensure fair access to providers of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Application Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Application Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Application procedures define the steps and requirements for AI providers to engage with AI regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Monitoring and Supervision">
      <data key="d0">Monitoring and Supervision</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Monitoring and supervision encompass the practices by which the functioning of AI regulatory sandboxes is overseen to ensure compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Learning Outcomes">
      <data key="d0">Learning Outcomes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Learning Outcomes are the educational results that arise from experiences within AI regulatory sandboxes, helping participants understand compliance and performance metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;Learning outcomes refer to the results and insights gained from the experiences in AI regulatory sandboxes that help providers enhance their systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0055dea9f51c003c924a93b2d83c057c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426574</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System Testing">
      <data key="d0">AI System Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">AI System Testing refers to the procedures and assessments conducted within AI regulatory sandboxes to evaluate AI systems' performance and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Centres of Excellence">
      <data key="d0">Centres of Excellence</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Centres of Excellence are organizations that provide specialized knowledge and research in AI, helping stakeholders in regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="participants">
      <data key="d0">participants</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Participants refer to individuals or groups involved in the safeguarding measures aimed at protecting fundamental rights, health, and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0b972a179b165ba7115316ba8d0d987</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national competent authorities">
      <data key="d0">national competent authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National competent authorities are governmental bodies responsible for the application of regulations and surveillance in their jurisdictions, particularly related to AI.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are governmental bodies that have the responsibility to ensure compliance with regulations regarding fundamental rights and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The national competent authorities oversee the registered places of business and ensure compliance with health, safety, and rights related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0b972a179b165ba7115316ba8d0d987&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="health and safety">
      <data key="d0">health and safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and safety refer to regulations and practices aimed at ensuring the well-being of individuals and protecting them from harm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0b972a179b165ba7115316ba8d0d987</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social Scoring">
      <data key="d0">Social Scoring</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Social Scoring is a practice where individuals or groups are evaluated based on their behaviors and characteristics, potentially leading to detrimental and unfair treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5eb0d79706d66f4b2474faeded28100a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Actors">
      <data key="d0">Public Actors</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Actors include government or state entities that may use AI Systems to score Natural Persons and make decisions affecting social context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5eb0d79706d66f4b2474faeded28100a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Private Actors">
      <data key="d0">Private Actors</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Private Actors consist of non-governmental organizations or companies that utilize AI Systems for social scoring purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5eb0d79706d66f4b2474faeded28100a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exclusion of Certain Groups">
      <data key="d0">Exclusion of Certain Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Exclusion of Certain Groups refers to the adverse effects that social scoring by AI Systems may have on specific demographic or social groups.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5eb0d79706d66f4b2474faeded28100a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discriminatory Outcomes">
      <data key="d0">Discriminatory Outcomes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discriminatory Outcomes are the negative consequences faced by individuals due to biased evaluations and classifications carried out by AI Systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Discriminatory outcomes are the adverse effects or biases that may arise when AI systems make incorrect assessments regarding individuals based on their data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0d79706d66f4b2474faeded28100a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content Generation Risks">
      <data key="d0">Content Generation Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Content Generation Risks refer to potential dangers associated with AI systems producing misleading content or impersonating individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7c3bb945919e1b0c6e146fabaaeff87b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="persons with disabilities">
      <data key="d0">persons with disabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Persons with disabilities refers to individuals who have physical or mental impairments that may hinder their full participation in society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-894310fd4a8abe83d92e12f2ddd1a907</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notifications">
      <data key="d0">notifications</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Notifications refer to messages or alerts that provide information, which should be made accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-894310fd4a8abe83d92e12f2ddd1a907</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accessible Formats">
      <data key="d0">Accessible Formats</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessible Formats refer to various ways of presenting information that can be easily perceived by individuals with disabilities, ensuring they receive notifications and information without barriers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-894310fd4a8abe83d92e12f2ddd1a907</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notifications">
      <data key="d0">Notifications</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Notifications are alerts or messages intended to convey important information, which should be adapted for accessibility for various audiences, including those with disabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-894310fd4a8abe83d92e12f2ddd1a907</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/132/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independence">
      <data key="d0">Independence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Independence refers to the principle that notified bodies must operate without influence from parties involved in the development or provision of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Independence signifies the ability of the National Competent Authorities to operate without external influence, maintaining impartiality in their decisions and actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea411b75c6825aab3a6b8a4983e34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/154/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objectivity">
      <data key="d0">Objectivity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Objectivity is a principle that mandates the National Competent Authorities to engage in actions based on facts and impartiality, avoiding bias.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea411b75c6825aab3a6b8a4983e34939</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/154/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality Rules">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality Rules provide guidelines to the members of National Competent Authorities regarding the handling of sensitive information while fulfilling their duties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea411b75c6825aab3a6b8a4983e34939</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/154/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Members of National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Members of National Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea411b75c6825aab3a6b8a4983e34939</data>
      <data key="d2">Members of the National Competent Authorities are required to adhere to Confidentiality Rules, safeguarding sensitive information from unauthorized disclosure.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/154/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real-time remote biometric identification systems">
      <data key="d0">real-time remote biometric identification systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technologies used by law enforcement for identifying individuals through biometric data under regulated circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technologies used for confirming the identity of individuals in public spaces, particularly for law enforcement purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technologies used in public spaces for law enforcement, monitored by the Commission through annual reports.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7127c7bb3049241e70ac955f8f0024b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4e750c132cad9fbfb3f5174e1949ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law enforcement authority">
      <data key="d0">law enforcement authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Law enforcement authorities are entities responsible for maintaining public order and safety, including the authorization and oversight of biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement authorities are public entities responsible for preventing, investigating, and prosecuting criminal offenses and ensuring public security.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement authority comprises public bodies responsible for preventing, investigating, and prosecuting criminal offenses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4e750c132cad9fbfb3f5174e1949ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/34/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reference database of persons">
      <data key="d0">reference database of persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The reference database of persons contains information necessary for identifying individuals within the scope defined by law enforcement authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4e750c132cad9fbfb3f5174e1949ec1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/34/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="publicly accessible spaces">
      <data key="d0">publicly accessible spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly accessible spaces refer to locations where individuals can be present freely, such as streets or parks, where biometric identification systems may be deployed for security purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4e750c132cad9fbfb3f5174e1949ec1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/34/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="safeguards and conditions">
      <data key="d0">safeguards and conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safeguards and conditions are measures established within regulatory frameworks to protect individual rights and ensure the responsible use of biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4e750c132cad9fbfb3f5174e1949ec1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/34/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="deployer">
      <data key="d0">deployer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A deployer is an entity using an AI system under its authority, excluding personal non-professional use.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployer refers to an individual or entity that has the authority to use or implement the information stored in the EU database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d447a0dff9a51bc6e0b8b9c92046aaae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427966</data>
    </node>
    <node id="authorised representative">
      <data key="d0">authorised representative</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An authorised representative is an entity in the Union that acts on behalf of a provider to fulfill regulatory obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;The authorised representative acts on behalf of providers and has the authority to terminate mandates for non-compliance with the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The authorised representative is an individual appointed to act on behalf of the provider for compliance-related matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-442777921e9a3bd01b79336245710651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="importer">
      <data key="d0">importer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An importer is an entity in the Union that brings an AI system from a third country to the market under the original provider's name.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="distributor">
      <data key="d0">distributor</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A distributor is an entity in the supply chain that makes an AI system available for market distribution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="operator">
      <data key="d0">operator</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An operator encompasses various roles including provider, manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer, or distributor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk">
      <data key="d0">Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk refers to the combination of the probability of an occurrence of harm and the severity of that harm, which is a critical consideration in the context of AI systems and their deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Placing on the Market">
      <data key="d0">Placing on the Market</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Placing on the market involves the first making available of an AI system or general-purpose AI model in the Union market, an essential step for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Placing on the market refers to the initial act of making an AI system available to consumers for commercial sale.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Making Available on the Market">
      <data key="d0">Making Available on the Market</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Making available on the market means providing access to an AI system or model for distribution or use in the Union, whether for free or in exchange for payment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Putting into Service">
      <data key="d0">Putting into Service</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Putting into service involves the supply of an AI system, marking its operational commencement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operator">
      <data key="d0">Operator</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An Operator is an individual or entity responsible for making AI systems available on the market and must take corrective actions when required.&lt;SEP&gt;An operator encompasses various roles including provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorized representative, importer, or distributor, involved in managing AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An Operator refers to an organization or individual that operates within a regulatory framework and can be subject to administrative fines for infringements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a9e7815086e5c37a3beb2705ee18d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Person">
      <data key="d0">Natural Person</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural person refers to an individual human being as opposed to a legal entity or organization.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural person refers to an individual human being who can act in a legal capacity, such as signing contracts or accepting responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Person refers to a human being as an individual, emphasizing the rights and protections afforded to them under law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69800a0e24a3f7afd28e97d0e1079c4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79847bb42790114b4e3db575c6fe603a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427754</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Person">
      <data key="d0">Legal Person</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A legal person includes organizations or entities that have legal rights and responsibilities, distinct from natural persons.&lt;SEP&gt;A legal person refers to an entity such as a corporation or organization that has legal rights and obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69800a0e24a3f7afd28e97d0e1079c4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/13/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Component">
      <data key="d0">Safety Component</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A safety component is an integral part of an AI system ensuring compliance with health and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The safety component in an AI system plays a critical role in ensuring the health and safety of users or property by fulfilling safety functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recall of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Recall of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recall of an AI system refers to actions taken to return a product to the provider due to safety concerns or other issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63b7f62ee5f6ce97705b963caea85497</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="intended purpose">
      <data key="d0">intended purpose</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The intended purpose refers to the specific function or goal for which an AI system is designed and provided by its provider.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426632</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reasonably foreseeable misuse">
      <data key="d0">reasonably foreseeable misuse</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Reasonably foreseeable misuse is the potential inappropriate use of an AI system that can occur due to human behavior or interaction, despite not aligning with the intended purpose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426632</data>
    </node>
    <node id="safety component">
      <data key="d0">safety component</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A safety component is essential part of an AI system that ensures safety and health are maintained, its failure could endanger users and property.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426632</data>
    </node>
    <node id="recall of an AI system">
      <data key="d0">recall of an AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The recall of an AI system involves measures taken to return the system to the provider or disable its usage for safety reasons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426632</data>
    </node>
    <node id="withdrawal of an AI system">
      <data key="d0">withdrawal of an AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Withdrawal refers to actions taken to prevent an AI system from being available in the market for reasons, often related to safety or compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426632</data>
    </node>
    <node id="performance of an AI system">
      <data key="d0">performance of an AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The performance of an AI system refers to its effectiveness in achieving the intended purpose as outlined by the provider.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426632</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national authority">
      <data key="d0">national authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A national authority is a government body responsible for establishing regulations and overseeing conformity assessment bodies in relation to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426632</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Authority">
      <data key="d0">National Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The National Authority oversees financial supervision of institutions and regulates the market presence of AI systems in relation to financial services.&lt;SEP&gt;The national authority is responsible for establishing procedures for assessment and monitoring of conformity assessment bodies related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Withdrawal of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Withdrawal of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Withdrawal of an AI system refers to measures that prevent an AI system in the supply chain from being made available on the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Performance of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance of an AI system indicates its ability to achieve its intended purpose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Substantial Modification">
      <data key="d0">Substantial Modification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Substantial Modification refers to significant changes in design or purpose applied to high-risk AI systems within the scope of the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Substantial modification refers to a significant change to an AI system affecting its compliance status or intended purpose after market entry.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Standard">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A harmonised standard defines specific technical requirements that products, including AI systems, must meet to ensure conformity with EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standard provides technical specifications to comply with requirements set under EU regulations regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised Standards are technical specifications published to ensure that AI model providers meet the necessary requirements for compliance in the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;A harmonised standard is a technical specification established by a European standardisation organisation to ensure compliance with legislation across EU Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ae5c70e1b98b5f33eb047bb55022e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-408ee65c3eab1e86c1c4207deaf4f216</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/117/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428439</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Specification">
      <data key="d0">Common Specification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Common specification is a set of technical specifications established under EU regulations for AI systems compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Common specifications are detailed technical requirements established for products in compliance with the overarching regulations for AI systems within the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The Common Specification is a framework or set of criteria that can be amended and is overseen by regulatory bodies like the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f20adf0cd08ecffde7f6a9e3860025d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b84ed9e420c0ae0245bb808d08db0f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428445</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 establishes a comprehensive legal framework for the European standardization system, as defined by the European Parliament. It outlines the procedures and conditions for drafting common specifications and harmonized standards, which are crucial for various products, including artificial intelligence systems, within the European Union. This regulation serves to ensure compliance with fundamental rights and obligations, as well as to establish conformity with safety standards across product markets.

The regulation delineates a governance structure and requires stakeholder engagement in the European standardization process. By fostering a collaborative environment, it aims to create a common market for standardized products and services, thereby facilitating trade and enhancing consumer protection among EU member states. Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 plays a pivotal role in impacting the compliance landscape by ensuring that products meet established standards, contributing to a cohesive and safe market environment, especially in relation to technical specifications and compliance measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85726b1098cb96ad81df40234ad5da52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da95eda13126b9bd230dc02d90951e42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ae5c70e1b98b5f33eb047bb55022e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214363bac320d3b288355fb10d6c0537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f32100de89356334a47cd2317dde09df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f3473e38ccd9ad84662b373166a5c2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/166/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428504</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation Data">
      <data key="d0">Validation Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Validation data is used to evaluate and tune the performance of an AI system to avoid underfitting or overfitting.&lt;SEP&gt;Validation data refers to datasets used to evaluate the performance of an AI system after it has been trained, ensuring its effectiveness and reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-92041f4b18683dbe895c82ad1d995a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Data">
      <data key="d0">Testing Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing data is utilized for independent evaluation of an AI system to confirm its expected performance prior to market deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Verification">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric verification is a process for confirming the identity of individuals by comparing their biometric data with previously provided information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sensitive Operational Data">
      <data key="d0">Sensitive Operational Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sensitive operational data refers to information pertinent to the prevention and prosecution of crimes, the disclosure of which could affect legal proceedings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Emotion Recognition System">
      <data key="d0">Emotion Recognition System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An emotion recognition system is an AI system designed to identify or infer emotions of individuals using their biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;The Emotion Recognition System is an AI system designed to identify or infer emotions and intentions of individuals based on their biometric data, extending to various emotions such as happiness, sadness, and more.&lt;SEP&gt;An emotion recognition system is an AI technology designed to detect and analyze human emotions based on various inputs such as facial expressions, voice tone, or physiological signals.&lt;SEP&gt;An emotion recognition system uses AI to analyze and interpret the emotional state of individuals based on various inputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35f73469c0e0803dabff693c3a8808fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Categorisation System">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Categorisation System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A biometric categorisation system is an AI system that assigns individuals to categories based on their biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;A biometric categorisation system utilizes biological characteristics, such as fingerprints or iris scans, to categorize and identify individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;A biometric categorization system utilizes AI to analyze biological data for the purpose of categorizing individuals based on unique physical traits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation Data Set">
      <data key="d0">Validation Data Set</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A validation data set is a portion of the training data set used to provide an evaluation of the AI system's performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Special Categories of Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Special Categories of Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Special Categories of Personal Data refer to sensitive information such as health, race, and biometrics which require stricter processing guidelines under EU laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data are those defined by European regulations that require additional protections, such as sensitive information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9acb869e8831be994323dab5f07993e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de448579f0f397ec535d8acdb68580bc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric verification">
      <data key="d0">biometric verification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric verification involves the automated process of confirming identity by comparing biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="special categories of personal data">
      <data key="d0">special categories of personal data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Special categories of personal data include sensitive information as defined under Article 9(1) and other related regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data refer to sensitive information that requires higher protection under regulations, typically encompassing data related to health, racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, and more.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc185ecb84a12901d24ae59e4dd5dfe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427784</data>
    </node>
    <node id="sensitive operational data">
      <data key="d0">sensitive operational data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sensitive operational data pertains to information related to preventing or investigating criminal activities, the disclosure of which could hinder criminal proceedings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="emotion recognition system">
      <data key="d0">emotion recognition system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An emotion recognition system uses biometric data to identify or infer the emotions of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The emotion recognition system is an AI system that identifies or infers emotions or intentions of natural persons based on biometric data, but excludes physical states or mere expressions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35f73469c0e0803dabff693c3a8808fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/18/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric categorisation system">
      <data key="d0">biometric categorisation system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A biometric categorisation system classifies individuals into specific categories based on their biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real-time remote biometric identification system">
      <data key="d0">real-time remote biometric identification system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A real-time remote biometric identification system allows for instant or near-instant identification of individuals based on biometric data captured without significant delays.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time systems identify individuals instantly by capturing and comparing biometric data without significant delay.&lt;SEP&gt;A real-time remote biometric identification system is a technology used for law enforcement purposes to identify individuals in publicly accessible spaces using biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;The real-time remote biometric identification system is a technological system used for identifying individuals in public spaces for law enforcement purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b23a5bf3ea6e9c99542abdf17cfaa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fbdf24f8b746547b54a3e43daaf33</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="post remote biometric identification system">
      <data key="d0">post remote biometric identification system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A post remote biometric identification system refers to any remote biometric identification system that does not operate in real-time, involving delays.&lt;SEP&gt;This system refers to remote biometric identification that does not occur in real-time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="publicly accessible space">
      <data key="d0">publicly accessible space</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly accessible space includes any physical location that can be accessed by individuals, regardless of entry conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are locations, both public and private, accessible to numerous persons without strict access conditions, regardless of capacity restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a3264abf04a576ae16d704acaaf3687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law enforcement">
      <data key="d0">law enforcement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Law enforcement encompasses a range of activities conducted by authorized authorities aimed at preventing, investigating, detecting, and prosecuting criminal offenses, thereby ensuring public security and compliance with the law. It refers to the system of agencies and officials responsible for upholding laws, maintaining public order, and safeguarding the community. This includes the roles played by various law enforcement agencies and officers who work collaboratively to enforce laws and prevent crime. Additionally, law enforcement may utilize advanced technologies, such as biometric identification systems, to enhance its effectiveness in ensuring safety and security within society. Overall, law enforcement is fundamental in maintaining public order and addressing criminal activities through a structured and organized approach.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7f6078e68943998b91775a85fbac31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-079fbdf24f8b746547b54a3e43daaf33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5345c3cccd7883e192f55328579d86d4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="serious incident">
      <data key="d0">serious incident</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A serious incident is defined as an incident involving an AI system that leads to serious harm or disruption, including death, health issues, or property harm.&lt;SEP&gt;A serious incident refers to any malfunctioning of an AI system that results in harmful consequences, whether direct or indirect, potentially impacting public safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission Decision of 24 January 2024">
      <data key="d0">Commission Decision of 24 January 2024</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission Decision of 24 January 2024 outlines guidelines for the governance and supervision of AI systems implemented by the AI Office.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission Decision of 24 January 2024 outlines the governance framework for AI systems and the role of the AI Office in monitoring AI activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric identification system">
      <data key="d0">biometric identification system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A biometric identification system uses biometric data to recognize individuals, typically in law enforcement and security applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94ebfb1fa7d304078345c66a61c6ecc1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="critical infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">critical infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Critical infrastructure entails essential systems and assets that are fundamental to the functioning of society and economy.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure refers to assets and systems essential for the functioning of a society and economy, whose disruption can lead to significant consequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure refers to essential systems and assets whose failure would impact national security, public health, or safety, as defined in the directive.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure refers to essential systems and assets vital to national security, economic security, public health, or safety, whose disruption may have serious consequences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427083</data>
    </node>
    <node id="non-personal data">
      <data key="d0">non-personal data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-personal data is defined as data that does not relate to an identified or identifiable individual.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-personal data refers to any information that does not relate to an identifiable person, often used in compliance contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="profiling">
      <data key="d0">profiling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Profiling involves the automated processing of personal data to evaluate certain personal aspects regarding an individual, often for decision-making purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real-world testing plan">
      <data key="d0">real-world testing plan</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A real-world testing plan is a document detailing how an AI system will be tested in actual conditions, including objectives and methodology.&lt;SEP&gt;A real-world testing plan outlines methodologies and objectives for testing AI systems in conditions that reflect their actual deployment environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="sandbox plan">
      <data key="d0">sandbox plan</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A sandbox plan is a document that describes an agreement between a provider and a competent authority outlining objectives and conditions for testing within a regulatory sandbox.&lt;SEP&gt;The sandbox plan is an agreement between a provider and competent authority outlining conditions for testing within a regulatory sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI regulatory sandbox">
      <data key="d0">AI regulatory sandbox</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI regulatory sandbox is a controlled environment set up by authorities to enable providers to test AI systems under regulatory oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI regulatory sandbox is a framework set by regulatory authorities that allows for the controlled testing and development of AI systems under supervision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-df3020e6887a24702cea8a3373082e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="subject">
      <data key="d0">subject</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Subject refers to a natural person who participates in testing or provides data for real-world testing of systems and products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="informed consent">
      <data key="d0">informed consent</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Informed consent is the process by which a subject voluntarily agrees to participate in testing or provide data, understanding the risks involved.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="serious harm">
      <data key="d0">serious harm</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious harm refers to significant damage to a person's health or major disruptions to critical infrastructure management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="obligations">
      <data key="d0">obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations refer to the duties or responsibilities mandated by legal frameworks, such as Union law, to protect rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="profiler">
      <data key="d0">profiler</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Profiling involves analyzing data to create data models that predict behaviors or characteristics of individuals based on specific criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Literacy">
      <data key="d0">AI Literacy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Literacy encompasses the understanding of AI systems, their benefits, risks, and ethical implications for users and society.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Literacy is a concept aimed at equipping providers, deployers, and affected persons with the necessary knowledge to make informed decisions regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Literacy pertains to the understanding and knowledge regarding the development, operation, and usage of artificial intelligence technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;AI literacy encompasses the skills, knowledge, and understanding necessary for responsible AI deployment and awareness of its risks and benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;AI literacy refers to the understanding and proficiency required to effectively operate and utilize AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b5df3c87d284ff92767412c5cae8b463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553e3df123166674b26c5dc07f2a83af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafe6ac227379dad776c22a5abc16ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/4/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427725</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Fake">
      <data key="d0">Deep Fake</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A deep fake refers to content (image, audio, video) that has been artificially manipulated to misrepresent reality, utilizing advanced AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep fake refers to manipulated digital content that imitates authentic persons, objects, or events, raising ethical and legal concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subjects">
      <data key="d0">Subjects</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Subjects are natural persons who participate in testing AI systems in real-world conditions, requiring informed consent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Widespread Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Widespread Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Widespread infringement describes actions that harm collective interests across multiple Member States in violation of Union law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Supervision">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Supervision</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory supervision refers to oversight mechanisms ensuring that AI systems comply with established legal and ethical standards during testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing in Real-World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Testing in Real-World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing in real-world conditions is the process of evaluating AI systems in actual environments to gather reliable data and assess performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Informed Consent">
      <data key="d0">Informed Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Informed Consent is a legal and ethical principle that ensures participants in the testing of AI systems, or any research, are fully aware of and agree to the testing processes, potential data usage, and all associated risks. It involves a systematic process where subjects voluntarily consent to participate, having received comprehensive information regarding the implications, risks, and conditions of the study. This process is crucial as it empowers participants by ensuring they have sufficient understanding to make informed decisions about their involvement in research or testing activities. In essence, Informed Consent safeguards the rights of participants by promoting transparency and voluntary participation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebb00fdd14767c86b1a8c766db05a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-295d382452d700dcc18edd615661d802</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/61/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428319</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Union Member States">
      <data key="d0">European Union Member States</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">European Union Member States are countries that adhere to Union law and participate in collective legal and regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Critical Infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">Critical Infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Critical Infrastructure encompasses essential systems and structures that are vital for the functioning of society and the economy.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure encompasses essential systems and assets that are vital for the functioning of a society, such as transportation, energy, and communication networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure refers to assets or systems essential for the functioning of society, which can be affected by AI and other technological advancements.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure includes essential systems and services that are vital for a community's functioning, which can be compromised by AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure refers to the essential systems and assets that are vital for the functioning of a society and economy, whose failure can have severe consequences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff9241c3a9f5f8fc78557cf5705c8c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c51b7bfc502a0e1b7fc0c076f574e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afaea4dcd95d49cc4d21cf9078216b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 57 and 60">
      <data key="d0">Article 57 and 60</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 57 and 60 of the regulation outline specific legal conditions and requirements related to the deployment and testing of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d973114c994e2a695be9f8562505452d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2022/2557">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2022/2557</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2022/2557 is a comprehensive legislative framework established by the European Union that addresses the safeguarding of critical infrastructure while enhancing the resilience of critical entities within the EU. It outlines laws pertinent to public safety and law enforcement and focuses on the regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies, defining essential terms and requirements for AI models. The directive emphasizes the protection of individual interests alongside critical infrastructure, highlighting the role of these entities in ensuring safety and security. Overall, Directive (EU) 2022/2557 serves as a vital instrument to ensure the safety and robustness of AI systems operating within critical infrastructures across the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afaea4dcd95d49cc4d21cf9078216b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2bf8c519aff48aa30866bbefc0dc688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-impact capabilities">
      <data key="d0">high-impact capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-impact capabilities denote advanced functions of AI models that may significantly influence markets and social dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;High-impact capabilities refer to advanced functionalities of AI models that can significantly influence various sectors and bring about profound changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="deep fake">
      <data key="d0">deep fake</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep fake refers to AI-generated or manipulated content-such as images, audio, or video-that imitates real persons or events, potentially deceiving viewers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="widespread infringement">
      <data key="d0">widespread infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Widespread infringement denotes actions or omissions against Union law that violate individual rights and have broader impacts across member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-generated Content">
      <data key="d0">AI-generated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-generated content encompasses various forms of media created or altered by artificial intelligence technologies, such as deep fakes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="individual interests">
      <data key="d0">individual interests</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Individual interests refer to the rights and protections afforded to persons, especially in the context of new technologies and their risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2395647569471a039f561bf725dfa39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI system">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI system is an AI framework that utilizes general-purpose AI models for diverse applications.&lt;SEP&gt;A general-purpose AI system is an artificial intelligence system designed to perform a variety of tasks and can integrate into other AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f80477304c8df58e48c2b09ede4a7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="downstream provider">
      <data key="d0">downstream provider</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A downstream provider integrates AI models into systems, facilitating their use in application contexts and ensuring they meet operational demands.&lt;SEP&gt;A downstream provider refers to an entity that offers an AI system, integrating AI models into their services, which may come from various sources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f80477304c8df58e48c2b09ede4a7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 97">
      <data key="d0">Recital 97</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 97 is part of the legislative text that provides context and rationale for the regulations surrounding general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 98">
      <data key="d0">Recital 98</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 98 is another segment in the Directive, discussing implications and responsibilities of AI developers and users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 99">
      <data key="d0">Recital 99</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 99 outlines considerations for the effects of AI technologies on society and the economy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 110">
      <data key="d0">Recital 110</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 110 emphasizes the significance of managing high-impact capabilities and systemic risks in AI applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6812c0a4d288d4b9c143a284b707d29</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="floating-point operation">
      <data key="d0">floating-point operation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A floating-point operation is a mathematical operation involving numbers that are typically represented in computer systems with fixed precision and scale.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f80477304c8df58e48c2b09ede4a7e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI model">
      <data key="d0">AI model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI model is a mathematical framework or algorithm used to process information and generate predictions or behaviors based on input data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f80477304c8df58e48c2b09ede4a7e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real numbers">
      <data key="d0">real numbers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real numbers encompass all the rational and irrational numbers, which include integers, fractions, and decimal numbers used in computing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f80477304c8df58e48c2b09ede4a7e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="contractual relations">
      <data key="d0">contractual relations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Contractual relations refer to the agreements and obligations between entities, especially regarding the provision and use of services or products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f80477304c8df58e48c2b09ede4a7e2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Harmonization Legislation">
      <data key="d0">Union Harmonization Legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union harmonization legislation is a framework of regulations that standardizes the conformity assessment of products across the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Expert Panels">
      <data key="d0">Expert Panels</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Expert panels comprise specialized groups that evaluate and provide guidance regarding medical devices under EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Expert Laboratories">
      <data key="d0">Expert Laboratories</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Expert laboratories are accredited facilities that conduct testing and assessment of medical devices to ensure compliance with EU standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reference Laboratories">
      <data key="d0">Reference Laboratories</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Reference laboratories serve as authoritative bodies for testing medical devices, ensuring adherence to EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and 2017/746">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and 2017/746</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">These regulations establish the rules and requirements for the market entry of medical devices in the European Union, focusing on safety and effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bodies, Groups, or Laboratories">
      <data key="d0">Bodies, Groups, or Laboratories</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">These are organizations or entities that have been established or accredited to perform tasks related to conformity assessment under Union harmonization legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c3f9e0d5137c2203e9fbadc5d6f93ca7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/147/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Panel of Independent Experts">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Panel of Independent Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Scientific Panel of Independent Experts is established to support enforcement activities related to regulations in the field of AI, advising and assisting the AI Office with various tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 74(11)">
      <data key="d0">Article 74(11)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 74(11) discusses cross-border market surveillance activities related to the governance of AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 74(11) pertains to cross-border market surveillance activities that the scientific panel supports.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 74(11) pertains to specific provisions regarding market surveillance authorities' joint activities under the AI Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Safeguard Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Union Safeguard Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Safeguard Procedure outlines the protocol for addressing objections raised by market surveillance authorities regarding AI practices within EU Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union Safeguard Procedure refers to the framework within which the AI Office carries out its duties, ensuring compliance with Union regulations regarding AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec59dcaa7ce835ce9dd1c42d507cf75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/81/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428500</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 81">
      <data key="d0">Article 81</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 81 outlines the Union safeguard procedures related to the regulation of AI models and their risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conflicts of Interest">
      <data key="d0">Conflicts of Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conflicts of Interest refer to situations where individuals in a position of authority in the Scientific Panel have personal stakes that may influence their impartiality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Declaration of Interests">
      <data key="d0">Declaration of Interests</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Declaration of Interests is a statement made by experts on the Scientific Panel regarding any personal interests that could influence their duties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Implementing Act">
      <data key="d0">Implementing Act</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Implementing Act refers to a formal legislative procedure in which the Commission adopts detailed provisions for the post-market monitoring plans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Implementing Act refers to legal provisions that define the conditions and procedures for scientific panel operations and the issuance of alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Implementing Act refers to legal frameworks established to provide detailed regulations regarding specific areas or sectors, subject to amendments by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b84ed9e420c0ae0245bb808d08db0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1b5a22fa12a7caf6d6a82166e9ac79b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428445</data>
    </node>
