      <data key="d5">1748426703</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorized Representatives">
      <data key="d0">Authorized Representatives</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorized Representatives act on behalf of providers that are not established in the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c89fbb177b0adfb819460dd999b9788d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426703</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Affected Persons">
      <data key="d0">Affected Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Affected Persons are individuals located in the Union who are impacted by the deployment of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected Persons are individuals or groups who are impacted by decisions made using AI systems and require comprehension of AI outputs to understand how these decisions affect their lives.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals who are impacted by decisions made using high-risk AI systems and have the right to obtain explanations for such decisions which might adversely affect their health, safety, or fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c89fbb177b0adfb819460dd999b9788d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ef04b3893d2080962790dc78128cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553e3df123166674b26c5dc07f2a83af</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/171/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427704</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 21">
      <data key="d0">Recital 21</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 21 is a specific guideline or reference within the regulation that outlines the application and scope for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c89fbb177b0adfb819460dd999b9788d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426714</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 22">
      <data key="d0">Recital 22</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 22 discusses the engagement of third countries and organizations regarding AI systems under international cooperation agreements.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 22 is another reference that specifies the parameters and context of the regulation in relation to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c89fbb177b0adfb819460dd999b9788d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426714</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 24">
      <data key="d0">Recital 24</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 24 details exceptions to the regulation concerning military, defense, or national security purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 24 refers to a specific part of the legal document discussing the applicability of regulations to AI systems and military purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c89fbb177b0adfb819460dd999b9788d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426714</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2002/58/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2002/58/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2002/58/EC addresses the processing of personal data and privacy in the electronic communications sector.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC addresses the protection of privacy in the electronic communications sector within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC pertains to the privacy and electronic communications in the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC concerns the processing of personal data and the protection of privacy in the electronic communications sector.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC relates to privacy and electronic communications, establishing rules for the confidentiality of communications and conditions for data storage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b5414adf1ebf7087a1a00f2e4fb3570b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ebb4e641a55d31b962b56d6017d2734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57118cd489d78b33ed75c63f33151aee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428375</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 11">
      <data key="d0">Recital 11</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 11 relates to the application of provisions on the liability of intermediary services stated in EU Regulation 2022/2065.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 25">
      <data key="d0">Recital 25</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 25 specifies that certain regulations do not apply to AI systems developed for scientific research and development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union harmonisation legislation">
      <data key="d0">Union harmonisation legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union harmonisation legislation refers to the body of EU law aimed at ensuring consistency across member states in relation to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to the body of laws in the EU that ensures consistent regulations across member states to facilitate trade and safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="military purposes">
      <data key="d0">military purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Military purposes refer to the use of technology or systems in defense operations, which are exempt from certain regulations pertaining to AI in the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights and freedoms">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights and freedoms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental rights and freedoms encompass the basic legal rights guaranteed to individuals under EU law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="scientific research and development">
      <data key="d0">scientific research and development</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Scientific research and development pertains to the activities undertaken to advance knowledge and technology, which may be exempt from some regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intermediary Services">
      <data key="d0">Intermediary Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intermediary Services involve services that facilitate communication or transactions between users and content, often utilizing AI technologies to enhance functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediary services connect users and service providers, often acting as platforms for communication or transaction, and are subject to specific regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b917b23f883123c9ae4bf6c69ae5e06</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/119/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 10(5)">
      <data key="d0">Article 10(5)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 10(5) refers to a specific provision within the regulation that outlines related obligations or conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 59">
      <data key="d0">Article 59</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 59 refers to provisions concerning the applicability of regulations related to AI systems and their development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Research Activities">
      <data key="d0">Research Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Research activities refer to systematic investigations aimed at discovering or interpreting facts, theories, and applications related to AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Activities">
      <data key="d0">Testing Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing activities involve assessing AI systems in controlled or real-world environments to evaluate performance and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Protection Laws">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Protection Laws</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer Protection Laws are regulations designed to safeguard the rights of consumers, particularly concerning the sale and use of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Consumer protection laws are regulations designed to protect the interests and rights of consumers, ensuring fair treatment by businesses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3eb172261ecd1825a8ea90f0090909ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac3e101757a5789343d428cd14e4874e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Product Safety Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Product Safety Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Product Safety Regulations are laws that ensure products, including AI systems, meet specific safety standards to protect users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac3e101757a5789343d428cd14e4874e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national security">
      <data key="d0">national security</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-217dd0b241eb263a726e72dd92814c0a</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States have the authority to determine national security measures, including how AI systems are managed and regulated.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426717</data>
    </node>
    <node id="rightsholders">
      <data key="d0">rightsholders</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Rightsholders are individuals or organizations that hold the rights to creative works and have the authority to allow or restrict their use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="copyright">
      <data key="d0">copyright</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Copyright is a legal framework that grants the creator of original work exclusive rights to its use and distribution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="text and data mining">
      <data key="d0">text and data mining</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Text and data mining involves techniques used to analyze and retrieve vast amounts of content, often protected by copyright.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="artists">
      <data key="d0">artists</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Artists are creators who produce original works, such as visual art, literature, or music, and are affected by copyright legislation regarding their creations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="authors">
      <data key="d0">authors</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Authors are writers who create literary works and have a stake in how their content is utilized and protected under copyright law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="creators">
      <data key="d0">creators</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Creators is a general term referring to individuals who generate content across various mediums, facing challenges posed by AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a27392402ccb8a7a70b92094f8dd984b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaint Submission">
      <data key="d0">Complaint Submission</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Complaint Submission refers to the process by which downstream providers can lodge complaints about potential infringements of AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426723</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Approved Codes of Practice">
      <data key="d0">Approved Codes of Practice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Approved Codes of Practice set the standards and guidelines that providers of AI models must adhere to ensure compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426723</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Economy">
      <data key="d0">Union Economy</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Economy refers to the economic system within a particular political and geographical union, emphasizing growth opportunities provided through innovation and research.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open-source Software and Data">
      <data key="d0">Open-source Software and Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Open-source software and data are types of software and data released under licences that allow users to freely access, modify, and share, promoting innovation and accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d0">General-purpose AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI models are a class of AI technology that must also comply with the common specifications established by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are advanced artificial intelligence systems capable of performing a wide range of tasks but may pose systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models are versatile artificial intelligence systems designed for a wide range of applications and should be released under open-source licences for transparency and accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3c51b7bfc502a0e1b7fc0c076f574e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214363bac320d3b288355fb10d6c0537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Free and Open-source Licence">
      <data key="d0">Free and Open-source Licence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A free and open-source licence allows users to access, use, modify, and distribute software and data freely, facilitating collaboration and innovation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Models">
      <data key="d0">Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Models in this context refer to software simulations or AI frameworks that can be created, modified, and shared under open-source conditions, contributing to research and development.&lt;SEP&gt;Models refer to computational representations or algorithms that can perform tasks, which may pose risks if they self-replicate or bias decision-making processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff9241c3a9f5f8fc78557cf5705c8c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Research and Innovation">
      <data key="d0">Research and Innovation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Research and Innovation encompass the activities of developing new knowledge and technologies, which are crucial for economic advancement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Users">
      <data key="d0">Users</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Users are individuals who utilize free and open-source software and data, capable of accessing, modifying, and redistributing these resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parameters">
      <data key="d0">Parameters</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Parameters refer to specific configurations of models, such as weights and architecture details, that must be made public under open-source guidelines to ensure transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;Parameters refer to the specific measurable factors that characterize the performance and capabilities of a model, influencing its generality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42bf8846c41a0070ff191a1386b2a4ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7998dcefaedb3e70eebeb29bedc0789f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/98/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/102/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU product rules 2022">
      <data key="d0">EU product rules 2022</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU product rules 2022 outline mandatory requirements for placing high-risk AI systems on the market within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2006/42/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2006/42/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2006/42/EC concerns machinery safety regulations that must be met prior to marketing products in the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2006/42/EC is a piece of EU legislation concerning the safety of machinery and modifying earlier directives to improve health standards in machinery use.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2006/42/EC pertains to machinery safety and sets requirements for the design and construction of machinery within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac4ae391b0af74fcc265e13a9005502f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union market">
      <data key="d0">Union market</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Union market is the economic area encompassing all member states of the European Union where products and services are traded under common regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;The 'Blue Guide'">
      <data key="d0">"The 'Blue Guide'</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The 'Blue Guide' is a guidance document provided by the European Commission detailing the implementation of EU product rules and ensuring harmonization across the EU market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2017/745 on medical devices">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2017/745 on medical devices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2017/745 governs the safety and performance of medical devices marketed in the EU, including those that may incorporate AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2017/746 on in vitro diagnostic medical devices">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2017/746 on in vitro diagnostic medical devices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2017/746 establishes requirements for in vitro diagnostic medical devices, ensuring compliance with health and safety standards in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 178/2002">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 178/2002</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 178/2002 establishes the general principles and requirements of food law in the European Union, ensuring food safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 1223/2009">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 1223/2009</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 1223/2009 pertains to cosmetic products, ensuring they are safe for consumers and properly regulated within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2001/83/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2001/83/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2001/83/EC aims to facilitate the free movement of medicines across the EU while ensuring safety and efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b740b6582df221140c232d3406281f9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Directive 2006/42/EC">
      <data key="d0">EU Directive 2006/42/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Directive 2006/42/EC is a piece of legislation related to machinery, establishing essential health and safety requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac4ae391b0af74fcc265e13a9005502f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 95/16/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 95/16/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 95/16/EC pertains to machinery and was amended by Directive 2006/42/EC to enhance safety regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac4ae391b0af74fcc265e13a9005502f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OJ L 117">
      <data key="d0">OJ L 117</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">OJ L 117 is a reference to an official journal publication from the EU containing legal acts, directives, and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac4ae391b0af74fcc265e13a9005502f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OJ L 157">
      <data key="d0">OJ L 157</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">OJ L 157 is another reference to an EU official journal publication that includes information on directives and regulations, such as Directive 95/16/EC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac4ae391b0af74fcc265e13a9005502f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The 'Blue Guide">
      <data key="d0">The 'Blue Guide</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abc588d012f1bc89cd1e08c6d43bb27a</data>
      <data key="d2">The 'Blue Guide' provides guidance on the implementation of the New Legislative Framework, ensuring all products meet EU standards for market access.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation 176">
      <data key="d0">Regulation 176</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation 176 focuses on improving the functioning of the internal market while promoting responsible AI use and ensuring protection of health, safety, and fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1db48dde4f93da16c9531d8351b22c36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/176/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426732</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charter of Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Charter of Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charter of Fundamental Rights contains essential rights related to democracy, rule of law, and protection against harmful effects of AI systems in the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter of Fundamental Rights outlines the fundamental rights of individuals within the EU, including dignity, privacy, and equality.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter of Fundamental Rights is a foundational document that delineates the rights and freedoms of individuals within the European Union and guides the ethical framing of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db48dde4f93da16c9531d8351b22c36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/176/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Principle of Subsidiarity">
      <data key="d0">Principle of Subsidiarity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Principle of Subsidiarity dictates that the Union should only act if objectives cannot be sufficiently achieved at the Member State level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1db48dde4f93da16c9531d8351b22c36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/176/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Principle of Proportionality">
      <data key="d0">Principle of Proportionality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Principle of Proportionality ensures that any action taken does not exceed what is necessary to achieve the desired objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1db48dde4f93da16c9531d8351b22c36</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/176/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Market">
      <data key="d0">Internal Market</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Internal Market refers to the economic space within the Union where goods, services, people, and capital can move freely, promoting competitive markets.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal market is the integrated economic system of the European Union, allowing for the free movement of goods, services, capital, and labor among member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1db48dde4f93da16c9531d8351b22c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/176/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union AI Testing Support Structures">
      <data key="d0">Union AI Testing Support Structures</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union AI Testing Support Structures are designated by the Commission to perform tasks related to the regulation of AI under Article 21(6) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.&lt;SEP&gt;Union AI Testing Support Structures are designed to support the enforcement and capability enhancement of Member States concerning AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9c4fb703fd804a96a166ec00e7efb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4825b8c430847477f9ab6dc8f1b19797</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/152/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/84/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 152">
      <data key="d0">Recital 152</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 152 refers to a specific provision or statement within a legislative or regulatory document concerning AI systems enforceability and support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9c4fb703fd804a96a166ec00e7efb74</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/152/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426745</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 114 TFEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 114 TFEU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 114 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union provides the legal basis for establishing uniform regulations across the EU internal market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 16 TFEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 16 TFEU</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 16 TFEU is a provision of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union that addresses the protection of personal data and is relevant to the regulation of biometric data processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union (TFEU) addresses the processing of personal data by Member States in areas related to justice and security.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union pertains to the protection of individuals concerning personal data processing, particularly in relation to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union pertains to the protection of personal data and privacy in the European Union legislative framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b477112713d917a03ba6f595ed62f6c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7f6078e68943998b91775a85fbac31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55631cb4906af7cdbc5803cac20d432d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/38/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428606</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Data Protection Board">
      <data key="d0">European Data Protection Board</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Board ensures consistent application of data protection rules within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Board is an independent European body that contributes to the consistent application of data protection law across the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Board is an independent European body that ensures consistent application of data protection rules across the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f6078e68943998b91775a85fbac31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a360e38774a35c72c4384c10d081a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/180/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426757</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Rules">
      <data key="d0">National Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National rules involve regulations that individual member states may implement to govern the development and ethical use of AI systems within their jurisdictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental rights obligations refer to legal commitments that ensure the protection of basic rights of individuals in the context of AI technology deployment and usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Certainty">
      <data key="d0">Legal Certainty</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal certainty refers to the assurance that laws and regulations are clear and predictable, thereby enabling fair and consistent enforcement of the law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Uniform Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Uniform Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Uniform obligations are consistent regulations or legal duties that all member states of the European Union must adhere to in order to harmonize laws across the internal market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI systems of biometric categorisation">
      <data key="d0">AI systems of biometric categorisation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems of biometric categorisation involve the use of artificial intelligence technologies to categorize individuals based on biometric data for identification and law enforcement purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f6078e68943998b91775a85fbac31</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Malicious Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Malicious Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Malicious third parties are individuals or groups that exploit vulnerabilities in systems for harmful purposes, particularly targeting AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ICT Infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">ICT Infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">ICT infrastructure encompasses all technology components that enable communication and data management, essential for supporting AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cyberattack">
      <data key="d0">Cyberattack</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Cyberattack refers to a malicious attempt to compromise the integrity, confidentiality, or availability of computer systems, including AI systems, often involving exploitation of vulnerabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Attacks">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Attacks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Adversarial attacks are tactics employed to manipulate AI systems by introducing deceptive input, leading to incorrect processing and outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial attacks are techniques used to manipulate AI models by introducing misleading data, which can compromise the model's output and accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/77/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Membership Inference">
      <data key="d0">Membership Inference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Membership inference refers to a type of attack where an adversary attempts to determine whether a specific data point was used to train a model, potentially revealing sensitive information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e005821863d6fa70e39abefcdd671b23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 June 2021">
      <data key="d0">18 June 2021</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">18 June 2021 is the date when the joint opinion of the European Data Protection Supervisor and the European Data Protection Board was delivered.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a360e38774a35c72c4384c10d081a180</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/180/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426757</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 42(1) and (2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 42(1) and (2)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 42(1) and (2) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 describes the consultative role of the European Data Protection Supervisor and Board in the context of data protection regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a360e38774a35c72c4384c10d081a180</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/180/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426757</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Authority">
      <data key="d0">Competent Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent Authorities are designated regulatory institutions within the Union tasked with overseeing compliance and enforcement regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Competent Authority is a regulatory body responsible for overseeing and ensuring compliance of high-risk AI systems under EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Competent Authority is the regulatory body within each Member State tasked with overseeing compliance and the functioning of Notified Bodies regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent Authority refers to the specific national body responsible for overseeing the compliance and activities within AI regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Competent Authority refers to the designated body responsible for overseeing and ensuring compliance with regulations in the context of AI regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427354</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorised Representatives">
      <data key="d0">Authorised Representatives</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorised Representatives are entities selected by providers of high-risk AI systems to act on their behalf in the Union market and ensure compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System Mandate">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System Mandate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI System Mandate is a documented authorization that enables appointed representatives to conduct certain compliance-related tasks for AI system providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Obligations are the legal requirements that providers and their authorised representatives must meet to ensure that high-risk AI systems are safe and compliant with applicable standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 12(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 12(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific provision within a regulatory framework that mandates the maintenance of logs by providers of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 12(1) details the requirements for logging and documentation that high-risk AI systems must adhere to for regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 12(1) refers to provisions regarding access to logs generated by high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c9c861dfef84b47d382d7c3a57b94afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f0b636a44a9e0af30b88362b202119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/21/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428103</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mandate">
      <data key="d0">Mandate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A mandate is a written authorization given by the provider to the authorized representative outlining their responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mandate involves a formal agreement empowering an authorized representative to liaise with competent authorities regarding compliance issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of Intermediary Services">
      <data key="d0">Providers of Intermediary Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of Intermediary Services are entities that embed AI systems or models into their services and must adhere to specific regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Actors">
      <data key="d0">Market Actors</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Actors are entities that place AI systems on the market or use them in the European Union, subject to regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management Framework">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Risk-Management Framework provided in Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 is designed to help identify and manage systemic risks associated with AI Systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8189d1d23247190f250b589837018fa0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/118/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">legal_document</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations (EU) 2016/679 establish guidelines for the processing of personal data, emphasizing the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations (EU) 2016/679 pertains to data protection and privacy for individuals in the European Union and European Economic Area.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation pertains to the protection of personal data and privacy in the European Union, commonly known as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation pertains to the protection of personal data and privacy of individuals within the European Union and the European Economic Area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9acb869e8831be994323dab5f07993e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b27dc39e557245814845f393e9bb76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">legal_document</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations (EU) 2018/1725 addresses the protection of personal data processed by EU institutions and bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulations (EU) 2018/1725 provide specific provisions on the processing of personal data by EU institutions, aiming to ensure similar protection as provided in Regulation (EU) 2016/679.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation governs the processing of personal data by EU institutions and bodies, providing a framework for data protection.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation relates to the protection of personal data in EU institutions and bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9acb869e8831be994323dab5f07993e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b27dc39e557245814845f393e9bb76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0198dcc8748fd4f1d62cf74ad13bbcbc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bias Detection and Correction">
      <data key="d0">Bias Detection and Correction</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias Detection and Correction is a process aimed at identifying and mitigating unfair biases in AI systems to ensure compliance with ethical standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Bias detection and correction are processes undertaken to identify and address bias within AI systems, ensuring fair and equitable treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Bias detection and correction refers to the measures required to identify and mitigate biases within AI systems to ensure fair outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b27dc39e557245814845f393e9bb76f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9acb869e8831be994323dab5f07993e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65688cdd97448f1f3932957595156d18</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/70/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 8 to 15">
      <data key="d0">Articles 8 to 15</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 8 to 15 refer to specific provisions within the regulation that detail various obligations and requirements for implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426797</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 25">
      <data key="d0">Article 25</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 25 sets forth additional requirements related to the implementation of the regulation, emphasizing compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426797</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 50">
      <data key="d0">Article 50</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 50 details transparency obligations that regulated entities must maintain within their operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 pertains to AI systems that require additional transparency measures for accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 requires additional transparency measures for certain AI systems and is part of the EU's regulatory framework on AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="State of the Art on AI">
      <data key="d0">State of the Art on AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The state of the art on AI refers to the current level of development and technical standards in artificial intelligence systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426797</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Local Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Local Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Local public authorities are governmental entities involved in enforcing regulations at the municipality level and are considered by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Local public authorities are governmental organizations that are involved in the implementation of regulations and support for SMEs and start-ups at the community level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8363b7ff75e2a59a44c744564b484596</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Harmonisation Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Harmonisation Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union harmonisation law refers to regulations and standards adopted to ensure consistency across member states within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7982e6435aa73ec0e21cfbbfe3f5ea87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426797</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open-Source License">
      <data key="d0">Open-Source License</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An open-source license allows software or models to be freely used, modified, and shared, provided that any derivative works are also shared under the same terms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e7bb7f2671f4090f24b5396183a3f1e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790">
      <data key="d0">Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790 specifies conditions for copyright law compliance regarding the use of datasets for training AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e7bb7f2671f4090f24b5396183a3f1e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Single Market">
      <data key="d0">Digital Single Market</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Digital Single Market refers to an initiative aimed at ensuring uniform regulations and a seamless digital economy across EU member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digital Single Market refers to an integrated market allowing digital goods and services to flow freely across Member States, enhancing the EU's digital economy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e9d6472f6799d71df39a63934dcde4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/104/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-purpose AI systems">
      <data key="d0">General-purpose AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI systems refer to AI technologies that can be utilized in various applications, potentially carrying high-risk implications when deployed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-457bf0e90f1920e6839b11cd66b1060b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/85/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of AI systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of AI systems refer to companies or entities that develop, manage, or supply AI technologies, especially those classified as high-risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-457bf0e90f1920e6839b11cd66b1060b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/85/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations under the Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Obligations under the Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations under the Regulation refer to the specific responsibilities that providers must adhere to when developing or deploying AI systems, particularly high-risk ones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-457bf0e90f1920e6839b11cd66b1060b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/85/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Binding Rules">
      <data key="d0">Binding Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Binding Rules are regulations designed to govern the implementation and operation of AI systems, ensuring compliance to specific standards and obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22ee21887c9f5c01959c0a57e3491fb2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Based Approach">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Based Approach</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Risk-Based Approach refers to a methodology that tailors rules and regulations according to the specific risks posed by AI systems, ensuring effectiveness in governance and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22ee21887c9f5c01959c0a57e3491fb2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unacceptable AI Practices">
      <data key="d0">Unacceptable AI Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Unacceptable AI Practices are specific actions or implementations within AI systems that are prohibited due to ethical or safety concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22ee21887c9f5c01959c0a57e3491fb2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/26/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="very large online platforms">
      <data key="d0">very large online platforms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Very large online platforms are digital services that host user-generated content and face specific obligations under Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 to manage systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="very large online search engines">
      <data key="d0">very large online search engines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Very large online search engines are search services that must comply with regulations regarding the detection of artificially generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers of certain AI systems">
      <data key="d0">providers of certain AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of certain AI systems are responsible for complying with the obligations set forth in Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 regarding the transparency of outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="currently deployed AI systems">
      <data key="d0">currently deployed AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Currently deployed AI systems refer to artificial intelligence technologies that are in use and required to adhere to the regulations concerning output transparency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers of very large online platforms">
      <data key="d0">providers of very large online platforms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of very large online platforms are digital service providers that must comply with stringent regulations related to managing systemic risks from their content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers of very large online search engines">
      <data key="d0">providers of very large online search engines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of very large online search engines are companies that manage search services and are subject to regulations for content detection and risk mitigation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="democratic processes">
      <data key="d0">democratic processes</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Democratic processes are the means through which individuals in society engage in decision-making, requiring educated participants.&lt;SEP&gt;Democratic processes refer to the mechanisms by which citizens participate in governance, which may be influenced by misleading AI-generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f557a252b7f04ee224d608a6628bd4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="civic discourse">
      <data key="d0">civic discourse</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Civic discourse encompasses public dialogue and discussion critical to democratic engagement, which may be affected by disinformation spread via AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="electoral processes">
      <data key="d0">electoral processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electoral processes are the methods and systems used for conducting elections, which could be impacted by disinformation and manipulated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Quality management involves the processes and practices that ensure the integrity and effectiveness of conformity assessments conducted by notified bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Professional Secrecy">
      <data key="d0">Professional Secrecy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Professional secrecy is the duty of personnel in notified bodies to protect sensitive information related to conformity assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Professional secrecy is the obligation of personnel within notified bodies to maintain confidentiality about information obtained during assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consultancy Services">
      <data key="d0">Consultancy Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consultancy services refer to advisory services that notified bodies must avoid to maintain impartiality in their assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Standardisation Organisations">
      <data key="d0">European Standardisation Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">European Standardisation Organisations are bodies that develop and publish technical standards across Europe, playing a crucial role in ensuring compliance with regulations established by the European Union. These organisations are involved in the creation and maintenance of standards that are essential for various sectors, including emerging fields such as artificial intelligence. They work closely with notified bodies to ensure that products and services meet the required compliance standards. Additionally, European Standardisation Organisations are responsible for drafting harmonised standards that align with EU regulations and requirements, thereby promoting consistency and quality within the European market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fbacc8a39fa85eaf6afc731174af8109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214363bac320d3b288355fb10d6c0537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f3473e38ccd9ad84662b373166a5c2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independence of Judgement">
      <data key="d0">Independence of Judgement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Independence of judgement involves the ability of notified bodies to make unbiased decisions without conflicts of interest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles of Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Articles of Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles of regulation refer to sections within legislative documents that outline guidelines for the operation of notified bodies and their assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Liability Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Liability Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Liability insurance is coverage that notified bodies are required to obtain for activities related to conformity assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426844</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Assessment Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Assessment Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Assessment procedures are documented steps that notified bodies must implement to ensure the effectiveness and integrity of evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93bf0556246eea991173613a2ccf1b73</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426844</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Law on the Protection of Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Union Law on the Protection of Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legislation related to data protection and privacy within the European Union, informing how data related to personal information must be handled.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c9c861dfef84b47d382d7c3a57b94afe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426865</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Data Protection">
      <data key="d0">Personal Data Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal standards and regulations that ensure the privacy and protection of personal data within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c9c861dfef84b47d382d7c3a57b94afe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426865</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2024/900">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2024/900</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2024/900 is a legislative act by the European Parliament that addresses the risks associated with AI systems influencing elections and referenda.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93e6a954a9283acf571ff61858a432ac</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/62/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426868</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charter of Fundamental Rights includes Article 39, which guarantees the right to vote in a democratic environment within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter of Fundamental Rights sets out the fundamental rights and freedoms guaranteed to individuals in the EU, influencing regulations such as those on AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93e6a954a9283acf571ff61858a432ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec304def59e7573aa1fecc006d51bea7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/1/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation 2024/900">
      <data key="d0">Regulation 2024/900</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation 2024/900 is a legal framework established by the European Parliament to manage political advertising and the influence of AI systems on electoral processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93e6a954a9283acf571ff61858a432ac</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/62/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426868</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voting Rights">
      <data key="d0">Voting Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Voting Rights encompass the entitlements granted to citizens to participate in elections, as protected under the Charter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93e6a954a9283acf571ff61858a432ac</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/62/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426868</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Election">
      <data key="d0">Election</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An Election is a formal decision-making process by which a population chooses individuals to hold public office, relevant to the content discussed regarding AI influence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93e6a954a9283acf571ff61858a432ac</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/62/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426874</data>
    </node>
    <node id="United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child">
      <data key="d0">United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child establishes the rights of children, emphasizing their protection and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNCRC General Comment No 25">
      <data key="d0">UNCRC General Comment No 25</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The UNCRC General Comment No 25 focuses on children’s rights in relation to the digital environment, emphasizing the need for protections for minors.&lt;SEP&gt;The UNCRC General Comment No 25 provides guidance on children's rights in relation to the digital environment.&lt;SEP&gt;UNCRC General Comment No 25 addresses children's rights in the digital environment, highlighting vulnerabilities and necessary protections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1219d54497e2a4a6af07e6b10274bc72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427581</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Union Policies">
      <data key="d0">European Union Policies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">European Union Policies are guidelines that implement the rights enshrined in the Charter of Fundamental Rights, focusing on protection and environmental issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to Human Dignity">
      <data key="d0">Right to Human Dignity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The right to human dignity is a fundamental principle ensuring respect for individuals' inherent worth and values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to Privacy">
      <data key="d0">Right to Privacy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Right to Privacy is a fundamental principle that ensures individuals can protect their personal information against misuse and unauthorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;The right to privacy is a fundamental human right that protects individuals from unauthorized intrusion into their personal lives.&lt;SEP&gt;The right to privacy protects individuals' personal and family life from unwarranted interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e010ebb9b0353d97d9e67673267bc415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea591e8c170e7b5ae61060a7a9c9e5fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/69/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/43/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428214</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to Freedom of Expression">
      <data key="d0">Right to Freedom of Expression</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This right allows individuals to express opinions freely without government censorship or punishment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to Education">
      <data key="d0">Right to Education</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The right to education guarantees access to quality education for all individuals, promoting personal and societal development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Children's Rights">
      <data key="d0">Children's Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Children's rights refer to specific protections and care requirements for children, ensuring their well-being and development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Impact on Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Impact on Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This phrase describes the various ways an AI system can potentially infringe upon or affect individuals' recognized rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rights of Persons with Disabilities">
      <data key="d0">Rights of Persons with Disabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This right ensures that individuals with disabilities are treated with equality and respect in all aspects of life, including access to resources and opportunities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gender Equality">
      <data key="d0">Gender Equality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Gender equality is a fundamental right that calls for equal treatment and opportunities regardless of gender.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to Non-Discrimination">
      <data key="d0">Right to Non-Discrimination</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This right guarantees that individuals are not treated unfairly based on personal characteristics such as race, gender, or disability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to an Effective Remedy">
      <data key="d0">Right to an Effective Remedy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This right ensures that individuals have access to legal means to address violations of their rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Right to Good Administration">
      <data key="d0">Right to Good Administration</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This right guarantees individuals the right to be treated justly and fairly in administrative processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety of Persons">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety of Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to the rights concerning the physical and mental well-being of individuals, ensuring that systems in place do not jeopardize their health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c99da125b1a260d6205d5ccdcda33d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/48/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operating System">
      <data key="d0">Operating System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The operating system is the software that supports a computer's basic functions and may need reassessment if changed in a high-risk AI system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a9cac9d5c84dcacd663b50bbd6c7786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/128/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Software Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Software Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Software architecture refers to the high-level structure of software systems, which requires reassessment if modified for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a9cac9d5c84dcacd663b50bbd6c7786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/128/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Procedure at National Level for Dealing with AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Procedure at National Level for Dealing with AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Procedure at National Level for Dealing with AI Systems outlines the steps and responsibilities for evaluating AI systems that present risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Review and Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Review and Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Review and Evaluation processes are conducted to assess the compliance and risks associated with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Correction Actions">
      <data key="d0">Correction Actions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Correction Actions refer to the measures required to ensure AI systems comply with regulations, including withdrawal or recall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk to Health or Safety">
      <data key="d0">Risk to Health or Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk to Health or Safety pertains to potential dangers posed by AI systems that could affect the well-being of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance involves adhering to regulatory laws and guidelines that govern the development and operation of AI Systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance refers to the process of adhering to established regulations and standards for AI systems in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance refers to the adherence to laws and regulations by operators involved in AI systems to ensure legal certainty in their operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-66e6524323a5bff7a82ba7868399e18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2252cbe714fc3b6aee570acd5f270ef</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Market">
      <data key="d0">National Market</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The National Market refers to the specific country or region where the AI system is proposed to operate or is being regulated.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Market refers to the specific market of a Member State where AI systems are evaluated and regulated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-compliant AI system">
      <data key="d0">Non-compliant AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-compliant AI systems are those AI technologies that fail to meet required regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 40 and 41">
      <data key="d0">Articles 40 and 41</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 40 and 41 contain harmonized standards or common specifications that help establish a presumption of conformity for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concerns over Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Concerns over Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Concerns over compliance refer to issues raised regarding the adherence to regulatory standards by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64d7c3502c744cfa90a7690ed32f3264</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Non-Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-Compliance refers to the violation of regulations or standards set for AI systems within the jurisdiction of the Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provisional Measure">
      <data key="d0">Provisional Measure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Provisional Measure is a temporary action taken by market surveillance authorities in response to non-compliance by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Rights">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory Rights refer to the procedural rights of operators concerning compliance notifications and measures taken by authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aed721d84482f8eb2ef2f8c288d59095</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Line 5 Directive">
      <data key="d0">Line 5 Directive</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687</data>
      <data key="d2">The Market Surveillance Authority is charged with notifying operators about compliance issues following the Line 5 Directive's requirements.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Expertise">
      <data key="d0">Union Expertise</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Expertise refers to the specialized knowledge and skills available at the Union level aimed at ensuring effective regulation of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4fa0ab303aa0764433ae306cd3e410cb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/162/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426913</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaints">
      <data key="d0">Complaints</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Complaints refer to the formal expressions raised by downstream providers regarding possible infringements of rules concerning AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4fa0ab303aa0764433ae306cd3e410cb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/162/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426913</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex III List">
      <data key="d0">Annex III List</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex III List is a part of the regulation that enumerates AI practices that may be amended by the Commission based on ongoing assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voluntary Codes of Conduct">
      <data key="d0">Voluntary Codes of Conduct</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Voluntary Codes of Conduct are guidelines developed to foster ethical practices among individuals and organizations working with AI, aiming to enhance literacy and responsible usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Voluntary Codes of Conduct are guidelines set to promote ethical practices and compliance in AI systems, particularly those deemed lower risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Voluntary codes of conduct are non-mandatory guidelines designed to foster ethical AI practices and responses to regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Voluntary codes of conduct are frameworks that organizations can adopt to guide ethical behavior and compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fafe6ac227379dad776c22a5abc16ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02c1809d1e7a16e9c8b3d0effff3a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standardisation Deliverables">
      <data key="d0">Standardisation Deliverables</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Standardisation Deliverables are specific outcomes or documents produced by regulatory bodies to ensure consistency in the development of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02c1809d1e7a16e9c8b3d0effff3a40</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2028">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2028</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">2 August 2028 is a significant date by which the Commission is required to evaluate the AI Office and its functionalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02c1809d1e7a16e9c8b3d0effff3a40</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Evaluation of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Evaluation of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The evaluation of AI systems refers to the process undertaken by authorities to assess the impact, effectiveness, and compliance of AI technologies with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Binding Measures or Actions">
      <data key="d0">Binding Measures or Actions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Binding measures or actions refer to legislative requirements that may be imposed to ensure compliance during the development and use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Economic and Social Committee">
      <data key="d0">European Economic and Social Committee</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Economic and Social Committee provides opinions and advises in the context of AI regulations and enforcement assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2031">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2031</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">By 2 August 2031, the Commission is scheduled to assess the enforcement of the AI Regulation and report findings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Levels">
      <data key="d0">Risk Levels</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk levels pertain to the categorization of AI systems based on their potential impact and the required evaluation methodologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Methodology">
      <data key="d0">Methodology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Methodology describes the systematic approaches developed for assessing AI risks and ensuring compliance with established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sectoral Union Harmonisation">
      <data key="d0">Sectoral Union Harmonisation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sectoral Union harmonisation focuses on aligning AI regulations with specific sectors to ensure effective governance across industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Specificities">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Specificities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory specificities refer to the unique requirements and considerations for different sectors in enforcing AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union agency">
      <data key="d0">Union agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Union agency is a proposed entity that may be established to resolve shortcomings identified in the enforcement of regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea7c61bb3faa96858aa76ce6e8ecae80</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Agency">
      <data key="d0">Union Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Union agency is a proposed entity that may be established to identify and resolve shortcomings related to the enforcement of regulations, potentially enhancing oversight and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea7c61bb3faa96858aa76ce6e8ecae80</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Findings Report">
      <data key="d0">Findings Report</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Findings Report provides an analysis of the assessed regulations and outlines necessary improvements for enforcement structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea7c61bb3faa96858aa76ce6e8ecae80</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 13">
      <data key="d0">Article 13</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 13 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 relates to specific obligations for high-risk AI systems used in law enforcement and the protection of personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 13 outlines the specific requirements for information and training that must be provided to deployers of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 13 outlines the requirements for testing AI systems, focusing on the roles of providers and deployers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428325</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GDPR Regulation 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">GDPR Regulation 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">GDPR Regulation 2016/680 refers to legislation enacted by the European Union to regulate data protection and privacy for individuals within the EU and the European Economic Area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1053de08f072032fc5edde1eb88ae570</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426953</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recommendation 2003/361/EC">
      <data key="d0">Recommendation 2003/361/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recommendation 2003/361/EC provides definitions and criteria aiding in understanding the classifications of micro- and small enterprises within certain regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation 2003/361/EC sets definitions and criteria for microenterprises and outlines compliance expectations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6b3a7a24bfd18cc84baf6173985e105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/63/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 28">
      <data key="d0">Article 28</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 28 relates to the notifying authority responsible for conducting assessments, designations, notifications, and monitoring activities for Notified Bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426967</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/943">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/943</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/943 addresses the protection of undisclosed know-how and business information against unlawful acquisition, use, and disclosure.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2016/943 is a legislative tool developed by the European Parliament and Council to protect trade secrets and intellectual property rights, particularly in relation to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;This Directive pertains to the protection of trade secrets and outlines the legal framework for safeguarding undisclosed know-how and business information in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="border control authorities">
      <data key="d0">border control authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Border control authorities manage the entry and exit of individuals at national borders, utilizing various technologies, including AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="market surveillance authorities">
      <data key="d0">market surveillance authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance Authorities are responsible for monitoring compliance with AI regulations at the national level to ensure safety and effectiveness of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities monitor the market to ensure compliance with regulations and protect public interests by ensuring product safety and adherence to legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for ensuring compliance with market regulations and may authorize the use of AI systems under specific conditions for public safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are regulatory bodies that have access to the information contained in the EU database for monitoring compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d447a0dff9a51bc6e0b8b9c92046aaae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8637916ea42060e68c1064d171c7c635</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/130/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427966</data>
    </node>
    <node id="intellectual property rights">
      <data key="d0">intellectual property rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intellectual property rights are legal rights that provide creators and inventors protection for their inventions and creative works, including trade secrets, patents, and copyrights.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights protect the ownership and usage of creations, inventions, and proprietary information in accordance with Union and national law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data protection measures">
      <data key="d0">data protection measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data protection measures are protocols and strategies implemented to safeguard sensitive information from unauthorized access, breaches, and misuse.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="cybersecurity measures">
      <data key="d0">cybersecurity measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity measures involve protections put in place to defend electronic data and information systems against cyber threats and attacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60ec41e4350eb50f98db60f37f74d3d7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International and Trade Agreements">
      <data key="d0">International and Trade Agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">International and trade agreements establish the rules for trade and cooperation between countries, including provisions for confidentiality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426988</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Law">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection Law is a legal framework within the EU that governs the processing and handling of personal data, aiming to safeguard individuals' privacy rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Data protection law encompasses regulations designed to protect personal data and privacy rights of individuals within the EU, including directives and regulations established by the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b12370838dd1a62b5ded5dc20979b9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/45/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428345</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory Authorities are entities responsible for overseeing compliance with laws and regulations, often tasked with managing confidentiality arrangements with third countries.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulatory authorities are government bodies that create and enforce rules and regulations within specific industries to ensure compliance and protect public interest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426988</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">EU National Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">EU National Competent Authorities are entities designated by each EU member state to oversee the implementation of EU law and regulations within their jurisdictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426988</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Security Clearance">
      <data key="d0">Security Clearance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Security Clearance refers to the level of authorization required for individuals to access sensitive documentation and information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426988</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-Border Cooperation">
      <data key="d0">Cross-Border Cooperation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cross-Border Cooperation involves collaboration between different national competent authorities to ensure effective supervision and compliance across jurisdictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-Border Cooperation involves the collaboration and communication between countries to share information and ensure regulatory adherence.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-Border Cooperation refers to the collaborative efforts between national competent authorities across different regions to enhance the operation and regulation of AI systems in the regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bilateral or Multilateral Confidentiality Arrangements">
      <data key="d0">Bilateral or Multilateral Confidentiality Arrangements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bilateral or Multilateral Confidentiality Arrangements are agreements between two or more countries to protect shared sensitive information from unauthorized disclosure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426988</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criminal Law of the Member States">
      <data key="d0">Criminal Law of the Member States</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal Law of the Member States encapsulates the legal obligations and rights concerning information exchange and confidentiality in criminal matters among nations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-756d4785a21d555261254273b91aea54</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748426988</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk Use Cases">
      <data key="d0">high-risk Use Cases</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk Use Cases refer to specific applications of AI systems that have been identified and categorized under the regulation for requiring stringent oversight and registration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="public authorities">
      <data key="d0">public authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Public authorities include government agencies and officials tasked with regulating and overseeing the deployment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="cybersecurity risks">
      <data key="d0">cybersecurity risks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity risks pertain to potential threats to the integrity, confidentiality, and availability of data and systems, particularly relating to AI deployment and database management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Database Functionality">
      <data key="d0">EU Database Functionality</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Database Functionality refers to the operational aspects and features that the EU database must possess to ensure effective registration and public access to high-risk AI system information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="secure non-public section">
      <data key="d0">secure non-public section</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The secure non-public section of the EU database is designed for sensitive information related to high-risk AI systems that require limited access due to security concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="derogation">
      <data key="d0">derogation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Derogation in this context refers to exemptions that allow certain AI systems to be classified differently than typically dictated by regulations concerning high-risk use cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems Regulation">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The High-Risk AI Systems Regulation refers to a regulatory framework addressing the risks associated with high-risk AI systems in various sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Sector">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Sector</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Law Enforcement Sector encompasses the use of AI technologies in policing and criminal justice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Migration Sector">
      <data key="d0">Migration Sector</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Migration Sector includes AI applications related to managing migration processes and policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Asylum Sector">
      <data key="d0">Asylum Sector</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Asylum Sector involves the use of AI technologies in the processing and management of asylum applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Border Control Management">
      <data key="d0">Border Control Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Border Control Management involves strategies and processes set by authorities to regulate the entry of individuals into a territory, ensuring security and legality.&lt;SEP&gt;Border Control Management involves the policies and practices that regulate the movement of people and goods across borders, ensuring national security and immigration laws are upheld.&lt;SEP&gt;Border Control Management refers to the use of AI in overseeing and managing national borders and immigration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Risks">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Risks</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission takes into account cybersecurity risks when managing the EU database, ensuring data protection and system integrity.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Derogation">
      <data key="d0">Derogation</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d2">Derogation allows for exceptions in the classification of certain AI systems defined in the high-risk Use Cases.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union institutions, bodies, offices, or agencies">
      <data key="d0">Union institutions, bodies, offices, or agencies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Union institutions, bodies, offices, or agencies encompass various governmental organizations within the European Union that may use AI for law enforcement support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427008</data>
    </node>
    <node id="natural person">
      <data key="d0">natural person</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural person refers to an individual human being whose fundamental rights may be impacted by the use of AI systems in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427008</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI profiling">
      <data key="d0">AI profiling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI profiling refers to the use of AI technologies to analyze and predict an individual's behavior or characteristics, which can lead to discrimination if misapplied.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="effective remedy">
      <data key="d0">effective remedy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The right to an effective remedy is a fundamental legal principle that ensures individuals can seek justice and redress for violations of their rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="right to a fair trial">
      <data key="d0">right to a fair trial</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The right to a fair trial is a fundamental legal right that guarantees individuals a fair and public hearing by an impartial tribunal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="presumption of innocence">
      <data key="d0">presumption of innocence</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The presumption of innocence is a legal principle that ensures a person is considered innocent until proven guilty in a court of law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="bias in AI systems">
      <data key="d0">bias in AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias in AI systems refers to systematic errors that lead to unfair outcomes, often affecting certain groups or individuals disproportionately.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Victimization Risk Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Victimization Risk Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Victimization risk assessment involves evaluating the likelihood of an individual becoming a victim of crime, often utilizing AI systems for analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Profiling Tools">
      <data key="d0">Profiling Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Profiling tools, including polygraphs, are used to evaluate personal characteristics and criminal behavior patterns for investigative purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criminal Offences">
      <data key="d0">Criminal Offences</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal offences are actions that violate laws, enforceable by legal penalties, and can involve extensive investigations by law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Criminal offences are actions that violate the law and are prosecuted under legal systems, which may involve individuals assessed by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Criminal offences refer to actions that violate laws and are punishable by the state, which AI systems may be used to detect, prevent, or investigate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593116201bc6ad18de913cc89dec1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcb340351b261f219fcf1a78d4f2f70</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Proceedings">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Proceedings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative proceedings involve processes conducted by governmental agencies, such as tax and customs authorities, which may not classify as high-risk AI use in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="defence rights">
      <data key="d0">defence rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Defence rights refer to the legal protections and rights afforded to individuals suspected of crimes, which ensure fair treatment in legal proceedings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c050cd15355d97e10ed144cad8796e7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="tools">
      <data key="d0">tools</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Tools refer to various legal mechanisms or instruments employed in the justice system to ensure the rights of suspects are upheld.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c050cd15355d97e10ed144cad8796e7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="functioning of systems">
      <data key="d0">functioning of systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The functioning of systems involves the operation and procedures of legal mechanisms that impact how suspects are treated in investigations and courtroom processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c050cd15355d97e10ed144cad8796e7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="court">
      <data key="d0">court</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Court is a formal judicial setting where legal proceedings take place, including the challenging of evidence and the rights of suspects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c050cd15355d97e10ed144cad8796e7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="suspects">
      <data key="d0">suspects</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Suspects are individuals who are under investigation for potential involvement in a crime and who have specific rights under the law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c050cd15355d97e10ed144cad8796e7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Institutions">
      <data key="d0">EU Institutions</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73</data>
      <data key="d2">Union institutions are responsible for establishing the guidelines and regulations surrounding the use of high-risk AI systems by law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standardisation Development Processes">
      <data key="d0">Standardisation Development Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Standardisation Development Processes refer to the activities aimed at establishing norms and standards for AI systems, which SMEs are invited to participate in.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427022</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Fees">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Fees</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Fees are charges levied on businesses, including SMEs, for procedures evaluating conformity to regulatory standards, particularly in the AI field.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Fees are charges related to the evaluation of compliance with standards, which are significant for SMEs and start-ups.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Fees refer to the costs associated with the evaluation process to ensure compliance with regulatory standards specific to the AI sector.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment fees refer to the costs associated with assessing whether products meet regulatory standards, which are adjusted for SMEs based on their size and market conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8363b7ff75e2a59a44c744564b484596</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Information Platforms">
      <data key="d0">Information Platforms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Information Platforms are resources developed to provide guidance and easy access to regulations and best practices for SMEs and startup operators in the AI sector.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427028</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Communication Campaigns">
      <data key="d0">Communication Campaigns</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Communication Campaigns are initiatives organized to raise awareness about the obligations and requirements set forth by the Regulation regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Communication Campaigns are organized efforts by the European Commission to raise awareness of regulatory obligations among SMEs and start-ups regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Communication Campaigns focus on raising awareness about regulatory obligations and are organized to help SMEs and start-ups understand compliance better.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="start-ups">
      <data key="d0">start-ups</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Start-ups are early-stage companies that are also considered within the economic interest context when outlining rules related to penalties.&lt;SEP&gt;Start-ups refer to newly established businesses, often characterized by innovative ideas and a need for support in compliance and costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c0980cd75cdf016ff776144a4a70db</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428007</data>
    </node>
    <node id="public procurement procedures">
      <data key="d0">public procurement procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public procurement procedures are methods through which public authorities purchase goods and services, including AI systems, with an emphasis on compliance and best practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427028</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Certification Costs">
      <data key="d0">Certification Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Certification Costs include expenses that SMEs and start-ups must manage when complying with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427028</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standardised Templates">
      <data key="d0">Standardised Templates</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Standardised Templates are predefined formats developed for areas covered by the Regulation to facilitate compliance and consistency among operators.&lt;SEP&gt;Standardised Templates refer to pre-prepared formats provided to assist SMEs in aligning with regulations, facilitating easier compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single Information Platform">
      <data key="d0">Single Information Platform</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Single Information Platform is a designated resource for public access to information regarding AI regulatory sandboxes and related reports.&lt;SEP&gt;The Single Information Platform is an initiative aimed at providing accessible information for SMEs regarding regulations and compliance processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Single Information Platform is intended to provide centralized, easy-to-use information regarding the Regulation for operators across the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Best Practices in Public Procurement Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Best Practices in Public Procurement Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Best Practices in Public Procurement Procedures involve strategies and methods that enhance efficiency and compliance in public contracting processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427028</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission Recommendation">
      <data key="d0">Commission Recommendation</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission Recommendation refers to a governance body that provides guidelines and definitions related to micro, small and medium-sized enterprises.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04be7eea1639aca68b0fb6dbe2e4fadd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="medium-sized enterprises">
      <data key="d0">medium-sized enterprises</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Medium-sized enterprises are businesses that fall within a specific classification often used in regulatory contexts to determine eligibility for various support measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04be7eea1639aca68b0fb6dbe2e4fadd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="support measures">
      <data key="d0">support measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Support measures refer to various policies and resources available to help medium-sized enterprises understand and comply with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04be7eea1639aca68b0fb6dbe2e4fadd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="micro enterprises">
      <data key="d0">micro enterprises</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Micro enterprises are small businesses that often have limited resources, and they are defined within regulatory frameworks for support and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04be7eea1639aca68b0fb6dbe2e4fadd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="small enterprises">
      <data key="d0">small enterprises</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Small enterprises are businesses that fall between micro and medium-sized, also defined by regulatory frameworks for eligibility for support measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04be7eea1639aca68b0fb6dbe2e4fadd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Value Chain">
      <data key="d0">AI Value Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI value chain encompasses the various stages, processes, and responsibilities involved in developing and deploying AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain encompasses all stages of AI model development, deployment, and monitoring, including collaboration with various stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI value chain encompasses all processes and activities involved in developing, deploying, and regulating AI technologies and their applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46a2185c0e7d022c2e0146a9f59929c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/101/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428624</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Protection">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity protection involves measures taken to secure AI models and systems from potential risks and vulnerabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity protection involves safeguarding AI models and their infrastructure from systemic risks, including cyberattacks and unauthorized access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Evaluations">
      <data key="d0">Model Evaluations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model evaluations are assessments conducted to ensure that AI models meet safety and performance standards before being placed on the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427045</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Testing">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Adversarial testing involves evaluating AI models under challenging conditions to identify vulnerabilities and potential risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427045</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management Policies">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management Policies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk-management policies are strategies implemented by providers to mitigate systemic risks associated with AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427045</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Market Monitoring">
      <data key="d0">Post-Market Monitoring</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-market monitoring refers to the ongoing assessment of AI models after they have been released to ensure their continued safety and effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427045</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Whistleblower">
      <data key="d0">Whistleblower</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A whistleblower is an individual who reports or exposes information on illegal or unethical activities within an organization, and is protected under Union law as per Directive (EU) 2019/1937.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5878750a2a2a6290f1a946976f92b6e4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/172/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Protection of Whistleblowers">
      <data key="d0">Protection of Whistleblowers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The protection of whistleblowers refers to legal safeguards provided to individuals who report misconduct, ensuring they are not subject to retaliation or discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5878750a2a2a6290f1a946976f92b6e4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/172/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorized Representative">
      <data key="d0">Authorized Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An authorized representative is a designated individual or entity appointed by a provider to act on their behalf in matters related to AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Authorized Representative is a person or entity appointed by providers from third countries to ensure compliance with EU regulations regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Authorized Representatives act on behalf of providers concerning regulatory compliance and communication with authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3af424118c8f8024a835a3de370430b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427828</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation on AI">
      <data key="d0">Regulation on AI</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Regulation on AI aims to improve the internal market for AI systems and ensure safety, protection of rights, and innovation within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation on Artificial Intelligence establishes a governance framework to coordinate and support the application of AI legislation at the national and Union levels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c21c2e02a12c7ec585b20f1ef155db81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission Decision of 24.1.2024">
      <data key="d0">Commission Decision of 24.1.2024</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission Decision establishes the European Artificial Intelligence Office and outlines its mission and responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission Decision of 24.1.2024 is a regulatory decision establishing the European Artificial Intelligence Office to enhance governance in AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8673fa897637be6cc00c6fd7cfbcafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EuroHPC Joint Undertaking">
      <data key="d0">EuroHPC Joint Undertaking</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The EuroHPC Joint Undertaking supports high-performance computing in Europe and is part of initiatives related to AI and digital technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance Framework">
      <data key="d0">Governance Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Governance Framework refers to the system established to coordinate and support the application of the Regulation on AI at both national and Union levels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Community">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Community</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Scientific Community includes experts and researchers engaged in the study and development of AI technologies, collaborating with regulatory bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Community is comprised of researchers and experts who provide insights and contributions to the implementation of AI regulations and advancements in the field.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Testing and Experimentation Facilities">
      <data key="d0">AI Testing and Experimentation Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">These facilities are part of the Digital Europe Programme aimed at advancing AI research, experimentation, and validation of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e28a697924414bd64214b20162364786</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Europe Programme">
      <data key="d0">Digital Europe Programme</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Digital Europe Programme is a European Union initiative focused on enhancing digital transformation across the EU member states, particularly through investment in digital technology and infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digital Europe Programme is a funding initiative by the European Union designed to support digital innovation and transformation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-816d4247559a68f4b8ceca952f4e1069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8673fa897637be6cc00c6fd7cfbcafb</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/144/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/148/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA">
      <data key="d0">Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA is a legal framework established for the European arrest warrant and the procedures for surrendering individuals between EU member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA relates to procedures regarding European arrest warrants among EU member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA outlines a framework for the European Union's procedural law regarding criminal offences and law enforcement cooperation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afaea4dcd95d49cc4d21cf9078216b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2bf8c519aff48aa30866bbefc0dc688</data>
