    <node id="European Central Bank">
      <data key="d0">European Central Bank</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Central Bank (ECB) is the central bank for the Euro and plays a crucial role in overseeing monetary policy within the Eurozone. It is responsible for the supervision of credit institutions and the stability and functioning of the financial system. The ECB's duties include not only implementing monetary policy but also ensuring the integrity and supervision of financial institutions within the European Union. By performing these tasks, the ECB contributes to the overall financial stability and prudential oversight of the Eurozone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-822d11ee35b843c977677acb37cb5e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceb3dc76830ec642fabf4620edacf57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5e21dde5d3a662be4300c54e8c07a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5feee5d6760dd9294ff28632c1064eee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/158/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427562</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2013/36/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2013/36/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2013/36/EU is a comprehensive regulation established by the European Parliament and Council, aimed at the prudential supervision of credit institutions and investment firms within the European Union. This directive focuses on ensuring access to these financial entities and outlines specific regulatory requirements that are crucial for maintaining financial stability in the banking sector. It sets forth the capital requirements necessary for credit institutions and investment firms, reinforcing the overall stability and health of the financial system in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-822d11ee35b843c977677acb37cb5e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceb3dc76830ec642fabf4620edacf57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f916ea8f111ac8a27b80c713b9819522&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5feee5d6760dd9294ff28632c1064eee</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/158/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 575/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 575/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 575/2013 outlines prudential requirements for credit institutions and investment firms.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 575/2013 sets capital requirements for credit institutions and investment firms within the European Union to ensure financial stability and resilience.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5feee5d6760dd9294ff28632c1064eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceb3dc76830ec642fabf4620edacf57</data>
