    <node id="15 October 2013">
      <data key="d0">15 October 2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The date on which the Council Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 was enacted, marking a significant step in financial regulation across Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db5e21dde5d3a662be4300c54e8c07a9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/158/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Credit Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Credit Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Credit Institutions are entities authorized to accept deposits and provide loans, regulated prudentially by the European Central Bank under the relevant regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db5e21dde5d3a662be4300c54e8c07a9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/158/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law-Enforcement Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Law-Enforcement Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Law-enforcement authorities are responsible for maintaining public order and safety, and may use high-risk AI systems in urgent situations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civil Protection Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Civil Protection Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil protection authorities are involved in emergency management and can deploy high-risk AI systems during urgent security threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Security">
      <data key="d0">Public Security</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Security refers to the measures and protocols established to protect the safety and welfare of the general public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Protection of Life and Health">
      <data key="d0">Protection of Life and Health</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Protection of Life and Health relates to measures aimed at ensuring individuals' safety and well-being against potential threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Environmental Protection">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Environmental Protection encompasses efforts and regulations aimed at preserving the natural environment, which is a priority for the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Protection encompasses policies and actions taken to safeguard the environment, natural resources, and ecosystems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a11bcb90e7333ffe457649980a31a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/2/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Key Industrial and Infrastructural Assets">
      <data key="d0">Key Industrial and Infrastructural Assets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Key Industrial and Infrastructural Assets refer to essential facilities and resources crucial for the functioning of society and the economy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Urgent Situations">
      <data key="d0">Urgent Situations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Urgent Situations are scenarios requiring immediate action due to significant threats to safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Urgent situations refer to circumstances that necessitate the immediate use of biometric identification systems without prior authorization due to pressing needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Urgent Situations describe scenarios that necessitate the immediate use of biometric identification systems without prior authorization due to pressing law enforcement needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26fcdeec947c5dfd024232093934843&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce4de2ee2430b55395c19336af7c01</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/35/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sensitivity of Operational Data">
      <data key="d0">Sensitivity of Operational Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sensitivity of Operational Data refers to confidential information related to the activities of law-enforcement authorities which must be safeguarded in the regulatory process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2207c69786b5e6add33d2fe8c768a341</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorization Process">
      <data key="d0">Authorization Process</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Authorization Process is the procedure through which the Market Surveillance Authority assesses and grants permits for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2207c69786b5e6add33d2fe8c768a341</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trading Unions">
      <data key="d0">Trading Unions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade unions represent the interests of workers and stakeholders in various industries, emphasizing the importance of inclusive practices in AI development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427136</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethical AI Guidelines">
      <data key="d0">Ethical AI Guidelines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethical AI guidelines provide a framework for developing AI technologies that prioritize trustworthiness, sustainability, and inclusivity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unions Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">Unions Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union’s Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI outline the fundamental principles and practices to ensure that AI systems are developed ethically and responsibly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance Mechanisms">
      <data key="d0">Governance Mechanisms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Governance mechanisms are structures and processes established to guide the ethical development, implementation, and monitoring of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Persons">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulnerable Persons encompasses groups that may be negatively impacted by AI systems, including individuals with disabilities and those affected by gender inequality.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable persons are individuals or groups who are at a higher risk of experiencing negative impacts from AI systems, including those with disabilities and gender inequalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable persons are individuals or groups who may be at greater risk of being adversely affected by AI systems and require special consideration in their development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30361d2283908d9b7babf63ae110a691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Cards">
      <data key="d0">Data Cards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data cards are tools that provide detailed information about the datasets used in AI systems, promoting transparency and ethical use of data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Stakeholders">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Stakeholders</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant stakeholders include business organizations, civil society organizations, academia, research organizations, trade unions, and consumer protection organizations involved in the development of initiatives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Barriers">
      <data key="d0">Technical Barriers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical barriers are obstacles that impede cross-border exchange of data and can hinder advancements in AI development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Business Organizations">
      <data key="d0">Business Organizations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Business organizations are entities involved in commerce and industry that may engage in developing voluntary codes of conduct and participating in sector initiatives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Research Organizations">
      <data key="d0">Research Organizations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Research organizations conduct studies and analyses that can shape policies and contribute to discussions surrounding data ethics and AI development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trade Unions">
      <data key="d0">Trade Unions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trade unions represent the interests of workers and can play a role in discussions about ethical practices and standards in the workplace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Protection Organizations">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Protection Organizations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer protection organizations advocate for the rights of consumers, ensuring that business practices adhere to ethical and regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b68a8b56a88e15576658c21fedd417e3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Solutions">
      <data key="d0">AI Solutions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Solutions refer to the technologies and applications of artificial intelligence aimed at achieving beneficial social and environmental outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-813ac9e32b54acc82ef6b73432a7cd7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/142/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Socio-Economic Inequalities">
      <data key="d0">Socio-Economic Inequalities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Socio-Economic Inequalities refer to disparities in wealth, income, and access to resources within society, which AI solutions aim to tackle.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-813ac9e32b54acc82ef6b73432a7cd7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/142/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Environmental Targets">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Targets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Environmental Targets are goals set to address environmental issues, which can be supported by AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-813ac9e32b54acc82ef6b73432a7cd7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/142/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Research and Development">
      <data key="d0">Research and Development</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Research and Development involves initiatives to create and improve AI solutions that align with social and environmental objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-813ac9e32b54acc82ef6b73432a7cd7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/142/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Interdisciplinary Cooperation">
      <data key="d0">Interdisciplinary Cooperation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Interdisciplinary Cooperation involves collaboration among experts from diverse fields like AI, social sciences, and environmental rights to develop solutions addressing key societal issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-813ac9e32b54acc82ef6b73432a7cd7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/142/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Workplace">
      <data key="d0">Workplace</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Workplace contexts are environments where AI systems may be used to assess emotional states, presenting ethical concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Education">
      <data key="d0">Education</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Education contexts are environments where the use of AI for detecting emotional states could lead to biased treatment of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Education is the formal process through which individuals acquire knowledge and skills relevant to the operation of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Education refers to the system through which learners acquire knowledge and skills, essential for participation in society and the economy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5df3c87d284ff92767412c5cae8b463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f557a252b7f04ee224d608a6628bd4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/4/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/56/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Concerns about AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Concerns about AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Concerns about AI systems refer to the serious issues regarding their ability to identify or infer emotions, highlighting ethical implications and reliability challenges.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Basis">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Basis</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The scientific basis for AI systems involves the foundational theories and principles that govern their ability to understand emotions, which are debated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Limited Reliability">
      <data key="d0">Limited Reliability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Limited reliability refers to the inconsistency of AI systems in accurately detecting or interpreting emotions across different contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lack of Specificity">
      <data key="d0">Lack of Specificity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Lack of specificity indicates that AI systems struggle to provide precise assessments of emotional states, leading to potential misinterpretations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Limited Generalisability">
      <data key="d0">Limited Generalisability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Limited generalisability denotes the AI systems' capability to operate effectively across diverse populations and cultures, which is often insufficient.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intrusive Technology">
      <data key="d0">Intrusive Technology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Intrusive technology refers to AI systems that may infringe on the privacy and rights of individuals by monitoring emotional states without consent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Power Imbalance">
      <data key="d0">Power Imbalance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Power imbalance highlights the unequal dynamics present in contexts like work or education, exacerbated by the use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prohibition of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Prohibition of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Prohibition of AI systems refers to the recommendation against the use of certain AI technologies in workplaces and educational settings to prevent harm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Medical or Safety Reasons">
      <data key="d0">Medical or Safety Reasons</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Exceptions for using AI systems include scenarios strictly for medical or safety purposes, such as therapeutic use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0c80a9013101dc32f29be5f179a89f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/44/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributors">
      <data key="d0">Distributors</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Distributors are entities involved in the distribution of high-risk AI systems and are notified regarding any non-compliance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are entities responsible for making high-risk AI systems available on the market and ensuring compliance with relevant regulations and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are operators responsible for the dissemination of AI systems and have legal obligations related to their role.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-66e6524323a5bff7a82ba7868399e18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/83/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Competent Authority">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Competent Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant Competent Authorities are governmental bodies that regulate and oversee the compliance of high-risk AI systems in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Relevant competent authorities are regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing the compliance and safety of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427151</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section 2 Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Section 2 Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 2 Requirements refer to the specific safety and compliance standards that high-risk AI systems must meet according to regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427151</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 16">
      <data key="d0">Article 16</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 16 of the AI Value Chain Regulation details the obligations of providers of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 outlines specific obligations of providers and importers related to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 outlines the obligations of providers regarding compliance and operational standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc759fa1feac4c57c23af89232f9785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorities Competent for High-Risk AI">
      <data key="d0">Authorities Competent for High-Risk AI</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorities competent for high-risk AI are regulatory bodies tasked with overseeing compliance and safety regulations of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1c74c72b39d6d10e4a07d1cd427ae52</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427151</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk Management encompasses strategies, processes, and practices aimed at identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks to ensure safety and compliance in various contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk Management is the systematic process of identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks associated with high-risk AI systems to ensure safety and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk management involves identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks to prevent negative outcomes, particularly in the context of technology and societal impact.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e6dce971d3a69afaac4e79066740b9aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff9241c3a9f5f8fc78557cf5705c8c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2116d706005368a535fd7d7c2950cc6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Publicly Accessible Space">
      <data key="d0">Publicly Accessible Space</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly accessible spaces are physical spaces that can be accessed by an undetermined number of individuals, irrespective of their purpose or ownership.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Private Spaces">
      <data key="d0">Private Spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Private spaces are areas restricted to specific individuals, not considered publicly accessible according to the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Company Premises">
      <data key="d0">Company Premises</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Company premises refer to locations that are managed by companies and are typically intended for employee access only.&lt;SEP&gt;Company premises refer to spaces intended solely for employees and service providers, thus not publicly accessible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Roads and Squares">
      <data key="d0">Public Roads and Squares</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public roads and squares are examples of publicly accessible spaces available for general use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Transport Stations">
      <data key="d0">Public Transport Stations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Bus, metro, and railway stations are included in the definition of publicly accessible spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sports Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Sports Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sports facilities such as swimming pools and gyms are categorized under publicly accessible spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Company and Factory Premises">
      <data key="d0">Company and Factory Premises</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Company and factory premises are non-public spaces meant for employees and service providers, thus excluded from publicly accessible classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Company and factory premises refer to locations that are intended to be accessed only by employees and service providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Roads">
      <data key="d0">Public Roads</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public roads are thoroughfares open to general use, classified as publicly accessible spaces as per the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transport Stations">
      <data key="d0">Transport Stations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transport stations, such as bus and railway stations, are examples of publicly accessible spaces where the public can enter and utilize transport services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Publicly Accessible Spaces Exclusions">
      <data key="d0">Publicly Accessible Spaces Exclusions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Certain spaces, like prisons and border controls, are explicitly excluded from being classified as publicly accessible spaces according to the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Context">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Context</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The regulatory context outlines the specific definitions and criteria involved in determining whether spaces are publicly accessible or not.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-470a46267ef42cc1327012a494ce0ac4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Private Residential Building">
      <data key="d0">Private Residential Building</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A private residential building may have hallways that are both publicly accessible and non-publicly accessible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Online Spaces">
      <data key="d0">Online Spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Online spaces are digital environments that are not considered physical spaces and therefore are not included in the discussion of accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Safety Law">
      <data key="d0">Public Safety Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public safety law encompasses regulations intended to ensure the safety and security of the public in various environments and situations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Authority">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The relevant authority is an individual or entity that possesses the official power to determine access to specific spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Factory Premises">
      <data key="d0">Factory Premises</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Factory premises are industrial locations used for manufacturing, designed to be accessed only by workers and service providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Offices and Workplaces">
      <data key="d0">Offices and Workplaces</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Offices and workplaces are areas specifically set up for work-related activities, meant to be utilized by authorized personnel only.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Accessibility">
      <data key="d0">Public Accessibility</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public accessibility defines whether physical spaces can be accessed by the general public or are restricted to authorized individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Signage Restrictions">
      <data key="d0">Signage Restrictions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Signage restrictions refer to the use of signs that indicate prohibitions or limitations on access to certain areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prisons">
      <data key="d0">Prisons</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Prisons are facilities that are not publicly accessible, serving as confinement locations for individuals who have been sentenced.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Border Control">
      <data key="d0">Border Control</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Border control pertains to measures taken by governments to regulate who or what enters or exits a country, often utilizing AI technologies for identification purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control refers to regulations and procedures at international borders that restrict public access to specific areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Individual Situation">
      <data key="d0">Individual Situation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Individual situation involves the unique context or circumstances surrounding a particular case of accessibility, requiring specific assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Locked Door">
      <data key="d0">Locked Door</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A locked door is a physical barrier indicating restricted access, which affects the evaluation of public accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open Gate">
      <data key="d0">Open Gate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An open gate serves as an indication of potential public access, though it needs to be assessed in conjunction with other factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e5e0a46da340ff1e11fc349f59e9e0a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/19/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427162</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model">
      <data key="d0">Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model refers to a conceptual representation or framework that can be determined by various parameters and is capable of performing distinctive tasks when trained with a large amount of data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7998dcefaedb3e70eebeb29bedc0789f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/98/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Supervision">
      <data key="d0">Self-Supervision</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-supervision is a training strategy that utilizes a large amount of data to enhance a model's ability to learn and generalize across tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7998dcefaedb3e70eebeb29bedc0789f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/98/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distinctive Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Distinctive Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Distinctive tasks are specific activities or functions that a model is trained to perform, showcasing its capabilities and versatility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7998dcefaedb3e70eebeb29bedc0789f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/98/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="significant generality">
      <data key="d0">significant generality</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7998dcefaedb3e70eebeb29bedc0789f</data>
      <data key="d2">The model is characterized by significant generality when it displays a wide range of capabilities after training.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/98/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Water Supply">
      <data key="d0">Water Supply</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Water supply systems are critical components of infrastructure, requiring AI systems for monitoring and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gas Supply">
      <data key="d0">Gas Supply</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Gas supply systems are vital for energy provision and can involve safety components monitored by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Heating Supply">
      <data key="d0">Heating Supply</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Heating supply systems are an essential part of infrastructure, monitored for safety through critical systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electricity Supply">
      <data key="d0">Electricity Supply</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electricity supply systems are fundamental for modern society and require oversight by safety components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Failure of Safety Components">
      <data key="d0">Failure of Safety Components</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Failure or malfunction of safety components can lead to risks impacting public health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cloud Computing Centres">
      <data key="d0">Cloud Computing Centres</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Cloud computing centres are facilities that manage digital data and may require fire alarm control systems as safety components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">Digital Infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital Infrastructure includes systems and technologies essential for managing data and support operations within critical sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Water Management Systems">
      <data key="d0">Water Management Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Water Management Systems are critical components of infrastructure that require accurate monitoring to ensure public health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gas Management Systems">
      <data key="d0">Gas Management Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Gas Management Systems are essential for the safe delivery of gas and include monitoring systems as safety components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Heating Management Systems">
      <data key="d0">Heating Management Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Heating Management Systems are designed to maintain safe temperatures and operate effectively within critical infrastructure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electricity Management Systems">
      <data key="d0">Electricity Management Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electricity Management Systems are infrastructure components that require strict safety protocols to avoid failures and ensure public safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Components">
      <data key="d0">Safety Components</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety Components are systems intended to safeguard public health and infrastructure integrity, crucial for risk management.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety components refer to the integral elements of products that ensure their operational safety, particularly when AI systems are involved.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-192f03d2933ad10489c5b8a9e36d2ccf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/47/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Components">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Components</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity Components protect digital infrastructure but are distinguished from safety components as they do not directly manage physical safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fire Alarm Systems">
      <data key="d0">Fire Alarm Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fire Alarm Systems are safety components used within cloud computing centres to protect against fire hazards and ensure operational continuity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Monitoring Systems">
      <data key="d0">Monitoring Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Monitoring Systems are technologies used to oversee the performance and safety of critical infrastructure operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194a93e438ef6e42d5b44a136147cfaf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/55/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notifying authority">
      <data key="d0">notifying authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The notifying authority is responsible for communicating changes and ensuring compliance among notified bodies and Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;The notifying authority is responsible for confirming the issuance, amendment, or re-issuance of certificates during the suspension or restriction of a notified body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notification Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Notification Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Notification Procedures refer to the regulatory processes outlined for notifying authorities and notified bodies regarding changes in activities or compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Certificate">
      <data key="d0">Certificate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Certificate is an official document validating the conformity of a product, which may remain valid for a specified period after a notified body ceases activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electronic Notification Tool">
      <data key="d0">Electronic Notification Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Electronic Notification Tool is a system used by notifying authorities to communicate changes regarding notified bodies efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cessation of Activities">
      <data key="d0">Cessation of Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cessation of Activities refers to the process in which a notified body stops its conformity assessment activities, leading to required notifications to relevant authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7386be7bd3bdbe2e4df94de9c70d8784</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Certificates">
      <data key="d0">Certificates</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Certificates are documents issued by notified bodies that confirm compliance with designated regulations and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Certificates are official documents that validate compliance with regulations for high-risk AI systems, indicating that they have met necessary safety and operational standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Certificates are formal documents issued by notified bodies that validate compliance with relevant standards for AI systems, with specified validity periods and requirements for extension or reassessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65d9e388dd47f8c8604a909fc7bfa39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcf2e7f28d217ab321153caf980fbfe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/44/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428589</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Legal Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal requirements are defined standards and regulations that organizations must comply with, particularly in relation to designated bodies and certification processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5bcf2e7f28d217ab321153caf980fbfe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427199</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Body Certificates">
      <data key="d0">Notified Body Certificates</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Notified Body Certificates refer to certifications issued by designated bodies to ensure that high-risk AI systems meet EU regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Suspension of Certificates">
      <data key="d0">Suspension of Certificates</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Suspension of Certificates refers to the temporary halting of certifications by the authority to ensure compliance and safety of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Withdrawal of Designation">
      <data key="d0">Withdrawal of Designation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Withdrawal of Designation occurs when a Notified Body is stripped of its authority to issue certificates due to non-compliance or risk factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="provider of the high-risk AI system">
      <data key="d0">provider of the high-risk AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The provider of the high-risk AI system is responsible for confirming the temporary assignment of monitoring functions to another notified body during suspension.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Suspension">
      <data key="d0">Suspension</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Suspension refers to the temporary halt of activities or validations related to a Notified Body, often due to issues with compliance or operational capacity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Restriction">
      <data key="d0">Restriction</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Restriction describes limitations placed on a Notified Body's ability to function or issue certificates, usually due to regulatory concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Existing Certificates">
      <data key="d0">Existing Certificates</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Existing Certificates are certifications that remain valid during a suspension or restriction under specific conditions outlined by regulatory authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Competent Authority">
      <data key="d0">National Competent Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Competent Authorities are governmental bodies responsible for overseeing compliance with AI regulations within their jurisdictions and coordinating sandbox activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Competent Authority is responsible for overseeing and regulating AI systems within its jurisdiction, including the issuance and management of relevant certifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56424a5db573173fc67a6e62dd2d96b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provisional Validity Certificate">
      <data key="d0">Provisional Validity Certificate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Provisional Validity Certificate is a temporary certification indicating that an AI system meets basic compliance criteria while undergoing further evaluation and assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d56424a5db573173fc67a6e62dd2d96b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Designation Withdrawal">
      <data key="d0">Designation Withdrawal</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Designation Withdrawal refers to the formal process when a certification or regulatory status for an AI system is revoked, leading to reassessment and potential new certifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d56424a5db573173fc67a6e62dd2d96b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider of the High-Risk AI System">
      <data key="d0">Provider of the High-Risk AI System</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba</data>
      <data key="d2">The provider of the High-Risk AI System must inform National Competent Authorities of changes regarding Notified Bodies responsible for monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427202</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Incident Reporting">
      <data key="d0">Incident Reporting</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Incident reporting refers to the process of documenting and notifying relevant authorities about serious incidents involving general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Lifecycle">
      <data key="d0">Model Lifecycle</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model lifecycle refers to the various stages of development and deployment of AI models, which influence risk factors across their existence.&lt;SEP&gt;The model lifecycle refers to the stages through which an AI model progresses, from development to deployment and ongoing maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c51b7bfc502a0e1b7fc0c076f574e26</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/110/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cyberattacks">
      <data key="d0">Cyberattacks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cyberattacks are malicious attempts to compromise the confidentiality, integrity, or availability of AI models and their associated data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Theft">
      <data key="d0">Model Theft</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Model theft involves the unauthorized acquisition of an AI model's underlying algorithms or data, posing significant risks to providers and users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de9b8f7d9312e3a2994cf6e1b14f1f9e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/115/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 63">
      <data key="d0">Article 63</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 63 refers to a specific legislative section that outlines derogations for microenterprises within regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6b3a7a24bfd18cc84baf6173985e105</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/63/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance System">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Market Surveillance System is a framework established to enforce compliance and oversee the safety of products in the market according to regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f123082dcc9e4aa9993ce2a5fd0377de</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/156/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427229</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independent Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Independent Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Independent Compliance refers to the principle that entities under surveillance should carry out their regulated tasks without undue influence or bias.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f123082dcc9e4aa9993ce2a5fd0377de</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/156/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427229</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Large Generative AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Large Generative AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Large generative AI models are categorized as general-purpose AI models that enable the flexible generation of various content forms including text, audio, images, and video.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Generative AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Generative AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Generative AI models are designed to produce various forms of content, showcasing flexibility and adaptability across multiple tasks and formats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content">
      <data key="d0">Content</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Content refers to any form of information or experience created for communication, including text, audio, images, and video.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Audio">
      <data key="d0">Audio</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Audio is a form of media that comprises sound recordings, including music, spoken word, and ambient sounds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Images">
      <data key="d0">Images</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Images are visual representations that can take various forms such as photographs, drawings, and digital art.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Video">
      <data key="d0">Video</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Video is a format for visual content that combines moving images and audio to convey information or entertainment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427243</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Horizon Europe">
      <data key="d0">Horizon Europe</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Horizon Europe is the EU Research and Innovation programme aimed at fostering innovation and maintaining Europe's competitiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-816d4247559a68f4b8ceca952f4e1069</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/144/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Funding Programmes">
      <data key="d0">Union Funding Programmes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Funding Programmes encompass various financial schemes established by the EU to support projects in member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-816d4247559a68f4b8ceca952f4e1069</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/144/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 66">
      <data key="d0">Recital 66</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 66 refers to a legislative event or reference, focusing on requirements for high-risk AI systems regarding risk management, data quality, and transparency, among other aspects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2116d706005368a535fd7d7c2950cc6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427248</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health">
      <data key="d0">Health</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Health pertains to the state of being free from illness or injury, which is a fundamental right being safeguarded through the requirements for AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Health refers to the physical and mental well-being of individuals, which can be impacted by the application of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2116d706005368a535fd7d7c2950cc6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427487</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety">
      <data key="d0">Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety encompasses the measures and protocols implemented to protect individuals from harm when interacting with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety entails the condition of being protected from or unlikely to cause danger, risk, or injury, emphasized in the context of AI system requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety involves the condition of being protected from or unlikely to cause danger, risk, or injury, crucial when evaluating high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2116d706005368a535fd7d7c2950cc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428066</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Market Monitoring Plan">
      <data key="d0">Post-Market Monitoring Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Post-Market Monitoring Plan outlines the documentation and monitoring requirements set by the Commission for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-474278e863b3ff46a7c4578eb30850a5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427253</data>
    </node>
    <node id="post-market monitoring system">
      <data key="d0">post-market monitoring system</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A post-market monitoring system is a regulatory framework that ensures the ongoing scrutiny and compliance of products, particularly high-risk AI systems, after they have entered the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paragraph 1">
      <data key="d0">paragraph 1</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraph 1 references a specific part of the legislative text that discusses the integration of necessary elements for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Paragraph 1 refers to the initial section that discusses the objectives and conditions regarding the use of biometric identification systems, highlighting necessary legal frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17b23a5bf3ea6e9c99542abdf17cfaa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paragraph 2">
      <data key="d0">paragraph 2</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraph 2 discusses provisions regarding the consistency in legislating for high-risk AI systems to avoid duplications and additional burdens on providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Paragraph 2 discusses the procedural requirements for notifying authorities regarding the use of biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17b23a5bf3ea6e9c99542abdf17cfaa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paragraph 3">
      <data key="d0">paragraph 3</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraph 3 describes the powers afforded to Member States to authorize biometric identification systems under specified legal conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Paragraph 3 outlines the requirements that providers of high-risk AI systems must meet when integrating existing systems with new legislations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17b23a5bf3ea6e9c99542abdf17cfaa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3adfd2c3d24b0ffaaec321d3b79c3f39</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/72/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Machine Learning Approaches">
      <data key="d0">Machine Learning Approaches</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Machine learning approaches are techniques used by AI systems to learn from data to achieve specific objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Logic and Knowledge-Based Approaches">
      <data key="d0">Logic and Knowledge-Based Approaches</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Logic and knowledge-based approaches are methodologies enabling AI systems to infer from encoded knowledge or symbolic representation of tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data">
      <data key="d0">Data</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Data is the input used by AI systems to learn and make inferences, impacting their capabilities and outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Data refers to information collected and processed by systems, including personal information and inputs required for AI operations, and is subject to legal and regulatory frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;Data refers to the information used for training, testing, and validating AI Systems, critical for ensuring their effectiveness and regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22fe2322637df933b39b478cbc8c7a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2252cbe714fc3b6aee570acd5f270ef</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Outputs">
      <data key="d0">Outputs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Outputs are the results generated by AI systems, including predictions, content, recommendations, or decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Environments">
      <data key="d0">Environments</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Environments refer to the various contexts in which AI systems operate, influencing their functions and interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Environments represent the contexts in which AI systems operate, influencing their functionality and interaction with users or other systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Autonomy">
      <data key="d0">Autonomy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Autonomy describes the capacity of AI systems to operate independently, showcasing self-learning and adaptiveness capabilities after deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Autonomy describes the degree to which AI systems can operate independently of human intervention and control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Learning Capabilities">
      <data key="d0">Self-Learning Capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-Learning Capabilities refer to the ability of AI systems to adapt and improve their performance based on accumulated experience and data.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-learning capabilities are features that allow AI systems to adapt and improve based on their experience and data after deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5f473c726cccbd493c4eb35ca6cec8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objectives">
      <data key="d0">Objectives</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Objectives refer to the defined goals or purposes that guide the operation of AI systems, which may differ from their intended purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427266</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Functional Outputs">
      <data key="d0">Functional Outputs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Functional Outputs are the results generated by AI systems, which can include predictions, recommendations, or decisions made by the systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427266</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stand-alone Basis">
      <data key="d0">Stand-alone Basis</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Stand-alone Basis indicates that AI systems can function independently, without being integrated into other products or systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427266</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Embedded Systems">
      <data key="d0">Embedded Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Embedded Systems are AI systems that are physically integrated into products, enhancing their capabilities and enabling smarter functionalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427266</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Embedded Systems">
      <data key="d0">Non-Embedded Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-Embedded Systems refer to AI systems that provide functionality without being integrated into products, working in tandem with them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427266</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometrics">
      <data key="d0">Biometrics</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometrics involve the measurement and statistical analysis of people's unique physical and behavioral characteristics, often used in security and identification processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427278</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Migration">
      <data key="d0">Migration</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Migration deals with the movement of people from one place to another, often across national borders, and is subject to various regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Migration refers to the process by which individuals move from one place to another, often for reasons such as seeking asylum, employment, or better living conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Migration refers to the process of individuals moving from one country to another, which may involve the use of high-risk AI systems for identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fcfee58701346b1cdfaa0595c615d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/73/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Asylum">
      <data key="d0">Asylum</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Asylum is a form of international protection given to individuals who have fled their home country due to persecution or fear of persecution.&lt;SEP&gt;Asylum is protection granted to individuals in a foreign country due to the fear of persecution in their home country.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administration of Justice">
      <data key="d0">Administration of Justice</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Administration of Justice encompasses the processes by which legal matters are adjudicated and justice is administered within a legal system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427280</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Artificial Intelligence Board">
      <data key="d0">European Artificial Intelligence Board</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Artificial Intelligence Board is a regulatory body that supports the Commission in promoting AI literacy tools and public awareness regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Board is an entity established to coordinate activities and oversight related to AI across Member States, ensuring active contribution towards Board tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Board is an authoritative body that consults on AI regulations and guidelines within Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Board is an organization consulted by the Commission regarding AI regulations and guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fe20aa0cce0b31f6a43c755317350d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553e3df123166674b26c5dc07f2a83af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b4f722f831bc4c8c4594e971e7b7654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dce9dde15c8e156ca0acc92343929</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/65/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Working Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Working Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Working Conditions refer to the environment and circumstances under which individuals work, which can be improved through the implementation of AI literacy measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-553e3df123166674b26c5dc07f2a83af</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">Trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trustworthy AI refers to AI practices that prioritize safety, ethical standards, and compliance with regulations to gain public and stakeholder trust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-553e3df123166674b26c5dc07f2a83af</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/20/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 58">
      <data key="d0">Article 58</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 58 refers to a regulatory provision that outlines the supervision of AI systems within an AI regulatory sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427298</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 60">
      <data key="d0">Article 60</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 60 deals with the access and user rights concerning data entered in the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 includes compliance criteria and conditions under which testing of AI systems must be conducted.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 refers to the framework that governs testing in real-world conditions, setting the legal precedent for Article 61.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 outlines specific provisions regarding the testing and implementation of high-risk AI systems within the regulatory framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cefadab290f58f81c115a49845f866d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebb00fdd14767c86b1a8c766db05a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951511d7a62f58da07aebc05f3e4f1c1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/61/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427966</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 61">
      <data key="d0">Article 61</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 61 involves procedures that market surveillance authorities follow in case of non-compliance during AI system testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 61 outlines the requirements for informed consent necessary for participation in testing within real-world conditions outside of designated AI regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 61 mandates that informed consent is required from subjects before testing AI systems, ensuring ethical practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebb00fdd14767c86b1a8c766db05a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/61/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428325</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prospective Provider">
      <data key="d0">Prospective Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A prospective provider is a person or entity looking to develop and deploy high-risk AI systems but has not yet done so.&lt;SEP&gt;The prospective provider refers to individuals or entities looking to offer AI systems and are subject to similar regulatory oversight during the testing phase.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428325</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Party">
      <data key="d0">Third Party</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Third parties refer to individuals or entities that may be involved in the testing process and can report compliance issues or incidents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="testing plan">
      <data key="d0">testing plan</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The testing plan refers to the official protocol detailing how the AI system is to be tested for compliance and effectiveness within Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6fadd3405f1febb84753df655c577486</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427308</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 54">
      <data key="d0">Article 54</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 54 refers to a specific regulation concerning authorized representatives of providers of general-purpose AI models in the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427313</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex XI">
      <data key="d0">Annex XI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex XI contains specifications related to the technical documentation that providers must follow when placing general-purpose AI models on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI is part of Directive (EU) 2019/790, detailing compliance requirements and methodologies for AI model documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI outlines the necessary technical documentation requirements for providers of AI models to ensure compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI refers to a specific section of legislation detailing compliance requirements and methodologies for various standards within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91d56158a4a9411ebe99783effcebca7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations are the responsibilities and legal requirements that must be met by users and providers regarding the deployment and use of the AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations refer to the compliance requirements that providers and authorized representatives must adhere to under the regulatory framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations refer to the tasks and responsibilities assigned to providers and authorized representatives under the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations refer to the responsibilities imposed on AI model providers to ensure compliance with copyright laws and transparency in training data usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Obligations refer to the requirements that entities, such as microenterprises, must fulfill in order to comply with regulations and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3917f629d239e59c1197ea2404615c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adccf24f1ddc4835908b879bcbe8674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994612dc34fa7cbfaae3dc6fdd1036d3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/146/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Model">
      <data key="d0">AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI Model refers to a computational model designed to perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, including learning, reasoning, and understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI model is a specific implementation of an AI system that processes input data and generates outputs based on learned patterns and algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343138c98bcd39f893aee610a717cfc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/133/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428465</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI models">
      <data key="d0">AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI models refer to various artificial intelligence systems developed for different applications, and they present systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6a477f9413013f3c0b13fcd9449cbb4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427328</data>
    </node>
    <node id="systemic risks">
      <data key="d0">systemic risks</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6a477f9413013f3c0b13fcd9449cbb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d41f7845b8c737d05150b060d51c16e</data>
      <data key="d2">AI models are associated with systemic risks in terms of their potential impacts and implications in various domains.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risks refer to the potential dangers posed by general-purpose AI models that could affect the entire system, particularly in regulatory contexts.</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 810/2009">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 810/2009</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 810/2009 establishes a Community Code on Visas, impacting travel document verification in the context of migration.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 810/2009 pertains to the establishment of a Community Code on Visas, influencing AI system usage in migration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357608662f50d4cb171a35b1ece5f9da</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees">
      <data key="d0">UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees outlines international obligations to protect refugees and is referenced in the context of AI system regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees provides the framework for international refugee protection, emphasizing the rights of refugees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357608662f50d4cb171a35b1ece5f9da</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Principle of Non-Refoulement">
      <data key="d0">Principle of Non-Refoulement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Principle of Non-Refoulement is a key tenet of international law preventing individuals from being returned to countries where they may face harm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Visa or Asylum Applications">
      <data key="d0">Visa or Asylum Applications</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"Visa or Asylum Applications are the formal processes through which natural persons request permission to enter a country for specific purposes.'</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Union Law">
      <data key="d0">European Union Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">European Union Law encompasses the legal framework and regulations ratified by member states of the EU, including the governance of biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;European Union Law governs the legal framework within which EU member states operate, impacting policies like migration and asylum.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6884d6c4641c256f66289e2e2b56965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Competent Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent Public Authorities are the authorized government bodies responsible for managing migration, asylum applications, and border control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Institutions">
      <data key="d0">European Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">European Institutions encompass various entities within the European Union that formulate and implement policies, including those related to migration and asylum.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Protection of Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Protection of Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Protection of Fundamental Rights refers to the legal safeguards that ensure individuals' rights, including free movement and non-discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation Directive 2013/32/EU">
      <data key="d0">Regulation Directive 2013/32/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2013/32/EU stipulates the procedures for granting and withdrawing international protection by member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13cd7281a4984edb2a5651f8501ee3c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2013/32/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2013/32/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2013/32/EU is a legislative act adopted by the European Parliament and the Council that outlines common procedures for granting and withdrawing international protection in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2013/32/EU outlines common procedures for granting and withdrawing international protection to asylum seekers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46239d1477a3073a0d3894e967d3cb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357608662f50d4cb171a35b1ece5f9da</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Geneva">
      <data key="d0">Geneva</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Geneva is the city where the UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees was originally done.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-357608662f50d4cb171a35b1ece5f9da</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="June 26, 2013">
      <data key="d0">June 26, 2013</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">June 26, 2013, is the date on which Directive 2013/32/EU was issued, marking a significant point in EU legislation regarding international protection procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46239d1477a3073a0d3894e967d3cb7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OJ L 180, 29.6.2013">
      <data key="d0">OJ L 180, 29.6.2013</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">This reference mentions the Official Journal of the European Union through which the directive was published, indicating an official record of legislative acts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46239d1477a3073a0d3894e967d3cb7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Protection">
      <data key="d0">International Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">International Protection refers to the safeguarding of individuals under threat from persecution or serious harm, with procedures established in Directive 2013/32/EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46239d1477a3073a0d3894e967d3cb7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Procedures for Granting and Withdrawing International Protection">
      <data key="d0">Common Procedures for Granting and Withdrawing International Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to the standardized legal processes outlined in the directive for evaluating applications for asylum or refugee status.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46239d1477a3073a0d3894e967d3cb7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessments">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessments</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity assessments are evaluations conducted to determine whether a product meets specific regulatory requirements before being marketed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc730bebf215fc150b211b590e39bd0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/126/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427340</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article R23">
      <data key="d0">Article R23</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article R23 of Annex I to Decision No 768/2008/EC outlines the procedures for notification of bodies involved in conformity assessments in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc730bebf215fc150b211b590e39bd0b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/126/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427340</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decision No 768/2008/EC">
      <data key="d0">Decision No 768/2008/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Decision No 768/2008/EC is a legislative framework that sets forth general principles for the functioning of the internal market regarding conformity assessments in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Decision No 768/2008/EC, enacted by the European Parliament and Council, complements regulations concerning product standards and market entry.&lt;SEP&gt;This decision provides a common framework for the marketing of products in the EU, establishing essential requirements and repealing previous decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc730bebf215fc150b211b590e39bd0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/126/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="August 2, 2026">
      <data key="d0">August 2, 2026</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">August 2, 2026, is the deadline by which Member States are required to ensure their AI regulatory sandboxes are operational at the national level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bba75fb7db46076875feb4aca1bd671</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427349</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exit Reports">
      <data key="d0">Exit Reports</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Exit Reports provide documentation of activities and outcomes for providers participating in the AI regulatory sandbox, facilitating regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427354</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Innovation">
      <data key="d0">Innovation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Innovation in AI refers to the development and implementation of new technologies and systems that enhance productivity and efficiency while adhering to ethical standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Innovation refers to the process of developing new ideas, products, or methods, which is a key focus within AI regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Innovation involves the process of developing new methodologies, ideas, or products, particularly in the context of rapidly evolving technologies like AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1bd36f2082e6f670210d08c02e3d502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec304def59e7573aa1fecc006d51bea7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/138/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Process">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Process</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Conformity Assessment Process involves evaluating whether AI systems meet regulatory requirements before market entry.&lt;SEP&gt;The Conformity Assessment Process is a procedure through which AI systems are evaluated to ensure compliance with regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427354</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Market for AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Union Market for AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Market for AI Systems refers to the marketplace for AI technologies and services within the European Union, subject to regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427358</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs)">
      <data key="d0">Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">SMEs, including start-ups, are businesses that are critical for innovation in the AI ecosystem, particularly in accessing the Union market.&lt;SEP&gt;Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) are businesses whose personnel numbers fall below certain limits. They are particularly mentioned in relation to the imposition of penalties and the consideration of their size during enforcement actions.&lt;SEP&gt;SMEs, including startups, are subject to specific administrative fines under the regulatory framework mentioned.&lt;SEP&gt;Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) are a key focus of the regulation, particularly startups that develop AI solutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c21c2e02a12c7ec585b20f1ef155db81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b14075f9663187b4b9cee91c38f3025d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc759fa1feac4c57c23af89232f9785</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/1/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/168/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/99/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exit Report">
      <data key="d0">Exit Report</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Exit Report is a document outlining the activities and results from an AI regulatory sandbox, used to demonstrate compliance and learning outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427358</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Ecosystem">
      <data key="d0">AI Ecosystem</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Ecosystem encompasses all stakeholders, technologies, and regulatory bodies involved in developing and deploying AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427358</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection Authorities are responsible for overseeing the processing of personal data as it relates to AI systems under regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4eef4854fd4874faaa253cee7218b476</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427358</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Data Protection Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Data Protection Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Data Protection Authorities are tasked with overseeing the processing of personal data and ensuring compliance with data protection regulations within the context of AI systems in the sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;National data protection authorities are organizations responsible for overseeing and enforcing data protection laws and regulations at a national level.&lt;SEP&gt;National Data Protection Authorities oversee data privacy and protection laws in Member States, ensuring compliance with regulations on biometric data usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-698790297e0868d1f8befe15f8307380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6884d6c4641c256f66289e2e2b56965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Binding Guidance">
      <data key="d0">Non-Binding Guidance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-Binding Guidance refers to the informal advice provided to stakeholders regarding compliance and regulatory issues in AI, helping them navigate the regulatory landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reports">
      <data key="d0">Reports</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Reports are documents submitted by national competent authorities detailing the progress and outcomes of AI regulatory sandboxes, including insights and recommendations for future actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annual Reports">
      <data key="d0">Annual Reports</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Annual Reports refer to documents published by the Commission documenting the use and oversight of biometric identification systems across Member States, based on aggregated data.&lt;SEP&gt;Annual Reports refer to the documents that authorities are required to submit detailing the implementation progress and results of AI regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6884d6c4641c256f66289e2e2b56965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Final Report">
      <data key="d0">Final Report</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Final Report is a summary document submitted at the termination of the AI regulatory sandbox, including comprehensive evaluations and recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ea6f686eb4c40a3f9d758b4efcf3418</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Online Search Engines">
      <data key="d0">Online Search Engines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Online search engines are platforms that use algorithms to retrieve and present information from the web, potentially enhanced by AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b917b23f883123c9ae4bf6c69ae5e06</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/119/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Online Chatbot">
      <data key="d0">Online Chatbot</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An online chatbot is an AI-powered interface that interacts with users through conversational dialogue, capable of performing information searches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b917b23f883123c9ae4bf6c69ae5e06</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/119/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technological Evolution">
      <data key="d0">Technological Evolution</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technological Evolution describes the progress and advancements in technology, especially regarding digital services and tools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b917b23f883123c9ae4bf6c69ae5e06</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/119/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Services">
      <data key="d0">Digital Services</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital Services refer to online services provided using digital technologies, including AI systems and online search engines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b917b23f883123c9ae4bf6c69ae5e06</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/119/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation on Data Protection">
      <data key="d0">Regulation on Data Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This regulation aims to protect personal data within the European Union and sets the framework for compliance, penalties, and enforcement measures to ensure data protection standards are met.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b14075f9663187b4b9cee91c38f3025d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/168/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Start-up">
      <data key="d0">Start-up</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Start-up is a newly established business, often in the technology sector, that aims to address a specific market need. They are often classified under SMEs and have specific considerations in compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b14075f9663187b4b9cee91c38f3025d</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/168/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing in Real World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Testing in Real World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing in Real World Conditions refers to the practice of evaluating AI systems outside of controlled environments, focusing on practical applications and real-life scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing in real-world conditions involves the practical assessment of high-risk AI systems to ensure their safety and compliance, including the ability for participants to withdraw consent.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing in real-world conditions refers to the evaluation of AI systems under realistic scenarios to ensure compliance with safety and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing in real-world conditions refers to the process of evaluating high-risk AI systems in realistic settings while adhering to legal safeguards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebb00fdd14767c86b1a8c766db05a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383d8a6d025576d908f0c7970d58be09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/61/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subjects of Testing">
      <data key="d0">Subjects of Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Subjects of Testing refers to individuals who take part in the testing process, requiring informed consent to participate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ebb00fdd14767c86b1a8c766db05a7c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/61/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427392</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Representative">
      <data key="d0">Legal Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A legal representative is an individual authorized to act on behalf of another, particularly in giving informed consent for testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal Representative refers to individuals or entities who can advocate for or make decisions on behalf of the subjects participating in testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-295d382452d700dcc18edd615661d802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebb00fdd14767c86b1a8c766db05a7c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/61/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427392</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Subjects">
      <data key="d0">Testing Subjects</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing subjects are individuals who participate in research or clinical testing and must provide informed consent before involvement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-295d382452d700dcc18edd615661d802</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/61/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427392</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2016/680 is a legal framework addressing the processing of personal data and biometric data in the context of law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427404</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-Time Remote Biometric Identification Systems">
      <data key="d0">Real-Time Remote Biometric Identification Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technologies that enable the identification of individuals by analyzing biometric data captured in real time, typically in public spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technologies used by law enforcement to identify individuals in publicly accessible spaces based on biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-time remote biometric identification systems are technologies used for identifying individuals in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e142ac7019ab93d80ef49579e8d0866e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6884d6c4641c256f66289e2e2b56965</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/5/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 specifies requirements and restrictions regarding the processing of personal data in law enforcement contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 outlines special protections for sensitive personal data, including biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 outlines the limitations on processing certain types of personal data, including biometric data, without explicit consent or other lawful bases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 details restrictions and conditions for processing personal data by EU institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fd24ee33b239cebb25bf3a99d82eb1b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/39/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Third parties are external entities that provide services to verify and ensure compliance with data governance regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties offer services related to data governance and compliance, often ensuring that data management practices meet regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties refer to entities that provide tools, services, processes, or AI components to the public under free and open-source licenses, focusing on AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties refer to organizations or individuals that supply tools, services, components, or processes that are integrated into high-risk AI systems in a collaborative effort.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3167c49292549db4146e77b8eba160c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b1b6d000ef2c2e744936b8e5264e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/90/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428388</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Free and Open-Source Tools">
      <data key="d0">Free and Open-Source Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Free and open-source tools are software or components accessible to the public for use and modification, often lacking mandatory compliance requirements related to AI value chain responsibilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Processes">
      <data key="d0">Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Processes refer to systematic sequences of actions or operations involved in delivering tools, services, or components, particularly in the context of AI value chain development and usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Processes refer to the systematic methods implemented by organizations and stakeholders to develop and regulate AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf6ae679199f6853488d22af6ebdf75</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/95/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation Practices">
      <data key="d0">Documentation Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation practices like model cards and data sheets provide essential details about AI tools and services, promoting transparency and responsible usage in the AI community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trustworthy AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Trustworthy AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trustworthy AI systems refer to artificial intelligence technologies that are designed to be reliable, ethical, and beneficial for users and society at large.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e327abeb2deab3469d3ca5e1cbc290e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/89/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Act">
      <data key="d0">Act</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Act refers to a specific legislative or regulatory document published within the framework of the European Union, which contains legal provisions and guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71fde45d5020bf70e473581364a21516</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="regulation 2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">regulation 2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation 2024/1689 is a specific legal act that outlines particular provisions or requirements established by the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71fde45d5020bf70e473581364a21516</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/105/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Professional Pilots">
      <data key="d0">Professional Pilots</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Professional Pilots are individuals whose fatigue states may be detected, highlighting a potential but excluded application of the Emotion Recognition System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35f73469c0e0803dabff693c3a8808fc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/18/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Drivers">
      <data key="d0">Drivers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Drivers are individuals whose emotional or physical states, such as fatigue, might be relevant in the context of preventing accidents, thus relating to the concerns addressed in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35f73469c0e0803dabff693c3a8808fc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/18/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Misuse">
      <data key="d0">AI Misuse</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Misuse refers to the potential for artificial intelligence technologies to be applied in harmful ways, including manipulation, exploitation, and social control practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Dignity">
      <data key="d0">Human Dignity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Dignity is a foundational moral principle that asserts the inherent worth of all individuals, demanding respect and protection from abusive practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Freedom">
      <data key="d0">Freedom</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Freedom refers to the state of being free from oppressive restrictions imposed by authority on one's way of life, behavior, or political views.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Equality">
      <data key="d0">Equality</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Equality is the state of being equal, especially in status, rights, and opportunities, a value emphasized in social justice and human rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Democracy">
      <data key="d0">Democracy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Democracy denotes a system of government by the whole population or all the eligible members of a state, typically through elected representatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Democracy is a system of government in which the citizens exercise power directly or elect representatives to form a governing body.&lt;SEP&gt;Democracy is a fundamental value that the Union aims to protect and promote through its regulations and policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7e9eb6e4da61705e152386e4c7c8412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a11bcb90e7333ffe457649980a31a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/61/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rule of Law">
      <data key="d0">Rule of Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Rule of Law ensures that all individuals and institutions are accountable under the law, a core principle the Union seeks to uphold.&lt;SEP&gt;Rule of Law is the principle that all people and institutions are subject to and accountable to law that is fairly applied and enforced.&lt;SEP&gt;The rule of law is the principle that all people and institutions are subject to and accountable to the law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7e9eb6e4da61705e152386e4c7c8412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24a11bcb90e7333ffe457649980a31a8</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/61/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/2/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428245</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rights of the Child">
      <data key="d0">Rights of the Child</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Rights of the Child are a set of entitlements recognized and formulated to ensure the well-being and protection of children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5fbe5a397983eea99c8efc6c422ef4f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/28/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427430</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 94">
      <data key="d0">Article 94</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 94 provides procedural guarantees related to the supervisory powers of the Commission in the context of AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff5e73e3b7c1de9ffa48661e94e87a5b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/88/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 75(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 75(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 75(3) outlines specific conditions under which market surveillance authorities can request the Commission's assistance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff5e73e3b7c1de9ffa48661e94e87a5b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/88/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 10">
      <data key="d0">Article 10</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 regulates the processing of biometric data and stipulates conditions for its use in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1da6e9cf5fd822e42b8f37d6d2798af0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/94/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427441</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 4 (1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 4 (1)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 4 (1) of Directive (EU) 2016/680 establishes fundamental principles such as lawfulness and transparency for data processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1da6e9cf5fd822e42b8f37d6d2798af0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/94/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427441</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Remote Biometric Identification">
      <data key="d0">Remote Biometric Identification</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Remote biometric identification refers to the use of AI systems to identify individuals from a distance using biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union and National Law">
      <data key="d0">Union and National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union and national law comprises the legal frameworks governing the use and processing of personal data, including biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Union and national law refers to the legal frameworks and regulations governing the conduct of testing in real-world conditions, particularly regarding AI technology and personal data protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a7fb5abd6ad1ba2e9256fc63dbda4a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428325</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Inaccuracies">
      <data key="d0">Technical Inaccuracies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical inaccuracies refer to errors in AI systems that can lead to biased results in biometric identifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Verification Systems">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Verification Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric verification systems are AI applications focused on validating the identity of natural persons for security purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a392041e8bab68fc3cbccc33e333ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Systems">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric systems are technological solutions designed to enhance cybersecurity and protect personal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b5f42708d566a2269e407d6a5b3e2847</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/54/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Large-Scale IT Systems">
      <data key="d0">Large-Scale IT Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Large-scale IT systems are complex structures that include AI systems, required to comply with regulatory measures outlined before specific deadlines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 111">
      <data key="d0">Article 111</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 111 refers to a regulatory framework concerning AI systems and their market compliance deadlines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex X">
      <data key="d0">Annex X</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex X is a section within a legal document that lists legal acts relevant to the compliance of large-scale IT systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="August 2027">
      <data key="d0">August 2027</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">August 2027 marks a key deadline for AI systems to comply with specified regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="August 2030">
      <data key="d0">August 2030</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">August 2030 is the compliance deadline by which certain AI systems must meet regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="August 2026">
      <data key="d0">August 2026</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">August 2026 marks the date when high-risk AI systems previously placed on the market may be subject to regulation changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operators of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Operators of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Operators of high-risk AI systems are responsible for implementing compliance measures as outlined in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2025">
      <data key="d0">2025</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">2025 is the cutoff date for general-purpose AI models to comply with upcoming regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca9d1e5f9ba8b1143fb541d7c5a4fd56</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Deadlines">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Deadlines</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance deadlines refer to specific dates by which providers of AI systems must meet regulatory requirements to continue operating legally.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3d709837f2bf640b25f168a3359606f3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex V">
      <data key="d0">Annex V</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex V contains specific requirements and information that must be included in the EU Declaration of Conformity for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex V is a section of the legislation related to the EU declaration of conformity, which outlines specific content requirements that must be adhered to.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0a6eb47abd8e339b7c043651460a0bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b577700d28d7be8a3a9320e2d5ff1c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427470</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Progress">
      <data key="d0">Technical Progress</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical progress refers to advancements and changes in technology that may necessitate updates to the existing standards and requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30b577700d28d7be8a3a9320e2d5ff1c</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427470</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management Measures">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk Management Measures are specific strategies and actions put in place to mitigate or control identified risks associated with the functioning of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk Management Measures refer to the strategies and procedures put in place to mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk management measures are strategies and actions implemented to mitigate potential risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951511d7a62f58da07aebc05f3e4f1c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training to Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Training to Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training to Deployers involves educating individuals responsible for operating AI systems, ensuring they understand risks and how to mitigate them effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Residual Risk">
      <data key="d0">Residual Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Residual Risk is the level of risk that remains after risk management measures have been implemented.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Paragraphs 1 to 9">
      <data key="d0">Paragraphs 1 to 9</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraphs 1 to 9 comprise sections of regulations that detail the risk management processes and considerations for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System Tests">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI System Tests are evaluations conducted to verify the performance and safety of AI systems before they are placed on the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Real-World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-World Conditions refer to the actual environmental contexts in which high-risk AI systems may be deployed and tested.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-world conditions refer to the practical environments in which high-risk AI systems are tested to ensure their effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951511d7a62f58da07aebc05f3e4f1c1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Risk Management Processes">
      <data key="d0">Internal Risk Management Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal risk management processes are systematic approaches organizations must establish to manage risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-951511d7a62f58da07aebc05f3e4f1c1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tasks of the Board">
      <data key="d0">Tasks of the Board</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Tasks of the Board detail the responsibilities and functions assigned to the Board in relation to the implementation of regulations surrounding AI and market surveillance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427516</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical and Regulatory Expertise">
      <data key="d0">Technical and Regulatory Expertise</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical and regulatory expertise refers to the knowledge and practices shared among Member States to ensure effective application of AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427516</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Best Practices">
      <data key="d0">Best Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Best practices denote the optimal methods and strategies collected and shared among Member States regarding the implementation of AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427516</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 46">
      <data key="d0">Article 46</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 46 outlines the derogation conditions related to conformity assessment procedures for AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 112">
      <data key="d0">Article 112</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 112 includes provisions regarding the evaluation, review and potential amendments to the AI Regulation based on the latest technological developments.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 112 refers to a specific section within the regulation that involves the evaluation and review of compliance and effectiveness of the regulation over time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Specifications">
      <data key="d0">Common Specifications</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Common Specifications are standards created to guide market operators and authorities in the use of AI technologies safely and effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Common Specifications refer to standards used when harmonised standards are either lacking or inadequate for compliance with EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Skills">
      <data key="d0">Digital Skills</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital Skills refer to the competencies required to effectively engage with AI technologies and participate in a digital economy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accountability">
      <data key="d0">Accountability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Accountability is a crucial aspect of AI governance, ensuring that there are mechanisms in place to address issues that arise from AI usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Operators">
      <data key="d0">Market Operators</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Operators are entities that engage in the facilitation and implementation of AI regulations among various stakeholders in the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427533</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Benchmarks">
      <data key="d0">Benchmarks</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Benchmarks are standards used to measure the capabilities of AI models, helping to determine their risk profiles and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Benchmarks refer to the standards and criteria used to evaluate the performance and compliance of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training Needs">
      <data key="d0">Training Needs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Training Needs pertain to the skills and knowledge required by staff in Member States to effectively implement AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427533</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Monitoring of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Monitoring of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Monitoring of AI Systems involves tracking and assessing the performance and compliance of AI systems to established guidelines and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7bb3413d9de075f3d726ec4825bbdf1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enforcement of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Enforcement of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Enforcement of AI Systems entails implementing rules and procedures to ensure AI systems adhere to standards and practices set forth by regulatory bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7bb3413d9de075f3d726ec4825bbdf1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Experiences with AI">
      <data key="d0">National Experiences with AI</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">National Experiences with AI refer to the various methods and practices adopted by individual countries in addressing issues related to AI development and implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7bb3413d9de075f3d726ec4825bbdf1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427535</data>
    </node>
    <node id="complaint">
      <data key="d0">complaint</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A complaint is a formal expression of dissatisfaction or concern raised by a person regarding a perceived infringement of rights related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2763d61443dcf3aa274192c53e098997</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/170/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="remedies">
      <data key="d0">remedies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Remedies refer to legal measures or actions available to individuals to address grievances and enforce their rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2763d61443dcf3aa274192c53e098997</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/170/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Economic Operators">
      <data key="d0">Economic Operators</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Economic Operators are entities involved in the marketing or sale of AI systems under the jurisdiction of the Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427560</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Competition Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Competition Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">National Competition Authorities are responsible for enforcing competition laws within their respective nations and ensuring compliance with the Union regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427560</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 14 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020">
      <data key="d0">Article 14 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 14 outlines the powers and responsibilities assigned to market surveillance authorities in enforcing compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems listed in Annex III">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems listed in Annex III</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI Systems detailed in Annex III of the Regulation that require special attention and monitoring under the law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 sets out the framework for the Single Supervisory Mechanism for the European banking system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Data Protection Supervisory Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Competent Data Protection Supervisory Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorities that oversee compliance with data protection laws within Member States as it relates to AI system regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 41 to 44">
      <data key="d0">Articles 41 to 44</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 41 to 44 of the Directive establish guidelines under which authorities can exercise their market surveillance duties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 41 to 44 of Directive (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Articles 41 to 44 of Directive (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">These articles outline specific provisions regarding the designation of authorities for data protection and their responsibilities under Directive (EU) 2016/680.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation and Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Documentation and Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation and Data Sets encompass the records and materials necessary to assess the compliance of high-risk AI systems under regulatory scrutiny.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Source Code">
      <data key="d0">Source Code</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Source Code refers to the programming code of high-risk AI systems that market surveillance authorities can access under certain conditions for compliance assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 85/374/EEC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 85/374/EEC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 85/374/EEC pertains to product liability and establishes rules for compensation in cases of harm caused by defective products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="platform work">
      <data key="d0">platform work</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Platform work refers to employment that is organized through online platforms, often characterized by precarious working conditions and specific regulatory challenges.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Rules">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonised Rules refer to a set of regulations established to ensure consistency in the market practices surrounding high-risk AI systems across the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised rules refer to a set of standardized regulations in the EU aimed at ensuring consistency in the application of laws related to data protection and privacy across member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-57118cd489d78b33ed75c63f33151aee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/10/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428375</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council Directive 85/374/EEC">
      <data key="d0">Council Directive 85/374/EEC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Council Directive 85/374/EEC is a legislative proposal aimed at aligning the laws concerning liability for defective products across EU Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;Council Directive 85/374/EEC outlines the principles of liability for defective products, ensuring compensation for harm caused by such products in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council Directive 85/374/EEC relates to liability for defective products in EU member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1219d54497e2a4a6af07e6b10274bc72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f66c7cfe484df668dde369788c6d3f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427581</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Platform Work">
      <data key="d0">Platform Work</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Platform Work refers to jobs that are organized through digital platforms, often characterized by non-standard work arrangements and regulatory issues regarding labor rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Platform work refers to job arrangements that leverage technology and online platforms, often creating unique employment challenges and rights issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427581</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulation on Employment">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulation on Employment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Regulation on Employment is aimed at improving working conditions and rights in the workplace, particularly concerning health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427581</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive on Platform Work">
      <data key="d0">Directive on Platform Work</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Directive on Platform Work addresses the improvement of working conditions specifically for gig economy workers and those involved in platform work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427581</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Collective Action Rights">
      <data key="d0">Collective Action Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Collective Action Rights are the rights associated with the ability of workers to negotiate and enforce collective agreements, as recognized by Union Law and domestic legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and Safety Regulations are laws and guidelines that ensure safe working environments and practices for employees across various sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive of the European Parliament">
      <data key="d0">Directive of the European Parliament</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Directive of the European Parliament aims at improving working conditions specifically for workers involved in platform work, establishing minimum standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EEC) No 339/93">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EEC) No 339/93</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EEC) No 339/93 was previously existing legislation that was repealed by Regulation (EC) No 765/2008.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation was previously in effect, related to certain accreditation and regulatory practices in the European Union, now repealed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1219d54497e2a4a6af07e6b10274bc72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654b17e6ab435ca442e9075545af0c79</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="25.6.2019">
      <data key="d0">25.6.2019</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The date 25.6.2019 may refer to a significant event or directive related to European legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-52f66c7cfe484df668dde369788c6d3f</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-Time Biometric Identification System">
      <data key="d0">Real-Time Biometric Identification System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-Time Biometric Identification Systems are technological systems used to identify individuals using biometric data in real time and are subject to regulatory oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb2b1ecdb0a779493d4236bdef52a5f1</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/36/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427588</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annual Report">
      <data key="d0">Annual Report</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Annual Report is a document prepared by the advisory forum summarizing its activities and findings over the year, which is made publicly available.&lt;SEP&gt;The Annual Report is a mandatory document that must be submitted by both the relevant market surveillance authorities and national data protection authorities to the Commission regarding the use of biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb2b1ecdb0a779493d4236bdef52a5f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ac4d6cae0afd3292516531be7716e9</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/36/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Value Chain Regulation">
      <data key="d0">AI Value Chain Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Value Chain Regulation outlines responsibilities for providers of high-risk AI systems and their obligations under specific articles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 85">
      <data key="d0">Recital 85</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 85 provides context and clarification regarding obligations and circumstances related to the provision of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 84">
      <data key="d0">Recital 84</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 84 discusses previous related considerations in the context of the obligations on providers of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third-Party Provider">
      <data key="d0">Third-Party Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A third-party provider refers to any entity that assists or contributes to the functioning and regulation of high-risk AI systems under the specified articles of the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427594</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Access">
      <data key="d0">Technical Access</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Access includes the permissions and tools necessary for providers of high-risk AI systems to operate and maintain compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical access refers to the information and resources that must be provided by providers for compliance with regulations governing high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02b30ca877df5f1c4eaed18ba9fb4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fe126564dfd9a342c90d435dae0173</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427597</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Initial Provider">
      <data key="d0">Initial Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Initial Provider is the entity originally offering an AI system and responsible for its compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2fe126564dfd9a342c90d435dae0173</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427602</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems Compliance">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI Systems Compliance refers to the obligations that must be fulfilled by providers of high-risk AI systems to ensure safety and efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2fe126564dfd9a342c90d435dae0173</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427602</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Written Agreement">
      <data key="d0">Written Agreement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Written Agreement refers to the formal contract made between providers and third parties to outline responsibilities and expectations regarding high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2fe126564dfd9a342c90d435dae0173</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427602</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation includes all technical records and data necessary for validating the compliance of AI Systems and their operational processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentation refers to the required information and records that must be maintained and provided to comply with high-risk AI system regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentation includes the comprehensive and accessible written materials that provide instructions for the use of the AI system, outlining its capabilities, limitations, and appropriate applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6adccf24f1ddc4835908b879bcbe8674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fe126564dfd9a342c90d435dae0173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2252cbe714fc3b6aee570acd5f270ef</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 87">
      <data key="d0">Recital 87</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 87 refers to a specific section or clause within a regulatory document focused on the obligations of high-risk AI system providers and their third-party suppliers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427602</data>
    </node>
    <node id="third party">
      <data key="d0">third party</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A third party in this context refers to any external entity that supplies tools, services, components, or processes that can be integrated into high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3150ae4fb871ce38df11dd1f2932123b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Property Rights">
      <data key="d0">Property Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Property rights refer to the legal rights individuals or organizations have to use and control property, including ownership and use restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be7ec602a72f4c2f19a5693b37872b32</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidential Business Information">
      <data key="d0">Confidential Business Information</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidential Business Information encompasses sensitive data that companies wish to keep secret to maintain a competitive advantage.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential business information includes sensitive data that gives a company a competitive edge and is protected by law against unauthorized disclosure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a33f9372e32e8879cc6f97cd662934d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7ec602a72f4c2f19a5693b37872b32</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/167/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428468</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 26(5)">
      <data key="d0">Article 26(5)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 26(5) addresses the operational monitoring of high-risk AI systems to ensure their proper functioning and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Logging Capabilities">
      <data key="d0">Logging Capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Logging capabilities relate to the technical functions that allow high-risk AI systems to automatically record important operational data concerning their usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Traceability">
      <data key="d0">Traceability</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Traceability refers to the ability to access and track the performance and compliance history of AI Systems consistently over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Traceability refers to the ability to track and verify the operation and modifications of high-risk AI systems through recorded logs and data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2252cbe714fc3b6aee570acd5f270ef</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/71/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 14(5)">
      <data key="d0">Article 14(5)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 14(5) refers to a specific provision or section within a legal or formal document, potentially discussing regulations or policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1707a8e9fa1107c63102bdcbf42885d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Framework">
      <data key="d0">Legal Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Framework is a category that encompasses rules, regulations, and standards guiding legal practices and assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1707a8e9fa1107c63102bdcbf42885d5</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="advisory forum">
      <data key="d0">advisory forum</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The advisory forum is a consultative body that provides opinions and advice to the Commission regarding regulatory matters.&lt;SEP&gt;The advisory forum is a group that assists the Commission in gathering expertise necessary for compliance and standardization matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428439</data>
    </node>
    <node id="standardisation requests">
      <data key="d0">standardisation requests</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Standardisation requests are formal requests issued by the Commission to guide the development of harmonized standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="stakeholders">
      <data key="d0">stakeholders</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholders refer to all parties involved in the standardization process, including SMEs, consumer organizations, and environmental and social representatives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European standardisation organisations">
      <data key="d0">European standardisation organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">European standardisation organisations are bodies responsible for developing and promoting European standards aligned with EU legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-895d6dbeb694bb42f8956b66c8927bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council Directives">
      <data key="d0">Council Directives</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Council Directives refer to legislative acts of the European Union that require member states to implement certain laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standardisation Request">
      <data key="d0">Standardisation Request</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Standardisation Request is a formal request to standardisation bodies to develop or amend standards that would help fulfill European regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A standardisation request is a formal request by the Commission to develop or revise standards that are necessary for compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8079d3300c156b781606811b2ee8aaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f3473e38ccd9ad84662b373166a5c2b</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748428289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EC Directive 2009/105/EC">
      <data key="d0">EC Directive 2009/105/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">EC Directive 2009/105/EC pertains to regulations set by the European Union aimed at governing specific legal and economic matters within the EU framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council Decision 87/95/EEC">
      <data key="d0">Council Decision 87/95/EEC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Council Decision 87/95/EEC refers to an earlier regulation that is being repealed in light of updated directives by the European Parliament and Council.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decision No 1673/2006/EC">
      <data key="d0">Decision No 1673/2006/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Decision No 1673/2006/EC is another regulatory measure that has been repealed in the process of updating EU legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2009/105/EC">
      <data key="d0">2009/105/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">2009/105/EC is an EC Directive concerning specific regulatory measures within the framework of European Union law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="87/95/EEC">
      <data key="d0">87/95/EEC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">87/95/EEC is a Council Decision that has been repealed by the new directive and pertains to earlier EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1673/2006/EC">
      <data key="d0">1673/2006/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">1673/2006/EC is another regulatory decision made by the Council of the European Union that has been repealed under new regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OJ L 316">
      <data key="d0">OJ L 316</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">OJ L 316 refers to the Official Journal of the European Union, where EU legislation, including directives and decisions, is published.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operators of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Operators of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Operators are individuals or organizations managing AI systems and are required to comply with the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2030 Deadline">
      <data key="d0">2030 Deadline</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The 2030 Deadline is an important date by which operators of AI systems must comply with the requirements of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Operators">
      <data key="d0">AI Operators</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Operators are the individuals or organizations responsible for managing and deploying AI systems, particularly those classified as high-risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Accountability">
      <data key="d0">Public Accountability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Accountability refers to the obligation of public authorities and AI operators to comply with regulatory requirements in the use of AI systems within large-scale IT systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Changes">
      <data key="d0">Significant Changes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Significant Changes denote alterations in the design or intended purpose of high-risk AI systems that trigger compliance requirements under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="End of 2030">
      <data key="d0">End of 2030</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">End of 2030 is the milestone by which operators of AI systems must ensure compliance with the conditions set forth in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union values">
      <data key="d0">Union values</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Union values refer to the principles that guide the development and regulation of technologies, particularly AI, ensuring alignment with fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Treaty on European Union (TEU)">
      <data key="d0">Treaty on European Union (TEU)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Treaty on European Union establishes the foundational legal framework for the European Union and includes provisions related to AI and human rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 2 of TEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 2 of TEU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 2 of the Treaty on European Union outlines the Union's values, which are essential for the ethical development of AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6 TEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 6 TEU</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 6 of the Treaty on European Union sets forth the Charter of Fundamental Rights, which guides the development of technologies like AI in a human-centric manner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human-Centric Technology">
      <data key="d0">Human-Centric Technology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Human-Centric Technology refers to technologies designed primarily to enhance human well-being and ensure the welfare of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2023/988">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2023/988</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2023/988 is a legislative framework established by the European Parliament and Council to ensure the safety of AI systems and products that are not deemed high-risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f32100de89356334a47cd2317dde09df</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/166/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427650</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2001/95/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2001/95/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2001/95/EC is a previous European measure focused on general product safety, which has been repealed by Regulation (EU) 2023/988.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f32100de89356334a47cd2317dde09df</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/166/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427650</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council Directive 87/357/EEC">
      <data key="d0">Council Directive 87/357/EEC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Council Directive 87/357/EEC is a previous regulation focused on general product safety, which has been repealed by subsequent regulations including Regulation (EU) 2023/988.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f32100de89356334a47cd2317dde09df</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/166/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427650</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 2320/2002">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 2320/2002</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 2320/2002 was a previous regulation concerning civil aviation security that has been repealed by Regulation (EC) No 300/2008.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf0d6bb3a9bb4e12605c032254429e91</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427672</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Union Aviation Safety Agency">
      <data key="d0">European Union Aviation Safety Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Union Aviation Safety Agency is responsible for ensuring safety in civil aviation within the EU, setting regulations, and overseeing compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/797">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/797</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2016/797 governs the interoperability of the rail system within the EU, aiming to facilitate seamless train operations across member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 715/2007">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 715/2007</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 715/2007 pertains to the type approval of motor vehicles with respect to emissions from light passenger and commercial vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 595/2009">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 595/2009 addresses type approval of motor vehicles and their trailers concerning emissions from heavy vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2007/46/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2007/46/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2007/46/EC regulates the type approval of motor vehicles and their trailers globally within the EU framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 552/2004">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 552/2004</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 552/2004 addresses air traffic management and is part of the regulatory framework for aviation safety in Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 552/2004 concerns the organization and use of airspace in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 216/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 216/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 216/2008 governs the establishment of common safety rules in civil aviation in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 216/2008 sets the fundamental requirements for the safety of civil aviation in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 2111/2005">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 2111/2005</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 2111/2005 establishes safety measures concerning flights operated by EU airlines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 1008/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 1008/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 1008/2008 relates to the regulation of air services in the EU market, ensuring fair competition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d4">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/</data>
      <data key="d5">1748427676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EC) No 78/2009, No 79/2009, and No 661/2009">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EC) No 78/2009, No 79/2009, and No 661/2009</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">These regulations are repealed by more recent legislation as part of the European Union's efforts to update vehicle safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460</data>
