      <data key="d9">chunk-dc0938655f22b840224fc49f2018dbf1</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/21/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426119</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Rights and Freedoms of Individuals">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation is designed to protect and promote the Rights and Freedoms of Individuals across the Union.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal protection,rights safeguard</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dc0938655f22b840224fc49f2018dbf1</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/21/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426119</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Commission">
      <data key="d6">83.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission is a key authority that enforces obligations set forth in the Regulation concerning various sectors, including AI model providers and the governance of Notified Bodies with respect to their identification numbers. It is responsible for the development, oversight, and implementation of regulations that not only address compliance costs for Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) but also ensure adherence to multiple articles established within the Regulation for operators.

Additionally, the Commission's role involves enforcing and reviewing the Regulation to guarantee compliance among Member States, thus maintaining the objectives established by the European Union. Overall, the Commission serves as the regulatory oversight body that ensures the effective application and compliance with the Regulation across different entities and sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is responsible for overseeing the implementation of the Regulation and ensuring Member States adhere to its provisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is responsible for creating and enforcing the Regulation regarding AI systems, including ensuring compliance with EU law.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is responsible for specifying guidelines under the Regulation that governs AI systems, ensuring compliance according to risk levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">10,compliance,framework enforcement,governance,organizational governance,oversight,policy administration,policy enforcement,regulatory authority,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a24148385124cc6a8cba737414c55a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fb722dbde5159480cfd0e4534fc632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4903f69522ce55807b4320731843ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e43bf41139a924443fd8b200d694f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6b3a7a24bfd18cc84baf6173985e105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816d4247559a68f4b8ceca952f4e1069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69eb093d5893337024ffe62fdcc78563</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/37/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/174/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/35/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/144/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428525</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="obligations on providers of general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The obligations are a part of the Regulation that pertains to the compliance standards for AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance requirements,legal framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426131</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Deployers">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Deployers must follow the guidelines set forth in regulations regarding the deployment and monitoring of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The regulation guides how deployers should interact with high-risk AI systems and ensures informed decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,governance,guidelines,informed usage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712fbb27f2ad82df6098ef5c90507342</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428101</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">92.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-Risk AI Systems are governed by specific Regulation aimed at establishing guidelines for their use and monitoring. This Regulation is designed to ensure compliance and operational standards for high-risk AI systems, emphasizing the importance of safety and effectiveness in their deployment. It targets these systems specifically, detailing the obligations and standards necessary for their responsible usage. Additionally, the Regulation outlines limitations and requirements to ensure that high-risk AI systems are designed and deployed safely. Furthermore, it aims to mitigate potential market disruption by enforcing strict implementation practices and ongoing monitoring of these systems.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are subject to specific regulations that outline how they should operate and the protections available for affected persons.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are required to conform to the Regulation, which ensures they are safe and compliant for market placement.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems must comply with regulations that mandate transparency and clear instructions for their use.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation specifies categories for High-Risk AI Systems and establishes requirements for their assessment and oversight.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI governance,compliance,conformity,legal framework,operational standards,regulatory compliance,regulatory focus,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight,regulatory requirement,risk classification,risk management,safety,transparency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d709837f2bf640b25f168a3359606f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36126d549d18d31512a9e98c8be8c3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e442b04ad431e8e1a74bf9fa0f8bc5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fb722dbde5159480cfd0e4534fc632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28ef04b3893d2080962790dc78128cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712fbb27f2ad82df6098ef5c90507342&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/174/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/129/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/171/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/93/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428165</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Biometric Identification">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation defines and governs the practices involved in biometric identification and its applications.</data>
      <data key="d8">biometric practices,legal framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5e666c69f3a12c76222f3212a19f9ffe</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/15/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426178</data>
