    <edge source="Regulation" target="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d6">27.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market Surveillance Authorities are responsible for monitoring compliance with regulations in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority operates under the Regulation to ensure market compliance and protect consumers.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Authorities execute the provisions outlined in the Regulation to ensure market compliance.</data>
      <data key="d8">enforcement,implementation,market compliance,market monitoring,oversight,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4fd25b8a323071b471e7df42fd1a91ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24b5f2c129e84e53724de4a8e9f61091&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/153/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427571</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d6">27.0</data>
      <data key="d7">National Competent Authorities enforce specific regulations set by Member States to ensure compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities act under the Regulation to ensure compliance with data protection and cybersecurity measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Competent Authorities implement the principles outlined in the Regulation to maintain objectivity and impartiality.</data>
      <data key="d8">enforcement,legal compliance,organizational responsibility,regulation implementation,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4fd25b8a323071b471e7df42fd1a91ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea411b75c6825aab3a6b8a4983e34939</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/153/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/154/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427055</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="European Data Protection Supervisor">
      <data key="d6">36.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the competent authority overseeing compliance with the Regulation for Union institutions.")&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor supervises the adherence to the Regulation within Union institutions and bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor operates under the Regulation that specifies data protection requirements and compliance mechanisms for Union Institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor enforces the Regulation, ensuring compliance among Union institutions and imposing penalties as necessary.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance framework,enforcement,regulatory authority,regulatory framework,supervision,supervisory authority</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5dfd9a8d23f85f04843c95f20a9172df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b14075f9663187b4b9cee91c38f3025d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-977670aa5941763001334246314af150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/100/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/168/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427387</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="SMEs">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The Regulation specifically targets SMEs, including start-ups, highlighting its relevance for their operations and compliance with AI systems.")</data>
      <data key="d8">business impact,regulatory focus</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-294c88b41db00dcd8f4482345b658105</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/70/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426202</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">78.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI Systems are subject to comprehensive Regulation that outlines their operational objectives and the functional contexts in which they are utilized. This Regulation specifically addresses high-risk AI systems, establishing guidelines for compliance in military and national security applications, and sets forth procedures for assessing their conformity. Operators of high-risk AI systems are required to meet specific compliance standards defined by the Regulation to avoid market disruptions. Additionally, the Regulation mandates that these AI systems must be traceable and compliant, ensuring accountability in their deployment and operation. Overall, the Regulation plays a crucial role in governing the functionality and compliance requirements of AI systems, particularly those that pose significant risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The categorization of AI Systems is directly related to the regulatory framework ensuring safety and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation provides guidelines for the operation and risks of AI Systems in decision-making contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation sets conditions under which AI Systems are categorized as high-risk or not, influencing their practical application.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI technology,classification criteria,compliance,governance,legal framework,operational context,operational guidelines,regulatory assessment,regulatory framework,regulatory requirements,risk assessment,safety standards,technology compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9a24148385124cc6a8cba737414c55a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2252cbe714fc3b6aee570acd5f270ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe20aa0cce0b31f6a43c755317350d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d295c76deab241026d89ef8fa9749c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-992499cbdbb7fa23e4ae622c35e9d42f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c75f03e9c9b58e1598f84630bbf10834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6b3a7a24bfd18cc84baf6173985e105</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/177/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/71/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/12/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/63/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428525</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Providers of high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must adhere to regulations that dictate the requirements and standards for implementing a Quality Management System.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems are encouraged to comply with the Regulation during the transitional period to ensure adherence to safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,standards compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5a4e48721924d3a1798f61c8810d78</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/178/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428358</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Providers">
      <data key="d6">19.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must comply with the Regulation governing high-risk AI systems, which dictates quality management and internal governance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers must follow the regulation directives to ensure their AI systems are developed within the legal framework for risk management.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,governance,operational guidelines</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043dd859ed68e9fbb76ff618fe32c054</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/65/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428029</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">77.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office is responsible for implementing actions related to the Regulation on conformity assessments and AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is tasked with supporting the enforcement and implementation of the Regulation concerning AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office plays a crucial role in the implementation and enforcement of the Regulation that governs the use of general-purpose AI models. It provides guidance and support to Member States and Competent Authorities, ensuring they adhere to the obligations outlined in the Regulation. The AI Office is responsible for keeping the rules and procedures mentioned in the Regulation up to date, thereby ensuring compliance with the stipulated codes of practice. Its operations are strictly guided by the obligations and guidelines set forth in the Regulation, which it is tasked with enforcing. Through these efforts, the AI Office contributes to effective oversight of AI models, ensuring alignment with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office oversees the implementation of the Regulation that enforces compliance with copyright obligations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,enforcement,governance,implementation,implementation support,operational guidelines,oversight,regulation,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight,regulatory support</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0ab303aa0764433ae306cd3e410cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7b16baf52f0573b141bf124a701c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a644c604bba8cdc33a7125c5db02395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994612dc34fa7cbfaae3dc6fdd1036d3</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/162/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/108/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/151/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428535</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d6">46.0</data>
      <data key="d7">General-purpose AI models must adhere to the obligations outlined in the Regulation if marketed before the compliance deadline.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation aims to address the systemic risks associated with general-purpose AI models through comprehensive obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation sets forth compliance obligations for providers of general-purpose AI models, necessitating adherence to specific guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation sets obligations specifically for providers of General-Purpose AI Models to ensure compliance with safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation stipulates the obligations and standards that must be adhered to by providers of General-Purpose AI Models.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI standards,accountability,compliance,compliance obligations,legal framework,obligations,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,regulatory standards,risk mitigation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d709837f2bf640b25f168a3359606f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd9734e617f6b77f1d098f074a31788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f3abbad4dddf2a8a56efeaa03cc7f28</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/114/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/109/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427462</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Directive (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation incorporates provisions from Directive (EU) 2016/680 to ensure that high-risk AI systems respect data protection standards in law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation provides a specific legal framework that is influenced by the rules outlined in Directive (EU) 2016/680 regarding the processing of data.</data>
      <data key="d8">data protection,legal framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b477112713d917a03ba6f595ed62f6c7</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/38/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428613</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Annex III">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Annex III details the types of high-risk AI systems that the Regulation seeks to govern, highlighting specific requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex III is part of the Regulation that outlines prohibited AI practices that can be amended based on the Commission's evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI governance,amendments,regulatory framework,regulatory specifics</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426936</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="remote biometric identification system">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation dictates how remote biometric identification systems should be used and establishes legal guidelines for their operation.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical use,legal framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-54d70bbcd80c52a665c6844c0f583b00</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/17/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426309</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Member States">
      <data key="d6">60.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are responsible for applying and enforcing regulations within their jurisdictions and must adhere to the provisions outlined in the Regulation set forth by the Commission. They play a crucial role in supporting the implementation of this Regulation, which impacts all Member States by establishing guidelines and practices related to artificial intelligence (AI). In addition, Member States are tasked with developing and adopting regulations to ensure coordinated law enforcement practices across different jurisdictions. They are also required to implement penalties in line with the Regulation. Furthermore, Member States have the authority to enforce the Regulation and can seek assistance from experts to aid in its implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States are tasked with enforcing the Regulation to prevent unjustified obstacles to high-risk AI systems in the market.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU law,compliance,cooperation,enforcement,governance,intergovernmental cooperation,legal alignment,legal framework,national enforcement,regulation compliance,regulatory adherence,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4fd25b8a323071b471e7df42fd1a91ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e442b04ad431e8e1a74bf9fa0f8bc5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756bc5b856a1d06a78ffd0aeb1d318b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a644c604bba8cdc33a7125c5db02395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2bf8c519aff48aa30866bbefc0dc688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15020eb940c70ceebc99b92dce7bdc7</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/129/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/66/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/153/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/151/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427797</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Penalties">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Penalties are established under the Regulation to enforce compliance and deter violations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation outlines the conditions under which penalties are to be applied for violations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,deterrence,enforcement,legal framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f519e0fb15239a9e7db009ac6e0ed402</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426328</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Conformity Assessment System">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation mandates the establishment of a Conformity Assessment System to ensure AI technologies adhere to standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,regulatory requirements</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426328</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Technological Advancements">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Technological Advancements necessitate the creation of the Regulation to address evolving risks in AI development.</data>
