      <data key="d7">The European Parliament operates within the framework of the European Union, legislating and regulating member state affairs.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament plays a critical role in shaping EU policies and directives regarding accessibility for persons with disabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union encompasses the European Parliament, which is responsible for creating regulations affecting high-risk AI systems and cybersecurity standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,governance structure,legislation,legislative body,policy development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b15dea67a3df634ebeaeb58168eda214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1503f34495e54a125e9f1df8902aa87</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/80/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/77/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428260</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Union sets the framework within which national competent authorities operate to regulate AI systems.</data>
