    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="Regulation 2024/1689">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Union oversees the establishment and publication of legal regulations, including Regulation 2024/1689.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,regulation publication</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3feec38e6ec4549038a615544ae6733b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/107/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426126</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="Commission">
      <data key="d6">55.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission is a key governing body within the European Union, playing a crucial role in managing various regulations and overseeing the EU database. It operates as part of the overall governance structure of the European Union, tasked with enforcing laws and regulations across member states. The Commission works under the authority and framework provided by the European Union to implement legislation, including important areas such as data protection and regulations related to artificial intelligence systems. As an executive body, the Commission is responsible for formulating regulations and standards that apply to all member states, ensuring compliance with the policies and directives established by the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d8">executive role,governance,institutional framework,regulation,regulatory body,regulatory framework,regulatory governance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6e6c53b12894d2e398aee9b5bbf9815f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3505c356c8e76e9f364115f4eb7ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-408ee65c3eab1e86c1c4207deaf4f216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d38e2dee253890587ca2dd6a1e4e0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c050fb13af07ed12982fe6bfe7abf4</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/169/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/41/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/117/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/131/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428447</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="Regulation (EU) 2019/881">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Union enforces Regulation (EU) 2019/881 across its member states as part of its regulatory framework for AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation (EU) 2019/881 is a legal measure put forth by the European Union to manage AI systems' compliance and governance.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,legislation,regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a0bafee65696de6d27593351f1c77561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/122/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427893</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="Europol">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Europol serves as a key agency under the framework of the European Union for law enforcement cooperation.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union governs regulations that Europol operates under to facilitate international law enforcement cooperation.</data>
      <data key="d8">agency relationship,governance,law enforcement cooperation,regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426164</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="Third Countries">
      <data key="d6">22.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Union enforces compliance regulations for AI providers located in Third Countries before they can access the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union's regulations apply to Third Countries when their AI systems are intended for use in the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union engages with Third Countries through agreements that facilitate regulatory compliance and mutual recognition of standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">international relations,international standards,market entry,regulatory cooperation,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0569fee390e7e2b777d0bdf161494796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3af424118c8f8024a835a3de370430b3</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/82/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/39/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427240</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">52.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Union (EU) plays a crucial role in the regulation and oversight of AI systems within its member states. It sets standards to ensure that these systems comply with safety and regulatory requirements, particularly focusing on high-risk AI systems through specific compliance mandates outlined in its regulations. The EU is dedicated to establishing a consistent approach to the deployment and regulation of AI technologies, aiming to protect personal rights and civil liberties, especially in the context of law enforcement activities. Furthermore, the European Union is actively involved in overseeing the development of ethical and trustworthy AI systems by implementing comprehensive regulations and guidelines that promote responsible AI usage.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,ethical considerations,ethical standards,governance,policy regulation,regulation,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight,safety,standards conformity,unity</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-42a8b91e450f13e8f10679d8814fac73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af6ca05841bc213c4c908da8ca15327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-492be2be76ac28fb634286d651691400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec3eaa28f8579b1ad50ea687816653a8</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/165/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428294</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="Member States">
      <data key="d6">63.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are countries that are part of the European Union and must comply with directives like Council Directive 85/374/EEC.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Union (EU) is a political and economic union comprising various Member States that collaborate to establish and enforce a wide array of policies and regulations. These Member States are obligated to comply with EU mandates, particularly concerning migration and asylum policies, as well as national security and defense regulations. Under the EU’s jurisdiction, they engage in law enforcement and judicial cooperation to ensure collective security and justice.

Moreover, the European Union and its Member States work together to formulate laws and regulations across various sectors, including the governance of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. They also focus on economic growth by creating a regulatory framework that supports small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and start-ups. Additionally, the Member States are tasked with implementing regulations related to data protection, adhering to the overarching guidelines set by the European Union. Thus, the collaboration within the European Union facilitates a cohesive approach to governance and regulation among its Member States.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU governance,compliance,cooperation,governance,implementation,legislative adherence,political structure,political union,regulation,regulatory body,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-073b0a5a910fcaf1208261b2d390896a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f66c7cfe484df668dde369788c6d3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a65cc9d5292452e105480a128495e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357608662f50d4cb171a35b1ece5f9da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7f21ee31292214036736eb415637fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b14075f9663187b4b9cee91c38f3025d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/143/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/3/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/168/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/24/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427585</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Union" target="Union">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Union acts as a governing body for the Union, establishing frameworks for cooperation among Member States.</data>
      <data key="d8">cooperation,governance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
