    <edge source="Member State" target="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d6">41.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Each Member State has a Market Surveillance Authority responsible for approving real-world testing of AI systems within their jurisdiction.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States delegate the responsibility of regulating high-risk AI systems to the Market Surveillance Authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States utilize the Market Surveillance Authority to evaluate AI systems' risks and compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority operates within a Member State, enforcing EU guidelines and handling product compliance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority operates under the jurisdiction of the Member State to ensure compliance with the Commission's decisions.</data>
      <data key="d8">delegation,government regulation,membership,national compliance,national enforcement,oversight,regulation enforcement,regulatory body,regulatory enforcement,regulatory governance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b90a181c1c97be5262cd1f7a3919d6d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c78946b57af53cc3de27b286cf36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7195e1644a22885c55968d2c801e0064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
