    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="National Public Authorities">
      <data key="d6">15.0</data>
      <data key="d7">National public authorities can request the market surveillance authority to organize testing of high-risk AI systems if documentation is insufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority collaborates with National Public Authorities to ensure compliance and address non-compliance issues regarding AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance enforcement,cooperation,regulatory compliance,regulatory role</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec7e335819a5f1bde0e8d27164f300</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426903</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="Member States">
      <data key="d6">53.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"Member States grant powers to the market surveillance authorities for regulatory oversight of AI systems.".&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority plays a crucial role in the regulation and oversight of AI systems within Member States. It is responsible for notifying Member States about non-compliance issues related to AI systems, particularly focusing on high-risk categories. Each Member State must communicate with the Market Surveillance Authority regarding the testing and compliance of these high-risk AI systems, ensuring that all regulations are met effectively.

To facilitate the enforcement of market regulations, Member States are required to designate a Market Surveillance Authority that will serve as a single point of contact. This designation allows for a streamlined approach to regulation enforcement, fostering coordination with sectoral authorities. Furthermore, the Market Surveillance Authority has the authority to issue authorizations concerning high-risk AI systems, which can be challenged by the Member States if necessary.

Member States are also empowered to define and delegate specific roles to their chosen Market Surveillance Authorities, thereby enhancing the overall compliance and regulatory framework within the EU. This multi-faceted approach ensures that the Market Surveillance Authority can effectively oversee AI systems and uphold the standards set forth by EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">7,authority designation,authorization process,collaboration,compliance,compliance reporting,contact point,governance,legal authority,public oversight,regulatory communication,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698242b390a097d688dcef4fc03d6687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c69786b5e6add33d2fe8c768a341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd25b8a323071b471e7df42fd1a91ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-816f53d15728655866c48a3917b944f0</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/79/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/153/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428325</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">45.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The market surveillance authority is responsible for overseeing and ensuring compliance related to high-risk AI systems.".&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority oversees the compliance of high-risk AI systems once they are in service to ensure ongoing adherence to regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority must authorize the use and placement of high-risk AI systems in the market based on compliance with safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority is responsible for overseeing the implementation and compliance of regulations pertaining to High-Risk AI Systems in various sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Authorities are tasked with overseeing compliance for High-Risk AI Systems as part of regulatory requirements."&lt;&lt;"AI regulation, oversight</data>
      <data key="d8">9,oversight,regulation,regulatory enforcement,regulatory oversight,regulatory responsibility,risk management,safety compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dc7337a14ce811d1b428089495124e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65b1d13b27fde0e7b2a8e91d717968dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0842049245a4a646a8a2e3b5c4cb5fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93c18ff4b78baf6a152a71902a137a02</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/46/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/159/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427571</data>
    </edge>
