    <edge source="Union" target="AI Regulatory Sandboxes">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI Regulatory Sandboxes are established within the framework of the Union's legal regulations to ensure compliance and promote innovation.</data>
      <data key="d8">innovation support,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18b91d6551e6619c2e37a056560c0319</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426013</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">64.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office is part of the initiatives aimed at enhancing Union capabilities in artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office operates within the framework of the Union, functioning under its jurisdiction and adhering to the established regulations and guidelines concerning AI systems. Its primary role is to implement AI regulatory practices and codes of conduct that reflect the interests of all parties involved at the Union level. The Union oversees the AI Office, which is responsible for monitoring and supervising AI systems to ensure compliance with these regulations. Additionally, the AI Office facilitates the creation of codes of practice that align with the broader regulatory framework set forth by the Union. Overall, the AI Office serves to address the needs and interests of stakeholders within the Union regarding AI practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office operates across the Union to provide information and raise awareness about the Regulation and related obligations.</data>
      <data key="d8">awareness raising,collaboration,cross-border governance,development,geographical focus,governance,jurisdiction,organizational structure,oversight,policy applicability,regulation,regulatory body,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0f9cd63caadadd16211ae50c5b12c14f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede6b0da3acfca47d4e90d51eb5fc4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4141f8e823eac643a256625a708aec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee723ad2204a364a1d2dbe158b59a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2d90ba5ad6c09478b10ca441d65c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/62/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/64/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428535</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union" target="Regulation (EU) 2019/1020">
      <data key="d6">19.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Union establishes and enforces Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 which governs the market surveillance of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union is the governing entity that enacts regulations such as Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 for compliance and product safety.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,regulation,regulatory framework</data>
