    <edge source="Member States" target="European Central Bank">
      <data key="d6">24.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are required to report relevant information to the European Central Bank for prudential supervisory tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States must report to the European Central Bank any significant findings from market surveillance activities related to prudential supervision.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Central Bank oversees financial stability in the Eurozone, collaborating with Member States to enforce financial regulations.</data>
