      <data key="d6">22.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are required to comply with the regulations enforced by the European Data Protection Supervisor, which includes the imposition of fines for non-compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States are tasked with facilitating coordination between the European Data Protection Supervisor and market surveillance authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States designate competent authorities like the European Data Protection Supervisor for implementing regulations."&lt;&lt;"authority designation, regulatory compliance</data>
