      <data key="d6">24.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"General-Purpose AI Models are a subset of AI systems that are subject to specific requirements and standards.")&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models can be integrated into various AI systems developed by different providers.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models serve as components within AI systems, although they are not considered systems themselves without additional components.</data>
      <data key="d8">application,category classification,components,integration,standardisation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8f93754b5b045f375c5040d0de011e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f1f6979dcac05f71b03e16c6362efe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad9133b1b75e03ab5dc35d035927dbb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/40/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428294</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Systems" target="Regulation for General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation also applies to AI systems that incorporate general-purpose models, ensuring compliance and safety in their operation.</data>
