    <edge source="European Parliament" target="Commission">
      <data key="d6">72.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission and the European Parliament engage in a collaborative legislative process wherein the Commission plays a crucial role in notifying the European Parliament about various legislative activities. The Commission must notify the European Parliament whenever a delegated act is adopted, thereby linking the two institutions directly in the legislative procedure. Furthermore, the Commission is responsible for presenting reports on the enforcement of AI regulations to the European Parliament, which reviews and takes action based on these findings.

As part of its regulatory duties, the Commission also submits evaluations to the European Parliament, which includes updates on the progress of standardization and regulation of AI models. This ongoing communication is essential as the European Parliament confers implementing powers on the Commission under EU regulations, solidifying the legislative framework. The European Parliament relies on the Commission for the preparation of delegated acts that require its scrutiny, and it is notified about proposed acts, receiving a defined period to respond or object to them. This structured interaction establishes a dynamic relationship between the Commission and the European Parliament, ensuring that legislative processes are transparent and that both entities fulfill their roles effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission is tasked with reporting to the European Parliament on the evaluation and review of the Regulation as part of its responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission and the European Parliament work together in the legislative process to draft and negotiate EU laws regarding AI systems and measurement standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,governance,legislation,legislative action,legislative collaboration,legislative process,legislative relationship,notification,oversight,regulatory oversight,regulatory process,regulatory reporting</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eef924ac2e26af24531952fcd79e9d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79b7078e45aa680595b27c1baab1b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fb722dbde5159480cfd0e4534fc632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638834e00b09677a065c6dc80878fa7</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/175/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/174/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/74/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428543</data>
    </edge>
