    <edge source="European Parliament" target="European Commission">
      <data key="d6">33.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The European Commission and the European Parliament collaborate on legislative proposals and regulations important for the EU.")&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission submits reports and assessments to the European Parliament as part of its obligation to inform and involve them in the legislative process.&lt;SEP&gt;There is a collaborative relationship between the European Parliament and European Commission as they work together on legislative matters concerning AI and ethical regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission must notify the European Parliament about adopted delegated acts that affect legislation.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,cooperation,governance,legislative process,notification,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0d4324ec2284f40e56458ffbe5d2da80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd90900e1cf6e0c8072e210c7e853791</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/8/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427960</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Parliament" target="Council of the European Union">
      <data key="d6">63.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Council of the European Union and the European Parliament play essential roles in the legislative process within the European Union, particularly in relation to cybersecurity regulations, including those pertaining to the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity (ENISA). Both entities collaborate to adopt legislation that ensures the representation of public interests and member states, working together to establish regulations and directives that form the foundation of EU law and standards.

Their cooperation extends to the adoption and amendment of laws, which necessitates mutual agreement between the two institutions. This collaborative dynamic is also evident in their regulatory efforts concerning high-risk AI systems, where both the European Parliament and the Council contribute to shaping the legal framework governing these emerging technologies. Overall, the cooperation between the Council of the European Union and the European Parliament is vital for creating and amending laws that affect a wide range of issues within the EU, including cybersecurity and artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament and the Council of the European Union work together in the legislative process to harmonize laws across the EU regarding measuring instruments.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU governance,EU legislation,collaboration,decision-making,democratic process,governance,joint effort,legislation,legislative bodies,legislative collaboration,policy development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b330c1d8e73efeff5ccfef0a4f9ecd54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ace04fdc35c72669aa7d3ef95d6460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72f817acfaca14a17a21a75176f408a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab052c1ea237cce80eb265d1e45d48c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-557acf7764c3014cc0e27cf73b9a0fb0</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/78/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/77/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/49/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/74/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428543</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="European Parliament" target="Council">
      <data key="d6">85.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both the European Parliament and the Council have the power to revoke the delegation of authority granted to the Commission, showing their oversight functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Both the European Parliament and the Council play a crucial role in the legislative process and can inform the Commission regarding their objections to acts.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament and the Council are integral legislative bodies within the framework of the European Union (EU), jointly involved in the preparation, review, and approval of various legislative acts. They collaborate closely in the legislative processes, particularly in areas such as the enactment of directives and regulations, including those concerning artificial intelligence (AI). Their partnership ensures comprehensive governance over legislative measures, as they work together to adopt applicable legislation and review reports submitted by the European Commission. This cooperative relationship is essential for the effective functioning of the EU's legislative framework.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament and the Council work together in the legislative process to pass new regulations and directives for the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament and the Council must both agree or not object to certain delegated acts for them to enter into force.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU governance,European Union,collaborative governance,decision-making,governance,joint decision-making,legislation,legislative agreement,legislative body,legislative collaboration,legislative power,legislative process,oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96fc50a27ad634f25ca804994bf54408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58064eb84a11a467b8fc7fc22d8c7b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eef924ac2e26af24531952fcd79e9d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd90900e1cf6e0c8072e210c7e853791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe046aaecfccb5283c765f34bd06ab21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1055eaf28da7935aee66a1acf9705b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02c1809d1e7a16e9c8b3d0effff3a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f966dd054aee06b6959f9cca80bffc</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/97/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/121/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/29/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427960</data>
    </edge>
