    <edge source="Commission" target="Board">
      <data key="d6">54.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Board and the Commission play vital roles in providing guidance and advice for the implementation of regulations. They collaborate closely to ensure effective implementation, utilizing input from the Advisory Forum. The Commission supports the Board's activities specifically in market surveillance and the evaluation of regulations. Together, they offer recommendations for the implementation of these regulations by national competent authorities. Additionally, the Commission is responsible for submitting reports to the Board concerning the status of National Competent Authorities, facilitating discussions and recommendations. Moreover, the Commission consults the Board during the process of preparing standardization requests related to AI systems, further highlighting their cooperative efforts in overseeing regulatory frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission consults the Board to develop guidelines for the implementation of AI systems based on risk classification.</data>
