    <edge source="Commission" target="Article 97">
      <data key="d6">33.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 97 empowers the Commission to modify existing regulations based on evidence regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission utilizes Article 97 to amend provisions based on existing evidence concerning AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission's ability to update regulations is defined within Article 97, allowing adjustments to criteria and guidelines for general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 97 grants the Commission the authority to amend thresholds and criteria for evaluating AI models, ensuring regulations remain relevant.</data>
      <data key="d8">amendment authority,amendment power,legal authority,legislative framework,regulation adaptation,regulatory authority,regulatory updates</data>
