      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428355</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">187.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office and the Commission engage in a collaborative partnership focused on the governance and oversight of artificial intelligence (AI) models. The primary responsibility of the AI Office is to evaluate AI technologies, assess associated risks, and respond to alerts concerning potential systemic risks, which are communicated to the Commission. In its oversight role, the Commission monitors the activities of the AI Office and holds the authority to appoint experts to facilitate these evaluations.

The Commission is responsible for establishing and updating regulations governing the operations of the AI Office, ensuring adherence to established codes of practice for AI models within the Union. This collaboration enables the AI Office to effectively assess risks and implement necessary regulatory measures. Both entities work together to enforce these regulations, creating a robust framework for the oversight of AI technology.

Additionally, the Commission consults with the AI Office to ensure effective implementation and enforcement of AI standards and regulations. The AI Office is empowered by the Commission to monitor compliance with regulations pertaining to systemic risks and has the right to request updates on the Commission's guidelines. This dynamic process is characterized by collaboration and direct communication, allowing for the ongoing adjustment of guidelines as necessary.

The Commission also evaluates the powers and resources of the AI Office, ensuring it is well-equipped to enforce AI regulations. In turn, the AI Office provides crucial methodologies and evaluations to the Commission regarding the risk levels and standards for AI systems. Together, both entities work to enhance compliance with EU regulations on AI systems and support the establishment of AI regulatory sandboxes to ensure adherence to these regulations.

Furthermore, the AI Office collaborates with the Commission in the establishment of codes of practice for content management and the development of thresholds and criteria for assessing AI models associated with systemic risks. Overall, their coordinated efforts address the challenges posed by AI systems within the overarching regulatory framework, promoting the development and oversight of functions and objectives related to AI.</data>
      <data key="d8">agency evaluation,assessment,assessment framework,collaboration,compliance,compliance standards,coordination,evaluation,governance,guideline development,information exchange,monitoring,monitoring compliance,organizational structure,oversight,regulatory collaboration,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement,regulatory framework,regulatory oversight,regulatory relationship,regulatory response,regulatory support,regulatory updates,risk management,supervisory role</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-95e4a754288e197556a2ac28696f415d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-408ee65c3eab1e86c1c4207deaf4f216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094ac0cdb13f3aae73279288ea0dd3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec36ff3483a4dfeb40db5ce54ff19937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfbc57f477c4bd1902758e6902584d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912c6c18744e587fbf617952631e25a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46b1355e6b7cbd10c4515c00ce75a0b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede6b0da3acfca47d4e90d51eb5fc4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f567c4be37bce779f921de15ad5f2a7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dee723ad2204a364a1d2dbe158b59a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855a53cf044206d9081c530a357042fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0ab303aa0764433ae306cd3e410cb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/162/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/96/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/179/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/117/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/50/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/64/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428399</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="Notified Bodies">
