      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="recall of an AI system">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers initiate recalls to manage safety concerns related to their AI systems and ensure compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance action,safety management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="withdrawal of an AI system">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The provider may also be responsible for the withdrawal of an AI system from the market if it poses safety issues.</data>
      <data key="d8">market control,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18590180ace1a86abda373a524de5d70</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers are obligated to submit documentation to Market Surveillance Authorities to demonstrate compliance with high-risk AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers must work under the scrutiny of market surveillance authorities to ensure compliance when testing their AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance oversight,provider oversight,regulatory responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-88c5862ea0c154cbf48da804ec3ebf8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427308</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Competent Authority">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must cooperate with Competent Authorities to provide necessary documentation and ensure conformity with AI system regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider must provide necessary documentation to the competent authority to demonstrate conformity of the AI system.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance checks,documentation,regulatory compliance,regulatory cooperation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Authorised Representatives">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers appoint Authorised Representatives to ensure compliance with Union regulations regarding high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="EU Declaration of Conformity">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must prepare and provide the EU Declaration of Conformity to verify adherence to safety and operational standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is responsible for ensuring that the products comply with the standards reflected in the EU Declaration of Conformity.</data>
      <data key="d8">certification,regulatory compliance,standards verification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Technical Documentation">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers are responsible for preparing Technical Documentation that supports the compliance of their high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider must compile and maintain technical documentation to demonstrate compliance with the regulation for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance support,documentation,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Conformity Assessment Procedure">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must ensure that a proper Conformity Assessment Procedure is performed in order for high-risk AI systems to be market compliant.</data>
      <data key="d8">assessment,compliance validation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bd0062b915b55f037927238a05b5f6e3</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Notified Body">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The provider may seek approval from a notified body to certify that their high-risk AI system meets required regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">certification,compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Logs">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The provider must provide competent authorities with access to logs generated by the AI system as part of the compliance demonstration process.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,data transparency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Mandate">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The mandate allows the authorized representative to represent the provider before competent authorities on compliance matters.</data>
      <data key="d8">authority representation,compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-047db7dca163c57bf9683404937e7ec5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426763</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Article 16">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 16 outlines the obligations of providers regarding the compliance of high-risk AI systems they produce.</data>
      <data key="d8">provider obligations,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427154</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">26.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers are responsible for the development and deployment of High-Risk AI Systems, ensuring that they meet safety requirements and risk management measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is responsible for creating high-risk AI systems and ensuring they meet necessary oversight standards before deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider must assess high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with regulatory requirements before they can be deployed.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,deployment,development responsibility,regulatory compliance,responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-1bca7fe15bcbe076f97f98b2f3479775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/6/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428151</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Testing Procedures">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must implement Testing Procedures to ensure their high-risk AI systems meet established safety and regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">provider responsibility,safety compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-49c0c407ca162ed969c2229a2a1fd323</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427498</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Risk Mitigation Measures">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The provider is encouraged to develop risk mitigation measures to safeguard against foreseeable misuse of the high-risk AI system.</data>
      <data key="d8">risk management,safety</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-858c2a77ba4972f9c4e3f47479bfef07</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/65/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428032</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="systemic risk">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers' general-purpose AI models are assessed in terms of their potential systemic risks by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d8">model evaluation,risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-db8c2328a0858ecaf11e83a00191d499</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428197</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Testing Plan">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Provider is responsible for creating and submitting the Testing Plan to the market surveillance authority for approval.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,regulatory process</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428325</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="High-Risk AI Systems Registration">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers need to undertake High-Risk AI Systems Registration to legally conduct tests under the Union framework.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI testing,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b9d2702da009744eb8f52b44fea2c463</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428325</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="National Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must comply with directives and regulations outlined by the National Market Surveillance Authority to ensure their AI system's safety in testing.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Market Surveillance Authority oversees and regulates the activities of providers conducting tests of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,oversight,regulatory body,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d21ee76ebe03dd794f42225c64861fb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428325</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Prospective Provider">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The prospective provider may transition into a provider once compliance standards and testing processes for AI systems are met.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,transition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428325</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Informed Consent">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must obtain informed consent from subjects involved in the testing of AI systems to respect their rights and data privacy.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethics,legal obligation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-17d875a9ff2b02237bb4b9ba04e5b92a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428325</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Provider" target="Testing Protocols">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The provider must adhere to testing protocols established for the evaluation of the AI system in real-world conditions.</data>
      <data key="d8">assessment standards,compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d21ee76ebe03dd794f42225c64861fb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/60/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428325</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Intellectual Property Rights" target="Trade Secrets">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Intellectual property rights and trade secrets both protect the proprietary information and innovations related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal rights,protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f51d60adf9ebc465ed7e51912ec15382</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/88/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425986</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trade Secrets" target="Data Privacy">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Maintaining Data Privacy is crucial for protecting Trade Secrets from unauthorized access or disclosure.</data>
      <data key="d8">confidentiality,protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trade Secrets" target="Providers">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers of AI models must ensure that any information classified as trade secrets is safeguarded in accordance with confidentiality requirements.</data>
      <data key="d8">business secrets,information protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426397</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trade Secrets" target="Confidential Business Information">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Trade secrets are a subset of confidential business information that require specific protections under law.</data>
      <data key="d8">business strategy,information protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-be7ec602a72f4c2f19a5693b37872b32</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/25/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427609</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trade Secrets" target="Confidentiality">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Maintaining Confidentiality is essential to protect Trade Secrets, which are vital for a business's competitive advantage.</data>
      <data key="d8">business confidentiality,protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a33f9372e32e8879cc6f97cd662934d5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/167/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428475</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI HLEG" target="Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI HLEG developed the Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI to promote ethical standards in AI technology.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical standards,guideline development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI HLEG" target="seven non-binding ethical principles">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The seven non-binding ethical principles were developed by the AI HLEG to ensure that AI systems are trustworthy and ethically sound.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical standards,principle establishment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI" target="seven non-binding ethical principles">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The seven non-binding ethical principles are part of the Ethics Guidelines aimed at ensuring trustworthy AI development and use.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical principles,guideline content</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="seven non-binding ethical principles" target="human agency and oversight">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Human agency and oversight is one of the seven principles designed to safeguard human dignity in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI governance,ethical principles</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="seven non-binding ethical principles" target="technical robustness and safety">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Technical robustness and safety is included among the seven ethical principles to ensure reliable AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical principles,reliability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="seven non-binding ethical principles" target="privacy and data governance">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Privacy and data governance is one of the principles aimed at protecting personal data in AI applications.</data>
      <data key="d8">data protection,ethical principles</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="seven non-binding ethical principles" target="transparency">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Transparency is emphasized in the principles to help users understand and trust AI interactions.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical principles,user trust</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="seven non-binding ethical principles" target="diversity, non-discrimination and fairness">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">This principle promotes inclusion and prevents bias in AI systems, aligning with the ethical guidelines set forth.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical principles,inclusion</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="seven non-binding ethical principles" target="societal and environmental well-being">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">This principle underscores the importance of sustainable and socially beneficial AI systems as per the ethical guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical principles,sustainability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="seven non-binding ethical principles" target="accountability">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Accountability is a necessary principle to ensure responsible use of AI systems as outlined by the guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical principles,responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99e3c1ebc6fdcd9e7001c2c435c9ed50</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Standardisation Organisations" target="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d6">15.0</data>
      <data key="d7">National Competent Authorities work with Standardisation Organisations to ensure AI compliance is aligned with established standards.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities may collaborate with standardisation organisations to ensure AI systems meet necessary standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,regulatory collaboration,standard compliance,standardization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b723cd62d18d234251f462581cbbf5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/139/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426579</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Standardisation Organisations" target="Conformity Assessment Obligations">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Standardisation Organisations set the standards that frame the Conformity Assessment Obligations AI providers must meet.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,standard setting</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7cb433a13c63064d370f7b39be368c2b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426579</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Privacy" target="Data Governance">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Data governance practices ensure that individual privacy rights are upheld in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,data protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Data Governance" target="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-risk AI systems must adhere to data governance practices to ensure responsible use of data, which can impact health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI ethics,responsible data use</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-06ef56265dcb6096b96bc5ee3bfe08c2</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/10/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427784</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Data Governance" target="Third Parties">
      <data key="d6">15.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Third parties facilitate data governance by providing services that ensure compliance with regulations and the integrity of data sets.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties provide certification services that enhance data governance practices and ensure compliance.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance services,data integrity,external validation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d1b1b6d000ef2c2e744936b8e5264e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428719939f639dff07b7393c2795962</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427989</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Data Governance" target="Compliance Services">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Data governance frameworks often rely on compliance services for verification and certification.</data>
      <data key="d8">data integrity,verification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d1b1b6d000ef2c2e744936b8e5264e46</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/67/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427989</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Data Governance" target="Protection of Personal Data">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Data Governance defines how organizations should manage personal data to comply with protection standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">data management,governance framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e010ebb9b0353d97d9e67673267bc415</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/69/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428214</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diversity" target="Non-Discrimination">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Diversity in AI development is essential for preventing discrimination and promoting equitable outcomes in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">equity,inclusivity</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-219c0f42877791608631c01683c4dad5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="academia" target="civil society">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Academia and civil society both play roles in the development of ethical principles and standards for societal benefit.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,ethical standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="civil society" target="standardisation organisations">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"Civil society and standardisation organizations work together to implement ethical practices and standards.")</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,standard development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ethical Principles" target="Voluntary Best Practices">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Ethical principles provide the foundation for developing voluntary best practices that organizations may adopt for better governance.</data>
      <data key="d8">foundational guidelines,governance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ethical Principles" target="Development">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The development process aims to create and refine ethical principles that guide behavior and decision-making in various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical governance,guideline creation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Voluntary Best Practices" target="Standards">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Voluntary best practices often inform the creation of formal standards within organizations and industries.</data>
      <data key="d8">practice to standardization,quality assurance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Voluntary Best Practices" target="Standardisation">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Standardisation can lead to the establishment of voluntary best practices that organizations might adopt voluntarily.</data>
      <data key="d8">formulation of practices,organizational compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Standards" target="Standardisation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Standardisation involves creating formal standards, which are critical for ensuring compliance and quality across various sectors.</data>
      <data key="d8">consistency,quality assurance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b2be10277d876389f0830e8754a644dd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425994</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Standards" target="Providers">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must adhere to standards that govern the development and deployment of AI models to ensure they are compliant with legal and ethical guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426397</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Standards" target="Compliance Assessment">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Standards are evaluated during compliance assessments to verify adherence and conformity by AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d8">conformity testing,evaluation criteria</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-135955417d9c4f07fe24d56cf4e32c04</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426397</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Deployers">
      <data key="d6">34.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Deployers are required to conduct assessments for the deployment of high-risk AI systems to protect fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers hold the responsibility for ensuring the proper implementation of high-risk AI systems, monitoring their performance and compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are responsible for the implementation and management of High-Risk AI Systems under the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers are required to understand and evaluate the functionality of high-risk AI systems to ensure their correct use.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,oversight,regulatory compliance,responsibility,responsibility assignment,risk management,usage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5be37dc741c889195eef418bf4bdaca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d466db10803ea1ed7cbdf3800e0caaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712fbb27f2ad82df6098ef5c90507342</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/91/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/72/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/26/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428101</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The assessment specifically evaluates the risks associated with the use of high-risk AI systems to fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d8">evaluation process,risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef622939e94ede992aa62caffda0eeab</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/27/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748425998</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Providers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">34.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-risk AI systems are developed and supplied by the providers, necessitating special contractual terms.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are responsible for implementing and managing High-Risk AI Systems that adhere to regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are responsible for manufacturing and placing high-risk AI Systems on the market, thereby governing their regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,contractual obligations,regulatory compliance,regulatory responsibility,system management,technology,technology supply</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3167c49292549db4146e77b8eba160c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ee76b22003d9dda0413f891ae1e1c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887d23f7f753b9f8b5b6ad22d38360be</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/20/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/90/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428388</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="CE Marking">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">CE marking is required for high-risk AI systems as an indication of compliance with EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems must bear the CE marking to signify compliance with regulatory standards for market freedom.</data>
      <data key="d8">certification,compliance,market standards,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a25b8d2308a532accd5bf77027c9a7df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e442b04ad431e8e1a74bf9fa0f8bc5f</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/16/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/129/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427797</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Regulatory Framework">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulatory Framework outlines the guidelines and requirements for identifying and managing High-Risk AI Systems within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d8">regulatory guidelines,safety standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426041</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Conformity Assessment Procedures">
      <data key="d6">29.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Conformity Assessment Procedures apply specifically to High-Risk AI Systems to ensure regulatory compliance and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Risk AI Systems undergo Conformity Assessment Procedures to ensure they meet safety and technical standards before approval.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity Assessment Procedures are developed specifically for the assessment of High-Risk AI Systems, ensuring they meet safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI compliance,assessment procedures,compliance,regulatory compliance,safety assessment,safety evaluation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7159c0fe88b88c3a3080fefad7a98419</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/173/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426967</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d6">45.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market Surveillance Authorities are tasked with overseeing compliance and safety assessments of high-risk AI systems under the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Authorities assess and monitor High-Risk AI Systems to ensure compliance and safety standards are met.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities focus on compliance activities specifically related to high-risk AI systems under EU regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Authorities focus on compliance related to High-Risk AI Systems to mitigate risks associated with their deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities are specifically tasked with monitoring high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance evaluation,compliance focus,regulatory focus,regulatory oversight,risk classification,risk management,safety oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-70fac425f08c058417791cd1d66faab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda722630e3447daa9258a423b2cbedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094ac0cdb13f3aae73279288ea0dd3f8</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427566</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="AI Office">
      <data key="d6">25.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office assists in ensuring compliance and oversight of high-risk AI systems under the directives established by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office is involved in the supervision and evaluation processes of High-Risk AI Systems alongside Market Surveillance Authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office oversees the compliance of high-risk AI systems, ensuring they meet established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance oversight,oversight,regulatory collaboration,regulatory support,risk management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a273f410d091773f8f78908d89074682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094ac0cdb13f3aae73279288ea0dd3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0873f73c77d97fdb97b3523748b32638</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/160/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/161/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/75/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427884</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="European Commission">
      <data key="d6">28.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The European Commission assesses and regulates high-risk AI systems to mitigate their potential risks to health and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission oversees the classification and regulation of high-risk AI systems to mitigate potential risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is responsible for regulating high-risk AI systems and setting criteria for their identification and management.</data>
      <data key="d8">regulation,regulatory authority,risk management,technology oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-07e87c64b9193b8ef1ad64f22e59474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b4365b37f348c4492d16b0258db2b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426862</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Article 97">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-risk AI systems are governed by regulations that the European Commission can amend under Article 97 to address safety concerns.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,legislative authority</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426070</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent authorities monitor and provide oversight concerning high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426070</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Health and Safety">
      <data key="d6">27.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Health and Safety standards are crucial for ensuring that high-risk AI systems do not pose a risk to individuals or society.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are classified based on their potential risk to health and safety, highlighting the need for strict regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The assessment of high-risk AI systems includes consideration of health and safety impacts to prevent potential harm.</data>
      <data key="d8">risk assessment,risk management,risk mitigation,safety,safety assessment,safety standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-909533e383afbbc7e4815cf0fcaee662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e87c64b9193b8ef1ad64f22e59474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427202</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Data Processing">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The nature and amount of data processed by high-risk AI systems is a critical factor in evaluating their risks and impacts.</data>
      <data key="d8">data analysis,risk evaluation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426070</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Vulnerable Position">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The identification of individuals in a vulnerable position is essential to assessing the potential negative impacts of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">risk assessment,social impact</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-40fea6c01126f1d5b9269b29322c34de</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426070</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d6">35.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-Risk AI Systems pose specific dangers that could infringe upon Fundamental Rights, necessitating careful assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;The classification of high-risk AI systems considers their impact on individuals' fundamental rights, necessitating protective measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The deployment of High-Risk AI Systems may affect Fundamental Rights by infringing on privacy, fairness, or other basic human rights.&lt;SEP&gt;The design of high-risk AI systems must consider and protect fundamental rights throughout their operation.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical considerations,ethical design,human rights,rights impact,rights protection,risk assessment,technology impact</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-07e87c64b9193b8ef1ad64f22e59474d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2567ed4486ee359c31fd399ca77e5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe2025206c39f7e4a18788aafe6a345</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/52/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/14/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/9/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428074</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d6">24.0</data>
      <data key="d7">National Competent Authorities assess High-Risk AI Systems to determine compliance with safety regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;National Competent Authorities enforce regulations concerning high-risk AI systems to ensure public safety and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities regulate and oversee the use and disclosure of high-risk AI systems to safeguard public and national security interests.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,oversight,public safety,regulation,regulatory oversight,risk management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c2b5e8ac0ca306f10d2418b0493cf1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc478de6f2db42158f4375b3746b2a3</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/7/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/78/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426988</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="National Public Authorities">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"National public authorities are empowered to request documentation and access to high-risk AI systems to perform their regulatory roles.".&lt;SEP&gt;National Public Authorities are responsible for managing and enforcing regulations concerning High-Risk AI Systems to protect public health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d8">documentation access,oversight,risk management,safety regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69dd3a3cd7b3f9b54e8170860963df4f</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426491</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Safeguard Procedure">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Safeguard Procedure is necessary to manage and enforce regulations regarding High-Risk AI Systems to prevent violations of rights.</data>
      <data key="d8">regulatory compliance,risk management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8484bd5b0709234bd04f595f21062cb4</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/157/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426074</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Notified Bodies">
      <data key="d6">35.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Notified Bodies assess conformity related to High-Risk AI Systems as part of regulatory procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified Bodies assess high-risk AI systems for compliance before they can enter the market, ensuring quality and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified bodies conduct conformity assessments on high-risk AI systems, ensuring their compliance with safety and performance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified Bodies verify the conformity of High-Risk AI Systems as part of their operational obligations under relevant regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">assessment,compliance,compliance assessment,compliance verification,conformity assessment,quality assurance,regulatory compliance,regulatory responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-219cf6d8c7b4aad1f5b0ef20e76dd301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27e18f1e7a64d4e39363cecdd238a532</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/38/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426967</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Regulation (EU) 2019/881">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-risk AI systems must comply with requirements set forth in Regulation (EU) 2019/881 to ensure cybersecurity and conformity.</data>
      <data key="d8">cybersecurity compliance,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426152</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Official Journal of the European Union">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Official Journal of the European Union publishes compliance information regarding high-risk AI systems, aiding in their certification.</data>
      <data key="d8">information dissemination,publication</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426152</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Article 10(4)">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-risk AI systems are presumed to comply with relevant requirements outlined in Article 10(4) when trained and tested appropriately.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,presumption of conformity</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426152</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Article 15">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-risk AI systems that are certified follow the cybersecurity requirements specified in Article 15 of Regulation (EU) 2019/881.</data>
      <data key="d8">certification,cybersecurity requirements</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-612f941c5aacf034e74375e9c0cf157d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/42/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426152</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Providers">
      <data key="d6">36.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers are responsible for ensuring that high-risk AI systems meet mandatory requirements for compliance and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are responsible for the management and adherence to regulatory requirements regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers have the responsibility for ensuring that high-risk AI systems meet the established compliance requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers develop high-risk AI systems that must undergo conformity assessments by Notified Bodies to ensure compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance requirement,product development,provider responsibility,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,regulatory responsibility,responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-492be2be76ac28fb634286d651691400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26d81b437e55548d31af147fd90ef23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9512f56ddf79fc1a7f65b696c84e2eb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/64/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427837</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Article 9">
      <data key="d6">25.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 9 emphasizes the need for a risk management system in the context of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 9 outlines the necessary risk management processes that must be implemented for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 9 establishes the criteria and framework for identifying high-risk AI systems across Member States.</data>
      <data key="d8">criteria establishment,regulatory details,regulatory framework,risk management,system requirements</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d5f6eeef12730fe7e1d6c295c7eaa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-492be2be76ac28fb634286d651691400</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/74/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427571</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Article 72">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 72 mandates the implementation of a post-market monitoring system for high-risk AI systems to ensure ongoing compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems require post-market monitoring as described in Article 72 to ensure their ongoing safety.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,post-market oversight,regulation,safety monitoring</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4f95db6a695983806a19cc3c8894b56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88ec674dfb566598c9f54b13ca64a3c4</data>
