      <data key="d11">1748426456</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="documentation">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office may require documentation from AI providers to ensure compliance with regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">documentation,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3e6126c3c3690a61de0436f93b2741fd</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/163/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="Scientific Panel">
      <data key="d6">63.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office and the Scientific Panel maintain a collaborative relationship, with the Scientific Panel providing essential expert advice to the AI Office regarding the implementation and enforcement of AI regulations. The AI Office plays a supportive role in assisting the Scientific Panel with tasks related to the evaluation and oversight of general-purpose AI models. The Scientific Panel is responsible for alerting the AI Office to potential systemic risks associated with these AI models, and its alerts can prompt the AI Office to conduct necessary evaluations. Furthermore, the Scientific Panel conducts evaluations and delivers findings to the AI Office regarding AI models that require monitoring for systemic risks, underscoring the importance of their partnership in ensuring the safe and effective regulation of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office oversees the establishment of the Scientific Panel to support regulatory activities in AI enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office may consult the Scientific Panel to ensure technical expertise informs the codes of practice for AI models.</data>
      <data key="d8">advisory support,alert system,assistance,collaboration,consultation,evaluation,evaluation trigger,expert panel,expertise,oversight,regulatory implementation,regulatory oversight,risk assessment,risk monitoring,support</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-831c946b1acae90a683cbc5ac489ffaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be11332f2ca4895c0b3e1f0560018e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a644c604bba8cdc33a7125c5db02395c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8209179d5378dd2b308defab64f33b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1b5a22fa12a7caf6d6a82166e9ac79b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/68/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/116/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/151/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428168</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="Qualified Alert">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A Qualified Alert is specifically directed to the AI Office for evaluating and responding to identified risks.</data>
      <data key="d8">formal notification,risk management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f1dadce264ce0bde619c89498814a8a8</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/90/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426173</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="Regulation (EU) 2019/1020">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office operates under the guidelines set forth in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office operates under the guidelines set forth in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 to enforce compliance and procedural rights.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance oversight,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0873f73c77d97fdb97b3523748b32638</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/75/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427884</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d6">51.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office plays a crucial role in the oversight and regulation of General-Purpose AI Models within the Union market. It is responsible for ensuring transparency regarding the data utilized in these models, promoting adherence to codes of practice that are currently being developed. Additionally, the AI Office monitors providers of General-Purpose AI Models to ensure compliance with established regulations, reinforcing safety and technical requirements for the entry of such models into the market. The institution's efforts are focused on creating guidelines that govern the operation of General-Purpose AI Models and address associated risks, thereby aiming to enhance accountability and safeguard users within the AI landscape.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,governance,involvement,market entry,monitoring,oversight,regulation,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,transparency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-831c946b1acae90a683cbc5ac489ffaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6477d7c505ff9323e02b84771a5cb45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-898711e7e6ddb7ddaceadb36ff94f179&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366448bb58f05fbe95d08e2bec3f1b28</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/107/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/116/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/89/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428172</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="Independent Experts">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office may engage Independent Experts to assist in evaluations and compliance assessments of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d8">evaluation,expert involvement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-608fa30e901d53cfe8a70a06d1760b00</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/164/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426239</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="Article 18 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office's operations are aligned with the procedural rights provided in Article 18 for the enforcement of compliance.</data>
      <data key="d8">procedural rights,regulatory compliance</data>
