    <edge source="AI Office" target="providers of general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must report incidents to the AI Office, reflecting the oversight role it plays in AI safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Office oversees the compliance of providers of general-purpose AI models and ensures regulatory adherence.</data>
      <data key="d8">accountability,incident reporting,oversight,regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bdcf8f8cc5bcd01cd9809a08b83c4dab</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/55/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426397</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d6">58.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office is actively involved in engaging with providers of general-purpose AI models to discuss and address systemic risks associated with these technologies. Its responsibilities include evaluating these models to ensure they comply with established regulations and assessing their systemic risks. The AI Office may interact with providers to gather necessary compliance information and is also tasked with overseeing the classification and notification process for models that could potentially present systemic risks. Additionally, the AI Office is responsible for monitoring these general-purpose AI models, particularly focusing on those that exhibit potential systemic risks. Its role extends to assessing the risks of general-purpose AI models based on defined thresholds and engaging with experts and stakeholders to better understand the capabilities and potential dangers linked to these models.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance evaluation,dialogue,engagement,information gathering,monitoring,oversight,regulation,regulatory engagement,regulatory responsibilities,risk assessment,risk management,risk mitigation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78ba06fc96beac812eca04fddc34af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3fc79c1ca06abe0f478974180491236&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e116bc92c8c7cf688c26ea188fd0b2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/93/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428197</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="APIs">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office utilizes APIs to access the general-purpose AI models for assessment purposes.</data>
      <data key="d8">evaluation process,technical access</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b624273f3ad633492c95cc1f3608920d</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/92/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426456</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI Office" target="Provider of General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI Office may engage in dialogues with the provider to discuss compliance before making formal requests for information.</data>
      <data key="d8">dialogue,information exchange</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
