      <data key="d11">1748426717</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI systems" target="Regulation (EU) 2022/2065">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The regulation addresses obligations related to AI systems, ensuring their outputs are transparent and compliant with legal standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI transparency,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426824</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI systems" target="democratic processes">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI systems can pose risks to democratic processes through the spread of disinformation, making regulation necessary for safeguarding democracy.</data>
      <data key="d8">disinformation risk,governance impact</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-809e7b6beac5228dbcfec6607a4d6405</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/136/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426824</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI systems" target="law enforcement authorities">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Law enforcement authorities utilize AI systems to aid in the detection, investigation, and prosecution of criminal offenses, raising issues of accuracy and fairness.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal implications,technology use</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427018</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI systems" target="national competent authorities">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">National competent authorities are responsible for ensuring the safe deployment of high-risk AI systems through proper certification processes.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI safety,regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e8e772b9822216e1506938086aedcaba</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/36/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427202</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI systems" target="facial recognition databases">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI systems are utilized to create and expand facial recognition databases, leading to privacy issues.</data>
      <data key="d8">privacy concerns,technology use</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea591e8c170e7b5ae61060a7a9c9e5fb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/43/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427698</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI systems" target="Mass Surveillance">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI systems are employed in mass surveillance to analyze data and identify individuals through facial recognition.</data>
      <data key="d8">surveillance impact,technology application</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea591e8c170e7b5ae61060a7a9c9e5fb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/43/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427698</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI systems" target="Facial Recognition Databases">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI systems enable the creation and expansion of facial recognition databases through data processing techniques.</data>
      <data key="d8">data management,technological integration</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea591e8c170e7b5ae61060a7a9c9e5fb</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/43/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427698</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="provider">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A provider is responsible for developing or placing an AI system on the market, which is central to their operations.</data>
      <data key="d8">development,market placement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="deployer">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A deployer utilizes AI systems as per their authority, playing a crucial role in the practical application of such systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">authority,utilization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="importer">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An importer brings an AI system from a third country to the Union market, facilitating its availability.</data>
      <data key="d8">international trade,market supply</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="distributor">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A distributor makes AI systems available in the market, linking providers with end-users.</data>
      <data key="d8">market access,supply chain</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="Placing on the Market">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The act of placing an AI system on the market is crucial for its legal availability and commercialization within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d8">availability,market introduction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="Putting into Service">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Putting an AI system into service marks the transition to operational use, essential for its functionality.</data>
      <data key="d8">functionality,operational readiness</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="Making Available on the Market">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Making an AI system available on the market is a necessary step to ensure it can be acquired by users or organizations.</data>
      <data key="d8">distribution,market accessibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5327e3021446f22c1f0b9f91a7a3682a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="real-world testing plan">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A real-world testing plan is crucial for evaluating the functionality and impact of an AI system under actual conditions.</data>
      <data key="d8">evaluation,testing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f518f21912bc99e646236ef5569a88e9</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/3/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI system" target="testing plan">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The AI system must adhere to the stipulated guidelines within the testing plan to ensure it meets regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6fadd3405f1febb84753df655c577486</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/76/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427308</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="model" target="research and development">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Models are often developed through research and development activities prior to their market introduction, reflecting the iterative nature of AI innovation.</data>
      <data key="d8">development,innovation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0f96f0c84ed2ea0ee7c72badcbbc5bf5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/97/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426054</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Integration">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The general-purpose AI model is a key component in the integration process of AI systems, enabling varied purposes and functionalities.</data>
      <data key="d8">model significance,operational roles</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c99635d8be9520a61f07475e6f38b608</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/100/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426062</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Article 51">
      <data key="d6">15.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 51 outlines requirements for providers associated with general-purpose AI models, particularly regarding notice to the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;The classification of a general-purpose AI model is contingent upon the requirements stated in Article 51, which dictates necessary notifications to the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,model classification,model oversight,risk management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426088</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Article 90">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 90 provides the Commission with the authority to assess and designate general-purpose AI models that present systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d8">model assessment,systemic risk</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426088</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Notification Requirements">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Notification requirements apply to providers of general-purpose AI models to inform the Commission of any systemic risks present.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,risk notification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8db527e2cb5184f356edf18fd10c9f36</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/52/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426088</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Scientific Panel">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The scientific panel can request relevant information about general-purpose AI models to fulfil its regulatory tasks.</data>
      <data key="d8">information request,regulatory task</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426459</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="AI Regulation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI regulation outlines the necessary procedures for classifying general-purpose AI models that may pose systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d8">classification,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426552</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="High-Impact Capabilities">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">General-purpose AI models are defined by their high-impact capabilities that necessitate specific regulatory scrutiny.</data>
      <data key="d8">classification,impact assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-656f81fa0b40b7a24d1c380c887e5b9a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/112/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426552</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Systemic Risk">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">General-Purpose AI Models can be classified based on their potential to contribute to systemic risk, creating a need for regulatory scrutiny.</data>
      <data key="d8">classification,risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d681a1b37904af3153a1df63c28a8142</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/113/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426773</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Generative AI Models">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Generative AI models can be classified as a type of general-purpose AI model due to their flexible application across diverse tasks.</data>
      <data key="d8">model classification,versatility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7d74787f82958c07195dad5ff4da3b57</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/99/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427243</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Floating Point Operations">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The use of Floating Point Operations is crucial in determining the capabilities of General-Purpose AI Models based on their training data usage.</data>
      <data key="d8">computational metrics,training assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e116bc92c8c7cf688c26ea188fd0b2fe</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/111/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428197</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Cumulative Computation">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Cumulative Computation is a key criterion used to determine whether a general-purpose AI model possesses high impact capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d8">capability assessment,evaluation metric</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428355</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="High Impact Capabilities">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High Impact Capabilities determine if a General-Purpose AI Model could pose systemic risk, leading to its classification.</data>
      <data key="d8">classification criteria,risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428355</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="General-Purpose AI Model" target="Technical Tools and Methodologies">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Technical Tools and Methodologies are necessary for evaluating General-Purpose AI Models, specifically in assessing their impact capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d8">assessment criteria,evaluation tools</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9e5484976fb39d2996307dda5a0931d6</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/51/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428355</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Article 97" target="The Commission">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 97 gives the Commission the authority to amend technical documentation requirements in response to technical progress.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission utilizes Article 97 as the legal foundation to amend regulations related to conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal authority,legislative power,regulatory amendment,regulatory authority</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/&lt;SEP&gt;https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427940</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Article 97" target="Annexes VI and VII">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 97 allows the Commission to amend Annexes VI and VII based on technical progress.</data>
      <data key="d8">amendment authority,technical updates</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b7e2e0b9693bb73297f4cae082e5aa75</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/43/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426498</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Article 97" target="Technical Documentation">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 97 is relevant to the amendments of technical documentation as it sets forth the empowerment for the Commission to make necessary changes.</data>
      <data key="d8">amendments,compliance assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427940</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Article 97" target="Legal Acts">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 97 pertains to the legal acts that govern the compliance and amendments required by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d8">legislative authority,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-27a108f2f49540d0239658b32477aab4</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427940</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Article 97" target="Annex XII">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 97 enables amendments to be made to Annex XII in response to technological advancements in compliance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d8">regulatory updates,technological evolution</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-91d56158a4a9411ebe99783effcebca7</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/53/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428053</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Safeguards">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent Authorities are responsible for ensuring that appropriate Safeguards are in place to protect individual rights in law enforcement activities.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,protection of rights</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3e7a853f20702bb64df032bcfe5c2e04</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/22/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426164</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Importers">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Importers must cooperate with competent authorities to demonstrate the safety and compliance of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance cooperation,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426175</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Technical Documentation">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent Authorities may request Technical Documentation from Importers to verify compliance of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">documentation review,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87ab257ee4df19878199b525e3ae854e</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/23/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426175</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Market Surveillance Authorities of Member States">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market surveillance authorities collaborate with competent authorities to ensure proper investigation and management of reports concerning serious incidents.</data>
      <data key="d8">oversight,regulatory cooperation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426389</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Initial Report">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An initial report regarding a serious incident must be sent to competent authorities for further investigation and action.</data>
      <data key="d8">preliminary notification,regulatory process</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b9e2425d325b96342fb76768707fe3cf</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/73/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426389</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Competent Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent Authorities oversee the actions and compliance of the Competent Market Surveillance Authority in enforcing AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-06455acfb04ed0ea0e1fcd7b8fa89595</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/141/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426696</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Providers of AI systems">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must closely cooperate with competent authorities to enable compliance with the relevant obligations outlined in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,regulatory cooperation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-457bf0e90f1920e6839b11cd66b1060b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/85/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426816</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Distributors">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Distributors are required to cooperate with competent authorities in ensuring compliance of high-risk AI systems with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance oversight,regulatory cooperation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2cacea1a9e8134dea64495d76d382dcc</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/24/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427151</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Obligations">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent authorities ensure providers and their representatives fulfill their obligations under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d8">enforcement,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4650c5b3d73643d93f915f7eeb206da5</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/54/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427331</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Providers of AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers of AI Systems receive guidance and support from Competent Authorities while participating in the AI regulatory sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d8">support and compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427363</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Regulatory Sandboxes">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Regulatory sandboxes rely on competent authorities to provide support, guidance, and regulatory oversight during innovation testing.</data>
      <data key="d8">oversight,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427363</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Exit Reports">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent authorities analyze exit reports to assess the outcomes of AI systems tested in regulatory sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance assessment,outcome evaluation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-25bb3d8d3e3c5a7c563c8d8cf0f4cecf</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/57/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427363</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Competent Authorities" target="Final Report">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent Authorities will compile the Final Report at the termination of the AI Regulatory Sandboxes, summarizing lessons learned and best practices.</data>
