    </edge>
    <edge source="Biometric Data" target="Article 3, point (18)">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Biometric Data is subject to the definitions provided in Article 3, point (18) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, emphasizing its relevance to EU data protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d8">EU regulations,data classification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d0d2c55c34335ae38db203f32e428ce7</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/14/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427874</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Biometric Data" target="Article 3, point (13)">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Biometric Data is explicitly governed by the conditions set forth in Article 3, point (13) of Directive (EU) 2016/680, relevant to law enforcement practices.</data>
      <data key="d8">data governance,legal implications</data>
