      <data key="d11">1748427539</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI" target="Union values">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The development of AI is directly tied to Union values, which must guide its regulatory framework to ensure trust and human-centric design.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,technology ethics</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427646</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI" target="Treaty on European Union (TEU)">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI regulations must comply with the principles outlined in the Treaty on European Union, especially regarding human rights.</data>
      <data key="d8">fundamental rights,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427646</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI" target="Article 2 of TEU">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 2 of the Treaty provides the values that should inform the development of AI as a technology serving people.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical guidelines,human-focused goals</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427646</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI" target="Article 6 TEU">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Article 6 of the Treaty emphasizes the Charter's role in ensuring that AI serves human well-being and fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical technology,human rights</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427646</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI" target="Human-Centric Technology">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI should be developed as a human-centric technology to prioritize the well-being of individuals and communities.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical technology,human welfare</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bfb2e966719f9f858b7cc80f302e2e30</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/6/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427646</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI" target="Digital Transformation">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Digital Transformation is driven by advancements in AI, which allow businesses to implement innovative technological solutions.</data>
      <data key="d8">business strategy,technological advancement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5bfe284b31053ed0488ca88518b58ac1</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/8/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427719</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI" target="Innovation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI technologies require continuous innovation to remain relevant and effective, emphasizing the need for development within regulated frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d8">regulation,technological advancement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f1bd36f2082e6f670210d08c02e3d502</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/138/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428381</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="law" target="competent personnel">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Law requires that personnel understand legal frameworks to ensure compliance and oversight of rights.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal compliance,regulatory oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426216</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="competent personnel" target="expertise">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Competent personnel's tasks are dependent on their expertise in specific fields like technology, AI, and law.</data>
      <data key="d8">knowledge application,specialization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426216</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="competent personnel" target="fundamental rights">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Personnel are tasked with the protection and supervision of fundamental rights as part of their roles.</data>
      <data key="d8">regulatory supervision,rights protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-cefc8b7d72abc98979ddfb70fd07da6a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/28/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426216</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fundamental rights" target="participants">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Participants are involved in protecting fundamental rights through their engagement in safeguarding practices.</data>
      <data key="d8">engagement,protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f0b972a179b165ba7115316ba8d0d987</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/58/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426579</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fundamental rights" target="natural person">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Natural persons possess fundamental rights that may be affected by the use of AI systems in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d8">human rights,legal protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427018</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fundamental rights" target="effective remedy">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Fundamental rights ensure that natural persons have the right to effective remedies when their rights are violated by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">human rights,legal enforcement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427018</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fundamental rights" target="right to a fair trial">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The right to a fair trial is a fundamental right that must be upheld even when using AI systems in law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d8">justice,legal protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b97cbb2fe13d416e4d611c2cf10a129b</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/59/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427018</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Quality Management System" target="Providers of high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers must implement a Quality Management System to ensure compliance with applicable regulations for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,quality assurance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c676949949696126d6968ce48edbc389</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/17/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426223</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Quality Management System" target="Testing Procedures">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Quality Management System must include Testing Procedures to ensure that high-risk AI systems are validated properly before usage.</data>
