    <edge source="Article 53" target="Provider of General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The provider must adhere to the documentation requirements outlined in Article 53 to ensure regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d8">documentation,regulatory requirements</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-cb013d3a164b5a474fe46af58022a9d0</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/91/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426459</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Obligations in Articles 53 and 55" target="Implementing Acts">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Implementing Acts are derived from the obligations set forth in Articles 53 and 55, outlining their application.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal compliance,regulatory framework</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-081bc40b24333163a9239c2c45190bcc</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426363</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Implementing Acts" target="Examination Procedure in Article 98(2)">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Examination Procedure in Article 98(2) provides the method for evaluating and adopting Implementing Acts.</data>
      <data key="d8">procedural guidelines,regulatory process</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-081bc40b24333163a9239c2c45190bcc</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426363</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Implementing Acts" target="Articles 53 and 55">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Implementing Acts are created to fulfill the obligations set forth in Articles 53 and 55, demonstrating a direct link between legislative requirements and regulatory measures.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal obligations,regulatory compliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-081bc40b24333163a9239c2c45190bcc</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/56/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426363</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union institutions" target="Bodies">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Union institutions are composed of various bodies that have designated roles within the EU governance structure.</data>
      <data key="d8">governance,structural relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426367</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union institutions" target="Agencies">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Union institutions include agencies responsible for specific regulatory and operational tasks within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d8">functional relationship,oversight</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426367</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Union institutions" target="Offices">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Union institutions encompass offices that participate in the administrative functions of governance and regulation.</data>
      <data key="d8">administration,operational relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426367</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bodies" target="Agencies">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Bodies can establish agencies to address specific issues and implement policies within the framework of the Union.</data>
      <data key="d8">organizational structure,specialization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8f950b0056f6fe5d8f4c1fed6ffcce00</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/23/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426367</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Deep Fakes" target="Transparency Obligation">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The transparency obligation applies specifically to deep fakes, ensuring users disclose their artificial nature to maintain clarity for viewers.</data>
      <data key="d8">content regulation,ethical standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Transparency Obligation" target="Manipulated Content">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The transparency obligation mandates that manipulated content be labeled to inform viewers of its artificial nature, enhancing ethical use.</data>
      <data key="d8">content regulation,ethical standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Transparency Obligation" target="Artificial Origin">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The transparency obligation supports the need for labeling content that is artificially generated or manipulated, addressing its origin.</data>
      <data key="d8">content labeling,ethical transparency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Providers of AI System" target="Deployed AI System">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Providers deploy AI systems to produce manipulated content, impacting various sectors, including media and creativity.</data>
      <data key="d8">media production,technology deployment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Deployed AI System" target="Manipulated Content">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Deployed AI systems are responsible for generating manipulated content that can misrepresent reality, requiring transparency.</data>
      <data key="d8">authenticity,content creation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Manipulated Content" target="Public Interest">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">When manipulated content is presented as information, it should align with public interest principles to maintain trust.</data>
      <data key="d8">information integrity,public welfare</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Public Interest" target="Risk Factors">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"Risk Factors can dictate when certain law enforcement actions, including the use of biometric identification, are deemed necessary to serve the Public Interest.")</data>
      <data key="d8">regulations,safety measures</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-1d0dcb7cb13665cdf8522e8f92cfb166</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/33/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748427083</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Public Interest" target="High-Quality Data Sets">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The provision of high-quality data sets is significant for serving the public interest in the context of AI system development.</data>
      <data key="d8">data access,public welfare</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9f2f4cab7db3f8f9288f3fd79ff9595e</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/68/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748428127</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Artificial Origin" target="Human Review Process">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The human review process ensures that AI-generated content with artificial origins undergoes scrutiny for quality and accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d8">content verification,quality assurance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-93a291f34d113ade59ae8d1ab3a9e32a</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI-generated text" target="human review">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI-generated text should be subjected to human review to maintain accuracy and credibility before publication.</data>
      <data key="d8">content accuracy,editorial standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="human review" target="editorial control">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Human review is often an aspect of the broader practice of editorial control over published content.</data>
      <data key="d8">editorial practices,quality assurance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="editorial control" target="natural or legal person">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Natural or legal persons are responsible for exercising editorial control over published content and ensuring accountability.</data>
      <data key="d8">content oversight,responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI-generated content" target="public interest">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">AI-generated content is often created with the aim of informing the public, thereby relating to public interest.</data>
      <data key="d8">information dissemination,responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AI-generated content" target="content publication">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Content publication may include AI-generated content, which is subject to human oversight to ensure its suitability for public distribution.</data>
      <data key="d8">content management,publication standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="public interest" target="editorial responsibility">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Editorial responsibility is essential in protecting public interest by ensuring that published information is accurate and reliable.</data>
      <data key="d8">accountability,public welfare</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="editorial responsibility" target="human oversight">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Human oversight is a critical component of maintaining editorial responsibility in content publication.</data>
      <data key="d8">accountability,quality assurance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87f9ef3e8ad0a13698aa0fdf5b5cfd51</data>
      <data key="d10">https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/recital/134/</data>
      <data key="d11">1748426369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authorities of Member States" target="Article 3">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market surveillance authorities operate under the guidelines set forth in Article 3 regarding serious incidents and reporting protocols.</data>
      <data key="d8">legislative compliance,regulatory framework</data>
